  "Commits": [
    {
      "Id": "1b3d839e",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-20T21:20:46.8803376-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n\nPlease ready the markdown article i have attached that documents my brand new technique for browser automation. I want to build a framework that can allow other developers to easily create browser automations that use this same technique. I also want you to study the unified harness js script i have attached. Please note in particular how it is able to in the deepseek portion, autoclick the continue button when it appears. For sites built with react, it needs to simulate the input and ensure its trusted for the react runtime. I want this to be apart of the framework so we can easily simulate input for any given react site and any given element. \nI also want you to develop an automated way to have the c# code build or generate a tamper monkey javascript that can be put into the browser in tamper monkey. The js script that runs in the browsers job will be to communicate back with the c# code and accept commands. Now i want the framework to have 2 ipc modes, one being http, and the other being web sockets. We want to have the http side be able to communicate bidirectionally, and either async, or synchronously. I also want to support realtime streaming of data via both styles of communication. This way if the scripts job ends up being something like streaming some data that the website is displaying in realtime, we can support that. \nI want to ensure the framework is highly modular, extensible, and very easy for a developer to get up and running with this kind of system. We should have support to easily be able to define our own commands for the IPC, and custom automations and detections for elements on a website.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nI have implemented the core architecture for the BYOB (Bring Your Own Browser) automation framework. I removed the empty \u0060Class1.cs\u0060 and created a modular structure. The framework includes an \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 that supports both HTTP Polling and WebSockets for bidirectional, async, and streaming communication. The \u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060 dynamically builds the Tampermonkey userscript, injecting the advanced React trusted-event spoofing and native value setters directly into the browser context. Extension methods are provided to easily trigger these React bypasses from C#.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Class1.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework\n{\n    public class Class1\n    {\n\n    }\n}\n==== REPLACE\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\IpcMode.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    public enum IpcMode\n    {\n        HttpPolling,\n        WebSocket\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\CommandMessage.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Text.Json.Serialization;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    public class CommandMessage\n    {\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022id\u0022)]\n        public string Id { get; set; } = Guid.NewGuid().ToString();\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022type\u0022)]\n        public string Type { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022payload\u0022)]\n        public object? Payload { get; set; }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\CommandResult.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System.Text.Json.Serialization;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    public class CommandResult\n    {\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022task_id\u0022)]\n        public string TaskId { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022status\u0022)]\n        public string Status { get; set; } = \u0022completed\u0022; // completed, streaming, error\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022output\u0022)]\n        public string? Output { get; set; }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\ScriptOptions.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    public class ScriptOptions\n    {\n        public string ScriptName { get; set; } = \u0022Generated Automation Bridge\u0022;\n        public string Namespace { get; set; } = \u0022automation.bridge\u0022;\n        public string Version { get; set; } = \u00221.0.0\u0022;\n        public List\u003Cstring\u003E MatchUrls { get; set; } = new() { \u0022*://*/*\u0022 };\n        public int Port { get; set; } = 8081;\n        public IpcMode Mode { get; set; } = IpcMode.HttpPolling;\n        public int PollingIntervalMs { get; set; } = 1000;\n        \n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Allows developers to append custom JS functions and register custom actions.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string CustomScript { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\BrowserClient.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Collections.Concurrent;\nusing System.Net.WebSockets;\nusing System.Text;\nusing System.Text.Json;\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Models;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Server\n{\n    public class BrowserClient\n    {\n        public string InstanceId { get; }\n        public IpcMode Mode { get; }\n        \n        private readonly WebSocket? _webSocket;\n        private readonly ConcurrentQueue\u003CCommandMessage\u003E _httpCommandQueue = new();\n        private readonly ConcurrentDictionary\u003Cstring, TaskCompletionSource\u003CCommandResult\u003E\u003E _pendingCommands = new();\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Triggered when the browser script streams partial data back for a long-running task.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public event EventHandler\u003CCommandResult\u003E? OnStreamDataReceived;\n\n        public BrowserClient(string instanceId, IpcMode mode, WebSocket? webSocket = null)\n        {\n            InstanceId = instanceId;\n            Mode = mode;\n            _webSocket = webSocket;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Sends a command to the browser and awaits the final result.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E SendCommandAsync(string type, object? payload = null, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var cmd = new CommandMessage { Type = type, Payload = payload };\n            var tcs = new TaskCompletionSource\u003CCommandResult\u003E();\n            _pendingCommands.TryAdd(cmd.Id, tcs);\n\n            if (Mode == IpcMode.WebSocket \u0026\u0026 _webSocket != null \u0026\u0026 _webSocket.State == WebSocketState.Open)\n            {\n                var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(cmd);\n                var bytes = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(json);\n                await _webSocket.SendAsync(new ArraySegment\u003Cbyte\u003E(bytes), WebSocketMessageType.Text, true, cancellationToken);\n            }\n            else if (Mode == IpcMode.HttpPolling)\n            {\n                _httpCommandQueue.Enqueue(cmd);\n            }\n            else\n            {\n                throw new InvalidOperationException(\u0022Client is disconnected or invalid IPC mode.\u0022);\n            }\n\n            await using (cancellationToken.Register(() =\u003E tcs.TrySetCanceled()))\n            {\n                return await tcs.Task;\n            }\n        }\n\n        internal bool TryGetNextHttpCommand(out CommandMessage? command)\n        {\n            return _httpCommandQueue.TryDequeue(out command);\n        }\n\n        internal void HandleResult(CommandResult result)\n        {\n            if (result.Status == \u0022streaming\u0022)\n            {\n                OnStreamDataReceived?.Invoke(this, result);\n            }\n            else\n            {\n                if (_pendingCommands.TryRemove(result.TaskId, out var tcs))\n                {\n                    if (result.Status == \u0022error\u0022)\n                        tcs.TrySetException(new Exception(result.Output));\n                    else\n                        tcs.TrySetResult(result);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\AutomationServer.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Collections.Concurrent;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.IO;\nusing System.Net;\nusing System.Net.WebSockets;\nusing System.Text;\nusing System.Text.Json;\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Models;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Server\n{\n    public class AutomationServer\n    {\n        private readonly int _port;\n        private HttpListener? _listener;\n        private readonly ConcurrentDictionary\u003Cstring, BrowserClient\u003E _clients = new();\n\n        public event EventHandler\u003CBrowserClient\u003E? OnClientConnected;\n\n        public AutomationServer(int port = 8081)\n        {\n            _port = port;\n        }\n\n        public async Task StartAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            _listener = new HttpListener();\n            _listener.Prefixes.Add($\u0022http://127.0.0.1:{_port}/\u0022);\n            _listener.Start();\n\n            Console.WriteLine($\u0022[AutomationServer] Listening on http://127.0.0.1:{_port}/\u0022);\n\n            while (!cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested)\n            {\n                try\n                {\n                    var context = await _listener.GetContextAsync();\n                    _ = Task.Run(() =\u003E HandleContextAsync(context, cancellationToken), cancellationToken);\n                }\n                catch (HttpListenerException) when (cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested)\n                {\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        public void Stop()\n        {\n            _listener?.Stop();\n            _listener?.Close();\n        }\n\n        public BrowserClient? GetClient(string instanceId)\n        {\n            _clients.TryGetValue(instanceId, out var client);\n            return client;\n        }\n\n        public IEnumerable\u003CBrowserClient\u003E GetAllClients() =\u003E _clients.Values;\n\n        private async Task HandleContextAsync(HttpListenerContext context, CancellationToken cancellationToken)\n        {\n            var request = context.Request;\n            var response = context.Response;\n\n            // Handle CORS for Tampermonkey cross-origin requests\n            response.AddHeader(\u0022Access-Control-Allow-Origin\u0022, \u0022*\u0022);\n            response.AddHeader(\u0022Access-Control-Allow-Methods\u0022, \u0022GET, POST, OPTIONS\u0022);\n            response.AddHeader(\u0022Access-Control-Allow-Headers\u0022, \u0022Content-Type\u0022);\n\n            if (request.HttpMethod == \u0022OPTIONS\u0022)\n            {\n                response.StatusCode = 200;\n                response.Close();\n                return;\n            }\n\n            if (request.IsWebSocketRequest)\n            {\n                await HandleWebSocketAsync(context, cancellationToken);\n                return;\n            }\n\n            string path = request.Url?.AbsolutePath ?? \u0022\u0022;\n\n            try\n            {\n                if (path.StartsWith(\u0022/api/command/\u0022))\n                {\n                    string instanceId = path.Substring(\u0022/api/command/\u0022.Length);\n                    var client = GetOrAddClient(instanceId, IpcMode.HttpPolling);\n\n                    if (client.TryGetNextHttpCommand(out var cmd))\n                    {\n                        await SendJsonAsync(response, new { command = cmd });\n                    }\n                    else\n                    {\n                        await SendJsonAsync(response, new { status = \u0022idle\u0022 });\n                    }\n                }\n                else if (path.StartsWith(\u0022/api/result/\u0022))\n                {\n                    string instanceId = path.Substring(\u0022/api/result/\u0022.Length);\n                    var client = GetOrAddClient(instanceId, IpcMode.HttpPolling);\n\n                    using var reader = new StreamReader(request.InputStream);\n                    string body = await reader.ReadToEndAsync(cancellationToken);\n                    var result = JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CCommandResult\u003E(body);\n\n                    if (result != null)\n                    {\n                        client.HandleResult(result);\n                    }\n\n                    await SendJsonAsync(response, new { status = \u0022acknowledged\u0022 });\n                }\n                else\n                {\n                    response.StatusCode = 404;\n                    response.Close();\n                }\n            }\n            catch (Exception ex)\n            {\n                Console.WriteLine($\u0022[AutomationServer] Error handling HTTP request: {ex.Message}\u0022);\n                response.StatusCode = 500;\n                response.Close();\n            }\n        }\n\n        private async Task HandleWebSocketAsync(HttpListenerContext context, CancellationToken cancellationToken)\n        {\n            var wsContext = await context.AcceptWebSocketAsync(null);\n            var webSocket = wsContext.WebSocket;\n            \n            string instanceId = context.Request.QueryString[\u0022instanceId\u0022] ?? Guid.NewGuid().ToString();\n            var client = new BrowserClient(instanceId, IpcMode.WebSocket, webSocket);\n            _clients[instanceId] = client;\n            OnClientConnected?.Invoke(this, client);\n\n            var buffer = new byte[1024 * 64];\n\n            try\n            {\n                while (webSocket.State == WebSocketState.Open \u0026\u0026 !cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested)\n                {\n                    var result = await webSocket.ReceiveAsync(new ArraySegment\u003Cbyte\u003E(buffer), cancellationToken);\n                    if (result.MessageType == WebSocketMessageType.Close)\n                    {\n                        await webSocket.CloseAsync(WebSocketCloseStatus.NormalClosure, \u0022\u0022, cancellationToken);\n                        break;\n                    }\n\n                    string message = Encoding.UTF8.GetString(buffer, 0, result.Count);\n                    var cmdResult = JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CCommandResult\u003E(message);\n                    if (cmdResult != null)\n                    {\n                        client.HandleResult(cmdResult);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            catch (Exception ex)\n            {\n                Console.WriteLine($\u0022[AutomationServer] WebSocket error: {ex.Message}\u0022);\n            }\n            finally\n            {\n                _clients.TryRemove(instanceId, out _);\n                if (webSocket.State != WebSocketState.Closed \u0026\u0026 webSocket.State != WebSocketState.Aborted)\n                {\n                    webSocket.Dispose();\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        private BrowserClient GetOrAddClient(string instanceId, IpcMode mode)\n        {\n            return _clients.GetOrAdd(instanceId, id =\u003E\n            {\n                var newClient = new BrowserClient(id, mode);\n                OnClientConnected?.Invoke(this, newClient);\n                return newClient;\n            });\n        }\n\n        private async Task SendJsonAsync(HttpListenerResponse response, object data)\n        {\n            response.ContentType = \u0022application/json\u0022;\n            var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(data);\n            var buffer = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(json);\n            response.ContentLength64 = buffer.Length;\n            await response.OutputStream.WriteAsync(buffer, 0, buffer.Length);\n            response.Close();\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ScriptGenerator.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System.Text;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Models;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Generators\n{\n    public static class ScriptGenerator\n    {\n        public static string Generate(ScriptOptions options)\n        {\n            var sb = new StringBuilder();\n\n            // Metadata Block\n            sb.AppendLine(\u0022// ==UserScript==\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine($\u0022// @name         {options.ScriptName}\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine($\u0022// @namespace    {options.Namespace}\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine($\u0022// @version      {options.Version}\u0022);\n            foreach (var url in options.MatchUrls)\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine($\u0022// @match        {url}\u0022);\n            }\n            sb.AppendLine(\u0022// @grant        GM_xmlhttpRequest\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine(\u0022// @run-at       document-idle\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine(\u0022// ==/UserScript==\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine();\n\n            sb.AppendLine(\u0022(function() {\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine(\u0022    \u0027use strict\u0027;\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine();\n            sb.AppendLine($\u0022    const PORT = {options.Port};\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine($\u0022    const INSTANCE_ID = \u0027bot_\u0027 \u002B Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9);\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine();\n\n            // React \u0026 DOM Utilities\n            sb.AppendLine(@\u0022\n    // --- React \u0026 DOM Utilities ---\n    const ReactUtils = {\n        simulateClick: function(element) {\n            try {\n                const reactKey = Object.keys(element).find(k =\u003E k.startsWith(\u0027__reactProps$\u0027) || k.startsWith(\u0027__reactEventHandlers$\u0027));\n                if (reactKey \u0026\u0026 element[reactKey]) {\n                    const props = element[reactKey];\n                    if (typeof props.onClick === \u0027function\u0027) {\n                        const nativeEvent = new MouseEvent(\u0027click\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true });\n                        const fakeNativeEvent = new Proxy(nativeEvent, {\n                            get(target, prop) {\n                                if (prop === \u0027isTrusted\u0027) return true;\n                                const value = Reflect.get(target, prop);\n                                if (typeof value === \u0027function\u0027) return value.bind(target);\n                                return value;\n                            }\n                        });\n                        props.onClick({\n                            bubbles: true, cancelable: true, preventDefault: () =\u003E {}, stopPropagation: () =\u003E {},\n                            target: element, currentTarget: element, nativeEvent: fakeNativeEvent\n                        });\n                        return \u0027React click simulated\u0027;\n                    }\n                }\n            } catch (e) { console.error(\u0027React click failed\u0027, e); }\n            \n            try {\n                element.focus();\n                element.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent(\u0027keydown\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, composed: true, key: \u0027Enter\u0027, code: \u0027Enter\u0027, keyCode: 13 }));\n                element.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent(\u0027keyup\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, composed: true, key: \u0027Enter\u0027, code: \u0027Enter\u0027, keyCode: 13 }));\n            } catch (e) {}\n\n            element.click();\n            return \u0027Native/Fallback click executed\u0027;\n        },\n        setNativeValue: function(element, value) {\n            element.focus();\n            let success = false;\n            try { success = document.execCommand(\u0027insertText\u0027, false, value); } catch (e) {}\n            if (!success) {\n                const valueSetter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(element, \u0027value\u0027)?.set;\n                const prototype = Object.getPrototypeOf(element);\n                const prototypeValueSetter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(prototype, \u0027value\u0027)?.set;\n                if (prototypeValueSetter \u0026\u0026 valueSetter !== prototypeValueSetter) {\n                    prototypeValueSetter.call(element, value);\n                } else if (valueSetter) {\n                    valueSetter.call(element, value);\n                } else {\n                    element.value = value;\n                }\n            }\n            element.dispatchEvent(new Event(\u0027input\u0027, { bubbles: true }));\n            element.dispatchEvent(new Event(\u0027change\u0027, { bubbles: true }));\n            return \u0027Value set\u0027;\n        }\n    };\n\n    // --- Command Registry ---\n    const actionHandlers = Object.create(null);\n\n    function registerAction(name, handler) {\n        actionHandlers[name] = handler;\n    }\n\n    // Built-in Commands\n    registerAction(\u0027REACT_CLICK\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        const el = document.querySelector(payload.selector);\n        if (!el) throw new Error(\u0027Element not found: \u0027 \u002B payload.selector);\n        return ReactUtils.simulateClick(el);\n    });\n\n    registerAction(\u0027SET_VALUE\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        const el = document.querySelector(payload.selector);\n        if (!el) throw new Error(\u0027Element not found: \u0027 \u002B payload.selector);\n        return ReactUtils.setNativeValue(el, payload.value);\n    });\n\n    registerAction(\u0027EVAL\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        return eval(payload.code);\n    });\n\u0022);\n\n            // IPC Logic\n            if (options.Mode == IpcMode.HttpPolling)\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine(@\u0022\n    // --- HTTP Polling IPC ---\n    const API_BASE = \u0060http://127.0.0.1:${PORT}/api\u0060;\n\n    function tmFetch(url, options = {}) {\n        return new Promise((resolve, reject) =\u003E {\n            GM_xmlhttpRequest({\n                method: options.method || \u0027GET\u0027,\n                url: url,\n                data: options.body,\n                headers: { \u0027Content-Type\u0027: \u0027application/json\u0027 },\n                onload: (res) =\u003E resolve(JSON.parse(res.responseText || \u0027{}\u0027)),\n                onerror: reject\n            });\n        });\n    }\n\n    async function sendResult(taskId, status, output) {\n        await tmFetch(\u0060${API_BASE}/result/${INSTANCE_ID}\u0060, {\n            method: \u0027POST\u0027,\n            body: JSON.stringify({ task_id: taskId, status: status, output: String(output) })\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Expose streaming capability to handlers\n    window.streamData = async function(taskId, data) {\n        await sendResult(taskId, \u0027streaming\u0027, data);\n    };\n\n    async function pollServer() {\n        try {\n            const data = await tmFetch(\u0060${API_BASE}/command/${INSTANCE_ID}\u0060);\n            if (data \u0026\u0026 data.command) {\n                const { id, type, payload } = data.command;\n                const handler = actionHandlers[type];\n                \n                if (handler) {\n                    try {\n                        const result = await handler(payload);\n                        await sendResult(id, \u0027completed\u0027, result);\n                    } catch (err) {\n                        await sendResult(id, \u0027error\u0027, err.message);\n                    }\n                } else {\n                    await sendResult(id, \u0027error\u0027, \u0027Unknown command: \u0027 \u002B type);\n                }\n            }\n        } catch (e) {\n            // Server offline or timeout\n        } finally {\n            setTimeout(pollServer, \u0022 \u002B options.PollingIntervalMs \u002B @\u0022);\n        }\n    }\n\n    pollServer();\n\u0022);\n            }\n            else if (options.Mode == IpcMode.WebSocket)\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine(@\u0022\n    // --- WebSocket IPC ---\n    let ws;\n\n    function connectWebSocket() {\n        ws = new WebSocket(\u0060ws://127.0.0.1:${PORT}/?instanceId=${INSTANCE_ID}\u0060);\n        \n        ws.onopen = () =\u003E console.log(\u0027WebSocket connected\u0027);\n        \n        ws.onmessage = async (event) =\u003E {\n            const cmd = JSON.parse(event.data);\n            const { id, type, payload } = cmd;\n            const handler = actionHandlers[type];\n            \n            if (handler) {\n                try {\n                    const result = await handler(payload);\n                    sendResult(id, \u0027completed\u0027, result);\n                } catch (err) {\n                    sendResult(id, \u0027error\u0027, err.message);\n                }\n            } else {\n                sendResult(id, \u0027error\u0027, \u0027Unknown command: \u0027 \u002B type);\n            }\n        };\n\n        ws.onclose = () =\u003E {\n            console.log(\u0027WebSocket disconnected, reconnecting...\u0027);\n            setTimeout(connectWebSocket, 2000);\n        };\n    }\n\n    function sendResult(taskId, status, output) {\n        if (ws \u0026\u0026 ws.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n            ws.send(JSON.stringify({ task_id: taskId, status: status, output: String(output) }));\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Expose streaming capability to handlers\n    window.streamData = async function(taskId, data) {\n        sendResult(taskId, \u0027streaming\u0027, data);\n    };\n\n    connectWebSocket();\n\u0022);\n            }\n\n            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(options.CustomScript))\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine(\u0022    // --- Custom User Script ---\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine(options.CustomScript);\n            }\n\n            sb.AppendLine(\u0022})();\u0022);\n\n            return sb.ToString();\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Extensions\\ReactExtensions.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Models;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Server;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Extensions\n{\n    public static class ReactExtensions\n    {\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Locates an element via CSS selector and simulates a trusted React click event.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E ClickReactElementAsync(this BrowserClient client, string selector, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022REACT_CLICK\u0022, new { selector }, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Locates an element via CSS selector and sets its value, bypassing React\u0027s native value tracking.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E SetReactInputValueAsync(this BrowserClient client, string selector, string value, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022SET_VALUE\u0022, new { selector, value }, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Evaluates raw JavaScript in the context of the page.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E EvaluateJavaScriptAsync(this BrowserClient client, string code, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022EVAL\u0022, new { code }, cancellationToken);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\nCitations\n\n- [https://github.com/Consensys/linea-ens](https://github.com/Consensys/linea-ens)",
      "ModelExplanation": "I have implemented the core architecture for the BYOB (Bring Your Own Browser) automation framework. I removed the empty \u0060Class1.cs\u0060 and created a modular structure. The framework includes an \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 that supports both HTTP Polling and WebSockets for bidirectional, async, and streaming communication. The \u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060 dynamically builds the Tampermonkey userscript, injecting the advanced React trusted-event spoofing and native value setters directly into the browser context. Extension methods are provided to easily trigger these React bypasses from C#.",
