      "UserPrompt": "[Attached Image: image]\n![image](/api/media/72e4ed9f14e64f8593a0a155873a3700)\n\nOk so now we need to fix the UI. Things are overlapping, and clipped. Also, please make all the button have anative look and feel, dont color them and make them flat. Also, make sure all text boxes and anything that has a FormBorderStyle property have its value set to FixedSingle.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nI have updated the UI layout in \u0060MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060 to fix the overlapping and clipping issues. \n\nHere is what was changed:\n1. **Native Buttons**: Removed all custom \u0060BackColor\u0060, \u0060ForeColor\u0060, and \u0060FlatStyle\u0060 properties from the buttons and added \u0060UseVisualStyleBackColor = true\u0060 to restore the native Windows 11 look and feel.\n2. **Border Styles**: Applied \u0060BorderStyle.FixedSingle\u0060 to the text boxes (\u0060txtCmdType\u0060, \u0060txtPayload\u0060), the list box (\u0060lstClients\u0060), and the rich text box (\u0060rtbLogs\u0060).\n3. **Layout \u0026 Clipping Fixes**: \n   - Set \u0060AutoSize = true\u0060 on the top labels and adjusted the X-coordinates of the top bar controls to ensure they never overlap.\n   - Added \u0060Anchor\u0060 properties to the Command Center controls. The payload text box now anchors to all four sides (\u0060Top | Bottom | Left | Right\u0060), and the action buttons anchor to the \u0060Bottom | Left\u0060. This ensures that when the window is resized, the controls scale fluidly instead of clipping off the edge of the screen.\n   - Adjusted the default \u0060SplitterDistance\u0060 to give the Command Center more breathing room on smaller displays.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\MainForm.Designer.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n            // \n            // lblPort\n            // \n            this.lblPort.Location = new System.Drawing.Point(10, 20);\n            this.lblPort.Name = \u0022lblPort\u0022;\n            this.lblPort.Text = \u0022Port:\u0022;\n            this.lblPort.Width = 40;\n            \n            // \n            // numPort\n            // \n            this.numPort.Location = new System.Drawing.Point(50, 18);\n            this.numPort.Maximum = new decimal(new int[] { 65535, 0, 0, 0 });\n            this.numPort.Minimum = new decimal(new int[] { 1024, 0, 0, 0 });\n            this.numPort.Name = \u0022numPort\u0022;\n            this.numPort.Value = new decimal(new int[] { 8081, 0, 0, 0 });\n            this.numPort.Width = 80;\n            \n            // \n            // lblMode\n            // \n            this.lblMode.Location = new System.Drawing.Point(150, 20);\n            this.lblMode.Name = \u0022lblMode\u0022;\n            this.lblMode.Text = \u0022IPC Mode:\u0022;\n            this.lblMode.Width = 70;\n            \n            // \n            // cmbMode\n            // \n            this.cmbMode.DropDownStyle = System.Windows.Forms.ComboBoxStyle.DropDownList;\n            this.cmbMode.Location = new System.Drawing.Point(220, 18);\n            this.cmbMode.Name = \u0022cmbMode\u0022;\n            this.cmbMode.Width = 120;\n            \n            // \n            // btnStart\n            // \n            this.btnStart.BackColor = System.Drawing.Color.DarkGreen;\n            this.btnStart.FlatStyle = System.Windows.Forms.FlatStyle.Flat;\n            this.btnStart.ForeColor = System.Drawing.Color.White;\n            this.btnStart.Location = new System.Drawing.Point(360, 16);\n            this.btnStart.Name = \u0022btnStart\u0022;\n            this.btnStart.Text = \u0022Start Server\u0022;\n            this.btnStart.Width = 100;\n            this.btnStart.Click \u002B= new System.EventHandler(this.BtnStart_Click);\n            \n            // \n            // btnStop\n            // \n            this.btnStop.BackColor = System.Drawing.Color.DarkRed;\n            this.btnStop.Enabled = false;\n            this.btnStop.FlatStyle = System.Windows.Forms.FlatStyle.Flat;\n            this.btnStop.ForeColor = System.Drawing.Color.White;\n            this.btnStop.Location = new System.Drawing.Point(470, 16);\n            this.btnStop.Name = \u0022btnStop\u0022;\n            this.btnStop.Text = \u0022Stop Server\u0022;\n            this.btnStop.Width = 100;\n            this.btnStop.Click