      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\r\n\r\nI have updated the UI layout in \u0060MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060 to fix the overlapping and clipping issues. \r\n\r\nHere is what was changed:\r\n1. **Native Buttons**: Removed all custom \u0060BackColor\u0060, \u0060ForeColor\u0060, and \u0060FlatStyle\u0060 properties from the buttons and added \u0060UseVisualStyleBackColor = true\u0060 to restore the native Windows 11 look and feel.\r\n2. **Border Styles**: Applied \u0060BorderStyle.FixedSingle\u0060 to the text boxes (\u0060txtCmdType\u0060, \u0060txtPayload\u0060), the list box (\u0060lstClients\u0060), and the rich text box (\u0060rtbLogs\u0060).\r\n3. **Layout \u0026 Clipping Fixes**: \r\n   - Set \u0060AutoSize = true\u0060 on the top labels and adjusted the X-coordinates of the top bar controls to ensure they never overlap.\r\n   - Added \u0060Anchor\u0060 properties to the Command Center controls. The payload text box now anchors to all four sides (\u0060Top | Bottom | Left | Right\u0060), and the action buttons anchor to the \u0060Bottom | Left\u0060. This ensures that when the window is resized, the controls scale fluidly instead of clipping off the edge of the screen.\r\n   - Adjusted the default \u0060SplitterDistance\u0060 to give the Command Center more breathing room on smaller displays.\r\n\r\n--CODESTART--\r\n\r\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\MainForm.Designer.cs**\r\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\r\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\r\n            // \r\n            // lblPort\r\n            // \r\n            this.lblPort.Location = new System.Drawing.Point(10, 20);\r\n            this.lblPort.Name = \u0022lblPort\u0022;\r\n            this.lblPort.Text = \u0022Port:\u0022;\r\n            this.lblPort.Width = 40;\r\n            \r\n            // \r\n            // numPort\r\n            // \r\n            this.numPort.Location = new System.Drawing.Point(50, 18);\r\n            this.numPort.Maximum = new decimal(new int[] { 65535, 0