      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nMy apologies for the previous parsing error. Because \u0060MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060 was a brand new file, the parser failed when I tried to use a \u0060SEARCH/REPLACE\u0060 block on it.\n\nI have corrected this by providing the entire source code for \u0060MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060 as a new file. I have also correctly refactored \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 to remove the manual UI code and call \u0060InitializeComponent()\u0060.\n\nThe UI fixes include:\n\n- **Native Buttons**: Removed custom colors and flat styles, and added \u0060UseVisualStyleBackColor = true\u0060 to restore the native Windows 11 look.\n- **Border Styles**: Applied \u0060BorderStyle.FixedSingle\u0060 to the text boxes, list box, and rich text box.\n- **Layout \u0026 Clipping Fixes**: Set \u0060AutoSize = true\u0060 on labels, adjusted X-coordinates in the top bar to prevent overlap, and added \u0060Anchor\u0060 properties to the Command Center controls so they scale fluidly when the window is resized.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    public class MainForm : Form\n    {\n        private AutomationServer? _server;\n        private CancellationTokenSource? _cts;\n        private System.Windows.Forms.Timer _clientRefreshTimer;\n\n        // UI Controls\n        private NumericUpDown numPort;\n        private ComboBox cmbMode;\n        private Button btnStart;\n        private Button btnStop;\n        private Button btnGenerate;\n        private ListBox lstClients;\n        private TextBox txtCmdType;\n        private TextBox txtPayload;\n        private Button btnSend;\n        private Button btnReactClick;\n        private Button btnEval;\n        private RichTextBox rtbLogs;\n\n        public MainForm()\n        {\n            InitializeUI();\n            \n            _clientRefreshTimer = new System.Windows.Forms.Timer { Interval = 2000