      "ModelExplanation": "I have refactored the layout in \u0060MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060 to use responsive containers (\u0060FlowLayoutPanel\u0060 and \u0060TableLayoutPanel\u0060) instead of fixed absolute positioning. This ensures that controls will dynamically resize, wrap, and fill available space without overlapping or getting cut off. I also created the missing \u0060TestBedApp.csproj\u0060 file and explicitly enabled \u0060PerMonitorV2\u0060 high DPI mode so the application scales crisply on modern displays.\n\nTo test these changes:\n\n- Run the \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 project.\n- Verify that the top panel controls (Port, IPC Mode, and buttons) are properly spaced and fully visible.\n- Verify that the \u0022Command Center\u0022 textboxes and buttons scale correctly when resizing the window.\n- Move the application between monitors with different DPI scaling (e.g., 100% and 150%) to confirm that the text and controls remain sharp and properly proportioned.",
