      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\r\n\r\nThe issue you are experiencing is a well-known WinForms bug where setting the \u0060FixedPanel\u0060 property on a \u0060SplitContainer\u0060 causes severe layout miscalculations during High DPI scaling initialization, resulting in panels being crushed to near-zero width/height. \r\n\r\nTo fix this, I have removed the \u0060FixedPanel\u0060 constraints so the splitters scale proportionally. I also explicitly defined \u0060Panel1MinSize\u0060 and \u0060Panel2MinSize\u0060 for both splitters. This guarantees that the \u0022Connected Clients\u0022 and \u0022Real-time Logs\u0022 sections can never be squished beyond a readable size, regardless of the monitor\u0027s DPI or how the window is resized.\r\n\r\nTo test these changes:\r\n1. Run the \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 project.\r\n2. Verify that the \u0022Connected Clients\u0022 list on the left is now fully visible and readable.\r\n3. Verify that the \u0022Real-time Logs\u0022 section at the bottom has plenty of vertical space.\r\n4. Try resizing the window to confirm the splitters respect the minimum sizes and scale proportionally.\r\n\r\n--CODESTART--\r\n\r\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\MainForm.Designer.cs**\r\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\r\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\r\n            // \r\n            // splitMain\r\n            // \r\n            this.splitMain.Dock = System.Windows.Forms.DockStyle.Fill;\r\n            this.splitMain.FixedPanel = System.Windows.Forms.FixedPanel.Panel2;\r\n            this.splitMain.Name = \u0022splitMain\u0022;\r\n            this.splitMain.Orientation = System.Windows.Forms.Orientation.Horizontal;\r\n            this.splitMain.Panel1.Controls.Add(this.splitTop);\r\n            this.splitMain.Panel2.Controls.Add(this.pnlLogs);\r\n            this.splitMain.SplitterDistance = 500;\r\n==== REPLACE\r\n            // \r\n            // splitMain\r\n            // \r\n            this.splitMain.Dock = System.Windows.Forms.DockStyle.Fill;\r\n            this.splitMain.Name = \u0022splitMain\u0022;\r\n            this.splitMain.Orientation = System.Windows.Forms.Orientation.Horizontal;\r\n            this.splitMain.Panel1.Controls.Add(this.splitTop);\r\n            this.splitMain.Panel1MinSize = 300;\r\n            this.splitMain.Panel2.Controls.Add(this.pnlLogs);\r\n            this.splitMain.Panel2MinSize = 150;\r\n            this.splitMain.SplitterDistance = 550;\r\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\r\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\r\n            // \r\n            // splitTop\r\n            // \r\n            this.splitTop.Dock = System.Windows.Forms.DockStyle.Fill;\r\n            this.splitTop.FixedPanel = System.Windows.Forms.FixedPanel.Panel1;\r\n            this.splitTop.Name = \u0022splitTop\u0022;\r\n            this.splitTop.Orientation = System.Windows.Forms.Orientation.Vertical;\r\n            this.splitTop.Panel1.Controls.Add(this.pnlClients);\r\n            this.splitTop.Panel2.Controls.Add(this.pnlCommands);\r\n            this.splitTop.SplitterDistance = 400;\r\n==== REPLACE\r\n            // \r\n            // splitTop\r\n            // \r\n            this.splitTop.Dock = System.Windows.Forms.DockStyle.Fill;\r\n            this.splitTop.Name = \u0022splitTop\u0022;\r\n            this.splitTop.Orientation = System.Windows.Forms.Orientation.Vertical;\r\n            this.splitTop.Panel1.Controls.Add(this.pnlClients);\r\n            this.splitTop.Panel1MinSize = 250;\r\n            this.splitTop.Panel2.Controls.Add(this.pnlCommands);\r\n            this.splitTop.Panel2MinSize = 400;\r\n            this.splitTop.SplitterDistance = 300;\r\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\r\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
      "ModelExplanation": "The issue you are experiencing is a well-known WinForms bug where setting the \u0060FixedPanel\u0060 property on a \u0060SplitContainer\u0060 causes severe layout miscalculations during High DPI scaling initialization, resulting in panels being crushed to near-zero width/height. \r\n\r\nTo fix this, I have removed the \u0060FixedPanel\u0060 constraints so the splitters scale proportionally. I also explicitly defined \u0060Panel1MinSize\u0060 and \u0060Panel2MinSize\u0060 for both splitters. This guarantees that the \u0022Connected Clients\u0022 and \u0022Real-time Logs\u0022 sections can never be squished beyond a readable size, regardless of the monitor\u0027s DPI or how the window is resized.\r\n\r\nTo test these changes:\r\n1. Run the \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 project.\r\n2. Verify that the \u0022Connected Clients\u0022 list on the left is now fully visible and readable.\r\n3. Verify that the \u0022Real-time Logs\u0022 section at the bottom has plenty of vertical space.\r\n4. Try resizing the window to confirm the splitters respect the minimum sizes and scale proportionally.",
