      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\nNow take a look at this project im working on. I want an easy way to use the winforms testbed app to develop a quick browser automation system to search up a query on google and then click on the search button. So to do this, i want to build a way for the system to be able to relay ALL the html elements of the DOM on the page the bridge is running on and then visually show that in the test bed app. Then we can have a point and click expierence to allow us to target specfic elements to performa automations on, such as text inputs, clicking buttons, simulating mouse clicks, ect. I also want a full editor developed to be able to define new behaviors for the syetm (such as new commnads, and assign them to automations, ect). We want to build this out into a full on editor for the system. I also want you to intelgrate a feature that will act similar to the inspect element feature in chrome. Where when we right click, inspect element, and in the chrome dev tools, when the user hovers over an html element in the displayed html code, it puts an overlay highlight square over the rect of that html element. I want this to be done with our element viewer as well, so when i click or hover over on an element in the report DOM contents, it will highlight that in the browser the same way dev tools does. This will assist in building automations.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nI have implemented the DOM Explorer and Automation Editor features.\n\n- **ScriptGenerator.cs**: Added \u0060GET_DOM\u0060, \u0060HIGHLIGHT_ELEMENT\u0060, and \u0060REMOVE_HIGHLIGHT\u0060 commands. The DOM serialization generates precise CSS selector paths for every element.\n- **ReactExtensions.cs**: Added extension methods for the new commands.\n- **MainForm.Designer.cs \u0026 MainForm.cs**: Replaced the command panel with a TabControl containing \u0022Raw Commands\u0022, \u0022DOM Explorer\u0022, and \u0022Automation Editor\u0022. The DOM Explorer uses a TreeView to display the DOM, highlights elements in the browser on selection, and provides a context menu to test actions or add them to an automation script. The Automation Editor allows building, editing, and running a sequence of actions.\n- **New Models**: Created \u0060DomNode.cs\u0060 and \u0060AutomationStep.cs\u0060 to support the new features.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Start the server and inject the generated script into a browser page.\n- Go to the \u0022DOM Explorer\u0022 tab and click \u0022Refresh DOM\u0022.\n- Expand the tree and click on elements to see them highlighted in the browser.\n- Right-click an element to test a click/set value, or add it to the Automation Editor.\n- Go to the \u0022Automation Editor\u0022 tab, configure your steps, and click \u0022Run Automation\u0022.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ScriptGenerator.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    registerAction(\u0027EVAL\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        return eval(payload.code);\n    });\n\u0022);\n==== REPLACE\n    registerAction(\u0027EVAL\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        return eval(payload.code);\n    });\n\n    function serializeElement(el) {\n        if (el.nodeType === Node.TEXT_NODE) {\n            const text = el.textContent.trim();\n            return text ? { type: \u0027text\u0027, text: text } : null;\n        }\n        if (el.nodeType !== Node.ELEMENT_NODE) return null;\n        \n        let path = \u0027\u0027;\n        if (el.tagName.toLowerCase() === \u0027html\u0027) {\n            path = \u0027html\u0027;\n        } else if (el.tagName.toLowerCase() === \u0027body\u0027) {\n            path = \u0027body\u0027;\n        } else {\n            let current = el;\n            let pathParts = [];\n            while (current \u0026\u0026 current.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE \u0026\u0026 current.tagName.toLowerCase() !== \u0027html\u0027 \u0026\u0026 current.tagName.toLowerCase() !== \u0027body\u0027) {\n                let index = 1;\n                let sibling = current.previousElementSibling;\n                while (sibling) {\n                    index\u002B\u002B;\n                    sibling = sibling.previousElementSibling;\n                }\n                pathParts.unshift(\u0060${current.tagName.toLowerCase()}:nth-child(${index})\u0060);\n                current = current.parentElement;\n            }\n            if (current \u0026\u0026 current.tagName.toLowerCase() === \u0027body\u0027) pathParts.unshift(\u0027body\u0027);\n            else if (current \u0026\u0026 current.tagName.toLowerCase() === \u0027html\u0027) pathParts.unshift(\u0027html\u0027);\n            path = pathParts.join(\u0027 \u003E \u0027);\n        }\n\n        const node = {\n            type: \u0027element\u0027,\n            tagName: el.tagName.toLowerCase(),\n            path: path,\n            attributes: {}\n        };\n        \n        for (let attr of el.attributes) {\n            node.attributes[attr.name] = attr.value;\n        }\n        \n        node.children = [];\n        for (let child of el.childNodes) {\n            const serializedChild = serializeElement(child);\n            if (serializedChild) node.children.push(serializedChild);\n        }\n        return node;\n    }\n\n    registerAction(\u0027GET_DOM\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        return serializeElement(document.documentElement);\n    });\n\n    let highlightOverlay = null;\n    registerAction(\u0027HIGHLIGHT_ELEMENT\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        const el = document.querySelector(payload.selector);\n        if (!el) return \u0027Element not found\u0027;\n        \n        if (!highlightOverlay) {\n            highlightOverlay = document.createElement(\u0027div\u0027);\n            highlightOverlay.style.position = \u0027absolute\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.backgroundColor = \u0027rgba(0, 150, 255, 0.3)\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.border = \u00272px solid rgba(0, 150, 255, 0.8)\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.pointerEvents = \u0027none\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.zIndex = \u0027999999\u0027;\n            document.body.appendChild(highlightOverlay);\n        }\n        \n        const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();\n        highlightOverlay.style.top = (rect.top \u002B window.scrollY) \u002B \u0027px\u0027;\n        highlightOverlay.style.left = (rect.left \u002B window.scrollX) \u002B \u0027px\u0027;\n        highlightOverlay.style.width = rect.width \u002B \u0027px\u0027;\n        highlightOverlay.style.height = rect.height \u002B \u0027px\u0027;\n        highlightOverlay.style.display = \u0027block\u0027;\n        \n        return \u0027Highlighted\u0027;\n    });\n\n    registerAction(\u0027REMOVE_HIGHLIGHT\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        if (highlightOverlay) {\n            highlightOverlay.style.display = \u0027none\u0027;\n        }\n        return \u0027Highlight removed\u0027;\n    });\n\u0022);\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Extensions\\ReactExtensions.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        public static Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E EvaluateJavaScriptAsync(this BrowserClient client, string code, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022EVAL\u0022, new { code }, cancellationToken);\n        }\n    }\n}\n==== REPLACE\n        public static Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E EvaluateJavaScriptAsync(this BrowserClient client, string code, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022EVAL\u0022, new { code }, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Retrieves a serialized representation of the DOM.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E GetDomAsync(this BrowserClient client, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022GET_DOM\u0022, null, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Highlights an element on the page using its CSS selector.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E HighlightElementAsync(this BrowserClient client, string selector, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022HIGHLIGHT_ELEMENT\u0022, new { selector }, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Removes the highlight overlay from the page.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E RemoveHighlightAsync(this BrowserClient client, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022REMOVE_HIGHLIGHT\u0022, null, cancellationToken);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\MainForm.Designer.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n            // \n            // pnlCommands\n            // \n            pnlCommands.Controls.Add(tlpCommands)