    {
      "Id": "b52d4f13",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-20T22:38:47.2261116-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "This is perfect! Now we need to fix a bug in the Set Vlaue automation operation. When we try it out, it does not set the text in a text area, but it will add text to any existing text in the text area. I want this to be designed so we can do both, either add text, or overwite any existing text with the vlaue we specified. \nAlso, we need to fix another bug where clients that have disconnected never dissappear from the connected clients list. When a client disconnects, it needs to be removed from the connected clients list.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nI have addressed both issues:\n\n- **Set Value Automation**: Added an \u0060Overwrite\u0060 boolean property to the \u0060AutomationStep\u0060 model (defaulting to \u0060true\u0060). The \u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060\u0027s \u0060setNativeValue\u0060 function was updated to accept an \u0060overwrite\u0060 parameter. If true, it clears the element natively before inserting the new text; if false, it appends the text. You can toggle this property in the Automation Editor\u0027s Property Grid.\n- **Disconnected Clients**: Added a \u0060LastSeen\u0060 timestamp to \u0060BrowserClient\u0060. The \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 now runs a background timer that evicts HTTP Polling clients if they haven\u0027t been seen in 10 seconds (WebSocket clients were already being removed on disconnect). The \u0060MainForm\u0060\u0027s UI timer was also updated to remove clients from the ListBox if they are no longer in the server\u0027s active client list.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 and start the server.\n- Generate the script, update Tampermonkey, and connect a client.\n- **Test Set Value**: Add a \u0022Set Value\u0022 step in the Automation Editor. Run it with \u0060Overwrite\u0060 set to \u0060true\u0060 (it should replace the text), then change \u0060Overwrite\u0060 to \u0060false\u0060 and run it again (it should append the text).\n- **Test Disconnect**: Close the browser tab running the script. Within 10 seconds, the client should automatically disappear from the \u0022Connected Clients\u0022 list.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Extensions\\ReactExtensions.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Locates an element via CSS selector and sets its value, bypassing React\u0027s native value tracking.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E SetReactInputValueAsync(this BrowserClient client, string selector, string value, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022SET_VALUE\u0022, new { selector, value }, cancellationToken);\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Locates an element via CSS selector and sets its value, bypassing React\u0027s native value tracking.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static Task\u003CCommandResult\u003E SetReactInputValueAsync(this BrowserClient client, string selector, string value, bool overwrite = true, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022SET_VALUE\u0022, new { selector, value, overwrite }, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ScriptGenerator.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        setNativeValue: function(element, value) {\n            element.focus();\n            let success = false;\n            try { success = document.execCommand(\u0027insertText\u0027, false, value); } catch (e) {}\n            if (!success) {\n                const valueSetter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(element, \u0027value\u0027)?.set;\n                const prototype = Object.getPrototypeOf(element);\n                const prototypeValueSetter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(prototype, \u0027value\u0027)?.set;\n                if (prototypeValueSetter \u0026\u0026 valueSetter !== prototypeValueSetter) {\n                    prototypeValueSetter.call(element, value);\n                } else if (valueSetter) {\n                    valueSetter.call(element, value);\n                } else {\n                    element.value = value;\n                }\n            }\n            element.dispatchEvent(new Event(\u0027input\u0027, { bubbles: true }));\n            element.dispatchEvent(new Event(\u0027change\u0027, { bubbles: true }));\n            return \u0027Value set\u0027;\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        setNativeValue: function(element, value, overwrite) {\n            element.focus();\n            if (overwrite) {\n                try { element.select(); } catch(e) {}\n                const valueSetter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(element, \u0027value\u0027)?.set;\n                const prototype = Object.getPrototypeOf(element);\n                const prototypeValueSetter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(prototype, \u0027value\u0027)?.set;\n                if (prototypeValueSetter \u0026\u0026 valueSetter !== prototypeValueSetter) {\n                    prototypeValueSetter.call(element, \u0027\u0027);\n                } else if (valueSetter) {\n                    valueSetter.call(element, \u0027\u0027);\n                } else {\n                    element.value = \u0027\u0027;\n                }\n            }\n            let success = false;\n            try { success = document.execCommand(\u0027insertText\u0027, false, value); } catch (e) {}\n            if (!success) {\n                const valueSetter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(element, \u0027value\u0027)?.set;\n                const prototype = Object.getPrototypeOf(element);\n                const prototypeValueSetter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(prototype, \u0027value\u0027)?.set;\n                const currentValue = overwrite ? \u0027\u0027 : element.value;\n                if (prototypeValueSetter \u0026\u0026 valueSetter !== prototypeValueSetter) {\n                    prototypeValueSetter.call(element, currentValue \u002B value);\n                } else if (valueSetter) {\n                    valueSetter.call(element, currentValue \u002B value);\n                } else {\n                    element.value = currentValue \u002B value;\n                }\n            }\n            element.dispatchEvent(new Event(\u0027input\u0027, { bubbles: true }));\n            element.dispatchEvent(new Event(\u0027change\u0027, { bubbles: true }));\n            return \u0027Value set\u0027;\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    registerAction(\u0027SET_VALUE\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        const el = document.querySelector(payload.selector);\n        if (!el) throw new Error(\u0027Element not found: \u0027 \u002B payload.selector);\n        return ReactUtils.setNativeValue(el, payload.value);\n    });\n==== REPLACE\n    registerAction(\u0027SET_VALUE\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        const el = document.querySelector(payload.selector);\n        if (!el) throw new Error(\u0027Element not found: \u0027 \u002B payload.selector);\n        const overwrite = payload.overwrite !== undefined ? payload.overwrite : true;\n        return ReactUtils.setNativeValue(el, payload.value, overwrite);\n    });\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\BrowserClient.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        public string InstanceId { get; }\n        public IpcMode Mode { get; }\n        \n        private readonly WebSocket? _webSocket;\n==== REPLACE\n        public string InstanceId { get; }\n        public IpcMode Mode { get; }\n        public DateTime LastSeen { get; internal set; } = DateTime.UtcNow;\n        \n        private readonly WebSocket? _webSocket;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\AutomationServer.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        private readonly int _port;\n        private HttpListener? _listener;\n        private readonly ConcurrentDictionary\u003Cstring, BrowserClient\u003E _clients = new();\n==== REPLACE\n        private readonly int _port;\n        private HttpListener? _listener;\n        private readonly ConcurrentDictionary\u003Cstring, BrowserClient\u003E _clients = new();\n        private System.Threading.Timer? _cleanupTimer;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        public async Task StartAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            _listener = new HttpListener();\n            _listener.Prefixes.Add($\u0022http://127.0.0.1:{_port}/\u0022);\n            _listener.Start();\n\n            Console.WriteLine($\u0022[AutomationServer] Listening on http://127.0.0.1:{_port}/\u0022);\n==== REPLACE\n        public async Task StartAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            _listener = new HttpListener();\n            _listener.Prefixes.Add($\u0022http://127.0.0.1:{_port}/\u0022);\n            _listener.Start();\n\n            _cleanupTimer = new System.Threading.Timer(CleanupStaleClients, null, TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5), TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));\n\n            Console.WriteLine($\u0022[AutomationServer] Listening on http://127.0.0.1:{_port}/\u0022);\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        public void Stop()\n        {\n            _listener?.Stop();\n            _listener?.Close();\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        public void Stop()\n        {\n            _cleanupTimer?.Dispose();\n            _listener?.Stop();\n            _listener?.Close();\n        }\n\n        private void CleanupStaleClients(object? state)\n        {\n            var threshold = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(-10);\n            foreach (var kvp in _clients)\n            {\n                if (kvp.Value.Mode == IpcMode.HttpPolling \u0026\u0026 kvp.Value.LastSeen \u003C threshold)\n                {\n                    _clients.TryRemove(kvp.Key, out _);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n                if (path.StartsWith(\u0022/api/command/\u0022))\n                {\n                    string instanceId = path.Substring(\u0022/api/command/\u0022.Length);\n                    var client = GetOrAddClient(instanceId, IpcMode.HttpPolling);\n\n                    if (client.TryGetNextHttpCommand(out var cmd))\n==== REPLACE\n                if (path.StartsWith(\u0022/api/command/\u0022))\n                {\n                    string instanceId = path.Substring(\u0022/api/command/\u0022.Length);\n                    var client = GetOrAddClient(instanceId, IpcMode.HttpPolling);\n                    client.LastSeen = DateTime.UtcNow;\n\n                    if (client.TryGetNextHttpCommand(out var cmd))\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n                else if (path.StartsWith(\u0022/api/result/\u0022))\n                {\n                    string instanceId = path.Substring(\u0022/api/result/\u0022.Length);\n                    var client = GetOrAddClient(instanceId, IpcMode.HttpPolling);\n\n                    using var reader = new StreamReader(request.InputStream);\n==== REPLACE\n                else if (path.StartsWith(\u0022/api/result/\u0022))\n                {\n                    string instanceId = path.Substring(\u0022/api/result/\u0022.Length);\n                    var client = GetOrAddClient(instanceId, IpcMode.HttpPolling);\n                    client.LastSeen = DateTime.UtcNow;\n\n                    using var reader = new StreamReader(request.InputStream);\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\Models\\AutomationStep.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        public string Selector { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n        public string Value { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        public override string ToString() =\u003E $\u0022{Name} ({ActionType})\u0022;\n==== REPLACE\n        public string Selector { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n        public string Value { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n        public bool Overwrite { get; set; } = true;\n\n        public override string ToString() =\u003E $\u0022{Name} ({ActionType})\u0022;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        private void ClientRefreshTimer_Tick(object? sender, EventArgs e)\n        {\n            if (_server == null) return;\n            \n            var activeClients = _server.GetAllClients().ToList();\n            var currentClients = lstClients.Items.Cast\u003CBrowserClient\u003E().ToList();\n\n            // Add new\n            foreach (var client in activeClients.Where(c =\u003E !currentClients.Any(cc =\u003E cc.InstanceId == c.InstanceId)))\n            {\n                lstClients.Items.Add(client);\n            }\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        private void ClientRefreshTimer_Tick(object? sender, EventArgs e)\n        {\n            if (_server == null) return;\n            \n            var activeClients = _server.GetAllClients().ToList();\n            var currentClients = lstClients.Items.Cast\u003CBrowserClient\u003E().ToList();\n\n            // Remove disconnected\n            for (int i = lstClients.Items.Count - 1; i \u003E= 0; i--)\n            {\n                var client = (BrowserClient)lstClients.Items[i];\n                if (!activeClients.Any(c =\u003E c.InstanceId == client.InstanceId))\n                {\n                    lstClients.Items.RemoveAt(i);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // Add new\n            foreach (var client in activeClients.Where(c =\u003E !currentClients.Any(cc =\u003E cc.InstanceId == c.InstanceId)))\n            {\n                lstClients.Items.Add(client);\n            }\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n                    else if (step.ActionType == AutomationActionType.SetValue)\n                    {\n                        res = await client.SetReactInputValueAsync(step.Selector, step.Value);\n                    }\n==== REPLACE\n                    else if (step.ActionType == AutomationActionType.SetValue)\n                    {\n                        res = await client.SetReactInputValueAsync(step.Selector, step.Value, step.Overwrite);\n                    }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\nCitations\n\n- [https://github.com/Consensys/linea-ens](https://github.com/Consensys/linea-ens)",
      "ModelExplanation": "I have addressed both issues:\n\n- **Set Value Automation**: Added an \u0060Overwrite\u0060 boolean property to the \u0060AutomationStep\u0060 model (defaulting to \u0060true\u0060). The \u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060\u0027s \u0060setNativeValue\u0060 function was updated to accept an \u0060overwrite\u0060 parameter. If true, it clears the element natively before inserting the new text; if false, it appends the text. You can toggle this property in the Automation Editor\u0027s Property Grid.\n- **Disconnected Clients**: Added a \u0060LastSeen\u0060 timestamp to \u0060BrowserClient\u0060. The \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 now runs a background timer that evicts HTTP Polling clients if they haven\u0027t been seen in 10 seconds (WebSocket clients were already being removed on disconnect). The \u0060MainForm\u0060\u0027s UI timer was also updated to remove clients from the ListBox if they are no longer in the server\u0027s active client list.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 and start the server.\n- Generate the script, update Tampermonkey, and connect a client.\n- **Test Set Value**: Add a \u0022Set Value\u0022 step in the Automation Editor. Run it with \u0060Overwrite\u0060 set to \u0060true\u0060 (it should replace the text), then change \u0060Overwrite\u0060 to \u0060false\u0060 and run it again (it should append the text).\n- **Test Disconnect**: Close the browser tab running the script. Within 10 seconds, the client should automatically disappear from the \u0022Connected Clients\u0022 list.",
