      "Timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:35:06.8052481-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "[Attached Image]\n\n[Attached Image]\n\nOk so we need a much better way to visually display all the DOM elemeents. As you can see in the attached screenshot, the list box isnt really the way to go. maybe we can make a custom control for this? I want to model it after what you see in the second screenshot, how dev tools renders the dom elements list in the chrome dev tools element inspector. Keep in mind we need to keep the right click menus that we currerntly have for right clicking on a dom element.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nI have created a custom \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 control that inherits from the standard WinForms \u0060TreeView\u0060. By setting \u0060DrawMode = TreeViewDrawMode.OwnerDrawText\u0060 and overriding the \u0060OnDrawNode\u0060 method, we can intercept the rendering and draw the DOM nodes with syntax highlighting (tags, attributes, strings) exactly like Chrome DevTools.\n\nBecause it inherits from \u0060TreeView\u0060, all of your existing right-click context menus and selection events will continue to work flawlessly. I also updated \u0060BuildTreeNode\u0060 in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 to generate a full string representation for the node\u0027s underlying \u0060Text\u0060 property, which ensures the WinForms engine calculates the correct width for the selection highlight and scrollbars.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 and connect a client.\n- Navigate to the \u0022DOM Explorer\u0022 tab and click \u0022Refresh DOM\u0022.\n- You will now see a beautifully syntax-highlighted DOM tree.\n- Right-click any element to verify the context menu still appears and functions correctly.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Drawing;\nusing System.Windows.Forms;\nusing TestBedApp.Models;\n\nnamespace TestBedApp.Controls\n{\n    public class DomTreeView : TreeView\n    {\n        private readonly Font _codeFont;\n        private readonly Color _selBgColor = Color.FromArgb(9, 71, 113);\n        private readonly Color _tagColor = Color.FromArgb(86, 156, 214);\n        private readonly Color _attrNameColor = Color.FromArgb(156, 220, 254);\n        private readonly Color _attrValueColor = Color.FromArgb(206, 145, 120);\n        private readonly Color _textColor = Color.FromArgb(212, 212, 212);\n        private readonly Color _punctColor = Color.FromArgb(128, 128, 128);\n\n        public DomTreeView()\n        {\n            DrawMode = TreeViewDrawMode.OwnerDrawText;\n            BackColor = Color.FromArgb(30, 30, 30);\n            ForeColor = Color.LightGray;\n            _codeFont = new Font(\u0022Consolas\u0022, 10F);\n            ItemHeight = 22;\n            ShowLines = true;\n            ShowPlusMinus = true;\n            ShowRootLines = true;\n        }\n\n        protected override void OnDrawNode(DrawTreeNodeEventArgs e)\n        {\n            if (e.Node == null || e.Graphics == null) return;\n\n            bool isSelected = (e.State \u0026 TreeNodeStates.Selected) != 0;\n            \n            using (var bgBrush = new SolidBrush(isSelected ? _selBgColor : BackColor))\n            {\n                e.Graphics.FillRectangle(bgBrush, e.Bounds);\n            }\n\n            if (e.Node.Tag is DomNode domNode)\n            {\n                int x = e.Bounds.Left \u002B 2;\n                int y = e.Bounds.Top \u002B ((e.Bounds.Height - _codeFont.Height) / 2);\n\n                void Draw(string text, Color color)\n                {\n                    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(text)) return;\n                    TextRenderer.DrawText(e.Graphics, text, _codeFont, new Point(x, y), color, TextFormatFlags.NoPadding);\n                    x \u002B= TextRenderer.MeasureText(e.Graphics, text, _codeFont, new Size(int.MaxValue, int.MaxValue), TextFormatFlags.NoPadding).Width;\n                }\n\n                if (domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022)\n                {\n                    Draw(\u0022\u003C\u0022, _punctColor);\n                    Draw(domNode.TagName, _tagColor);\n\n                    if (domNode.Attributes != null)\n                    {\n                        foreach (var attr in domNode.Attributes)\n                        {\n                            Draw(\u0022 \u0022, _textColor);\n                            Draw(attr.Key, _attrNameColor);\n                            Draw(\u0022=\u0022, _punctColor);\n                            Draw($\u0022\\\u0022{attr.Value}\\\u0022\u0022, _attrValueColor);\n                        }\n                    }\n\n                    Draw(\u0022\u003E\u0022, _punctColor);\n\n                    if (e.Node.Nodes.Count \u003E 0 \u0026\u0026 !e.Node.IsExpanded)\n                    {\n                        Draw(\u0022...\u0022, _punctColor);\n                        Draw($\u0022\u003C/\u0022, _punctColor);\n                        Draw(domNode.TagName, _tagColor);\n                        Draw(\u0022\u003E\u0022, _punctColor);\n                    }\n                }\n                else if (domNode.Type == \u0022text\u0022)\n                {\n                    Draw($\u0022\\\u0022{domNode.Text}\\\u0022\u0022, _textColor);\n                }\n            }\n            else\n            {\n                TextRenderer.DrawText(e.Graphics, e.Node.Text, _codeFont, new Point(e.Bounds.Left \u002B 2, e.Bounds.Top \u002B ((e.Bounds.Height - _codeFont.Height) / 2)), isSelected ? Color.White : _textColor, TextFormatFlags.NoPadding);\n            }\n        }\n\n        protected override void Dispose(bool disposing)\n        {\n            if (disposing)\n            {\n                _codeFont?.Dispose();\n            }\n            base.Dispose(disposing);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        private TreeNode BuildTreeNode(DomNode domNode)\n        {\n            string text = domNode.Type == \u0022text\u0022 ? $\u0022\\\u0022{domNode.Text}\\\u0022\u0022 : $\u0022\u003C{domNode.TagName}\u003E\u0022;\n            if (domNode.Attributes != null \u0026\u0026 domNode.Attributes.TryGetValue(\u0022id\u0022, out var id))\n            {\n                text \u002B= $\u0022 #{id}\u0022;\n            }\n            if (domNode.Attributes != null \u0026\u0026 domNode.Attributes.TryGetValue(\u0022class\u0022, out var cls))\n            {\n                text \u002B= $\u0022 .{cls.Replace(\u0022 \u0022, \u0022.\u0022)}\u0022;\n            }\n\n            var treeNode = new TreeNode(text)\n            {\n                Tag = domNode\n            };\n\n            if (domNode.Children != null)\n            {\n                foreach (var child in domNode.Children)\n                {\n                    treeNode.Nodes.Add(BuildTreeNode(child));\n                }\n            }\n\n            return treeNode;\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        private TreeNode BuildTreeNode(DomNode domNode)\n        {\n            string text = \u0022\u0022;\n            if (domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022)\n            {\n                text = $\u0022\u003C{domNode.TagName}\u0022;\n                if (domNode.Attributes != null)\n                {\n                    foreach (var attr in domNode.Attributes)\n                    {\n                        text \u002B= $\u0022 {attr.Key}=\\\u0022{attr.Value}\\\u0022\u0022;\n                    }\n                }\n                text \u002B= \u0022\u003E\u0022;\n                text \u002B= $\u0022...\u003C/{domNode.TagName}\u003E\u0022; // Pad width for collapsed state\n            }\n            else\n            {\n                text = $\u0022\\\u0022{domNode.Text}\\\u0022\u0022;\n            }\n\n            var treeNode = new TreeNode(text)\n            {\n                Tag = domNode\n            };\n\n            if (domNode.Children != null)\n            {\n                foreach (var child in domNode.Children)\n                {\n                    treeNode.Nodes.Add(BuildTreeNode(child));\n                }\n            }\n\n            return treeNode;\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\MainForm.Designer.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        private System.Windows.Forms.TreeView tvDom;\n==== REPLACE\n        private TestBedApp.Controls.DomTreeView tvDom;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n            //\n            // tvDom\n            //\n            tvDom.Dock = DockStyle.Fill;\n            tvDom.Location = new Point(0, 0);\n            tvDom.Name = \u0022tvDom\u0022;\n            tvDom.Size = new Size(400, 402);\n            tvDom.TabIndex = 0;\n            tvDom.AfterSelect \u002B= TvDom_AfterSelect;\n            tvDom.NodeMouseClick \u002B= TvDom_NodeMouseClick;\n==== REPLACE\n            //\n            // tvDom\n            //\n            tvDom.Dock = DockStyle.Fill;\n            tvDom.Location = new Point(0, 0);\n            tvDom.Name = \u0022tvDom\u0022;\n            tvDom.Size = new Size(400, 402);\n            tvDom.TabIndex = 0;\n            tvDom.AfterSelect \u002B= TvDom_AfterSelect;\n            tvDom.NodeMouseClick \u002B= TvDom_NodeMouseClick;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n            splitDom.Panel1.ResumeLayout(false);\n            splitDom.Panel2.ResumeLayout(false);\n            splitDom.Panel2.PerformLayout();\n            ((System.ComponentModel.ISupportInitialize)splitDom).EndInit();\n            splitDom.ResumeLayout(false);\n            tabEditor.ResumeLayout(false);\n            pnlEditorTop.ResumeLayout(false);\n            splitEditor.Panel1.ResumeLayout(false);\n            splitEditor.Panel2.ResumeLayout(false);\n            ((System.ComponentModel.ISupportInitialize)splitEditor).EndInit();\n            splitEditor.ResumeLayout(false);\n            tlpCommands.ResumeLayout(false);\n            tlpCommands.PerformLayout();\n            pnlCmdButtons.ResumeLayout(false);\n            pnlCmdButtons.PerformLayout();\n            pnlLogs.ResumeLayout(false);\n            ResumeLayout(false);\n            PerformLayout();\n        }\n\n        #endregion\n==== REPLACE\n            splitDom.Panel1.ResumeLayout(false);\n            splitDom.Panel2.ResumeLayout(false);\n            splitDom.Panel2.PerformLayout();\n            ((System.ComponentModel.ISupportInitialize)splitDom).EndInit();\n            splitDom.ResumeLayout(false);\n            tabEditor.ResumeLayout(false);\n            pnlEditorTop.ResumeLayout(false);\n            splitEditor.Panel1.ResumeLayout(false);\n            splitEditor.Panel2.ResumeLayout(false);\n            ((System.ComponentModel.ISupportInitialize)splitEditor).EndInit();\n            splitEditor.ResumeLayout(false);\n            tlpCommands.ResumeLayout(false);\n            tlpCommands.PerformLayout();\n            pnlCmdButtons.ResumeLayout(false);\n            pnlCmdButtons.PerformLayout();\n            pnlLogs.ResumeLayout(false);\n            ResumeLayout(false);\n            PerformLayout();\n        }\n\n        #endregion\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n            splitDom = new SplitContainer();\n            tvDom = new TreeView();\n            txtElementDetails = new TextBox();\n==== REPLACE\n            splitDom = new SplitContainer();\n            tvDom = new TestBedApp.Controls.DomTreeView();\n            txtElementDetails = new TextBox();\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
      "ModelExplanation": "I have created a custom \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 control that inherits from the standard WinForms \u0060TreeView\u0060. By setting \u0060DrawMode = TreeViewDrawMode.OwnerDrawText\u0060 and overriding the \u0060OnDrawNode\u0060 method, we can intercept the rendering and draw the DOM nodes with syntax highlighting (tags, attributes, strings) exactly like Chrome DevTools.\n\nBecause it inherits from \u0060TreeView\u0060, all of your existing right-click context menus and selection events will continue to work flawlessly. I also updated \u0060BuildTreeNode\u0060 in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 to generate a full string representation for the node\u0027s underlying \u0060Text\u0060 property, which ensures the WinForms engine calculates the correct width for the selection highlight and scrollbars.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 and connect a client.\n- Navigate to the \u0022DOM Explorer\u0022 tab and click \u0022Refresh DOM\u0022.\n- You will now see a beautifully syntax-highlighted DOM tree.\n- Right-click any element to verify the context menu still appears and functions correctly.",
