      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\r\n\r\nThe rendering bug you are experiencing during the expand/collapse animation is a known issue with WinForms. The \u0060TreeView\u0060 control uses a temporary memory DC (Device Context) to animate the expansion. \u0060TextRenderer.DrawText\u0060 uses the older GDI API, which often fails to respect the origin or clipping region of these temporary animation DCs, causing the text to draw at the top-left of the control.\r\n\r\nTo fix this permanently, I have switched the drawing logic in \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 from \u0060TextRenderer.DrawText\u0060 (GDI) to \u0060e.Graphics.DrawString\u0060 (GDI\u002B). GDI\u002B natively respects the memory DCs and clipping regions used during the animation. I also enabled \u0060ClearTypeGridFit\u0060 to ensure the text remains just as crisp as it was before.\r\n\r\nTo test:\r\n1. Run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 and load the DOM.\r\n2. Expand and collapse various nodes in the tree.\r\n3. Verify that the text no longer bleeds or flickers at the top of the control during the animation.\r\n\r\n--CODESTART--\r\n\r\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs**\r\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\r\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\r\n        protected override void OnDrawNode(DrawTreeNodeEventArgs e)\r\n        {\r\n            if (e.Node == null || e.Graphics == null) return;\r\n\r\n            bool isSelected = (e.State \u0026 TreeNodeStates.Selected) != 0;\r\n            \r\n            using (var bgBrush = new SolidBrush(isSelected ? _selBgColor : BackColor))\r\n            {\r\n                e.Graphics.FillRectangle(bgBrush, e.Bounds);\r\n            }\r\n\r\n            if (e.Node.Tag is DomNode domNode)\r\n            {\r\n                int x = e.Bounds.Left \u002B 2;\r\n                int y = e.Bounds.Top \u002B ((e.Bounds.Height - _codeFont.Height) / 2);\r\n\r\n                void Draw(string text, Color color)\r\n                {\r\n                    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(text)) return;\r\n                    TextRenderer.DrawText(e.Graphics, text, _codeFont, new Point(x, y), color, TextFormatFlags.NoPadding | TextFormatFlags.PreserveGraphicsClipping);\r\n                    x \u002B= TextRenderer.MeasureText(e.Graphics, text, _codeFont, new Size(int.MaxValue, int.MaxValue), TextFormatFlags.NoPadding).Width;\r\n                }\r\n\r\n                if (domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022)\r\n                {\r\n                    Draw(\u0022\u003C\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n                    Draw(domNode.TagName, _tagColor);\r\n\r\n                    if (domNode.Attributes != null)\r\n                    {\r\n                        foreach (var attr in domNode.Attributes)\r\n                        {\r\n                            Draw(\u0022 \u0022, _textColor);\r\n                            Draw(attr.Key, _attrNameColor);\r\n                            Draw(\u0022=\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n                            Draw($\u0022\\\u0022{attr.Value}\\\u0022\u0022, _attrValueColor);\r\n                        }\r\n                    }\r\n\r\n                    Draw(\u0022\u003E\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n\r\n                    if (e.Node.Nodes.Count \u003E 0 \u0026\u0026 !e.Node.IsExpanded)\r\n                    {\r\n                        Draw(\u0022...\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n                        Draw($\u0022\u003C/\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n                        Draw(domNode.TagName, _tagColor);\r\n                        Draw(\u0022\u003E\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n                    }\r\n                }\r\n                else if (domNode.Type == \u0022text\u0022)\r\n                {\r\n                    Draw($\u0022\\\u0022{domNode.Text}\\\u0022\u0022, _textColor);\r\n                }\r\n            }\r\n            else\r\n            {\r\n                TextRenderer.DrawText(e.Graphics, e.Node.Text, _codeFont, new Point(e.Bounds.Left \u002B 2, e.Bounds.Top \u002B ((e.Bounds.Height - _codeFont.Height) / 2)), isSelected ? Color.White : _textColor, TextFormatFlags.NoPadding | TextFormatFlags.PreserveGraphicsClipping);\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n==== REPLACE\r\n        protected override void OnDrawNode(DrawTreeNodeEventArgs e)\r\n        {\r\n            if (e.Node == null || e.Graphics == null) return;\r\n\r\n            // Use GDI\u002B drawing to prevent animation bleeding issues\r\n            e.Graphics.TextRenderingHint = System.Drawing.Text.TextRenderingHint.ClearTypeGridFit;\r\n\r\n            bool isSelected = (e.State \u0026 TreeNodeStates.Selected) != 0;\r\n            \r\n            using (var bgBrush = new SolidBrush(isSelected ? _selBgColor : BackColor))\r\n            {\r\n                e.Graphics.FillRectangle(bgBrush, e.Bounds);\r\n            }\r\n\r\n            using (var format = new StringFormat(StringFormat.GenericTypographic))\r\n            {\r\n                format.FormatFlags |= StringFormatFlags.MeasureTrailingSpaces | StringFormatFlags.NoWrap;\r\n\r\n                if (e.Node.Tag is DomNode domNode)\r\n                {\r\n                    float x = e.Bounds.Left \u002B 2;\r\n                    float y = e.Bounds.Top \u002B ((e.Bounds.Height - _codeFont.Height) / 2f);\r\n\r\n                    void Draw(string text, Color color)\r\n                    {\r\n                        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(text)) return;\r\n                        using (var brush = new SolidBrush(color))\r\n                        {\r\n                            e.Graphics.DrawString(text, _codeFont, brush, x, y, format);\r\n                        }\r\n                        x \u002B= e.Graphics.MeasureString(text, _codeFont, new PointF(x, y), format).Width;\r\n                    }\r\n\r\n                    if (domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022)\r\n                    {\r\n                        Draw(\u0022\u003C\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n                        Draw(domNode.TagName, _tagColor);\r\n\r\n                        if (domNode.Attributes != null)\r\n                        {\r\n                            foreach (var attr in domNode.Attributes)\r\n                            {\r\n                                Draw(\u0022 \u0022, _textColor);\r\n                                Draw(attr.Key, _attrNameColor);\r\n                                Draw(\u0022=\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n                                Draw($\u0022\\\u0022{attr.Value}\\\u0022\u0022, _attrValueColor);\r\n                            }\r\n                        }\r\n\r\n                        Draw(\u0022\u003E\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n\r\n                        if (e.Node.Nodes.Count \u003E 0 \u0026\u0026 !e.Node.IsExpanded)\r\n                        {\r\n                            Draw(\u0022...\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n                            Draw($\u0022\u003C/\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n                            Draw(domNode.TagName, _tagColor);\r\n                            Draw(\u0022\u003E\u0022, _punctColor);\r\n                        }\r\n                    }\r\n                    else if (domNode.Type == \u0022text\u0022)\r\n                    {\r\n                        Draw($\u0022\\\u0022{domNode.Text}\\\u0022\u0022, _textColor);\r\n                    }\r\n                }\r\n                else\r\n                {\r\n                    float y = e.Bounds.Top \u002B ((e.Bounds.Height - _codeFont.Height) / 2f);\r\n                    using (var brush = new SolidBrush(isSelected ? Color.White : _textColor))\r\n                    {\r\n                        e.Graphics.DrawString(e.Node.Text, _codeFont, brush, e.Bounds.Left \u002B 2, y, format);\r\n                    }\r\n                }\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\r\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
      "ModelExplanation": "The rendering bug you are experiencing during the expand/collapse animation is a known issue with WinForms. The \u0060TreeView\u0060 control uses a temporary memory DC (Device Context) to animate the expansion. \u0060TextRenderer.DrawText\u0060 uses the older GDI API, which often fails to respect the origin or clipping region of these temporary animation DCs, causing the text to draw at the top-left of the control.\r\n\r\nTo fix this permanently, I have switched the drawing logic in \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 from \u0060TextRenderer.DrawText\u0060 (GDI) to \u0060e.Graphics.DrawString\u0060 (GDI\u002B). GDI\u002B natively respects the memory DCs and clipping regions used during the animation. I also enabled \u0060ClearTypeGridFit\u0060 to ensure the text remains just as crisp as it was before.\r\n\r\nTo test:\r\n1. Run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 and load the DOM.\r\n2. Expand and collapse various nodes in the tree.\r\n3. Verify that the text no longer bleeds or flickers at the top of the control during the animation.",
