      "UserPrompt": "[Attached Image]\n\nNow we just need to make one final change. I want to get rid of the tool tip text that shows when i hoever my mouse over an element. Its annoying and not helpful at all.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nOverrode the \u0060CreateParams\u0060 property in the \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 control to include the \u0060TVS_NOTOOLTIPS\u0060 (\u00600x0080\u0060) window style. This disables the default Windows behavior that automatically displays tooltips when hovering over nodes with truncated text.\n\n**How to test:**\n\n- Run the \u0060TestBedApp\u0060.\n- Fetch and load a DOM tree into the DOM Explorer.\n- Resize the DOM Explorer pane so that some node text is truncated (cut off by the right edge).\n- Hover your mouse over the truncated node text.\n- Verify that the tooltip no longer appears.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        public DomTreeView()\n        {\n            DrawMode = TreeViewDrawMode.OwnerDrawText;\n            BackColor = Color.FromArgb(30, 30, 30);\n            ForeColor = Color.LightGray;\n            _codeFont = new Font(\u0022Consolas\u0022, 10F);\n            ItemHeight = 22;\n            ShowLines = true;\n            ShowPlusMinus = true;\n            ShowRootLines = true;\n        }\n\n        protected override void OnDrawNode(DrawTreeNodeEventArgs e)\n==== REPLACE\n        public DomTreeView()\n        {\n            DrawMode = TreeViewDrawMode.OwnerDrawText;\n            BackColor = Color.FromArgb(30, 30, 30);\n            ForeColor = Color.LightGray;\n            _codeFont = new Font(\u0022Consolas\u0022, 10F);\n            ItemHeight = 22;\n            ShowLines = true;\n            ShowPlusMinus = true;\n            ShowRootLines = true;\n        }\n\n        protected override CreateParams CreateParams\n        {\n            get\n            {\n                CreateParams cp = base.CreateParams;\n                cp.Style |= 0x0080; // TVS_NOTOOLTIPS\n                return cp;\n            }\n        }\n\n        protected override void OnDrawNode(DrawTreeNodeEventArgs e)\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
      "ModelExplanation": "Overrode the \u0060CreateParams\u0060 property in the \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 control to include the \u0060TVS_NOTOOLTIPS\u0060 (\u00600x0080\u0060) window style. This disables the default Windows behavior that automatically displays tooltips when hovering over nodes with truncated text.\n\n**How to test:**\n\n- Run the \u0060TestBedApp\u0060.\n- Fetch and load a DOM tree into the DOM Explorer.\n- Resize the DOM Explorer pane so that some node text is truncated (cut off by the right edge).\n- Hover your mouse over the truncated node text.\n- Verify that the tooltip no longer appears.",
