    {
      "Id": "ed231e23",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-21T02:53:53.6902006-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "[Attached Image: image.png]\n![image.png](/api/media/62c86e7934794d48bf3a9b2352e2ef45)\n\nOk this is better, however, it seems we are having some sort of error thats seen on the js console. The illegal return statment does not happen anymore, and the console log code does run, however, we never get a response back in the winforms app, and it also spits out the error seen in the screenshot on the dev tools js console.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nThe error occurs because of JavaScript context isolation. Tampermonkey scripts run in an isolated \u0022sandbox\u0022 environment. When you define \u0060window[id]\u0060 in the Tampermonkey script, it is attached to the sandbox\u0027s window object. However, when you inject a \u0060\u003Cscript\u003E\u0060 tag into the DOM, that code executes in the target page\u0027s native context. The page\u0027s context cannot see the sandbox\u0027s variables, so \u0060window[\u0027eval_...\u0027]\u0060 is undefined, throwing the \u0060TypeError\u0060.\n\nTo fix this, we need to bridge the gap between the page context and the sandbox context. We can do this by having the injected script dispatch a \u0060CustomEvent\u0060 on the \u0060document\u0060 containing the serialized result, which the Tampermonkey script can listen for.\n\n### How to test:\n\n- Click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script** in the TestBedApp and update your Tampermonkey script.\n- Reload the target page to connect the updated client.\n- Send the payload \u0060console.log(\u0027Hello from C#\u0027); return \u0027Success\u0027;\u0060 via the **Test Eval (JS)** button. The C# app will now correctly receive the \u0060Success\u0060 response.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ScriptGenerator.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    registerAction(\u0027EVAL\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        return new Promise((resolve, reject) =\u003E {\n            const id = \u0027eval_\u0027 \u002B Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9);\n            window[id] = (err, res) =\u003E {\n                delete window[id];\n                if (err) reject(new Error(err));\n                else resolve(res);\n            };\n            \n            const code = \u0060\n                (async function() {\n                    try {\n                        const res = await (async function() { ${payload.code} })();\n                        window[\u0027${id}\u0027](null, res);\n                    } catch (e) {\n                        window[\u0027${id}\u0027](e.message || String(e), null);\n                    } finally {\n                        const s = document.getElementById(\u0027${id}_script\u0027);\n                        if (s) s.remove();\n                    }\n                })();\n            \u0060;\n            \n            try {\n                if (typeof GM_addElement === \u0027function\u0027) {\n                    GM_addElement(\u0027script\u0027, { id: id \u002B \u0027_script\u0027, textContent: code });\n                } else {\n                    const script = document.createElement(\u0027script\u0027);\n                    script.id = id \u002B \u0027_script\u0027;\n                    script.textContent = code;\n                    document.body.appendChild(script);\n                }\n            } catch (e) {\n                reject(new Error(\u0027Script injection failed: \u0027 \u002B e.message));\n            }\n        });\n    });\n==== REPLACE\n    registerAction(\u0027EVAL\u0027, async (payload) =\u003E {\n        return new Promise((resolve, reject) =\u003E {\n            const id = \u0027eval_\u0027 \u002B Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9);\n            \n            const listener = (e) =\u003E {\n                document.removeEventListener(id, listener);\n                try {\n                    const data = JSON.parse(e.detail);\n                    if (data.err) reject(new Error(data.err));\n                    else resolve(data.res);\n                } catch (err) {\n                    reject(err);\n                }\n            };\n            document.addEventListener(id, listener);\n            \n            const code = \u0060\n                (async function() {\n                    let result = { err: null, res: null };\n                    try {\n                        result.res = await (async function() { ${payload.code} })();\n                    } catch (e) {\n                        result.err = e.message || String(e);\n                    } finally {\n                        document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(\u0027${id}\u0027, { detail: JSON.stringify(result) }));\n                        const s = document.getElementById(\u0027${id}_script\u0027);\n                        if (s) s.remove();\n                    }\n                })();\n            \u0060;\n            \n            try {\n                if (typeof GM_addElement === \u0027function\u0027) {\n                    GM_addElement(\u0027script\u0027, { id: id \u002B \u0027_script\u0027, textContent: code });\n                } else {\n                    const script = document.createElement(\u0027script\u0027);\n                    script.id = id \u002B \u0027_script\u0027;\n                    script.textContent = code;\n                    document.body.appendChild(script);\n                }\n            } catch (e) {\n                document.removeEventListener(id, listener);\n                reject(new Error(\u0027Script injection failed: \u0027 \u002B e.message));\n            }\n        });\n    });\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
      "ModelExplanation": "The error occurs because of JavaScript context isolation. Tampermonkey scripts run in an isolated \u0022sandbox\u0022 environment. When you define \u0060window[id]\u0060 in the Tampermonkey script, it is attached to the sandbox\u0027s window object. However, when you inject a \u0060\u003Cscript\u003E\u0060 tag into the DOM, that code executes in the target page\u0027s native context. The page\u0027s context cannot see the sandbox\u0027s variables, so \u0060window[\u0027eval_...\u0027]\u0060 is undefined, throwing the \u0060TypeError\u0060.\n\nTo fix this, we need to bridge the gap between the page context and the sandbox context. We can do this by having the injected script dispatch a \u0060CustomEvent\u0060 on the \u0060document\u0060 containing the serialized result, which the Tampermonkey script can listen for.\n\n### How to test:\n\n- Click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script** in the TestBedApp and update your Tampermonkey script.\n- Reload the target page to connect the updated client.\n- Send the payload \u0060console.log(\u0027Hello from C#\u0027); return \u0027Success\u0027;\u0060 via the **Test Eval (JS)** button. The C# app will now correctly receive the \u0060Success\u0060 response.",
