    {
      "Id": "07aab826",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-24T18:38:39.2372003-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "I tried this ona  react deepseek page, and it does not auto refresh the dom element list when the dom on the page changes in realtime. It only works when i maually switch away from the dom viewer tab.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nThe issue you\u0027re experiencing is caused by a critical bug in how the WebSocket server parses incoming messages, combined with a lack of concurrency control for DOM refreshes.\n\nWhen the server receives a message, it was checking if the raw JSON string contained the word \u0060\u0022event\u0022\u0060 to determine if it was an event or a command result. Because a React page like DeepSeek has a massive DOM that almost certainly contains the word \u0022event\u0022 (e.g., in CSS like \u0060pointer-events\u0060 or script tags), the server mistakenly swallowed the \u0060GET_DOM\u0060 result as an event. This caused the \u0060await client.GetDomAsync()\u0060 task to hang forever, permanently breaking the auto-refresh cycle.\n\nAdditionally, I\u0027ve added a concurrency lock (\u0060_isRefreshingDom\u0060) to prevent overlapping refresh requests from spamming the browser, and I\u0027ve added logic to save and restore the **expanded state** of all your tree nodes so the tree doesn\u0027t collapse every time the DOM updates.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Run the updated server and connect the browser.\n- The DOM will now properly auto-refresh in real-time without hanging.\n- Expand a few nodes in the tree; notice that they stay expanded even when the DOM updates.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\AutomationServer.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n                    string message = Encoding.UTF8.GetString(ms.ToArray());\n                    if (message.Contains(\u0022\\\u0022event\\\u0022\u0022))\n                    {\n                        var evt = JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CEventMessage\u003E(message);\n                        if (evt != null)\n                        {\n                            client.HandleEvent(evt);\n                        }\n                    }\n                    else\n                    {\n                        var cmdResult = JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CCommandResult\u003E(message);\n                        if (cmdResult != null)\n                        {\n                            client.HandleResult(cmdResult);\n                        }\n                    }\n==== REPLACE\n                    string message = Encoding.UTF8.GetString(ms.ToArray());\n                    using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(message);\n                    if (doc.RootElement.TryGetProperty(\u0022event\u0022, out _))\n                    {\n                        var evt = JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CEventMessage\u003E(message);\n                        if (evt != null)\n                        {\n                            client.HandleEvent(evt);\n                        }\n                    }\n                    else\n                    {\n                        var cmdResult = JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CCommandResult\u003E(message);\n                        if (cmdResult != null)\n                        {\n                            client.HandleResult(cmdResult);\n                        }\n                    }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        private async Task RefreshDomAsync(BrowserClient client)\n        {\n            try\n            {\n                var result = await client.GetDomAsync();\n                if (result.Status == \u0022completed\u0022 \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrEmpty(result.Output))\n                {\n                    var rootNode = JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CDomNode\u003E(result.Output);\n                    if (rootNode != null)\n                    {\n                        string? selectedPath = (tvDom.SelectedNode?.Tag as DomNode)?.Path;\n\n                        tvDom.BeginUpdate();\n                        tvDom.Nodes.Clear();\n                        var treeNode = BuildTreeNode(rootNode);\n                        tvDom.Nodes.Add(treeNode);\n                        treeNode.Expand();\n\n                        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(selectedPath))\n                        {\n                            var nodeToSelect = FindNodeByPath(treeNode, selectedPath);\n                            if (nodeToSelect != null)\n                            {\n                                tvDom.SelectedNode = nodeToSelect;\n                                nodeToSelect.EnsureVisible();\n                            }\n                        }\n                        tvDom.EndUpdate();\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            catch (Exception ex)\n            {\n                Log($\u0022[ERR] Failed to fetch DOM: {ex.Message}\u0022, Color.Red);\n            }\n        }\n\n        private TreeNode? FindNodeByPath(TreeNode root, string path)\n==== REPLACE\n        private bool _isRefreshingDom = false;\n\n        private async Task RefreshDomAsync(BrowserClient client)\n        {\n            if (_isRefreshingDom) return;\n            _isRefreshingDom = true;\n\n            try\n            {\n                var result = await client.GetDomAsync();\n                if (result.Status == \u0022completed\u0022 \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrEmpty(result.Output))\n                {\n                    var rootNode = JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CDomNode\u003E(result.Output);\n                    if (rootNode != null)\n                    {\n                        string? selectedPath = (tvDom.SelectedNode?.Tag as DomNode)?.Path;\n                        var expandedPaths = new HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E();\n                        if (tvDom.Nodes.Count \u003E 0)\n                        {\n                            SaveExpandedState(tvDom.Nodes[0], expandedPaths);\n                        }\n\n                        tvDom.BeginUpdate();\n                        try\n                        {\n                            tvDom.Nodes.Clear();\n                            var treeNode = BuildTreeNode(rootNode);\n                            tvDom.Nodes.Add(treeNode);\n                            \n                            treeNode.Expand();\n                            RestoreExpandedState(treeNode, expandedPaths);\n\n                            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(selectedPath))\n                            {\n                                var nodeToSelect = FindNodeByPath(treeNode, selectedPath);\n                                if (nodeToSelect != null)\n                                {\n                                    tvDom.SelectedNode = nodeToSelect;\n                                    nodeToSelect.EnsureVisible();\n                                }\n                            }\n                        }\n                        finally\n                        {\n                            tvDom.EndUpdate();\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            catch (Exception ex)\n            {\n                Log($\u0022[ERR] Failed to fetch DOM: {ex.Message}\u0022, Color.Red);\n            }\n            finally\n            {\n                _isRefreshingDom = false;\n            }\n        }\n\n        private void SaveExpandedState(TreeNode node, HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E expandedPaths)\n        {\n            if (node.IsExpanded \u0026\u0026 node.Tag is DomNode domNode \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrEmpty(domNode.Path))\n            {\n                expandedPaths.Add(domNode.Path);\n            }\n            foreach (TreeNode child in node.Nodes)\n            {\n                SaveExpandedState(child, expandedPaths);\n            }\n        }\n\n        private void RestoreExpandedState(TreeNode node, HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E expandedPaths)\n        {\n            if (node.Tag is DomNode domNode \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrEmpty(domNode.Path) \u0026\u0026 expandedPaths.Contains(domNode.Path))\n            {\n                node.Expand();\n            }\n            foreach (TreeNode child in node.Nodes)\n            {\n                RestoreExpandedState(child, expandedPaths);\n            }\n        }\n\n        private TreeNode? FindNodeByPath(TreeNode root, string path)\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
      "ModelExplanation": "The issue you\u0027re experiencing is caused by a critical bug in how the WebSocket server parses incoming messages, combined with a lack of concurrency control for DOM refreshes.\n\nWhen the server receives a message, it was checking if the raw JSON string contained the word \u0060\u0022event\u0022\u0060 to determine if it was an event or a command result. Because a React page like DeepSeek has a massive DOM that almost certainly contains the word \u0022event\u0022 (e.g., in CSS like \u0060pointer-events\u0060 or script tags), the server mistakenly swallowed the \u0060GET_DOM\u0060 result as an event. This caused the \u0060await client.GetDomAsync()\u0060 task to hang forever, permanently breaking the auto-refresh cycle.\n\nAdditionally, I\u0027ve added a concurrency lock (\u0060_isRefreshingDom\u0060) to prevent overlapping refresh requests from spamming the browser, and I\u0027ve added logic to save and restore the **expanded state** of all your tree nodes so the tree doesn\u0027t collapse every time the DOM updates.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Run the updated server and connect the browser.\n- The DOM will now properly auto-refresh in real-time without hanging.\n- Expand a few nodes in the tree; notice that they stay expanded even when the DOM updates.",
