      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\nThis works, but in the dom element view, the element isnt selected in the viewer control.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nSet \u0060HideSelection = false\u0060 on the \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 and updated the custom drawing logic to explicitly check \u0060e.Node.IsSelected\u0060. This ensures the selected DOM node remains highlighted in the viewer even when the WinForms application loses focus (e.g., when you are actively clicking elements inside the browser).\n\nTo test:\n\n- Start the server and connect a browser client.\n- Click an element in the browser.\n- Observe that the corresponding node in the DOM Explorer tab is now visibly selected and highlighted, even while the browser window has focus.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        public DomTreeView()\n        {\n            DrawMode = TreeViewDrawMode.OwnerDrawText;\n            BackColor = Color.FromArgb(30, 30, 30);\n            ForeColor = Color.LightGray;\n            _codeFont = new Font(\u0022Consolas\u0022, 10F);\n            ItemHeight = 22;\n            ShowLines = true;\n            ShowPlusMinus = true;\n            ShowRootLines = true;\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        public DomTreeView()\n        {\n            DrawMode = TreeViewDrawMode.OwnerDrawText;\n            BackColor = Color.FromArgb(30, 30, 30);\n            ForeColor = Color.LightGray;\n            _codeFont = new Font(\u0022Consolas\u0022, 10F);\n            ItemHeight = 22;\n            ShowLines = true;\n            ShowPlusMinus = true;\n            ShowRootLines = true;\n            HideSelection = false;\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n            // Use GDI\u002B drawing to prevent animation bleeding issues\n            e.Graphics.TextRenderingHint = System.Drawing.Text.TextRenderingHint.ClearTypeGridFit;\n\n            bool isSelected = (e.State \u0026 TreeNodeStates.Selected) != 0;\n\n            // Clear the background to prevent artifacts from previous longer text states (e.g., when expanding/collapsing)\n==== REPLACE\n            // Use GDI\u002B drawing to prevent animation bleeding issues\n            e.Graphics.TextRenderingHint = System.Drawing.Text.TextRenderingHint.ClearTypeGridFit;\n\n            bool isSelected = (e.State \u0026 TreeNodeStates.Selected) != 0 || e.Node.IsSelected;\n\n            // Clear the background to prevent artifacts from previous longer text states (e.g., when expanding/collapsing)\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
      "ModelExplanation": "Set \u0060HideSelection = false\u0060 on the \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 and updated the custom drawing logic to explicitly check \u0060e.Node.IsSelected\u0060. This ensures the selected DOM node remains highlighted in the viewer even when the WinForms application loses focus (e.g., when you are actively clicking elements inside the browser).\n\nTo test:\n\n- Start the server and connect a browser client.\n- Click an element in the browser.\n- Observe that the corresponding node in the DOM Explorer tab is now visibly selected and highlighted, even while the browser window has focus.",
