    {
      "Id": "710fd997",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-24T21:06:08.7170355-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "Now lets make it use the middle mouse button when clicking on elements in the browser instead of the left mouse button. Also please use this current version of the code base thats attached.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nUpdated \u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060 to simulate middle mouse button clicks (\u0060button: 1\u0060) instead of left clicks. This includes updating the React synthetic event payload, dispatching \u0060MouseEvent\u0060s with \u0060button: 1\u0060, adding \u0060auxclick\u0060 dispatching for standard middle-click behavior, and replacing the hardcoded \u0060element.click()\u0060 (which only does left clicks) with explicit event dispatches. Also added an \u0060auxclick\u0060 listener to the browser event sync so physical middle clicks are captured by the testbed.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Click \u0022Generate \u0026 Copy Script\u0022 in the testbed and update your Tampermonkey script.\n- Reload the target webpage to inject the new script.\n- Use the \u0022Test React Click\u0022 button or run an automation sequence with a Click step.\n- Verify that the target element receives a middle click (e.g., opening a link in a new tab, or triggering middle-click specific event listeners).\n- Physically middle-click an element in the browser and verify it highlights in the DOM Explorer.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ScriptGenerator.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n                        const nativeEvent = new MouseEvent(\u0027click\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true });\n                        const fakeNativeEvent = new Proxy(nativeEvent, {\n                            get(target, prop) {\n                                if (prop === \u0027isTrusted\u0027) return true;\n                                const value = Reflect.get(target, prop);\n                                if (typeof value === \u0027function\u0027) return value.bind(target);\n                                return value;\n                            }\n                        });\n                        props.onClick({\n                            bubbles: true, cancelable: true, preventDefault: () =\u003E {}, stopPropagation: () =\u003E {},\n                            target: element, currentTarget: element, nativeEvent: fakeNativeEvent\n                        });\n==== REPLACE\n                        const nativeEvent = new MouseEvent(\u0027click\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, button: 1 });\n                        const fakeNativeEvent = new Proxy(nativeEvent, {\n                            get(target, prop) {\n                                if (prop === \u0027isTrusted\u0027) return true;\n                                const value = Reflect.get(target, prop);\n                                if (typeof value === \u0027function\u0027) return value.bind(target);\n                                return value;\n                            }\n                        });\n                        props.onClick({\n                            bubbles: true, cancelable: true, preventDefault: () =\u003E {}, stopPropagation: () =\u003E {},\n                            target: element, currentTarget: element, nativeEvent: fakeNativeEvent, button: 1\n                        });\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n            const tag = element.tagName.toLowerCase();\n            if (tag !== \u0027button\u0027 \u0026\u0026 tag !== \u0027a\u0027 \u0026\u0026 tag !== \u0027input\u0027) {\n                try {\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027mousedown\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window }));\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027mouseup\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window }));\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027click\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window }));\n                } catch (e) {}\n            } else {\n                if (typeof element.click === \u0027function\u0027) {\n                    try { element.click(); } catch (e) {}\n                } else {\n                    try { element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027click\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window })); } catch (e) {}\n                }\n            }\n==== REPLACE\n            const tag = element.tagName.toLowerCase();\n            if (tag !== \u0027button\u0027 \u0026\u0026 tag !== \u0027a\u0027 \u0026\u0026 tag !== \u0027input\u0027) {\n                try {\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027mousedown\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window, button: 1 }));\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027mouseup\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window, button: 1 }));\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027click\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window, button: 1 }));\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027auxclick\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window, button: 1 }));\n                } catch (e) {}\n            } else {\n                try {\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027mousedown\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window, button: 1 }));\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027mouseup\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window, button: 1 }));\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027click\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window, button: 1 }));\n                    element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\u0027auxclick\u0027, { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window, button: 1 }));\n                } catch (e) {}\n            }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    // --- Browser Event Sync ---\n    document.addEventListener(\u0027click\u0027, (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 typeof sendEvent === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            const path = getElementPath(e.target);\n            if (path) {\n                sendEvent(\u0027ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0027, { path: path });\n            }\n        }\n    }, true);\n==== REPLACE\n    // --- Browser Event Sync ---\n    document.addEventListener(\u0027click\u0027, (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 typeof sendEvent === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            const path = getElementPath(e.target);\n            if (path) {\n                sendEvent(\u0027ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0027, { path: path });\n            }\n        }\n    }, true);\n\n    document.addEventListener(\u0027auxclick\u0027, (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 e.button === 1 \u0026\u0026 typeof sendEvent === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            const path = getElementPath(e.target);\n            if (path) {\n                sendEvent(\u0027ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0027, { path: path });\n            }\n        }\n    }, true);\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\nCitations\n\n- [https://github.com/martin1194/refined-prun](https://github.com/martin1194/refined-prun)",
      "ModelExplanation": "Updated \u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060 to simulate middle mouse button clicks (\u0060button: 1\u0060) instead of left clicks. This includes updating the React synthetic event payload, dispatching \u0060MouseEvent\u0060s with \u0060button: 1\u0060, adding \u0060auxclick\u0060 dispatching for standard middle-click behavior, and replacing the hardcoded \u0060element.click()\u0060 (which only does left clicks) with explicit event dispatches. Also added an \u0060auxclick\u0060 listener to the browser event sync so physical middle clicks are captured by the testbed.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Click \u0022Generate \u0026 Copy Script\u0022 in the testbed and update your Tampermonkey script.\n- Reload the target webpage to inject the new script.\n- Use the \u0022Test React Click\u0022 button or run an automation sequence with a Click step.\n- Verify that the target element receives a middle click (e.g., opening a link in a new tab, or triggering middle-click specific event listeners).\n- Physically middle-click an element in the browser and verify it highlights in the DOM Explorer.",
