    {
      "Id": "d8c73a76",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-24T21:08:09.5398077-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "This works, but the left clicks still also selects elements in the browser live. We need to disable the left click! The middle click works now though.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nRemoved the standard \u0060click\u0060 event listener from the browser event sync logic in \u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060. Now, only the \u0060auxclick\u0060 listener remains, ensuring that only physical middle clicks (\u0060button === 1\u0060) will trigger the \u0060ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0060 event and select elements in the testbed\u0027s DOM Explorer. Left clicks will be completely ignored by the sync mechanism.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Click \u0022Generate \u0026 Copy Script\u0022 in the testbed and update your Tampermonkey script.\n- Reload the target webpage.\n- Left-click an element in the browser and verify it does **not** highlight in the DOM Explorer.\n- Middle-click an element and verify it **does** highlight in the DOM Explorer.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ScriptGenerator.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    // --- Browser Event Sync ---\n    document.addEventListener(\u0027click\u0027, (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 typeof sendEvent === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            const path = getElementPath(e.target);\n            if (path) {\n                sendEvent(\u0027ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0027, { path: path });\n            }\n        }\n    }, true);\n\n    document.addEventListener(\u0027auxclick\u0027, (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 e.button === 1 \u0026\u0026 typeof sendEvent === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            const path = getElementPath(e.target);\n            if (path) {\n                sendEvent(\u0027ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0027, { path: path });\n            }\n        }\n    }, true);\n==== REPLACE\n    // --- Browser Event Sync ---\n    document.addEventListener(\u0027auxclick\u0027, (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 e.button === 1 \u0026\u0026 typeof sendEvent === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            const path = getElementPath(e.target);\n            if (path) {\n                sendEvent(\u0027ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0027, { path: path });\n            }\n        }\n    }, true);\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
      "ModelExplanation": "Removed the standard \u0060click\u0060 event listener from the browser event sync logic in \u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060. Now, only the \u0060auxclick\u0060 listener remains, ensuring that only physical middle clicks (\u0060button === 1\u0060) will trigger the \u0060ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0060 event and select elements in the testbed\u0027s DOM Explorer. Left clicks will be completely ignored by the sync mechanism.\n\nTo test:\n\n- Click \u0022Generate \u0026 Copy Script\u0022 in the testbed and update your Tampermonkey script.\n- Reload the target webpage.\n- Left-click an element in the browser and verify it does **not** highlight in the DOM Explorer.\n- Middle-click an element and verify it **does** highlight in the DOM Explorer.",
