    {
      "Id": "a234c9c4",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-27T15:22:27.679169-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "[Attached Image: image]\n![image](/api/media/a520ac299eb44828be484726b6623e25)\n\nSo we need to do some work on the part of the system that handles the middle mouse button clicks that select elements on the page. For some reason, it works just fine in chrome based browsers, but in firefox, it only works for one or 2 clicks, and then it stops working. What happens is that after those 1 or 2 clicks, every time I middle mouse click iot brings up the scrolling icon for the page. as seen in the screenshot. I want to fix this so that it works just like chrome based browsers do and we can always middle mouse click and select elements.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\n### Changes Made\n- **Prevent Middle-Click Autoscroll \u0026 Default Actions (\u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060)**:\n  - Updated the browser event sync logic to intercept \u0060mousedown\u0060, \u0060mouseup\u0060, \u0060auxclick\u0060, and \u0060click\u0060 events for the middle mouse button (\u0060e.button === 1\u0060) in the capture phase with \u0060{ capture: true, passive: false }\u0060 on both \u0060window\u0060 and \u0060document\u0060.\n  - Added \u0060e.preventDefault()\u0060 and \u0060e.stopPropagation()\u0060 on \u0060mousedown\u0060 (where Firefox\u0027s \u0060AutoScrollChild\u0060 checks \u0060defaultPrevented\u0060 before showing the autoscroll icon) as well as on \u0060mouseup\u0060, \u0060auxclick\u0060, and \u0060click\u0060.\n  - Triggered element selection (\u0060ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0060) immediately on \u0060mousedown\u0060 (with a deduplicated fallback on \u0060auxclick\u0060) and ensured text-node targets resolve to their parent element.\n- **Prevent Highlight Overlay Overflow (\u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060)**:\n  - Added \u0060box-sizing: border-box\u0060 to \u0060#__baf_highlight_overlay\u0060 so highlighting full-viewport elements does not add 4px of border overflow and make non-scrollable pages scrollable.\n\n### How to Test\n1. Build and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060.\n2. Click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script** and paste/save the updated script into Tampermonkey in Firefox.\n3. Reload the target page in Firefox and middle-click multiple elements repeatedly across the page.\n4. Verify that the Firefox autoscroll icon no longer appears and every middle-click reliably selects and highlights the clicked element in the DOM Explorer.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ScriptGenerator.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        if (!highlightOverlay) {\n            highlightOverlay = document.createElement(\u0027div\u0027);\n            highlightOverlay.id = \u0027__baf_highlight_overlay\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.position = \u0027absolute\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.backgroundColor = \u0027rgba(0, 150, 255, 0.3)\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.border = \u00272px solid rgba(0, 150, 255, 0.8)\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.pointerEvents = \u0027none\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.zIndex = \u0027999999\u0027;\n            document.body.appendChild(highlightOverlay);\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        if (!highlightOverlay) {\n            highlightOverlay = document.createElement(\u0027div\u0027);\n            highlightOverlay.id = \u0027__baf_highlight_overlay\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.position = \u0027absolute\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.backgroundColor = \u0027rgba(0, 150, 255, 0.3)\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.border = \u00272px solid rgba(0, 150, 255, 0.8)\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.boxSizing = \u0027border-box\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.pointerEvents = \u0027none\u0027;\n            highlightOverlay.style.zIndex = \u0027999999\u0027;\n            document.body.appendChild(highlightOverlay);\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n            sb.AppendLine(@\u0022\n    // --- Browser Event Sync ---\n    document.addEventListener(\u0027auxclick\u0027, (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 e.button === 1 \u0026\u0026 typeof sendEvent === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            const path = getElementPath(e.target);\n            if (path) {\n                sendEvent(\u0027ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0027, { path: path });\n            }\n        }\n    }, true);\n\u0022);\n==== REPLACE\n            sb.AppendLine(@\u0022\n    // --- Browser Event Sync ---\n    let lastMiddleDownTime = 0;\n\n    const handleMiddleMouseSelection = (e) =\u003E {\n        if (typeof sendEvent === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            const target = e.target \u0026\u0026 e.target.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE ? e.target : (e.target ? e.target.parentElement : null);\n            const path = getElementPath(target);\n            if (path) {\n                sendEvent(\u0027ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0027, { path: path });\n            }\n        }\n    };\n\n    const onMiddleMouseDown = (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 e.button === 1) {\n            e.preventDefault();\n            e.stopPropagation();\n            const now = Date.now();\n            if (now - lastMiddleDownTime \u003E 50) {\n                lastMiddleDownTime = now;\n                handleMiddleMouseSelection(e);\n            }\n        }\n    };\n\n    const onMiddleMouseUp = (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 e.button === 1) {\n            e.preventDefault();\n            e.stopPropagation();\n        }\n    };\n\n    const onMiddleAuxClick = (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 e.button === 1) {\n            e.preventDefault();\n            e.stopPropagation();\n            const now = Date.now();\n            if (now - lastMiddleDownTime \u003E 1000) {\n                lastMiddleDownTime = now;\n                handleMiddleMouseSelection(e);\n            }\n        }\n    };\n\n    const onMiddleClick = (e) =\u003E {\n        if (e.isTrusted \u0026\u0026 e.button === 1) {\n            e.preventDefault();\n            e.stopPropagation();\n        }\n    };\n\n    [window, document].forEach(target =\u003E {\n        target.addEventListener(\u0027mousedown\u0027, onMiddleMouseDown, { capture: true, passive: false });\n        target.addEventListener(\u0027mouseup\u0027, onMiddleMouseUp, { capture: true, passive: false });\n        target.addEventListener(\u0027auxclick\u0027, onMiddleAuxClick, { capture: true, passive: false });\n        target.addEventListener(\u0027click\u0027, onMiddleClick, { capture: true, passive: false });\n    });\n\u0022);\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
      "ModelExplanation": "### Changes Made\n- **Prevent Middle-Click Autoscroll \u0026 Default Actions (\u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060)**:\n  - Updated the browser event sync logic to intercept \u0060mousedown\u0060, \u0060mouseup\u0060, \u0060auxclick\u0060, and \u0060click\u0060 events for the middle mouse button (\u0060e.button === 1\u0060) in the capture phase with \u0060{ capture: true, passive: false }\u0060 on both \u0060window\u0060 and \u0060document\u0060.\n  - Added \u0060e.preventDefault()\u0060 and \u0060e.stopPropagation()\u0060 on \u0060mousedown\u0060 (where Firefox\u0027s \u0060AutoScrollChild\u0060 checks \u0060defaultPrevented\u0060 before showing the autoscroll icon) as well as on \u0060mouseup\u0060, \u0060auxclick\u0060, and \u0060click\u0060.\n  - Triggered element selection (\u0060ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0060) immediately on \u0060mousedown\u0060 (with a deduplicated fallback on \u0060auxclick\u0060) and ensured text-node targets resolve to their parent element.\n- **Prevent Highlight Overlay Overflow (\u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060)**:\n  - Added \u0060box-sizing: border-box\u0060 to \u0060#__baf_highlight_overlay\u0060 so highlighting full-viewport elements does not add 4px of border overflow and make non-scrollable pages scrollable.\n\n### How to Test\n1. Build and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060.\n2. Click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script** and paste/save the updated script into Tampermonkey in Firefox.\n3. Reload the target page in Firefox and middle-click multiple elements repeatedly across the page.\n4. Verify that the Firefox autoscroll icon no longer appears and every middle-click reliably selects and highlights the clicked element in the DOM Explorer.",
      "Diffs": [
