    {
      "Id": "71626413",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-27T16:10:46.4798379-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\nOK so this project is pretty good so far. however, io want to add a system top it that will make it very easy for developers to scrape data off of a website they are working with. We need to make this system intuitive and easy to use but have a rich and highly functional API for other developers to tap into. I want the Testbed app to be able to easily allow the user to get the data they want, but do such with a point and click style of system. No coding should be requiered. Just like the browser automation system does. \nI want a way to see the final results or at least get a preview. I also want to be able to include automations in a scrape if needed. WE also need to be able to define what its looking for to scrape.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n- **Core Scraping Models (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\u0060)**:\n\n- **\u0060ScrapeField\u0060 \u0026 \u0060ScrapeExtractionType\u0060**: Defines what data to extract from matched elements (\u0060InnerText\u0060, \u0060TextContent\u0060, \u0060InnerHtml\u0060, \u0060OuterHtml\u0060, \u0060Value\u0060, \u0060Attribute\u0060, \u0060Href\u0060, \u0060Src\u0060, \u0060DataAttribute\u0060, \u0060ComputedStyle\u0060, \u0060Exists\u0060, \u0060Count\u0060), along with regex filtering, trimming, default fallbacks, and multi-element matching (\u0060MatchAllElements\u0060).\n- **\u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060**: Defines a complete scrape job including \u0060ContainerSelector\u0060 for repeating item lists/rows, \u0060Fields\u0060, pre-scrape and post-scrape automation sequence hooks (\u0060PreScrapeSequenceName\u0060, \u0060PostScrapeSequenceName\u0060), and multi-page pagination (\u0060EnablePagination\u0060, \u0060NextPageSelector\u0060, \u0060PaginationSequenceName\u0060, \u0060MaxPages\u0060, \u0060PageDelayMs\u0060, \u0060DeduplicateRows\u0060).\n- **\u0060ScrapeResult\u0060**: Encapsulates scraped records with built-in export and transformation helpers (\u0060ToJson\u0060, \u0060ToCsv\u0060, \u0060ToDataTable\u0060, \u0060BindTo\u003CT\u003E\u0060, \u0060GetColumnValues\u0060, \u0060GetFirstValue\u0060, \u0060SaveToJsonFileAsync\u0060, \u0060SaveToCsvFileAsync\u0060, \u0060Merge\u0060).\n- **\u0060AutomationProject\u0060 \u0026 \u0060AutomationStep\u0060 Integration**: Added \u0060Scrapes\u0060 persistence to \u0060AutomationProject\u0060 and \u0060AutomationActionType.Scrape\u0060 so scrape jobs can also be triggered as steps inside automation sequences.\n- **\u0060DomNode\u0060 Helpers**: Added smart field creation (\u0060CreateScrapeField\u0060), extraction type detection (\u0060GetSuggestedExtractionType\u0060), field naming (\u0060GetSuggestedFieldName\u0060), and path generalization (\u0060GetGeneralizedPath\u0060).\n- **Scraping Engine, Fluent API \u0026 Browser Userscript (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.Scraping\u0060, \u0060Extensions\u0060, \u0060Generators\u0060)**:\n\n- **\u0060DataScraper\u0060**: Executes single-page or paginated scrape definitions, coordinates pre/post/pagination \u0060AutomationSequence\u0060 runs via \u0060AutomationRunner\u0060, and exposes lifecycle events (\u0060OnScrapeStarted\u0060, \u0060OnScrapePageCompleted\u0060, \u0060OnScrapeCompleted\u0060, \u0060OnScrapeFailed\u0060) as well as one-line extraction methods (\u0060ExtractValueAsync\u0060, \u0060ExtractListAsync\u0060, \u0060ExtractTableAsync\u0060).\n- **\u0060ScrapeBuilder\u0060 \u0026 \u0060ReactExtensions\u0060**: Added a fluent builder API (\u0060client.CreateScrape(...)\u0060) and extension methods on \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 (\u0060ExecuteScrapeAsync\u0060, \u0060ExecuteProjectScrapesAsync\u0060, \u0060ScrapeElementAsync\u0060, \u0060ScrapeElementsAsync\u0060, \u0060ScrapeTableAsync\u0060, \u0060HighlightElementsAsync\u0060).\n- **\u0060SelectorHelper\u0060 \u0026 \u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060**: Added \u0060SCRAPE_DATA\u0060, \u0060SCRAPE_TABLE\u0060, and \u0060HIGHLIGHT_ELEMENTS\u0060 commands to the generated Tampermonkey script with automatic relative selector resolution inside repeating containers and multi-element visual highlighting in the browser.\n- **Point-and-Click Data Scraper UI (\u0060TestBedApp\u0060)**:\n\n- **DOM Explorer Context Menu**: Added right-click point-and-click actions on any DOM element to test-scrape an element, add a single or repeating scrape field, set a repeating container, or set a pagination \u0022Next\u0022 button (with on-the-fly scrape list creation).\n- **Data Scraper Tab**: Added a dedicated \u0060Data Scraper\u0060 tab to manage scrape lists, configure repeating containers and pre/post/pagination automations, edit field extraction rules, highlight matched elements in the live browser, preview results in both a \u0060Table View\u0060 (\u0060DataGridView\u0060) and \u0060JSON View\u0060, and export results to CSV or JSON.\n\n### How to Test\n\n- Build and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060, click **Start Server**, and click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script** to update your Tampermonkey userscript in the browser.\n- In **DOM Explorer** (or via middle-clicking an element in the browser), right-click any element and select:\n\n- **Set as Repeating Container For... -\u003E (\u002B New Scrape List...)** (if scraping a repeating list/table of items), or\n- **Add Scrape Field To... -\u003E (\u002B New Scrape List...)** / **Add Repeating Field (All Similar) To...** to add fields with zero coding.\n- Switch to the **Data Scraper** tab to inspect or refine the extracted fields, click **Highlight** to visually verify all matched elements in the browser, optionally attach a **Pre-Scrape** or **Post-Scrape** automation list or **Pagination** selector, and click **Preview Scrape**.\n- View the extracted dataset in the **Table View** or **JSON View** and test **Export CSV...**, **Export JSON...**, or **Copy JSON**.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\ScrapeField.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System.ComponentModel;\nusing System.Text.Json.Serialization;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    public enum ScrapeExtractionType\n    {\n        InnerText,\n        TextContent,\n        InnerHtml,\n        OuterHtml,\n        Value,\n        Attribute,\n        Href,\n        Src,\n        DataAttribute,\n        ComputedStyle,\n        Exists,\n        Count\n    }\n\n    public class ScrapeField\n    {\n        [Category(\u00221. General\u0022)]\n        [Description(\u0022The column/property name for this extracted value.\u0022)]\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022name\u0022)]\n        public string Name { get; set; } = \u0022New Field\u0022;\n\n        [Category(\u00221. General\u0022)]\n        [Description(\u0022CSS selector for the target element(s). Can be a full path or relative to the Scrape Definition\u0027s ContainerSelector.\u0022)]\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022selector\u0022)]\n        public string Selector { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [Category(\u00222. Extraction\u0022)]\n        [Description(\u0022Specifies what data to extract from the matched DOM element.\u0022)]\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022extractionType\u0022)]\n        public ScrapeExtractionType ExtractionType { get; set; } = ScrapeExtractionType.InnerText;\n\n        [Category(\u00222. Extraction\u0022)]\n        [Description(\u0022Name of the attribute, data-* key, or CSS style property when ExtractionType is Attribute, DataAttribute, or ComputedStyle.\u0022)]\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022attributeName\u0022)]\n        public string AttributeName { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [Category(\u00222. Extraction\u0022)]\n        [Description(\u0022When true, matches all similar elements on the page (if no ContainerSelector is used) or joins multiple matches within a container.\u0022)]\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022matchAllElements\u0022)]\n        public bool MatchAllElements { get; set; } = false;\n\n        [Category(\u00223. Formatting \u0026 Filtering\u0022)]\n        [Description(\u0022Fallback value if the element is not found or the extracted value is empty.\u0022)]\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022defaultValue\u0022)]\n        public string DefaultValue { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [Category(\u00223. Formatting \u0026 Filtering\u0022)]\n        [Description(\u0022Optional Regular Expression pattern to extract or filter the scraped string.\u0022)]\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022regexPattern\u0022)]\n        public string RegexPattern { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [Category(\u00223. Formatting \u0026 Filtering\u0022)]\n        [Description(\u0022Regex capture group index to return when RegexPattern is specified (0 for full match).\u0022)]\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022regexGroup\u0022)]\n        public int RegexGroup { get; set; } = 0;\n\n        [Category(\u00223. Formatting \u0026 Filtering\u0022)]\n        [Description(\u0022Whether to trim leading and trailing whitespace from the extracted value.\u0022)]\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022trim\u0022)]\n        public bool Trim { get; set; } = true;\n\n        public ScrapeField Clone()\n        {\n            return new ScrapeField\n            {\n                Name = Name,\n                Selector = Selector,\n                ExtractionType = ExtractionType,\n                AttributeName = AttributeName,\n                MatchAllElements = MatchAllElements,\n                DefaultValue = DefaultValue,\n                RegexPattern = RegexPattern,\n                RegexGroup = RegexGroup,\n                Trim = Trim\n            };\n        }\n\n        public override string ToString()\n        {\n            string extra = (ExtractionType == ScrapeExtractionType.Attribute ||\n                            ExtractionType == ScrapeExtractionType.DataAttribute ||\n                            ExtractionType == ScrapeExtractionType.ComputedStyle) \u0026\u0026\n                           !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(AttributeName)\n                ? $\u0022{ExtractionType}:{AttributeName}\u0022\n                : ExtractionType.ToString();\n\n            if (MatchAllElements)\n            {\n                extra \u002B= \u0022, All\u0022;\n            }\n\n            return $\u0022{Name} [{extra}]\u0022;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\ScrapeDefinition.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.Text.Json.Serialization;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Scraping;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    public class ScrapeDefinition\n    {\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022id\u0022)]\n        public string Id { get; set; } = Guid.NewGuid().ToString();\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022name\u0022)]\n        public string Name { get; set; } = \u0022New Scrape\u0022;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022isActive\u0022)]\n        public bool IsActive { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022containerSelector\u0022)]\n        public string ContainerSelector { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022fields\u0022)]\n        public List\u003CScrapeField\u003E Fields { get; set; } = new();\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022preScrapeSequenceName\u0022)]\n        public string PreScrapeSequenceName { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022postScrapeSequenceName\u0022)]\n        public string PostScrapeSequenceName { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022enablePagination\u0022)]\n        public bool EnablePagination { get; set; } = false;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022nextPageSelector\u0022)]\n        public string NextPageSelector { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022paginationSequenceName\u0022)]\n        public string PaginationSequenceName { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022maxPages\u0022)]\n        public int MaxPages { get; set; } = 1;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022waitBeforeScrapeMs\u0022)]\n        public int WaitBeforeScrapeMs { get; set; } = 300;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022pageDelayMs\u0022)]\n        public int PageDelayMs { get; set; } = 1000;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022deduplicateRows\u0022)]\n        public bool DeduplicateRows { get; set; } = false;\n\n        public bool MoveFieldUp(int index)\n        {\n            if (index \u003C= 0 || index \u003E= Fields.Count) return false;\n            var field = Fields[index];\n            Fields.RemoveAt(index);\n            Fields.Insert(index - 1, field);\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        public bool MoveFieldDown(int index)\n        {\n            if (index \u003C 0 || index \u003E= Fields.Count - 1) return false;\n            var field = Fields[index];\n            Fields.RemoveAt(index);\n            Fields.Insert(index \u002B 1, field);\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Sets the repeating container selector and automatically converts any existing child field selectors to be relative to the container.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void SetContainerAndRelativizeFields(string containerSelector)\n        {\n            ContainerSelector = containerSelector?.Trim() ?? string.Empty;\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(ContainerSelector))\n                return;\n\n            foreach (var field in Fields)\n            {\n                if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(field.Selector) \u0026\u0026\n                    SelectorHelper.IsInsideContainer(ContainerSelector, field.Selector))\n                {\n                    field.Selector = SelectorHelper.MakeRelativeSelector(ContainerSelector, field.Selector);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Generates a unique field name within this definition based on a base name.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetUniqueFieldName(string baseName)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(baseName))\n                baseName = \u0022Field\u0022;\n\n            string candidate = baseName.Trim();\n            int counter = 2;\n            while (Fields.Exists(f =\u003E string.Equals(f.Name, candidate, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)))\n            {\n                candidate = $\u0022{baseName.Trim()}_{counter}\u0022;\n                counter\u002B\u002B;\n            }\n            return candidate;\n        }\n\n        public override string ToString() =\u003E Name;\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\ScrapeResult.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.Data;\nusing System.IO;\nusing System.Linq;\nusing System.Reflection;\nusing System.Text;\nusing System.Text.Json;\nusing System.Text.Json.Serialization;\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    public class ScrapeResult\n    {\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022scrapeId\u0022)]\n        public string ScrapeId { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022scrapeName\u0022)]\n        public string ScrapeName { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022success\u0022)]\n        public bool Success { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022errorMessage\u0022)]\n        public string? ErrorMessage { get; set; }\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022timestampUtc\u0022)]\n        public DateTime TimestampUtc { get; set; } = DateTime.UtcNow;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022pagesScraped\u0022)]\n        public int PagesScraped { get; set; } = 1;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022records\u0022)]\n        public List\u003CDictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E Records { get; set; } = new();\n\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public int RecordCount =\u003E Records.Count;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns all distinct column/field names across all scraped records.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public IReadOnlyList\u003Cstring\u003E GetColumnNames()\n        {\n            var columns = new List\u003Cstring\u003E();\n            var seen = new HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\n\n            foreach (var record in Records)\n            {\n                foreach (var key in record.Keys)\n                {\n                    if (seen.Add(key))\n                    {\n                        columns.Add(key);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            return columns;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Retrieves all values for a specific field across all scraped records.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public IEnumerable\u003Cstring?\u003E GetColumnValues(string fieldName)\n        {\n            foreach (var record in Records)\n            {\n                if (record.TryGetValue(fieldName, out var val))\n                {\n                    yield return val;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Retrieves the first scraped value for the specified field name, or null if not present.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string? GetFirstValue(string fieldName)\n        {\n            var firstRecord = Records.FirstOrDefault();\n            if (firstRecord != null \u0026\u0026 firstRecord.TryGetValue(fieldName, out var val))\n            {\n                return val;\n            }\n            return null;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Serializes the scraped records to a JSON string.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string ToJson(bool writeIndented = true, bool recordsOnly = false)\n        {\n            var options = new JsonSerializerOptions { WriteIndented = writeIndented };\n            return recordsOnly\n                ? JsonSerializer.Serialize(Records, options)\n                : JsonSerializer.Serialize(this, options);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Formats the scraped records as a CSV string.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string ToCsv(char delimiter = \u0027,\u0027)\n        {\n            var columns = GetColumnNames();\n            if (columns.Count == 0)\n                return string.Empty;\n\n            var sb = new StringBuilder();\n            sb.AppendLine(string.Join(delimiter, columns.Select(c =\u003E EscapeCsvField(c, delimiter))));\n\n            foreach (var record in Records)\n            {\n                var rowValues = columns.Select(col =\u003E\n                {\n                    record.TryGetValue(col, out var val);\n                    return EscapeCsvField(val ?? string.Empty, delimiter);\n                });\n                sb.AppendLine(string.Join(delimiter, rowValues));\n            }\n\n            return sb.ToString();\n        }\n\n        private static string EscapeCsvField(string field, char delimiter)\n        {\n            if (field.Contains(delimiter) || field.Contains(\u0027\u0022\u0027) || field.Contains(\u0027\\r\u0027) || field.Contains(\u0027\\n\u0027))\n            {\n                return $\u0022\\\u0022{field.Replace(\u0022\\\u0022\u0022, \u0022\\\u0022\\\u0022\u0022)}\\\u0022\u0022;\n            }\n            return field;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Converts the scraped records into a \u003Csee cref=\u0022DataTable\u0022/\u003E suitable for UI binding or data processing.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public DataTable ToDataTable()\n        {\n            var table = new DataTable(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(ScrapeName) ? \u0022ScrapeResults\u0022 : ScrapeName);\n            var columns = GetColumnNames();\n\n            foreach (var col in columns)\n            {\n                table.Columns.Add(col, typeof(string));\n            }\n\n            foreach (var record in Records)\n            {\n                var row = table.NewRow();\n                foreach (var col in columns)\n                {\n                    if (record.TryGetValue(col, out var val) \u0026\u0026 val != null)\n                    {\n                        row[col] = val;\n                    }\n                    else\n                    {\n                        row[col] = string.Empty;\n                    }\n                }\n                table.Rows.Add(row);\n            }\n\n            return table;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Maps the scraped records onto strongly-typed C# objects of type \u003Ctypeparamref name=\u0022T\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public List\u003CT\u003E BindTo\u003CT\u003E() where T : new()\n        {\n            var results = new List\u003CT\u003E(Records.Count);\n            var props = typeof(T).GetProperties(BindingFlags.Public | BindingFlags.Instance)\n                .Where(p =\u003E p.CanWrite)\n                .ToDictionary(p =\u003E p.Name, p =\u003E p, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\n\n            foreach (var record in Records)\n            {\n                var instance = new T();\n                foreach (var kvp in record)\n                {\n                    string normalizedKey = kvp.Key.Replace(\u0022 \u0022, \u0022\u0022).Replace(\u0022_\u0022, \u0022\u0022).Replace(\u0022-\u0022, \u0022\u0022);\n                    if (!props.TryGetValue(kvp.Key, out var prop))\n                    {\n                        prop = props.Values.FirstOrDefault(p =\u003E\n                            string.Equals(p.Name.Replace(\u0022_\u0022, \u0022\u0022), normalizedKey, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));\n                    }\n\n                    if (prop != null \u0026\u0026 kvp.Value != null)\n                    {\n                        try\n                        {\n                            Type targetType = Nullable.GetUnderlyingType(prop.PropertyType) ?? prop.PropertyType;\n                            object? converted = targetType == typeof(string)\n                                ? kvp.Value\n                                : Convert.ChangeType(kvp.Value, targetType);\n                            prop.SetValue(instance, converted);\n                        }\n                        catch\n                        {\n                            // Skip unconvertible fields\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                results.Add(instance);\n            }\n\n            return results;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Merges records from another \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeResult\u0022/\u003E into this instance.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void Merge(ScrapeResult other, bool deduplicate = false)\n        {\n            if (other == null) return;\n\n            if (!deduplicate)\n            {\n                Records.AddRange(other.Records);\n                return;\n            }\n\n            var existingFingerprints = new HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E(Records.Select(GetRecordFingerprint));\n            foreach (var rec in other.Records)\n            {\n                if (existingFingerprints.Add(GetRecordFingerprint(rec)))\n                {\n                    Records.Add(rec);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        internal static string GetRecordFingerprint(Dictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E record)\n        {\n            return string.Join(\u0022|\u0022, record.OrderBy(k =\u003E k.Key, StringComparer.Ordinal).Select(k =\u003E $\u0022{k.Key}={k.Value}\u0022));\n        }\n\n        public void SaveToJsonFile(string filePath, bool recordsOnly = false)\n        {\n            File.WriteAllText(filePath, ToJson(true, recordsOnly));\n        }\n\n        public Task SaveToJsonFileAsync(string filePath, bool recordsOnly = false, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return File.WriteAllTextAsync(filePath, ToJson(true, recordsOnly), cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        public void SaveToCsvFile(string filePath, char delimiter = \u0027,\u0027)\n        {\n            File.WriteAllText(filePath, ToCsv(delimiter), Encoding.UTF8);\n        }\n\n        public Task SaveToCsvFileAsync(string filePath, char delimiter = \u0027,\u0027, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return File.WriteAllTextAsync(filePath, ToCsv(delimiter), Encoding.UTF8, cancellationToken);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Scraping\\SelectorHelper.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Linq;\nusing System.Text.RegularExpressions;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Models;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Scraping\n{\n    public static class SelectorHelper\n    {\n        private static readonly Regex NthChildRegex = new(@\u0022:nth-child\\(\\d\u002B\\)\u0022, RegexOptions.IgnoreCase | RegexOptions.Compiled);\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Removes :nth-child(N) from a single selector segment.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static string StripNthChild(string segment)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(segment))\n                return string.Empty;\n\n            return NthChildRegex.Replace(segment, string.Empty).Trim();\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Generalizes a CSS path by removing :nth-child(N) from the final element segment so it matches all sibling elements of the same tag.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static string GeneralizeSelector(string selector)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selector))\n                return string.Empty;\n\n            var parts = selector.Split(\u0027\u003E\u0027, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries)\n                .Select(p =\u003E p.Trim())\n                .ToArray();\n\n            if (parts.Length == 0)\n                return selector.Trim();\n\n            parts[^1] = StripNthChild(parts[^1]);\n            return string.Join(\u0022 \u003E \u0022, parts);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Generalizes a repeating field selector by finding the most likely repeating ancestor or leaf segment in the DOM tree.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static string GeneralizeRepeatingFieldSelector(string selector, DomNode? rootDom = null)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selector))\n                return string.Empty;\n\n            var parts = selector.Split(\u0027\u003E\u0027, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries)\n                .Select(p =\u003E p.Trim())\n                .ToArray();\n\n            if (parts.Length == 0)\n                return selector;\n\n            if (rootDom != null)\n            {\n                // Walk from parent up to root looking for a parent node whose tag repeats under its own parent\n                for (int i = parts.Length - 2; i \u003E= 1; i--)\n                {\n                    string ancestorPath = string.Join(\u0022 \u003E \u0022, parts.Take(i));\n                    var ancestorNode = rootDom.FindByPath(ancestorPath);\n                    if (ancestorNode?.Children != null)\n                    {\n                        string childTag = StripNthChild(parts[i]);\n                        int sameTagCount = ancestorNode.Children.Count(c =\u003E\n                            c.Type == \u0022element\u0022 \u0026\u0026\n                            string.Equals(c.TagName, childTag, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));\n\n                        if (sameTagCount \u003E 1)\n                        {\n                            var generalizedParts = parts.ToArray();\n                            generalizedParts[i] = StripNthChild(generalizedParts[i]);\n                            return string.Join(\u0022 \u003E \u0022, generalizedParts);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            return GeneralizeSelector(selector);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Determines whether \u003Cparamref name=\u0022fieldSelector\u0022/\u003E is located inside (or equals) \u003Cparamref name=\u0022containerSelector\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static bool IsInsideContainer(string containerSelector, string fieldSelector)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(containerSelector) || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(fieldSelector))\n                return false;\n\n            var cParts = containerSelector.Split(\u0027\u003E\u0027, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries)\n                .Select(p =\u003E p.Trim())\n                .ToArray();\n\n            var fParts = fieldSelector.Split(\u0027\u003E\u0027, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries)\n                .Select(p =\u003E p.Trim())\n                .ToArray();\n\n            if (fParts.Length \u003C cParts.Length)\n                return false;\n\n            for (int i = 0; i \u003C cParts.Length; i\u002B\u002B)\n            {\n                if (!string.Equals(StripNthChild(cParts[i]), StripNthChild(fParts[i]), StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\n                {\n                    return false;\n                }\n            }\n\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Converts a full DOM path into a selector relative to \u003Cparamref name=\u0022containerSelector\u0022/\u003E if it resides inside the container.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static string MakeRelativeSelector(string containerSelector, string fieldSelector)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(fieldSelector))\n                return \u0022:scope\u0022;\n\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(containerSelector))\n                return fieldSelector.Trim();\n\n            if (!IsInsideContainer(containerSelector, fieldSelector))\n                return fieldSelector.Trim();\n\n            var cParts = containerSelector.Split(\u0027\u003E\u0027, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries)\n                .Select(p =\u003E p.Trim())\n                .ToArray();\n\n            var fParts = fieldSelector.Split(\u0027\u003E\u0027, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries)\n                .Select(p =\u003E p.Trim())\n                .ToArray();\n\n            if (fParts.Length == cParts.Length)\n                return \u0022:scope\u0022;\n\n            return string.Join(\u0022 \u003E \u0022, fParts.Skip(cParts.Length));\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Scraping\\DataScraper.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.Linq;\nusing System.Text.Json;\nusing System.Text.RegularExpressions;\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Automation;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Extensions;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Models;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Server;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Scraping\n{\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// High-level execution engine for running structured web scraping jobs, single-element extractions,\n    /// HTML table extractions, and multi-page automated scrapes.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class DataScraper\n    {\n        private readonly AutomationRunner _runner;\n\n        public event EventHandler\u003CScrapeEventArgs\u003E? OnScrapeStarted;\n        public event EventHandler\u003CScrapePageEventArgs\u003E? OnScrapePageCompleted;\n        public event EventHandler\u003CScrapeEventArgs\u003E? OnScrapeCompleted;\n        public event EventHandler\u003CScrapeEventArgs\u003E? OnScrapeFailed;\n\n        public DataScraper(AutomationRunner? runner = null)\n        {\n            _runner = runner ?? new AutomationRunner();\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Executes all active \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeDefinition\u0022/\u003E items in an \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationProject\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task\u003CList\u003CScrapeResult\u003E\u003E RunProjectScrapesAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            AutomationProject project,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (client == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(client));\n            if (project == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(project));\n\n            var results = new List\u003CScrapeResult\u003E();\n            foreach (var scrape in project.Scrapes.Where(s =\u003E s.IsActive))\n            {\n                cancellationToken.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();\n                var res = await RunScrapeAsync(client, scrape, project.Sequences, cancellationToken);\n                results.Add(res);\n            }\n\n            return results;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Executes a single \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeDefinition\u0022/\u003E, including any configured pre-scrape automation,\n        /// multi-page pagination, and post-scrape automation.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task\u003CScrapeResult\u003E RunScrapeAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            ScrapeDefinition definition,\n            IEnumerable\u003CAutomationSequence\u003E? availableSequences = null,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (client == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(client));\n            if (definition == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(definition));\n\n            var sequenceLookup = availableSequences?\n                .Where(s =\u003E !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(s.Name))\n                .GroupBy(s =\u003E s.Name, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                .ToDictionary(g =\u003E g.Key, g =\u003E g.First(), StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n                ?? new Dictionary\u003Cstring, AutomationSequence\u003E(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\n\n            var aggregateResult = new ScrapeResult\n            {\n                ScrapeId = definition.Id,\n                ScrapeName = definition.Name,\n                TimestampUtc = DateTime.UtcNow,\n                PagesScraped = 0\n            };\n\n            OnScrapeStarted?.Invoke(this, new ScrapeEventArgs(definition));\n\n            try\n            {\n                // 1. Run Pre-Scrape Automation Sequence if configured\n                if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(definition.PreScrapeSequenceName) \u0026\u0026\n                    sequenceLookup.TryGetValue(definition.PreScrapeSequenceName, out var preSeq))\n                {\n                    await _runner.RunSequenceAsync(client, preSeq, cancellationToken);\n                }\n\n                if (definition.WaitBeforeScrapeMs \u003E 0)\n                {\n                    await Task.Delay(definition.WaitBeforeScrapeMs, cancellationToken);\n                }\n\n                int totalPagesToScrape = definition.EnablePagination ? Math.Max(1, definition.MaxPages) : 1;\n                var seenFingerprints = new HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E();\n\n                // 2. Scrape Page Loop\n                for (int page = 1; page \u003C= totalPagesToScrape; page\u002B\u002B)\n                {\n                    cancellationToken.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();\n\n                    var pageRecords = await ExecuteSinglePageScrapeInternalAsync(client, definition, cancellationToken);\n                    var addedPageRecords = new List\u003CDictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E();\n\n                    foreach (var record in pageRecords)\n                    {\n                        if (definition.DeduplicateRows)\n                        {\n                            string fp = ScrapeResult.GetRecordFingerprint(record);\n                            if (!seenFingerprints.Add(fp))\n                                continue;\n                        }\n\n                        aggregateResult.Records.Add(record);\n                        addedPageRecords.Add(record);\n                    }\n\n                    aggregateResult.PagesScraped = page;\n                    OnScrapePageCompleted?.Invoke(this, new ScrapePageEventArgs(definition, page, addedPageRecords));\n\n                    // Advance to next page if more pages remain\n                    if (page \u003C totalPagesToScrape \u0026\u0026 definition.EnablePagination)\n                    {\n                        bool advanced = false;\n\n                        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(definition.PaginationSequenceName) \u0026\u0026\n                            sequenceLookup.TryGetValue(definition.PaginationSequenceName, out var pageSeq))\n                        {\n                            await _runner.RunSequenceAsync(client, pageSeq, cancellationToken);\n                            advanced = true;\n                        }\n                        else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(definition.NextPageSelector))\n                        {\n                            try\n                            {\n                                await client.ClickReactElementAsync(definition.NextPageSelector, cancellationToken);\n                                advanced = true;\n                            }\n                            catch\n                            {\n                                // Next page element not found or no longer clickable; stop pagination cleanly\n                                break;\n                            }\n                        }\n\n                        if (!advanced)\n                            break;\n\n                        if (definition.PageDelayMs \u003E 0)\n                        {\n                            await Task.Delay(definition.PageDelayMs, cancellationToken);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // 3. Run Post-Scrape Automation Sequence if configured\n                if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(definition.PostScrapeSequenceName) \u0026\u0026\n                    sequenceLookup.TryGetValue(definition.PostScrapeSequenceName, out var postSeq))\n                {\n                    await _runner.RunSequenceAsync(client, postSeq, cancellationToken);\n                }\n\n                aggregateResult.Success = true;\n                OnScrapeCompleted?.Invoke(this, new ScrapeEventArgs(definition, aggregateResult));\n                return aggregateResult;\n            }\n            catch (Exception ex)\n            {\n                aggregateResult.Success = false;\n                aggregateResult.ErrorMessage = ex.Message;\n                OnScrapeFailed?.Invoke(this, new ScrapeEventArgs(definition, aggregateResult, ex));\n                throw;\n            }\n        }\n\n        private async Task\u003CList\u003CDictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E\u003E ExecuteSinglePageScrapeInternalAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            ScrapeDefinition definition,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken)\n        {\n            var payload = new\n            {\n                containerSelector = definition.ContainerSelector,\n                fields = definition.Fields.Select(f =\u003E new\n                {\n                    name = f.Name,\n                    selector = f.Selector,\n                    extractionType = f.ExtractionType.ToString(),\n                    attributeName = f.AttributeName,\n                    defaultValue = f.DefaultValue,\n                    regexPattern = f.RegexPattern,\n                    regexGroup = f.RegexGroup,\n                    trim = f.Trim,\n                    matchAllElements = f.MatchAllElements\n                }).ToList()\n            };\n\n            var cmdResult = await client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022SCRAPE_DATA\u0022, payload, cancellationToken);\n            var records = ParseRecordsFromCommandOutput(cmdResult.Output);\n\n            // Apply C#-side post-processing (Regex/Trim/DefaultValue fallback) in case custom scripts returned raw strings\n            foreach (var record in records)\n            {\n                foreach (var field in definition.Fields)\n                {\n                    if (!record.TryGetValue(field.Name, out var rawVal) || string.IsNullOrEmpty(rawVal))\n                    {\n                        record[field.Name] = field.DefaultValue;\n                        continue;\n                    }\n\n                    string processed = field.Trim ? rawVal.Trim() : rawVal;\n                    if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(field.RegexPattern))\n                    {\n                        try\n                        {\n                            var match = Regex.Match(processed, field.RegexPattern);\n                            if (match.Success)\n                            {\n                                processed = field.RegexGroup \u003E= 0 \u0026\u0026 field.RegexGroup \u003C match.Groups.Count\n                                    ? match.Groups[field.RegexGroup].Value\n                                    : match.Value;\n                            }\n                            else\n                            {\n                                processed = field.DefaultValue;\n                            }\n                        }\n                        catch\n                        {\n                            // Keep processed value if regex is invalid\n                        }\n                    }\n\n                    record[field.Name] = processed;\n                }\n            }\n\n            return records;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Previews a single \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeField\u0022/\u003E against the current page.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task\u003CScrapeResult\u003E PreviewFieldAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            ScrapeField field,\n            string? containerSelector = null,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var tempDef = new ScrapeDefinition\n            {\n                Name = $\u0022Preview: {field.Name}\u0022,\n                ContainerSelector = containerSelector ?? string.Empty,\n                WaitBeforeScrapeMs = 0,\n                Fields = new List\u003CScrapeField\u003E { field }\n            };\n\n            return RunScrapeAsync(client, tempDef, null, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Extracts a single value from the first element matching \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selector\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task\u003Cstring?\u003E ExtractValueAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            string selector,\n            ScrapeExtractionType extractionType = ScrapeExtractionType.InnerText,\n            string? attributeName = null,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var field = new ScrapeField\n            {\n                Name = \u0022Value\u0022,\n                Selector = selector,\n                ExtractionType = extractionType,\n                AttributeName = attributeName ?? string.Empty,\n                MatchAllElements = false\n            };\n\n            var res = await PreviewFieldAsync(client, field, null, cancellationToken);\n            return res.GetFirstValue(\u0022Value\u0022);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Extracts a list of values from all elements matching \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selector\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task\u003CList\u003Cstring\u003E\u003E ExtractListAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            string selector,\n            ScrapeExtractionType extractionType = ScrapeExtractionType.InnerText,\n            string? attributeName = null,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var field = new ScrapeField\n            {\n                Name = \u0022Item\u0022,\n                Selector = selector,\n                ExtractionType = extractionType,\n                AttributeName = attributeName ?? string.Empty,\n                MatchAllElements = true\n            };\n\n            var res = await PreviewFieldAsync(client, field, null, cancellationToken);\n            return res.GetColumnValues(\u0022Item\u0022)\n                .Where(v =\u003E v != null)\n                .Select(v =\u003E v!)\n                .ToList();\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Automatically extracts an HTML \u0026lt;table\u0026gt; into a structured \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeResult\u0022/\u003E using the table\u0027s headers as column names.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task\u003CScrapeResult\u003E ExtractTableAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            string tableSelector = \u0022table\u0022,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (client == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(client));\n\n            var cmdResult = await client.SendCommandAsync(\u0022SCRAPE_TABLE\u0022, new { selector = tableSelector }, cancellationToken);\n            var records = ParseRecordsFromCommandOutput(cmdResult.Output);\n\n            return new ScrapeResult\n            {\n                ScrapeName = $\u0022Table ({tableSelector})\u0022,\n                Success = cmdResult.Status == \u0022completed\u0022,\n                PagesScraped = 1,\n                Records = records\n            };\n        }\n\n        internal static List\u003CDictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E ParseRecordsFromCommandOutput(string? output)\n        {\n            var records = new List\u003CDictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E();\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(output))\n                return records;\n\n            try\n            {\n                using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(output);\n                JsonElement recordsElement = doc.RootElement;\n\n                if (doc.RootElement.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Object \u0026\u0026\n                    doc.RootElement.TryGetProperty(\u0022records\u0022, out var prop) \u0026\u0026\n                    prop.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Array)\n                {\n                    recordsElement = prop;\n                }\n\n                if (recordsElement.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Array)\n                {\n                    foreach (var item in recordsElement.EnumerateArray())\n                    {\n                        if (item.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Object)\n                        {\n                            var dict = new Dictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E();\n                            foreach (var kvp in item.EnumerateObject())\n                            {\n                                dict[kvp.Name] = kvp.Value.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Null\n                                    ? null\n                                    : kvp.Value.ToString();\n                            }\n                            records.Add(dict);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            catch\n            {\n                // Return empty list if output is not valid JSON\n            }\n\n            return records;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Scraping\\ScrapeBuilder.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Automation;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Models;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Server;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Scraping\n{\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Fluent builder for programmatically constructing and executing \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeDefinition\u0022/\u003E workflows.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class ScrapeBuilder\n    {\n        private readonly BrowserClient? _client;\n        private readonly ScrapeDefinition _definition;\n        private readonly List\u003CAutomationSequence\u003E _sequences = new();\n\n        public ScrapeBuilder(string name = \u0022Scrape\u0022, BrowserClient? client = null)\n        {\n            _client = client;\n            _definition = new ScrapeDefinition { Name = name };\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Sets the CSS selector for repeating item containers (e.g., product cards or table rows).\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapeBuilder WithContainer(string containerSelector)\n        {\n            _definition.ContainerSelector = containerSelector;\n            return this;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Adds a field to extract from each container or from the page.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapeBuilder Field(\n            string name,\n            string selector,\n            ScrapeExtractionType extractionType = ScrapeExtractionType.InnerText,\n            string attributeName = \u0022\u0022,\n            bool matchAllElements = false,\n            string defaultValue = \u0022\u0022,\n            string regexPattern = \u0022\u0022)\n        {\n            _definition.Fields.Add(new ScrapeField\n            {\n                Name = name,\n                Selector = selector,\n                ExtractionType = extractionType,\n                AttributeName = attributeName,\n                MatchAllElements = matchAllElements,\n                DefaultValue = defaultValue,\n                RegexPattern = regexPattern\n            });\n            return this;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Configures an \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationSequence\u0022/\u003E to run prior to scraping.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapeBuilder WithPreScrapeAutomation(AutomationSequence sequence)\n        {\n            if (sequence == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(sequence));\n            _definition.PreScrapeSequenceName = sequence.Name;\n            _sequences.Add(sequence);\n            return this;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Configures an \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationSequence\u0022/\u003E to run after scraping finishes.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapeBuilder WithPostScrapeAutomation(AutomationSequence sequence)\n        {\n            if (sequence == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(sequence));\n            _definition.PostScrapeSequenceName = sequence.Name;\n            _sequences.Add(sequence);\n            return this;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Enables multi-page scraping by clicking a \u0022Next Page\u0022 selector between pages.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapeBuilder WithPagination(string nextPageSelector, int maxPages = 5, int pageDelayMs = 1000, bool deduplicateRows = false)\n        {\n            _definition.EnablePagination = true;\n            _definition.NextPageSelector = nextPageSelector;\n            _definition.MaxPages = maxPages;\n            _definition.PageDelayMs = pageDelayMs;\n            _definition.DeduplicateRows = deduplicateRows;\n            return this;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Enables multi-page scraping using a custom \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationSequence\u0022/\u003E to advance pages.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapeBuilder WithPaginationSequence(AutomationSequence paginationSequence, int maxPages = 5, int pageDelayMs = 1000, bool deduplicateRows = false)\n        {\n            if (paginationSequence == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(paginationSequence));\n            _definition.EnablePagination = true;\n            _definition.PaginationSequenceName = paginationSequence.Name;\n            _definition.MaxPages = maxPages;\n            _definition.PageDelayMs = pageDelayMs;\n            _definition.DeduplicateRows = deduplicateRows;\n            _sequences.Add(paginationSequence);\n            return this;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns the built \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeDefinition\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapeDefinition Build() =\u003E _definition;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Executes the built scrape definition against the associated or provided \u003Csee cref=\u0022BrowserClient\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task\u003CScrapeResult\u003E ExecuteAsync(\n            BrowserClient? client = null,\n            DataScraper? scraper = null,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var targetClient = client ?? _client ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\u0022A BrowserClient must be provided to execute the scrape.\u0022);\n            var activeScraper = scraper ?? new DataScraper();\n            return activeScraper.RunScrapeAsync(targetClient, _definition, _sequences, cancellationToken);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\AutomationProject.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022sequences\u0022)]\n        public List\u003CAutomationSequence\u003E Sequences { get; set; } = new();\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Builds a \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScriptOptions\u0022/\u003E instance configured from this project\u0027s match rules.\n==== REPLACE\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022sequences\u0022)]\n        public List\u003CAutomationSequence\u003E Sequences { get; set; } = new();\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022scrapes\u0022)]\n        public List\u003CScrapeDefinition\u003E Scrapes { get; set; } = new();\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Builds a \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScriptOptions\u0022/\u003E instance configured from this project\u0027s match rules.\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\AutomationStep.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    public enum AutomationActionType\n    {\n        Click,\n        SetValue,\n        EvaluateScript,\n        Custom\n    }\n==== REPLACE\n    public enum AutomationActionType\n    {\n        Click,\n        SetValue,\n        EvaluateScript,\n        Scrape,\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
      "ModelExplanation": "### Summary of Changes\n\n- **Core Scraping Models (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\u0060)**:\n\n- **\u0060ScrapeField\u0060 \u0026 \u0060ScrapeExtractionType\u0060**: Defines what data to extract from matched elements (\u0060InnerText\u0060, \u0060TextContent\u0060, \u0060InnerHtml\u0060, \u0060OuterHtml\u0060, \u0060Value\u0060, \u0060Attribute\u0060, \u0060Href\u0060, \u0060Src\u0060, \u0060DataAttribute\u0060, \u0060ComputedStyle\u0060, \u0060Exists\u0060, \u0060Count\u0060), along with regex filtering, trimming, default fallbacks, and multi-element matching (\u0060MatchAllElements\u0060).\n- **\u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060**: Defines a complete scrape job including \u0060ContainerSelector\u0060 for repeating item lists/rows, \u0060Fields\u0060, pre-scrape and post-scrape automation sequence hooks (\u0060PreScrapeSequenceName\u0060, \u0060PostScrapeSequenceName\u0060), and multi-page pagination (\u0060EnablePagination\u0060, \u0060NextPageSelector\u0060, \u0060PaginationSequenceName\u0060, \u0060MaxPages\u0060, \u0060PageDelayMs\u0060, \u0060DeduplicateRows\u0060).\n- **\u0060ScrapeResult\u0060**: Encapsulates scraped records with built-in export and transformation helpers (\u0060ToJson\u0060, \u0060ToCsv\u0060, \u0060ToDataTable\u0060, \u0060BindTo\u003CT\u003E\u0060, \u0060GetColumnValues\u0060, \u0060GetFirstValue\u0060, \u0060SaveToJsonFileAsync\u0060, \u0060SaveToCsvFileAsync\u0060, \u0060Merge\u0060).\n- **\u0060AutomationProject\u0060 \u0026 \u0060AutomationStep\u0060 Integration**: Added \u0060Scrapes\u0060 persistence to \u0060AutomationProject\u0060 and \u0060AutomationActionType.Scrape\u0060 so scrape jobs can also be triggered as steps inside automation sequences.\n- **\u0060DomNode\u0060 Helpers**: Added smart field creation (\u0060CreateScrapeField\u0060), extraction type detection (\u0060GetSuggestedExtractionType\u0060), field naming (\u0060GetSuggestedFieldName\u0060), and path generalization (\u0060GetGeneralizedPath\u0060).\n- **Scraping Engine, Fluent API \u0026 Browser Userscript (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.Scraping\u0060, \u0060Extensions\u0060, \u0060Generators\u0060)**:\n\n- **\u0060DataScraper\u0060**: Executes single-page or paginated scrape definitions, coordinates pre/post/pagination \u0060AutomationSequence\u0060 runs via \u0060AutomationRunner\u0060, and exposes lifecycle events (\u0060OnScrapeStarted\u0060, \u0060OnScrapePageCompleted\u0060, \u0060OnScrapeCompleted\u0060, \u0060OnScrapeFailed\u0060) as well as one-line extraction methods (\u0060ExtractValueAsync\u0060, \u0060ExtractListAsync\u0060, \u0060ExtractTableAsync\u0060).\n- **\u0060ScrapeBuilder\u0060 \u0026 \u0060ReactExtensions\u0060**: Added a fluent builder API (\u0060client.CreateScrape(...)\u0060) and extension methods on \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 (\u0060ExecuteScrapeAsync\u0060, \u0060ExecuteProjectScrapesAsync\u0060, \u0060ScrapeElementAsync\u0060, \u0060ScrapeElementsAsync\u0060, \u0060ScrapeTableAsync\u0060, \u0060HighlightElementsAsync\u0060).\n- **\u0060SelectorHelper\u0060 \u0026 \u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060**: Added \u0060SCRAPE_DATA\u0060, \u0060SCRAPE_TABLE\u0060, and \u0060HIGHLIGHT_ELEMENTS\u0060 commands to the generated Tampermonkey script with automatic relative selector resolution inside repeating containers and multi-element visual highlighting in the browser.\n- **Point-and-Click Data Scraper UI (\u0060TestBedApp\u0060)**:\n\n- **DOM Explorer Context Menu**: Added right-click point-and-click actions on any DOM element to test-scrape an element, add a single or repeating scrape field, set a repeating container, or set a pagination \u0022Next\u0022 button (with on-the-fly scrape list creation).\n- **Data Scraper Tab**: Added a dedicated \u0060Data Scraper\u0060 tab to manage scrape lists, configure repeating containers and pre/post/pagination automations, edit field extraction rules, highlight matched elements in the live browser, preview results in both a \u0060Table View\u0060 (\u0060DataGridView\u0060) and \u0060JSON View\u0060, and export results to CSV or JSON.\n\n### How to Test\n\n- Build and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060, click **Start Server**, and click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script** to update your Tampermonkey userscript in the browser.\n- In **DOM Explorer** (or via middle-clicking an element in the browser), right-click any element and select:\n\n- **Set as Repeating Container For... -\u003E (\u002B New Scrape List...)** (if scraping a repeating list/table of items), or\n- **Add Scrape Field To... -\u003E (\u002B New Scrape List...)** / **Add Repeating Field (All Similar) To...** to add fields with zero coding.\n- Switch to the **Data Scraper** tab to inspect or refine the extracted fields, click **Highlight** to visually verify all matched elements in the browser, optionally attach a **Pre-Scrape** or **Post-Scrape** automation list or **Pagination** selector, and click **Preview Scrape**.\n- View the extracted dataset in the **Table View** or **JSON View** and test **Export CSV...**, **Export JSON...**, or **Copy JSON**.",
      "Diffs": [
