    {
      "Id": "91834be2",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-27T17:34:10.8614461-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "This is perfect! Now we need to do one more thing. When the system moves to the next page during a scrape,. we need to ensure that there is a way to add a delay so that it waits for a specified amout of time before it moves onto the next page. This will avoid triggering rate limits from a site. Now if we do get rate limited, and we get a 429 http response code, i want the system to check and see if there is a Retry-After Header on the response and if so, report that back to the UI and then try again once the date and time for the retry has been reached. Or if it just gives us a timeout in seconds or whatever, wait till that elapses and then for each page turn there after, ensure it waits that specified amount of time and we can see that in the UI. Thios way the site can report to us how long we need the delay to be,. or we can specify one of our own in advance so we dont ever get a 429 respo0nse/.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n- **Pre-Navigation Page Turn Delay (\u0060DataScraper.cs\u0060, \u0060ScrapeBuilder.cs\u0060, \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Moved the \u0060PageDelayMs\u0060 wait to execute **before** advancing to the next page during pagination so requests are spaced out to avoid triggering rate limits.\n- Added a **Page Delay (ms):** numeric control (\u0060numPageDelayMs\u0060) to the **Data Scraper** tab in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 so you can configure the page delay in advance and see live updates in the UI.\n- Added \u0060OnPageTurnDelay\u0060 on \u0060DataScraper\u0060 so the UI logs and displays the active wait duration before each page turn.\n- **HTTP 429 \u0026 \u0060Retry-After\u0060 Header Detection (\u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060, \u0060BrowserClient.cs\u0060, \u0060ReactExtensions.cs\u0060, \u0060DataScraper.cs\u0060, \u0060BrowserEventArgs.cs\u0060, \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Updated the userscript in \u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060 to detect HTTP \u0060429\u0060 status codes (via \u0060PerformanceNavigationTiming.responseStatus\u0060 and page heuristics) and read the \u0060Retry-After\u0060 response header (via \u0060GM_xmlhttpRequest\u0060 / \u0060fetch\u0060 headers).\n- Added \u0060RELOAD_PAGE\u0060 action and \u0060ReloadPageAsync\u0060 extension method to retry rate-limited pages.\n- Added \u0060EnsurePageNotRateLimitedAsync\u0060 and \u0060ParseRetryAfter\u0060 in \u0060DataScraper.cs\u0060:\n\n- If \u0060Retry-After\u0060 contains a target HTTP date/time, it reports the retry timestamp to the UI (\u0060OnRateLimitDetected\u0060), waits until that exact date/time is reached, and then reloads/retries the page.\n- If \u0060Retry-After\u0060 contains a timeout in seconds, it updates \u0060definition.PageDelayMs\u0060 (and updates the \u0060Page Delay (ms):\u0060 control in the UI), waits for the timeout to elapse, retries the current page, and uses that new delay before every subsequent page turn.\n\n### How to Test\n\n- Build and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060.\n- Click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script** and update the Tampermonkey script in your browser, then reload the target page.\n- In the **Data Scraper** tab under **Container \u0026 Automation Hooks**, set **Page Delay (ms):** (e.g., \u00601500\u0060) to wait 1.5 seconds before each page turn.\n- Run a paginated scrape. Before each page turn, the status bar and log will show the configured delay. If the site returns HTTP \u0060429\u0060, the log and status bar will display the parsed \u0060Retry-After\u0060 date/time or timeout in seconds, automatically update **Page Delay (ms):** in the UI if a seconds timeout was specified, wait until the retry window elapses, and retry the page.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ScriptGenerator.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    const INSTANCE_ID = getOrCreateInstanceId();\n    const PAGE_LOAD_ID = \u0027page_\u0027 \u002B Date.now() \u002B \u0027_\u0027 \u002B Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 7);\n\n    function waitForDocumentComplete(timeoutMs = 30000) {\n        return new Promise((resolve) =\u003E {\n            const buildState = () =\u003E ({\n                pageLoadId: PAGE_LOAD_ID,\n                url: window.location.href,\n                readyState: document.readyState,\n                title: document.title || \u0027\u0027\n            });\n            if (document.readyState === \u0027complete\u0027) {\n                requestAnimationFrame(() =\u003E resolve(buildState()));\n                return;\n            }\n            let settled = false;\n            const finish = () =\u003E {\n                if (settled) return;\n                settled = true;\n                window.removeEventListener(\u0027load\u0027, finish);\n                document.removeEventListener(\u0027readystatechange\u0027, onReadyState);\n                requestAnimationFrame(() =\u003E resolve(buildState()));\n            };\n            const onReadyState = () =\u003E {\n                if (document.readyState === \u0027complete\u0027) finish();\n            };\n            window.addEventListener(\u0027load\u0027, finish, { once: true });\n            document.addEventListener(\u0027readystatechange\u0027, onReadyState);\n            setTimeout(finish, timeoutMs);\n        });\n    }\u0022);\n==== REPLACE\n    const INSTANCE_ID = getOrCreateInstanceId();\n    const PAGE_LOAD_ID = \u0027page_\u0027 \u002B Date.now() \u002B \u0027_\u0027 \u002B Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 7);\n\n    function parseRetryAfterFromRawHeaders(rawHeaders) {\n        if (!rawHeaders || typeof rawHeaders !== \u0027string\u0027) return null;\n        const lines = rawHeaders.split(/\\r?\\n/);\n        for (const line of lines) {\n            const idx = line.indexOf(\u0027:\u0027);\n            if (idx \u003E 0) {\n                const key = line.substring(0, idx).trim().toLowerCase();\n                const val = line.substring(idx \u002B 1).trim();\n                if (key === \u0027retry-after\u0027 || key === \u0027x-retry-after\u0027 || key === \u0027ratelimit-reset\u0027 || key === \u0027x-ratelimit-reset\u0027) {\n                    return val;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return null;\n    }\n\n    async function probeCurrentPageHeaders() {\n        if (typeof GM_xmlhttpRequest === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            try {\n                const gmRes = await new Promise((resolve) =\u003E {\n                    GM_xmlhttpRequest({\n                        method: \u0027HEAD\u0027,\n                        url: window.location.href,\n                        onload: (res) =\u003E {\n                            const retry = parseRetryAfterFromRawHeaders(res.responseHeaders || \u0027\u0027);\n                            resolve({ status: res.status, retryAfter: retry });\n                        },\n                        onerror: () =\u003E resolve(null),\n                        ontimeout: () =\u003E resolve(null),\n                        timeout: 5000\n                    });\n                });\n                if (gmRes \u0026\u0026 (gmRes.retryAfter || gmRes.status === 429)) {\n                    return gmRes;\n                }\n            } catch (e) {}\n        }\n\n        try {\n            const res = await fetch(window.location.href, {\n                method: \u0027HEAD\u0027,\n                credentials: \u0027same-origin\u0027,\n                cache: \u0027no-store\u0027\n            });\n            let retry = null;\n            if (res.headers \u0026\u0026 typeof res.headers.get === \u0027function\u0027) {\n                retry = res.headers.get(\u0027Retry-After\u0027) ||\n                        res.headers.get(\u0027retry-after\u0027) ||\n                        res.headers.get(\u0027X-Retry-After\u0027) ||\n                        res.headers.get(\u0027RateLimit-Reset\u0027) ||\n                        res.headers.get(\u0027X-RateLimit-Reset\u0027);\n            }\n            return { status: res.status, retryAfter: retry };\n        } catch (e) {}\n\n        return null;\n    }\n\n    async function detectPageHttpStatus() {\n        let statusCode = 200;\n        let retryAfter = null;\n\n        try {\n            const navEntries = performance.getEntriesByType \u0026\u0026 performance.getEntriesByType(\u0027navigation\u0027);\n            if (navEntries \u0026\u0026 navEntries.length \u003E 0 \u0026\u0026 typeof navEntries[0].responseStatus === \u0027number\u0027 \u0026\u0026 navEntries[0].responseStatus \u003E 0) {\n                statusCode = navEntries[0].responseStatus;\n            }\n        } catch (e) {}\n\n        const titleText = (document.title || \u0027\u0027).trim();\n        const bodySample = (document.body \u0026\u0026 document.body.innerText) ? document.body.innerText.substring(0, 2000) : \u0027\u0027;\n        if (