      "UserPrompt": "[Attached Image]\n\nThe root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n[17:36:23.473] [SYS] Loaded project from C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\bin\\Debug\\net10.0-windows\\Saves\\firstProject.json\n[17:36:51.528] [SYS] Starting Automation Server on port 9999...\n[17:36:52.863] [SYS] Client Connected: bot_80696gyx5 via WebSocket\n[17:36:52.903] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=1\n[17:36:55.941] [SCRAPE] --- Starting Scrape: Scrape 1 ---\n[17:36:55.950] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=1\n[17:36:56.258] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=1\n[17:36:56.271] [SCRAPE] Page 1 extracted 50 record(s).\n[17:36:56.273] [SCRAPE] Waiting 10000 ms before moving to page 2...\n[17:37:06.716] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=1\n[17:37:06.984] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=1\n[17:37:07.245] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=1\n[17:37:07.511] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=1\n[17:37:08.757] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=2\n[17:37:08.763] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=2\n[17:37:08.871] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=2\n[17:37:08.981] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=2\n[17:37:08.985] [SCRAPE] Page 2 extracted 50 record(s).\n[17:37:09.010] [SCRAPE] Waiting 10000 ms before moving to page 3...\n[17:37:19.467] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=2\n[17:37:19.750] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=2\n[17:37:20.018] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=2\n[17:37:20.284] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=2\n[17:37:21.667] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=3\n[17:37:21.670] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=3\n[17:37:21.770] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=3\n[17:37:21.882] [NAV \u003C- bot_80696gyx5] Page loaded: https://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=3\n[17:37:21.886] [SCRAPE] Page 3 extracted 50 record(s).\n[17:37:21.888] [SCRAPE] Waiting 10000 ms before moving to page 4...\n[17:37:51.605] [SYS] Client Disconnected: bot_80696gyx5\n[17:38:17.331] [SCRAPE] Completed \u0027Scrape 1\u0027: 150 total record(s) across 3 page(s).\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\nOk so the scraping system works great in this project. However, for this particular site, it keeps rate limiting us. Even when i do a 10 second delay between page switches, it still ends up hitting us with the 429 rate limit. If you notice the logs above, it seems that the page is being loaded many times. I think thats a bug we need to fix and a big part of the reason why im getting rate limited so much on this site. \nThe site is:\nhttps://swappa.com/imei/tac?page=4",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\n### Root Cause \u0026 Changes\n\n- **Fixed Duplicate Link Navigation in \u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060**:\n\n- Previously, \u0060ReactUtils.simulateClick\u0060 invoked \u0060target.click()\u0060 (which natively initiates a browser navigation on \u0060\u003Ca href\u003E\u0060 links) **and then** 25ms later executed \u0060setTimeout(() =\u003E { window.location.href = href; }, 25)\u0060, firing two HTTP \u0060GET\u0060 requests 25ms apart on every page turn and tripping burst rate limiters.\n- Added a controlled \u0060safeNavigate\u0060 helper and a \u0060window\u0060 bubble-phase click interceptor for \u0060\u003Ca href\u003E\u0060 links so each page turn performs **only one** HTTP \u0060GET\u0060 request.\n- **Prevented Empty-Body \u0060HTTP 429\u0060 Responses from Unloading Tampermonkey (\u0060chrome-error://chromewebdata/\u0060)**:\n\n- When sites like \u0060swappa.com\u0060 return \u0060HTTP 429\u0060 with an empty response body on a top-level navigation, Chrome replaces the document with its internal \u0060chrome-error://chromewebdata/\u0060 error page (\u0022This page isn\u0027t working - HTTP ERROR 429\u0022), where Chrome disables Tampermonkey userscripts and drops the WebSocket connection.\n- \u0060safeNavigate\u0060 now performs same-origin navigations and reloads via an in-page \u0060fetch\u0060, keeping the userscript and WebSocket connection alive if \u0060429\u0060 is returned, reading \u0060Retry-After\u0060 headers directly from the response, displaying an in-page status banner, and reporting the \u0060429\u0060 state to \u0060DataScraper\u0060 so it can wait and retry automatically.\n- **Eliminated \u0060Page loaded\u0060 Log Spam \u0026 Redundant Polling (\u0060BrowserClient.cs\u0060, \u0060ReactExtensions.cs\u0060, \u0060DataScraper.cs\u0060, \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- \u0060BrowserClient.HandleEvent\u0060 now only raises \u0060OnPageLoaded\u0060 when \u0060pageLoadId\u0060 changes (or when reporting a \u0060429\u0060 status), preventing \u0060WaitForPageLoadAsync\u0060 from logging duplicate \u0060[NAV] Page loaded\u0060 lines for the same page instance.\n- \u0060WaitForPageTransitionAsync\u0060 now exits immediately if \u0060CurrentPageLoadId\u0060 has already transitioned and no longer spams \u0060WAIT_FOR_PAGE_LOAD\u0060 every 250ms against the unloading page.\n- \u0060BrowserClient.AttachWebSocketAsync\u0060 no longer re-sends navigation/click commands (\u0060REACT_CLICK\u0060, \u0060NAVIGATE\u0060, \u0060RELOAD_PAGE\u0060, \u0060WAIT_FOR_PAGE_LOAD\u0060) across WebSocket reconnections.\n\n### How to Test\n\n- Rebuild and launch **TestBedApp**, then start the server.\n- Click **\u0022Generate \u0026 Copy Script\u0022** and paste the updated script into Tampermonkey (replacing the previous script), then reload the \u0060swappa.com/imei/tac?page=1\u0060 tab so the new userscript is active.\n- Run your multi-page scrape in the **Data Scraper** tab. Observe in **Real-time Logs** that each page loads only once per page transition, and if a \u0060429\u0060 occurs, the browser tab remains connected and automatically waits and retries.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ScriptGenerator.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    const INSTANCE_ID = getOrCreateInstanceId();\n    const PAGE_LOAD_ID = \u0027page_\u0027 \u002B Date.now() \u002B \u0027_\u0027 \u002B Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 7);\n\n    function parseRetryAfterFromRawHeaders(rawHeaders) {\n==== REPLACE\n    const INSTANCE_ID = getOrCreateInstanceId();\n    let PAGE_LOAD_ID = \u0027page_\u0027 \u002B Date.now() \u002B \u0027_\u0027 \u002B Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 7);\n    let currentPageState = null;\n\n    function showRateLimitBanner(url, retryAfter) {\n        try {\n            let banner = document.getElementById(\u0027__baf_ratelimit_banner\u0027);\n            if (!banner) {\n                banner = document.createElement(\u0027div\u0027);\n                banner.id = \u0027__baf_ratelimit_banner\u0027;\n                banner.style.position = \u0027fixed\u0027;\n                banner.style.top = \u00270\u0027;\n                banner.style.left = \u00270\u0027;\n                banner.style.right = \u00270\u0027;\n                banner.style.backgroundColor = \u0027rgba(200, 80, 0, 0.95)\u0027;\n                banner.style.color = \u0027#fff\u0027;\n                banner.style.padding = \u002710px 16px\u0027;\n                banner.style.fontFamily = \u0027Segoe UI, sans-serif\u0027;\n                banner.style.fontSize = \u002714px\u0027;\n                banner.style.fontWeight = \u0027bold\u0027;\n                banner.style.zIndex = \u00272147483647\u0027;\n                banner.style.textAlign = \u0027center\u0027;\n                banner.style.boxShadow = \u00270 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.4)\u0027;\n                (document.documentElement || document.body).appendChild(banner);\n            }\n            const retryMsg = retryAfter ? \u0060 (Retry-After: ${retryAfter})\u0060 : \u0027\u0027;\n            banner.textContent = \u0060[Automation Bridge] HTTP 429 Rate Limit detected on ${url}${retryMsg} \u2014 Keeping session alive and waiting to retry...\u0060;\n        } catch (e) {}\n    }\n\n    function clearRateLimitBanner() {\n        try {\n            const banner = document.getElementById(\u0027__baf_ratelimit_banner\u0027);\n            if (banner) banner.remove();\n        } catch (e) {}\n    }\n\n    function parseRetryAfterFromRawHeaders(rawHeaders) {\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    function waitForDocumentComplete(timeoutMs = 30000) {\n        return new Promise((resolve) =\u003E {\n            const buildStateAsync = async () =\u003E {\n                const httpInfo = await detectPageHttpStatus();\n                return {\n                    pageLoadId: PAGE_LOAD_ID,\n               