    {
      "Id": "ae233d3a",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-27T19:00:32.1386895-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\n\nSo this system works great! Now i want to add a new tab and some features that are aimed at reverse engineering. I want to build a feature into the project that allows me to click a button once its been connected toa  site, and allow mw to dump all the html of the site, alll the css, and any javascript that\u0027s loaded. Now i want there to be 4 buttons, one for each operation and one to dump everything. \nMake sure that these new features are built ionto the api and the UI side is just a wrapper around the new APIs we will be adding.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\n### Overview of Changes\n1. **Reverse Engineering Models (\u0060SiteResourceItem\u0060, \u0060SiteDumpOptions\u0060, \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060, \u0060SiteDumpEventArgs\u0060)**:\n   - Added \u0060SiteResourceType\u0060 (\u0060Html\u0060, \u0060Css\u0060, \u0060JavaScript\u0060) and \u0060SiteDumpType\u0060 (\u0060Html\u0060, \u0060Css\u0060, \u0060JavaScript\u0060, \u0060All\u0060) enums.\n   - Added \u0060SiteResourceItem\u0060 to represent individual dumped assets (document HTML, iframes, external/inline/constructed CSS stylesheets, and external/inline/dynamic JS scripts) with helper methods to format metadata and save individual files (\u0060SaveToFile\u0060 / \u0060SaveToFileAsync\u0060).\n   - Added \u0060SiteDumpOptions\u0060 to configure what asset types and sources are included during a dump.\n   - Added \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060 with methods to retrieve combined HTML/CSS/JS sources (\u0060GetCombinedHtml\u0060, \u0060GetCombinedCss\u0060, \u0060GetCombinedJavaScript\u0060, \u0060GetCombinedContent\u0060), serialize to JSON (\u0060ToJson\u0060), save combined output (\u0060SaveCombinedToFile\u0060), and export structured site dumps (\u0060index.html\u0060, \u0060css/\u0060, \u0060js/\u0060, \u0060manifest.json\u0060) to a directory (\u0060SaveToDirectory\u0060 / \u0060SaveToDirectoryAsync\u0060).\n2. **Reverse Engineering Engine \u0026 \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 API (\u0060SiteDumper\u0060, \u0060ReactExtensions\u0060, \u0060AutomationRunner\u0060)**:\n   - Added \u0060SiteDumper\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.ReverseEngineering\u0060 with \u0060DumpHtmlAsync\u0060, \u0060DumpCssAsync\u0060, \u0060DumpJavaScriptAsync\u0060, \u0060DumpAllAsync\u0060, and \u0060DumpSiteAsync\u0060, plus lifecycle events (\u0060OnDumpStarted\u0060, \u0060OnDumpCompleted\u0060, \u0060OnDumpFailed\u0060).\n   - Added \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 extension methods (\u0060DumpHtmlAsync\u0060, \u0060DumpCssAsync\u0060, \u0060DumpJavaScriptAsync\u0060, \u0060DumpAllAsync\u0060, \u0060DumpSiteAsync\u0060) in \u0060ReactExtensions\u0060.\n   - Added \u0060AutomationActionType.DumpSite\u0060 support to \u0060AutomationRunner\u0060.\n3. **Userscript Reverse Engineering Actions (\u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060)**:\n   - Added \u0060ReverseEngineeringUtils\u0060 and registered \u0060DUMP_HTML\u0060, \u0060DUMP_CSS\u0060, \u0060DUMP_JS\u0060, and \u0060DUMP_SITE\u0060 commands in the generated Tampermonkey script.\n   - Uses \u0060GM_xmlhttpRequest\u0060 (with \u0060fetch\u0060 and CSSOM \u0060cssRules\u0060 fallbacks) to retrieve cross-origin external stylesheets and scripts, inline \u0060\u003Cstyle\u003E\u0060 and \u0060\u003Cscript\u003E\u0060 blocks, constructed stylesheets, and dynamically loaded scripts from \u0060performance.getEntriesByType(\u0027resource\u0027)\u0060, while stripping framework highlight overlays from the dumped HTML.\n4. **TestBedApp UI (\u0060MainForm\u0060, \u0060MainForm.Designer\u0060)**:\n   - Added a **Reverse Engineering** tab to \u0060MainForm\u0060 featuring the 4 dump buttons (**Dump HTML**, **Dump CSS**, **Dump JavaScript**, **Dump Everything**), resource filter \u0026 options checkboxes, a resource inspector list, individual and combined source viewers, and file/folder export buttons that wrap the new API methods.\n\n### How to Test\n1. Build and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060.\n2. Click **Start Server**, then click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script** and install/update the Tampermonkey userscript in your browser.\n3. Open any website in the browser and verify the client appears in **Connected Clients**.\n4. Open the **Reverse Engineering** tab and test the 4 buttons:\n   - **Dump HTML**: Extracts and displays the full page HTML (and any accessible iframe HTML).\n   - **Dump CSS**: Extracts all external \u0060\u003Clink rel=\u0022stylesheet\u0022\u003E\u0060, inline \u0060\u003Cstyle\u003E\u0060, and constructed CSSOM stylesheets.\n   - **Dump JavaScript**: Extracts all external \u0060\u003Cscript src\u003E\u0060, inline \u0060\u003Cscript\u003E\u0060, and dynamically loaded JS resources.\n   - **Dump Everything**: Extracts all HTML, CSS, and JavaScript in a single operation.\n5. Select individual assets on the left to inspect their source code and metadata, switch between the combined HTML/CSS/JS tabs, or click **Save Dump to Folder...** to write the full structured site dump to disk.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\SiteResourceItem.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.IO;\nusing System.Text;\nusing System.Text.Json.Serialization;\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    public enum SiteResourceType\n    {\n        Html,\n        Css,\n        JavaScript\n    }\n\n    public enum SiteDumpType\n    {\n        Html,\n        Css,\n        JavaScript,\n        All\n    }\n\n    public class SiteResourceItem\n    {\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022name\u0022)]\n        public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022category\u0022)]\n        public SiteResourceType Category { get; set; } = SiteResourceType.Html;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022sourceType\u0022)]\n        public string SourceType { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022url\u0022)]\n        public string Url { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022content\u0022)]\n        public string Content { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022sizeBytes\u0022)]\n        public long SizeBytes { get; set; }\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022index\u0022)]\n        public int Index { get; set; }\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022error\u0022)]\n        public string? Error { get; set; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a human-readable size string (e.g., \u002214.2 KB\u0022).\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetFormattedSize()\n        {\n            long bytes = SizeBytes \u003E 0 ? SizeBytes : Encoding.UTF8.GetByteCount(Content ?? string.Empty);\n            if (bytes \u003C 1024)\n                return $\u0022{bytes} B\u0022;\n            if (bytes \u003C 1024 * 1024)\n                return $\u0022{bytes / 1024.0:0.1} KB\u0022;\n            return $\u0022{bytes / (1024.0 * 1024.0):0.2} MB\u0022;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a multi-line summary of this resource\u0027s metadata.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetFormattedDetails()\n        {\n            var sb = new StringBuilder();\n            sb.AppendLine($\u0022Name:        {Name}\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine($\u0022Category:    {Category}\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine($\u0022Source Type: {SourceType}\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine($\u0022Size:        {GetFormattedSize()} ({SizeBytes:N0} bytes)\u0022);\n            sb.AppendLine($\u0022URL:         {Url}\u0022);\n            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Error))\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine($\u0022Error:       {Error}\u0022);\n            }\n            return sb.ToString();\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Saves this resource\u0027s content to the specified file path.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void SaveToFile(string filePath)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(filePath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022File path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(filePath));\n\n            string? dir = Path.GetDirectoryName(filePath);\n            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(dir))\n            {\n                Directory.CreateDirectory(dir);\n            }\n\n            File.WriteAllText(filePath, Content ?? string.Empty, Encoding.UTF8);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Asynchronously saves this resource\u0027s content to the specified file path.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task SaveToFileAsync(string filePath, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(filePath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022File path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(filePath));\n\n            string? dir = Path.GetDirectoryName(filePath);\n            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(dir))\n            {\n                Directory.CreateDirectory(dir);\n            }\n\n            return File.WriteAllTextAsync(filePath, Content ?? string.Empty, Encoding.UTF8, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        public override string ToString()\n        {\n            string tag = Category switch\n            {\n                SiteResourceType.Html =\u003E \u0022HTML\u0022,\n                SiteResourceType.Css =\u003E \u0022CSS\u0022,\n                SiteResourceType.JavaScript =\u003E \u0022JS\u0022,\n                _ =\u003E Category.ToString().ToUpperInvariant()\n            };\n\n            string errSuffix = !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Error) ? \u0022 [!]\u0022 : string.Empty;\n            return $\u0022[{tag} | {SourceType}] {Name} ({GetFormattedSize()}){errSuffix}\u0022;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\SiteDumpOptions.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System.Text.Json.Serialization;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Configuration options controlling which page resources are extracted during a reverse-engineering site dump.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class SiteDumpOptions\n    {\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022includeHtml\u0022)]\n        public bool IncludeHtml { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022includeCss\u0022)]\n        public bool IncludeCss { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022includeJavaScript\u0022)]\n        public bool IncludeJavaScript { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022includeInlineCss\u0022)]\n        public bool IncludeInlineCss { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022includeExternalCss\u0022)]\n        public bool IncludeExternalCss { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022includeConstructedCss\u0022)]\n        public bool IncludeConstructedCss { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022includeInlineScripts\u0022)]\n        public bool IncludeInlineScripts { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022includeExternalScripts\u0022)]\n        public bool IncludeExternalScripts { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022includePerformanceResourceScripts\u0022)]\n        public bool IncludePerformanceResourceScripts { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022includeIframes\u0022)]\n        public bool IncludeIframes { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022fetchTimeoutMs\u0022)]\n        public int FetchTimeoutMs { get; set; } = 15000;\n\n        public SiteDumpOptions Clone()\n        {\n            return new SiteDumpOptions\n            {\n                IncludeHtml = IncludeHtml,\n                IncludeCss = IncludeCss,\n                IncludeJavaScript = IncludeJavaScript,\n                IncludeInlineCss = IncludeInlineCss,\n                IncludeExternalCss = IncludeExternalCss,\n                IncludeConstructedCss = IncludeConstructedCss,\n                IncludeInlineScripts = IncludeInlineScripts,\n                IncludeExternalScripts = IncludeExternalScripts,\n                IncludePerformanceResourceScripts = IncludePerformanceResourceScripts,\n                IncludeIframes = IncludeIframes,\n                FetchTimeoutMs = FetchTimeoutMs\n            };\n        }\n\n        public static SiteDumpOptions ForType(SiteDumpType dumpType, SiteDumpOptions? baseOptions = null)\n        {\n            var opts = baseOptions?.Clone() ?? new SiteDumpOptions();\n            opts.IncludeHtml = dumpType == SiteDumpType.Html || dumpType == SiteDumpType.All;\n            opts.IncludeCss = dumpType == SiteDumpType.Css || dumpType == SiteDumpType.All;\n            opts.IncludeJavaScript = dumpType == SiteDumpType.JavaScript || dumpType == SiteDumpType.All;\n            return opts;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\SiteDumpResult.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.IO;\nusing System.Linq;\nusing System.Text;\nusing System.Text.Json;\nusing System.Text.Json.Serialization;\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Contains all extracted HTML, CSS, and JavaScript assets from a reverse-engineering site dump operation,\n    /// along with helper methods for combining, serializing, and exporting the dumped files to disk.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class SiteDumpResult\n    {\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022dumpType\u0022)]\n        public SiteDumpType DumpType { get; set; } = SiteDumpType.All;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022pageUrl\u0022)]\n        public string PageUrl { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022pageTitle\u0022)]\n        public string PageTitle { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022timestampUtc\u0022)]\n        public DateTime TimestampUtc { get; set; } = DateTime.UtcNow;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022success\u0022)]\n        public bool Success { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022errorMessage\u0022)]\n        public string? ErrorMessage { get; set; }\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022html\u0022)]\n        public string Html { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022htmlResources\u0022)]\n        public List\u003CSiteResourceItem\u003E HtmlResources { get; set; } = new();\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022cssResources\u0022)]\n        public List\u003CSiteResourceItem\u003E CssResources { get; set; } = new();\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022javascriptResources\u0022)]\n        public List\u003CSiteResourceItem\u003E JavaScriptResources { get; set; } = new();\n\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public int TotalResourceCount =\u003E HtmlResources.Count \u002B CssResources.Count \u002B JavaScriptResources.Count;\n\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public long TotalSizeBytes =\u003E GetAllResources().Sum(r =\u003E r.SizeBytes \u003E 0 ? r.SizeBytes : Encoding.UTF8.GetByteCount(r.Content ?? string.Empty));\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a flat read-only list of all dumped HTML, CSS, and JavaScript resource items.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public IReadOnlyList\u003CSiteResourceItem\u003E GetAllResources()\n        {\n            var all = new List\u003CSiteResourceItem\u003E(TotalResourceCount);\n            all.AddRange(HtmlResources);\n            all.AddRange(CssResources);\n            all.AddRange(JavaScriptResources);\n            return all;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a human-readable total size string (e.g. \u0022512.4 KB\u0022).\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetFormattedTotalSize()\n        {\n            long bytes = TotalSizeBytes;\n            if (bytes \u003C 1024)\n                return $\u0022{bytes} B\u0022;\n            if (bytes \u003C 1024 * 1024)\n                return $\u0022{bytes / 1024.0:0.1} KB\u0022;\n            return $\u0022{bytes / (1024.0 * 1024.0):0.2} MB\u0022;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns the combined HTML source across the main document and any captured iframes.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetCombinedHtml()\n        {\n            if (HtmlResources.Count \u003C= 1)\n                return !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Html) ? Html : (HtmlResources.FirstOrDefault()?.Content ?? string.Empty);\n\n            var sb = new StringBuilder();\n            foreach (var item in HtmlResources)\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine($\u0022\u003C!-- ======================================================================\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine($\u0022     HTML Resource #{item.Index}: {item.Name} ({item.SourceType})\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine($\u0022     URL: {item.Url}\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine($\u0022     ====================================================================== --\u003E\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine(item.Content);\n                sb.AppendLine();\n            }\n            return sb.ToString();\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns all dumped CSS stylesheets concatenated into a single stylesheet with source headers.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetCombinedCss()\n        {\n            if (CssResources.Count == 0)\n                return string.Empty;\n\n            var sb = new StringBuilder();\n            foreach (var item in CssResources)\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine(\u0022/* ======================================================================\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine($\u0022   CSS Resource #{item.Index}: {item.Name} ({item.SourceType})\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine($\u0022   URL: {item.Url}\u0022);\n                if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(item.Error))\n                {\n                    sb.AppendLine($\u0022   Error: {item.Error}\u0022);\n                }\n                sb.AppendLine(\u0022   ====================================================================== */\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine(item.Content);\n                sb.AppendLine();\n            }\n            return sb.ToString();\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns all dumped JavaScript resources concatenated into a single script with source headers.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetCombinedJavaScript()\n        {\n            if (JavaScriptResources.Count == 0)\n                return string.Empty;\n\n            var sb = new StringBuilder();\n            foreach (var item in JavaScriptResources)\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine(\u0022// ======================================================================\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine($\u0022// JS Resource #{item.Index}: {item.Name} ({item.SourceType})\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine($\u0022// URL: {item.Url}\u0022);\n                if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(item.Error))\n                {\n                    sb.AppendLine($\u0022// Error: {item.Error}\u0022);\n                }\n                sb.AppendLine(\u0022// ======================================================================\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine(item.Content);\n                sb.AppendLine();\n            }\n            return sb.ToString();\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns the combined text output corresponding to \u003Csee cref=\u0022DumpType\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetCombinedContent()\n        {\n            return DumpType switch\n            {\n                SiteDumpType.Html =\u003E GetCombinedHtml(),\n                SiteDumpType.Css =\u003E GetCombinedCss(),\n                SiteDumpType.JavaScript =\u003E GetCombinedJavaScript(),\n                _ =\u003E BuildFullCombinedSummary()\n            };\n        }\n\n        private string BuildFullCombinedSummary()\n        {\n            var sb = new StringBuilder();\n            if (HtmlResources.Count \u003E 0 || !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Html))\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine(\u0022/* ==================== DUMPED HTML ==================== */\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine(GetCombinedHtml());\n                sb.AppendLine();\n            }\n            if (CssResources.Count \u003E 0)\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine(\u0022/* ==================== DUMPED CSS ==================== */\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine(GetCombinedCss());\n                sb.AppendLine();\n            }\n            if (JavaScriptResources.Count \u003E 0)\n            {\n                sb.AppendLine(\u0022/* ==================== DUMPED JAVASCRIPT ==================== */\u0022);\n                sb.AppendLine(GetCombinedJavaScript());\n            }\n            return sb.ToString();\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Serializes the entire \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpResult\u0022/\u003E to JSON.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string ToJson(bool writeIndented = true)\n        {\n            return JsonSerializer.Serialize(this, new JsonSerializerOptions { WriteIndented = writeIndented });\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Saves the combined dump output to a single file.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void SaveCombinedToFile(string filePath)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(filePath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022File path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(filePath));\n\n            string? dir = Path.GetDirectoryName(filePath);\n            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(dir))\n            {\n                Directory.CreateDirectory(dir);\n            }\n\n            File.WriteAllText(filePath, GetCombinedContent(), Encoding.UTF8);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Asynchronously saves the combined dump output to a single file.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task SaveCombinedToFileAsync(string filePath, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(filePath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022File path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(filePath));\n\n            string? dir = Path.GetDirectoryName(filePath);\n            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(dir))\n            {\n                Directory.CreateDirectory(dir);\n            }\n\n            return File.WriteAllTextAsync(filePath, GetCombinedContent(), Encoding.UTF8, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Writes all dumped HTML, CSS, and JavaScript resources as individual files and combined bundles into \u003Cparamref name=\u0022directoryPath\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string SaveToDirectory(string directoryPath, bool includeCombinedFiles = true, bool includeManifest = true)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(directoryPath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022Directory path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(directoryPath));\n\n            Directory.CreateDirectory(directoryPath);\n\n            // 1. Save HTML\n            if (HtmlResources.Count \u003E 0 || !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Html))\n            {\n                string mainHtml = !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Html) ? Html : (HtmlResources[0].Content ?? string.Empty);\n                File.WriteAllText(Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022index.html\u0022), mainHtml, Encoding.UTF8);\n\n                if (HtmlResources.Count \u003E 1)\n                {\n                    string htmlDir = Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022html\u0022);\n                    Directory.CreateDirectory(htmlDir);\n                    var usedNames = new HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\n                    foreach (var item in HtmlResources)\n                    {\n                        string fileName = EnsureUniqueFileName(SanitizeFileName(item.Name, $\u0022document-{item.Index}.html\u0022), usedNames);\n                        File.WriteAllText(Path.Combine(htmlDir, fileName), item.Content ?? string.Empty, Encoding.UTF8);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            // 2. Save CSS\n            if (CssResources.Count \u003E 0)\n            {\n                string cssDir = Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022css\u0022);\n                Directory.CreateDirectory(cssDir);\n                var usedNames = new HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\n\n                foreach (var item in CssResources)\n                {\n                    string fileName = EnsureUniqueFileName(SanitizeFileName(item.Name, $\u0022style-{item.Index}.css\u0022), usedNames);\n                    File.WriteAllText(Path.Combine(cssDir, fileName), item.Content ?? string.Empty, Encoding.UTF8);\n                }\n\n                if (includeCombinedFiles)\n                {\n                    File.WriteAllText(Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022combined.css\u0022), GetCombinedCss(), Encoding.UTF8);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // 3. Save JavaScript\n            if (JavaScriptResources.Count \u003E 0)\n            {\n                string jsDir = Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022js\u0022);\n                Directory.CreateDirectory(jsDir);\n                var usedNames = new HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\n\n                foreach (var item in JavaScriptResources)\n                {\n                    string fileName = EnsureUniqueFileName(SanitizeFileName(item.Name, $\u0022script-{item.Index}.js\u0022), usedNames);\n                    File.WriteAllText(Path.Combine(jsDir, fileName), item.Content ?? string.Empty, Encoding.UTF8);\n                }\n\n                if (includeCombinedFiles)\n                {\n                    File.WriteAllText(Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022combined.js\u0022), GetCombinedJavaScript(), Encoding.UTF8);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // 4. Save Manifest\n            if (includeManifest)\n            {\n                var manifest = new\n                {\n                    dumpType = DumpType.ToString(),\n                    pageUrl = PageUrl,\n                    pageTitle = PageTitle,\n                    timestampUtc = TimestampUtc,\n                    totalResources = TotalResourceCount,\n                    totalSizeBytes = TotalSizeBytes,\n                    resources = GetAllResources().Select(r =\u003E new\n                    {\n                        r.Index,\n                        r.Name,\n                        Category = r.Category.ToString(),\n                        r.SourceType,\n                        r.Url,\n                        r.SizeBytes,\n                        r.Error\n                    }).ToList()\n                };\n\n                string manifestJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(manifest, new JsonSerializerOptions { WriteIndented = true });\n                File.WriteAllText(Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022manifest.json\u0022), manifestJson, Encoding.UTF8);\n            }\n\n            return directoryPath;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Asynchronously writes all dumped HTML, CSS, and JavaScript resources into \u003Cparamref name=\u0022directoryPath\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task\u003Cstring\u003E SaveToDirectoryAsync(\n            string directoryPath,\n            bool includeCombinedFiles = true,\n            bool includeManifest = true,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(directoryPath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022Directory path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(directoryPath));\n\n            Directory.CreateDirectory(directoryPath);\n\n            if (HtmlResources.Count \u003E 0 || !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Html))\n            {\n                string mainHtml = !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Html) ? Html : (HtmlResources[0].Content ?? string.Empty);\n                await File.WriteAllTextAsync(Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022index.html\u0022), mainHtml, Encoding.UTF8, cancellationToken);\n\n                if (HtmlResources.Count \u003E 1)\n                {\n                    string htmlDir = Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022html\u0022);\n                    Directory.CreateDirectory(htmlDir);\n                    var usedNames = new HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\n                    foreach (var item in HtmlResources)\n                    {\n                        string fileName = EnsureUniqueFileName(SanitizeFileName(item.Name, $\u0022document-{item.Index}.html\u0022), usedNames);\n                        await File.WriteAllTextAsync(Path.Combine(htmlDir, fileName), item.Content ?? string.Empty, Encoding.UTF8, cancellationToken);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (CssResources.Count \u003E 0)\n            {\n                string cssDir = Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022css\u0022);\n                Directory.CreateDirectory(cssDir);\n                var usedNames = new HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\n\n                foreach (var item in CssResources)\n                {\n                    string fileName = EnsureUniqueFileName(SanitizeFileName(item.Name, $\u0022style-{item.Index}.css\u0022), usedNames);\n                    await File.WriteAllTextAsync(Path.Combine(cssDir, fileName), item.Content ?? string.Empty, Encoding.UTF8, cancellationToken);\n                }\n\n                if (includeCombinedFiles)\n                {\n                    await File.WriteAllTextAsync(Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022combined.css\u0022), GetCombinedCss(), Encoding.UTF8, cancellationToken);\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (JavaScriptResources.Count \u003E 0)\n            {\n                string jsDir = Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022js\u0022);\n                Directory.CreateDirectory(jsDir);\n                var usedNames = new HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\n\n                foreach (var item in JavaScriptResources)\n                {\n                    string fileName = EnsureUniqueFileName(SanitizeFileName(item.Name, $\u0022script-{item.Index}.js\u0022), usedNames);\n                    await File.WriteAllTextAsync(Path.Combine(jsDir, fileName), item.Content ?? string.Empty, Encoding.UTF8, cancellationToken);\n                }\n\n                if (includeCombinedFiles)\n                {\n                    await File.WriteAllTextAsync(Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022combined.js\u0022), GetCombinedJavaScript(), Encoding.UTF8, cancellationToken);\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (includeManifest)\n            {\n                var manifest = new\n                {\n                    dumpType = DumpType.ToString(),\n                    pageUrl = PageUrl,\n                    pageTitle = PageTitle,\n                    timestampUtc = TimestampUtc,\n                    totalResources = TotalResourceCount,\n                    totalSizeBytes = TotalSizeBytes,\n                    resources = GetAllResources().Select(r =\u003E new\n                    {\n                        r.Index,\n                        r.Name,\n                        Category = r.Category.ToString(),\n                        r.SourceType,\n                        r.Url,\n                        r.SizeBytes,\n                        r.Error\n                    }).ToList()\n                };\n\n                string manifestJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(manifest, new JsonSerializerOptions { WriteIndented = true });\n                await File.WriteAllTextAsync(Path.Combine(directoryPath, \u0022manifest.json\u0022), manifestJson, Encoding.UTF8, cancellationToken);\n            }\n\n            return directoryPath;\n        }\n\n        private static string SanitizeFileName(string? rawName, string fallback)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(rawName))\n                return fallback;\n\n            var invalidChars = Path.GetInvalidFileNameChars();\n            var sb = new StringBuilder(rawName.Length);\n            foreach (char c in rawName.Trim())\n            {\n                sb.Append(Array.IndexOf(invalidChars, c) \u003E= 0 ? \u0027_\u0027 : c);\n            }\n\n            string cleaned = sb.ToString().Trim(\u0027.\u0027);\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(cleaned))\n                return fallback;\n\n            if (cleaned.Length \u003E 100)\n            {\n                string ext = Path.GetExtension(cleaned);\n                string baseName = Path.GetFileNameWithoutExtension(cleaned);\n                cleaned = baseName.Substring(0, Math.Min(baseName.Length, 85)) \u002B ext;\n            }\n\n            return cleaned;\n        }\n\n        private static string EnsureUniqueFileName(string candidate, HashSet\u003Cstring\u003E usedNames)\n        {\n            if (usedNames.Add(candidate))\n                return candidate;\n\n            string ext = Path.GetExtension(candidate);\n            string baseName = Path.GetFileNameWithoutExtension(candidate);\n            int counter = 2;\n            while (true)\n            {\n                string numbered = $\u0022{baseName}_{counter}{ext}\u0022;\n                if (usedNames.Add(numbered))\n                    return numbered;\n                counter\u002B\u002B;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\ReverseEngineering\\SiteDumper.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.Text;\nusing System.Text.Json;\nusing System.Threading;\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Models;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Server;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.ReverseEngineering\n{\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// High-level reverse engineering engine for dumping all loaded HTML, CSS stylesheets, and JavaScript assets from a connected browser tab.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class SiteDumper\n    {\n        public event EventHandler\u003CSiteDumpEventArgs\u003E? OnDumpStarted;\n        public event EventHandler\u003CSiteDumpEventArgs\u003E? OnDumpCompleted;\n        public event EventHandler\u003CSiteDumpEventArgs\u003E? OnDumpFailed;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Dumps all HTML from the currently loaded site.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task\u003CSiteDumpResult\u003E DumpHtmlAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            SiteDumpOptions? options = null,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return DumpSiteAsync(client, SiteDumpType.Html, options, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Dumps all external, inline, and constructed CSS stylesheets from the currently loaded site.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task\u003CSiteDumpResult\u003E DumpCssAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            SiteDumpOptions? options = null,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return DumpSiteAsync(client, SiteDumpType.Css, options, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Dumps all external, inline, and dynamically loaded JavaScript files from the currently loaded site.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task\u003CSiteDumpResult\u003E DumpJavaScriptAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            SiteDumpOptions? options = null,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return DumpSiteAsync(client, SiteDumpType.JavaScript, options, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Dumps all HTML, CSS, and JavaScript from the currently loaded site in a single operation.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task\u003CSiteDumpResult\u003E DumpAllAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            SiteDumpOptions? options = null,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            return DumpSiteAsync(client, SiteDumpType.All, options, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Executes a site dump of the specified \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpType\u0022/\u003E against the target \u003Csee cref=\u0022BrowserClient\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task\u003CSiteDumpResult\u003E DumpSiteAsync(\n            BrowserClient client,\n            SiteDumpType dumpType,\n            SiteDumpOptions? options = null,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (client == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(client));\n\n            var resolvedOptions = SiteDumpOptions.ForType(dumpType, options);\n            string commandName = dumpType switch\n            {\n                SiteDumpType.Html =\u003E \u0022DUMP_HTML\u0022,\n                SiteDumpType.Css =\u003E \u0022DUMP_CSS\u0022,\n                SiteDumpType.JavaScript =\u003E \u0022DUMP_JS\u0022,\n                _ =\u003E \u0022DUMP_SITE\u0022\n            };\n\n            OnDumpStarted?.Invoke(this, new SiteDumpEventArgs(dumpType));\n\n            try\n            {\n                var cmdResult = await client.SendCommandAsync(commandName, resolvedOptions, cancellationToken);\n                var dumpResult = ParseSiteDumpOutput(cmdResult.Output, dumpType, client.CurrentUrl);\n                dumpResult.Success = cmdResult.Status == \u0022completed\u0022;\n\n                OnDumpCompleted?.Invoke(this, new SiteDumpEventArgs(dumpType, dumpResult));\n                return dumpResult;\n            }\n            catch (Exception ex)\n            {\n                var failedResult = new SiteDumpResult\n                {\n                    DumpType = dumpType,\n                    PageUrl = client.CurrentUrl ?? string.Empty,\n                    TimestampUtc = DateTime.UtcNow,\n                    Success = false,\n                    ErrorMessage = ex.Message\n                };\n                OnDumpFailed?.Invoke(this, new SiteDumpEventArgs(dumpType, failedResult, ex));\n                throw;\n            }\n        }\n\n        internal static SiteDumpResult ParseSiteDumpOutput(string? rawOutput, SiteDumpType dumpType, string? fallbackUrl)\n        {\n            var result = new SiteDumpResult\n            {\n                DumpType = dumpType,\n                PageUrl = fallbackUrl ?? string.Empty,\n                TimestampUtc = DateTime.UtcNow,\n                Success = true\n            };\n\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(rawOutput))\n                return result;\n\n            try\n            {\n                using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(rawOutput);\n                var root = doc.RootElement;\n                if (root.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.Object)\n                    return result;\n\n                if (root.TryGetProperty(\u0022pageUrl\u0022, out var urlProp) \u0026\u0026 urlProp.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.String)\n                {\n                    result.PageUrl = urlProp.GetString() ?? result.PageUrl;\n                }\n\n                if (root.TryGetProperty(\u0022pageTitle\u0022, out var titleProp) \u0026\u0026 titleProp.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.String)\n                {\n                    result.PageTitle = titleProp.GetString() ?? string.Empty;\n                }\n\n                if (root.TryGetProperty(\u0022html\u0022, out var htmlProp) \u0026\u0026 htmlProp.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.String)\n                {\n                    result.Html = htmlProp.GetString() ?? string.Empty;\n                }\n\n                if (root.TryGetProperty(\u0022htmlResources\u0022, out var htmlArr) \u0026\u0026 htmlArr.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Array)\n                {\n                    result.HtmlResources = ParseResourceList(htmlArr, SiteResourceType.Html);\n                }\n\n                if (root.TryGetProperty(\u0022cssResources\u0022, out var cssArr) \u0026\u0026 cssArr.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Array)\n                {\n                    result.CssResources = ParseResourceList(cssArr, SiteResourceType.Css);\n                }\n\n                if (root.TryGetProperty(\u0022javascriptResources\u0022, out var jsArr) \u0026\u0026 jsArr.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.Array)\n                {\n                    result.JavaScriptResources = ParseResourceList(jsArr, SiteResourceType.JavaScript);\n                }\n\n                if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(result.Html) \u0026\u0026 result.HtmlResources.Count \u003E 0)\n                {\n                    result.Html = result.HtmlResources[0].Content;\n                }\n            }\n            catch\n            {\n                // Fallback if a custom script returned plain HTML string\n                if (dumpType == SiteDumpType.Html)\n                {\n                    result.Html = rawOutput;\n                    result.HtmlResources.Add(new SiteResourceItem\n                    {\n                        Index = 1,\n                        Name = \u0022document.html\u0022,\n                        Category = SiteResourceType.Html,\n                        SourceType = \u0022Document\u0022,\n                        Url = result.PageUrl,\n                        Content = rawOutput,\n                        SizeBytes = Encoding.UTF8.GetByteCount(rawOutput)\n                    });\n                }\n            }\n\n            return result;\n        }\n\n        private static List\u003CSiteResourceItem\u003E ParseResourceList(JsonElement arrayElement, SiteResourceType defaultCategory)\n        {\n            var list = new List\u003CSiteResourceItem\u003E();\n            int idx = 1;\n\n            foreach (var elem in arrayElement.EnumerateArray())\n            {\n                if (elem.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.Object)\n                    continue;\n\n                string content = elem.TryGetProperty(\u0022content\u0022, out var contentProp) \u0026\u0026 contentProp.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.String\n                    ? (contentProp.GetString() ?? string.Empty)\n                    : string.Empty;\n\n                long sizeBytes = elem.TryGetProperty(\u0022sizeBytes\u0022, out var sizeProp) \u0026\u0026 sizeProp.TryGetInt64(out long parsedSize)\n                    ? parsedSize\n                    : Encoding.UTF8.GetByteCount(content);\n\n                int itemIndex = elem.TryGetProperty(\u0022index\u0022, out var idxProp) \u0026\u0026 idxProp.TryGetInt32(out int parsedIdx)\n                    ? parsedIdx\n                    : idx;\n\n                var category = defaultCategory;\n                if (elem.TryGetProperty(\u0022category\u0022, out var catProp) \u0026\u0026 catProp.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.String)\n                {\n                    if (Enum.TryParse\u003CSiteResourceType\u003E(catProp.GetString(), true, out var parsedCat))\n                    {\n                        category = parsedCat;\n                    }\n                }\n\n                var item = new SiteResourceItem\n                {\n                    Index = itemIndex,\n                    Name = elem.TryGetProperty(\u0022name\u0022, out var nameProp) \u0026\u0026 nameProp.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.String\n                        ? (nameProp.GetString() ?? $\u0022resource-{itemIndex}\u0022)\n                        : $\u0022resource-{itemIndex}\u0022,\n                    Category = category,\n                    SourceType = elem.TryGetProperty(\u0022sourceType\u0022, out var stProp) \u0026\u0026 stProp.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.String\n                        ? (stProp.GetString() ?? \u0022External\u0022)\n                        : \u0022External\u0022,\n                    Url = elem.TryGetProperty(\u0022url\u0022, out var urlProp) \u0026\u0026 urlProp.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.String\n                        ? (urlProp.GetString() ?? string.Empty)\n                        : string.Empty,\n                    Content = content,\n                    SizeBytes = sizeBytes,\n                    Error = elem.TryGetProperty(\u0022error\u0022, out var errProp) \u0026\u0026 errProp.ValueKind == JsonValueKind.String\n                        ? errProp.GetString()\n                        : null\n                };\n\n                list.Add(item);\n                idx\u002B\u002B;\n            }\n\n            return list;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\BrowserEventArgs.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    public class ScrapePageEventArgs : EventArgs\n    {\n        public ScrapeDefinition Definition { get; }\n        public int PageNumber { get; }\n        public System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList\u003CSystem.Collections.Generic.Dictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E PageRecords { get; }\n\n        public ScrapePageEventArgs(\n            ScrapeDefinition definition,\n            int pageNumber,\n            System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList\u003CSystem.Collections.Generic.Dictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E pageRecords)\n        {\n            Definition = definition;\n            PageNumber = pageNumber;\n            PageRecords = pageRecords;\n        }\n    }\n}\n==== REPLACE\n    public class ScrapePageEventArgs : EventArgs\n    {\n        public ScrapeDefinition Definition { get; }\n        public int PageNumber { get; }\n        public System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList\u003CSystem.Collections.Generic.Dictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E PageRecords { get; }\n\n        public ScrapePageEventArgs(\n            ScrapeDefinition definition,\n            int pageNumber,\n            System.C