      "Timestamp": "2026-10-27T19:48:25.4097995-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\nPLease study this project. I want to see if we can build a chrome extension that will function as an easier way to hjookup the program to a given website. Id like to be able to make the extension so that it will see every single tab thats open and report back to the system what tabs are open. Once you select a tab to start working with, it will inject the script into that tab and then allow for full interaction. But we should be able to easily switch to a different tab as well. \n\nThis will make it muich easier to hook up the system to a webpage, instead oif having to target the url via the url matching and then paste the script into tamper monkey. But keep in mind, I want to still retain the legacy system thats powered by tamper monkey.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\n### Overview of Changes\n\n- **Chrome Extension (Manifest V3) \u0026 Generator (\u0060ChromeExtensionGenerator\u0060, \u0060ChromeExtension\\\u0060)**:\n\n- Added a complete Manifest V3 Chrome Extension (\u0060manifest.json\u0060, \u0060background.js\u0060, \u0060content_relay.js\u0060, \u0060bridge.js\u0060, \u0060popup.html\u0060, \u0060popup.js\u0060) in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\ChromeExtension\\\u0060 along with \u0060ChromeExtensionGenerator\u0060 to programmatically generate/export the extension pre-configured with the server\u0027s port and IPC mode.\n- **Real-Time Tab Discovery**: \u0060background.js\u0060 monitors all open Chrome tabs across windows (\u0060chrome.tabs.query\u0060, \u0060onCreated\u0060, \u0060onUpdated\u0060, \u0060onRemoved\u0060, \u0060onActivated\u0060) and streams the live list of \u0060BrowserTabInfo\u0060 items to \u0060AutomationServer\u0060.\n- **On-Demand Script Injection \u0026 Tab Switching**: Selecting a tab injects \u0060content_relay.js\u0060 (\u0060ISOLATED\u0060 world) and \u0060bridge.js\u0060 (\u0060MAIN\u0060 world) via \u0060chrome.scripting.executeScript\u0060. Switching to another tab cleanly disposes the previous tab\u0027s bridge (\u0060window.__baf_bridge.dispose()\u0060)\u2014removing highlights, observers, and listeners\u2014and injects the bridge into the newly selected tab.\n- **CSP \u0026 CORS Immunity**: \u0060content_relay.js\u0060 and \u0060background.js\u0060 provide a privileged \u0060GM_xmlhttpRequest\u0060 bridge to the \u0060MAIN\u0060 world script so IPC polling, headers probing, and cross-origin CSS/JS reverse-engineering dumps bypass page Content-Security-Policy and CORS restrictions.\n- **Automatic Navigation Persistence**: When an attached tab performs a full-page reload or cross-origin navigation, \u0060background.js\u0060 automatically re-injects the bridge using the same \u0060tab_{tabId}\u0060 instance ID so \u0060WaitForPageTransitionAsync\u0060, pagination, and sequences continue uninterrupted.\n- **Framework \u0026 Server Enhancements (\u0060AutomationServer\u0060, \u0060BrowserClient\u0060, \u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060, \u0060BrowserTabInfo\u0060)**:\n\n- Updated \u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060 to support clean lifecycle disposal (\u0060window.__baf_bridge.dispose()\u0060), extension runtime configuration (\u0060window.__BAF_EXTENSION_CONFIG\u0060), and the extension \u0060GM_xmlhttpRequest\u0060 relay while retaining full backward compatibility with Tampermonkey userscripts.\n- Updated \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 to accept the Chrome Extension controller connection (\u0060/?role=extension\u0060 WebSocket and \u0060/api/ext/*\u0060 HTTP endpoints), track open \u0060BrowserTabInfo\u0060 tabs, and expose \u0060SwitchToExtensionTabAsync\u0060, \u0060DetachExtensionTabAsync\u0060, \u0060FocusExtensionTabAsync\u0060, and \u0060RequestExtensionTabsRefreshAsync\u0060.\n- Updated \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 with \u0060TabId\u0060, \u0060PageTitle\u0060, \u0060IsExtensionClient\u0060, and \u0060DisplayName\u0060 properties while keeping legacy Tampermonkey \u0060bot_*\u0060 clients working side-by-side.\n- **TestBedApp UI Integration (\u0060MainForm\u0060)**:\n\n- Added a **Chrome Extension - Open Tabs** panel to the left sidebar displaying connection status, tab search filter, auto-switch mode toggle, and the live list of open Chrome tabs.\n- Clicking an open tab in the list (or clicking **Inject / Switch**) immediately injects the automation script into that tab, connects its \u0060BrowserClient\u0060, selects it, and loads its DOM tree.\n- Added an **Export Chrome Extension...** button in the top bar (and under the **File** menu) to export the unpacked extension folder, and configured **Start Server** to automatically sync the built-in \u0060ChromeExtension\u0060 folder with the active port and IPC mode.\n\n### How to Test\n\n- Build and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060, then click **Start Server** (or click **Export Chrome Extension...** to export the extension to a folder).\n- In Chrome, navigate to \u0060chrome://extensions\u0060, enable **Developer mode**, click **Load unpacked**, and select \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\ChromeExtension\u0060 (or your exported folder).\n- Observe the **Chrome Extension - Open Tabs** list in \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 populate with all open Chrome tabs.\n- Click any tab in **Chrome Extension - Open Tabs** to inject the bridge script and begin interacting with it via **DOM Explorer**, **Raw Commands**, **Automation Editor**, **Data Scraper**, or **Reverse Engineering**.\n- Click any other tab in **Chrome Extension - Open Tabs** (or use the Chrome Extension toolbar popup) to switch active automation to that tab. Legacy Tampermonkey scripts generated via **Generate \u0026 Copy Script** continue to work simultaneously.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\BrowserTabInfo.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Text.Json.Serialization;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\n{\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Represents an open browser tab reported by the BAF Chrome Extension.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class BrowserTabInfo\n    {\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022tabId\u0022)]\n        public int TabId { get; set; }\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022windowId\u0022)]\n        public int WindowId { get; set; }\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022index\u0022)]\n        public int Index { get; set; }\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022title\u0022)]\n        public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022url\u0022)]\n        public string Url { get; set; } = string.Empty;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022active\u0022)]\n        public bool Active { get; set; }\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022status\u0022)]\n        public string Status { get; set; } = \u0022complete\u0022;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022canInject\u0022)]\n        public bool CanInject { get; set; } = true;\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022isInjected\u0022)]\n        public bool IsInjected { get; set; }\n\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022instanceId\u0022)]\n        public string InstanceId\n        {\n            get =\u003E string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_instanceId) ? $\u0022tab_{TabId}\u0022 : _instanceId;\n            set =\u003E _instanceId = value ?? string.Empty;\n        }\n        private string _instanceId = string.Empty;\n\n        public override string ToString()\n        {\n            string statusTag = IsInjected\n                ? \u0022[HOOKED] \u0022\n                : (!CanInject ? \u0022[RESTRICTED] \u0022 : (Active ? \u0022* \u0022 : string.Empty));\n\n            string displayTitle = !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Title) ? Title.Trim() : \u0022(Untitled Tab)\u0022;\n            if (displayTitle.Length \u003E 42)\n            {\n                displayTitle = displayTitle.Substring(0, 39) \u002B \u0022...\u0022;\n            }\n\n            string hostOrUrl = Url;\n            if (Uri.TryCreate(Url, UriKind.Absolute, out var uri) \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(uri.Host))\n            {\n                hostOrUrl = uri.Host \u002B (uri.AbsolutePath != \u0022/\u0022 ? uri.AbsolutePath : string.Empty);\n                if (hostOrUrl.Length \u003E 36)\n                {\n                    hostOrUrl = hostOrUrl.Substring(0, 33) \u002B \u0022...\u0022;\n                }\n            }\n\n            return $\u0022{statusTag}[#{TabId}] {displayTitle} ({hostOrUrl})\u0022;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\BrowserEventArgs.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    public class SiteDumpEventArgs : EventArgs\n    {\n        public SiteDumpType DumpType { get; }\n        public SiteDumpResult? Result { get; }\n        public Exception? Error { get; }\n\n        