    {
      "Id": "120824ba",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-27T20:21:13.4847217-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\nOk so this project works amazingly! However, we need to improve the dom tree viewer. For sites that have very large DOMs, it bogs doiwn the entire app when the tree viewer tries to render it. It also bogs down the program when i highlight an element on the site, and then the dom viewer control has to update. We need to make this far moprpe efficent, and mutli threaded so it does not clog up the UI thread. I want iot to seemlessely work for sites that have vbery large DOMs and we not get the entire programs UI freezing, or the DOM viewer control flickering a lot wh en it tries to select the element we selected in the browser on the page.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Virtualized, Flicker-Free \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 Control (\u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060)**:\n   - Replaced the eager Win32 \u0060SysTreeView32\u0060 node creation (\u0060TreeNode\u0060 per DOM element) with a virtualized, double-buffered owner-drawn tree control that only renders the rows visible in the viewport (~25\u201340 rows regardless of whether the DOM has 100 or 100,000\u002B nodes).\n   - Removed \u0060WS_EX_COMPOSITED\u0060 (which conflicted with \u0060SysTreeView32\u0060 expand/scroll animations) in favor of \u0060OptimizedDoubleBuffer | AllPaintingInWmPaint | UserPaint\u0060, cached GDI brushes/pens, token width caching, horizontal viewport culling, and dark-themed scrollbars.\n   - Added \u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060 to pre-index all DOM nodes into an \u0060O(1)\u0060 path lookup table (\u0060ItemsByKey\u0060), parent lookup chain, and pre-tokenized syntax-highlighted display segments (with automatic truncation of massive inline attributes like base64 data URIs or SVG paths for tree display).\n   - Added \u0060SelectNodeByPath\u0060 to expand ancestor paths in memory, update the flat visible row list, center the target row in the viewport, and repaint in a single frame with zero flicker.\n\n2. **Multi-Threaded DOM Deserialization, Coalesced Refreshes \u0026 Debounced Highlighting (\u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060, \u0060ReactExtensions.cs\u0060, \u0060DomNode.cs\u0060, \u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060)**:\n   - Offloaded JSON deserialization (\u0060GetDomNodeAsync\u0060) and \u0060DomTreeSnapshot.Build\u0060 to background worker threads (\u0060Task.Run\u0060) so large DOM payloads never block the UI thread.\n   - Added a coalescing refresh queue in \u0060MainForm.RefreshDomAsync\u0060 so rapid \u0060DOM_CHANGED\u0060 events do not overlap or freeze the UI, while preserving scroll position and any recent user selection.\n   - Added debounced browser highlighting (\u0060HighlightElementInBrowserDebounced\u0060) and immediate browser-side highlight on middle-click in \u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060 to avoid redundant IPC round-trips and \u0060DOM_CHANGED\u0060 feedback loops.\n   - Optimized \u0060DomNode.FindByPath\u0060 to use \u0060O(depth)\u0060 prefix matching instead of scanning the entire tree.\n\n### How to Test\n1. Build and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060, start the server, and connect to a site with a very large DOM.\n2. Open the **DOM Explorer** tab and scroll, expand, and collapse nodes; verify that scrolling and expanding are instantaneous with no UI lag.\n3. Middle-click elements on the webpage to select them in the **DOM Explorer**; verify that the highlight appears immediately on the page and the DOM tree jumps directly to the element without freezing or flickering.\n4. Use the arrow keys (\u0060Up\u0060, \u0060Down\u0060, \u0060Left\u0060, \u0060Right\u0060) and right-click context menu actions in the DOM Explorer to verify smooth navigation and element inspection.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Extensions\\ReactExtensions.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Retrieves and deserializes the page DOM into a \u003Csee cref=\u0022DomNode\u0022/\u003E tree.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static async Task\u003CDomNode?\u003E GetDomNodeAsync(this BrowserClient client, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var result = await client.GetDomAsync(cancellationToken);\n            if (result.Status == \u0022completed\u0022 \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrEmpty(result.Output))\n            {\n                return JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CDomNode\u003E(result.Output, DomJsonSerializerOptions);\n            }\n            return null;\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Retrieves and deserializes the page DOM into a \u003Csee cref=\u0022DomNode\u0022/\u003E tree on a background thread.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static async Task\u003CDomNode?\u003E GetDomNodeAsync(this BrowserClient client, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var result = await client.GetDomAsync(cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n            if (result.Status == \u0022completed\u0022 \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrEmpty(result.Output))\n            {\n                string rawJson = result.Output;\n                return await Task.Run(\n                    () =\u003E JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CDomNode\u003E(rawJson, DomJsonSerializerOptions),\n                    cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n            }\n            return null;\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomNode.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Recursively searches this DOM subtree for a node matching the specified CSS path.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public DomNode? FindByPath(string path)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(path)) return null;\n            if (Path == path) return this;\n\n            if (Children != null)\n            {\n                foreach (var child in Children)\n                {\n                    var found = child.FindByPath(path);\n                    if (found != null) return found;\n                }\n            }\n\n            return null;\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Searches this DOM subtree for a node matching the specified CSS path using fast prefix pruning.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public DomNode? FindByPath(string path)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(path)) return null;\n            if (string.Equals(Path, path, StringComparison.Ordinal)) return this;\n\n            if (Children != null \u0026\u0026 Children.Count \u003E 0)\n            {\n                // Fast O(depth) path walk when child paths are prefixes of the target path\n                for (int i = 0; i \u003C Children.Count; i\u002B\u002B)\n                {\n                    var child = Children[i];\n                    if (child.Type != \u0022element\u0022 || string.IsNullOrEmpty(child.Path))\n                        continue;\n\n                    if (string.Equals(child.Path, path, StringComparison.Ordinal))\n                        return child;\n\n                    if (path.Length \u003E child.Path.Length \u0026\u0026\n                        path.StartsWith(child.Path, StringComparison.Ordinal) \u0026\u0026\n                        path[child.Path.Length] == \u0027 \u0027)\n                    {\n                        var foundOnPrefix = child.FindByPath(path);\n                        if (foundOnPrefix != null)\n                            return foundOnPrefix;\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // Fallback scan for non-prefixed roots (such as \u0022html\u0022 -\u003E \u0022body\u0022)\n                for (int i = 0; i \u003C Children.Count; i\u002B\u002B)\n                {\n                    var child = Children[i];\n                    if (child.Type != \u0022element\u0022)\n                        continue;\n\n                    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(child.Path) \u0026\u0026\n                        child.Path != \u0022html\u0022 \u0026\u0026\n                        !path.StartsWith(child.Path, StringComparison.Ordinal))\n                    {\n                        continue;\n                    }\n\n                    var found = child.FindByPath(path);\n                    if (found != null)\n                        return found;\n                }\n            }\n\n            return null;\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ScriptGenerator.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        for (let attr of el.attributes) {\n            node.attributes[attr.name] = attr.value;\n        }\n\n        node.children = [];\n        if (depth \u003C MAX_DOM_DEPTH) {\n            let elementIndex = 0;\n            for (let child of el.childNodes) {\n                if (child.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE) {\n                    elementIndex\u002B\u002B;\n                    if (isInternalBridgeNode(child)) continue;\n                    const childTag = child.tagName.toLowerCase();\n                    const childPath = childTag === \u0027body\u0027\n                        ? \u0027body\u0027\n                        : \u0060${path} \u003E ${childTag}:nth-child(${elementIndex})\u0060;\n                    const serializedChild = serializeElement(child, depth \u002B 1, childPath);\n                    if (serializedChild) node.children.push(serializedChild);\n                } else if (child.nodeType === Node.TEXT_NODE) {\n                    const serializedText = serializeElement(child, depth \u002B 1, null);\n                    if (serializedText) node.children.push(serializedText);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return node;\n==== REPLACE\n        const attrs = el.attributes;\n        if (attrs) {\n            for (let i = 0, len = attrs.length; i \u003C len; i\u002B\u002B) {\n                const attr = attrs[i];\n                node.attributes[attr.name] = attr.value;\n            }\n        }\n\n        node.children = [];\n        if (depth \u003C MAX_DOM_DEPTH) {\n            let elementIndex = 0;\n            const childNodes = el.childNodes;\n            for (let i = 0, len = childNodes.length; i \u003C len; i\u002B\u002B) {\n                const child = childNodes[i];\n                if (child.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE) {\n                    elementIndex\u002B\u002B;\n                    if (isInternalBridgeNode(child)) continue;\n                    const childTag = child.tagName.toLowerCase();\n                    const childPath = childTag === \u0027body\u0027\n                        ? \u0027body\u0027\n                        : \u0060${path} \u003E ${childTag}:nth-child(${elementIndex})\u0060;\n                    const serializedChild = serializeElement(child, depth \u002B 1, childPath);\n                    if (serializedChild) node.children.push(serializedChild);\n                } else if (child.nodeType === Node.TEXT_NODE) {\n                    const serializedText = serializeElement(child, depth \u002B 1, null);\n                    if (serializedText) node.children.push(serializedText);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return node;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n    const handleMiddleMouseSelection = (e) =\u003E {\n        if (typeof sendEvent === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            const target = e.target \u0026\u0026 e.target.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE ? e.target : (e.target ? e.target.parentElement : null);\n            const path = getElementPath(target);\n            if (path) {\n                sendEvent(\u0027ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0027, { path: path });\n            }\n        }\n    };\n==== REPLACE\n    const handleMiddleMouseSelection = (e) =\u003E {\n        if (typeof sendEvent === \u0027function\u0027) {\n            const target = e.target \u0026\u0026 e.target.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE ? e.target : (e.target ? e.target.parentElement : null);\n            const path = getElementPath(target);\n            if (path) {\n                highlightedElement = target;\n                lastHighlightRect = { top: null, left: null, width: null, height: null, display: null };\n                updateHighlightPosition();\n                startHighlightTracking();\n                sendEvent(\u0027ELEMENT_CLICKED\u0027, { path: path });\n            }\n        }\n    };\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\nusing System;\nusing System.Drawing;\nusing System.Windows.Forms;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Models;\n\nnamespace TestBedApp.Controls\n{\n    public class DomTreeView : TreeView\n    {\n        private readonly Font _codeFont;\n        private readonly Color _selBgColor = Color.FromArgb(9, 71, 113);\n        private readonly Color _tagColor = Color.FromArgb(86, 156, 214);\n        private readonly Color _attrNameColor = Color.FromArgb(156, 220, 254);\n        private readonly Color _attrValueColor = Color.FromArgb(206, 145, 120);\n        private readonly Color _textColor = Color.FromArgb(212, 212, 212);\n        private readonly Color _punctColor = Color.FromArgb(128, 128, 128);\n\n        public DomTreeView()\n        {\n            DrawMode = TreeViewDrawMode.OwnerDrawText;\n            BorderStyle = BorderStyle.FixedSingle;\n            BackColor = Color.FromArgb(30, 30, 30);\n            ForeColor = Color.LightGray;\n            _codeFont = new Font(\u0022Consolas\u0022, 10F);\n            ItemHeight = 24;\n            ShowLines = true;\n            ShowPlusMinus = true;\n            ShowRootLines = true;\n            HideSelection = false;\n        }\n\n        protected override void OnHandleCreated(EventArgs e)\n        {\n            base.OnHandleCreated(e);\n            UpdateItemHeight();\n        }\n\n        protected override void OnDpiChangedAfterParent(EventArgs e)\n        {\n            base.OnDpiChangedAfterParent(e);\n            UpdateItemHeight();\n        }\n\n        private void UpdateItemHeight()\n        {\n            int scaledHeight = (int)Math.Ceiling(24 * (DeviceDpi / 96f));\n            ItemHeight = Math.Max(_codeFont.Height \u002B 6, scaledHeight);\n        }\n\n        protected override CreateParams CreateParams\n        {\n            get\n            {\n                CreateParams cp = base.CreateParams;\n                cp.Style |= 0x0080; // TVS_NOTOOLTIPS\n                cp.ExStyle |= 0x02000000; // WS_EX_COMPOSITED (Double buffering to prevent flicker)\n                return cp;\n            }\n        }\n\n        protected override void OnDrawNode(DrawTreeNodeEventArgs e)\n        {\n            if (e.Node == null || e.Graphics == null) return;\n\n            // Fix for WinForms TreeView animation bug where nodes are drawn at the top left\n            if (!e.Node.IsVisible || e.Bounds.IsEmpty || e.Bounds.Y != e.Node.Bounds.Y) return;\n\n            // Use GDI\u002B drawing to prevent animation bleeding issues\n            e.Graphics.TextRenderingHint = System.Drawing.Text.TextRenderingHint.ClearTypeGridFit;\n\n            bool isSelected = (e.State \u0026 TreeNodeStates.Selected) != 0 || e.Node.IsSelected;\n\n            // Clear the background to prevent artifacts from previous longer text states (e.g., when expanding/collapsing)\n            using (var clearBrush = new SolidBrush(BackColor))\n            {\n                int clearWidth = Math.Max(e.Bounds.Width, ClientSize.Width);\n                e.Graphics.FillRectangle(clearBrush, new Rectangle(e.Bounds.Left, e.Bounds.Top, clearWidth, e.Bounds.Height));\n            }\n\n            using (var format = new StringFormat(StringFormat.GenericTypographic))\n            {\n                format.FormatFlags |= StringFormatFlags.MeasureTrailingSpaces | StringFormatFlags.NoWrap;\n\n                float y = e.Bounds.Top \u002B ((e.Bounds.Height - _codeFont.Height) / 2f);\n                var parts = new System.Collections.Generic.List\u003C(string text, Color color)\u003E();\n\n                if (e.Node.Tag is DomNode domNode)\n                {\n                    if (domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022)\n                    {\n                        parts.Add((\u0022\u003C\u0022, _punctColor));\n                        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(domNode.TagName))\n                            parts.Add((domNode.TagName, _tagColor));\n\n                        if (domNode.Attributes != null)\n                        {\n                            foreach (var attr in domNode.Attributes)\n                            {\n                                parts.Add((\u0022 \u0022, _textColor));\n                                parts.Add((attr.Key, _attrNameColor));\n                                parts.Add((\u0022=\u0022, _punctColor));\n                                parts.Add(($\u0022\\\u0022{attr.Value}\\\u0022\u0022, _attrValueColor));\n                            }\n                        }\n\n                        parts.Add((\u0022\u003E\u0022, _punctColor));\n\n                        if (e.Node.Nodes.Count \u003E 0 \u0026\u0026 !e.Node.IsExpanded)\n                        {\n                            parts.Add((\u0022...\u0022, _punctColor));\n                            parts.Add((\u0022\u003C/\u0022, _punctColor));\n                            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(domNode.TagName))\n                                parts.Add((domNode.TagName, _tagColor));\n                            parts.Add((\u0022\u003E\u0022, _punctColor));\n                        }\n                    }\n                    else if (domNode.Type == \u0022text\u0022)\n                    {\n                        parts.Add(($\u0022\\\u0022{domNode.Text}\\\u0022\u0022, _textColor));\n                    }\n                }\n                else\n                {\n                    parts.Add((e.Node.Text, isSelected ? Color.White : _textColor));\n                }\n\n                // Measure total width\n                float totalWidth = 0;\n                float tempX = e.Bounds.Left \u002B 2;\n                foreach (var part in parts)\n                {\n                    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(part.text)) continue;\n                    float w = e.Graphics.MeasureString(part.text, _codeFont, new PointF(tempX, y), format).Width;\n                    totalWidth \u002B= w;\n                    tempX \u002B= w;\n                }\n\n                // Draw selection background\n                if (isSelected)\n                {\n                    RectangleF bgRect = new RectangleF(e.Bounds.Left, e.Bounds.Top, totalWidth \u002B 4, e.Bounds.Height);\n                    using (var selBrush = new SolidBrush(_selBgColor))\n                    {\n                        e.Graphics.FillRectangle(selBrush, bgRect);\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // Draw text\n                float x = e.Bounds.Left \u002B 2;\n                foreach (var part in parts)\n                {\n                    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(part.text)) continue;\n                    using (var brush = new SolidBrush(part.color))\n                    {\n                        e.Graphics.DrawString(part.text, _codeFont, brush, x, y, format);\n                    }\n                    x \u002B= e.Graphics.MeasureString(part.text, _codeFont, new PointF(x, y), format).Width;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        protected override void Dispose(bool disposing)\n        {\n            if (disposing)\n            {\n                _codeFont?.Dispose();\n            }\n            base.Dispose(disposing);\n        }\n    }\n}\n==== REPLACE\nusing System;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.ComponentModel;\nusing System.Drawing;\nusing System.Text;\nusing System.Windows.Forms;\nusing BrowserAutomationFramework.Models;\nusing TestBedApp.Utils;\n\nnamespace TestBedApp.Controls\n{\n    public enum DomTokenColor : byte\n    {\n        Punctuation,\n        TagName,\n        AttributeName,\n        AttributeValue,\n        TextContent\n    }\n\n    public readonly struct DomDisplayPart\n    {\n        public readonly string Text;\n        public readonly DomTokenColor ColorType;\n\n        public DomDisplayPart(string text, DomTokenColor colorType)\n        {\n            Text = text;\n            ColorType = colorType;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public sealed class DomTreeItem\n    {\n        public DomNode Node { get; }\n        public string UniqueKey { get; }\n        public string? ParentKey { get; }\n        public int Depth { get; }\n        public List\u003CDomTreeItem\u003E Children { get; } = new();\n        public bool HasChildren =\u003E Children.Count \u003E 0;\n        public DomDisplayPart[] OpenParts { get; }\n        public DomDisplayPart[] CollapsedSuffixParts { get; }\n        public int EstimatedCharLength { get; }\n\n        internal int MeasuredFontGeneration;\n        internal int[]? OpenPartWidths;\n        internal int[]? CollapsedSuffixWidths;\n        internal int OpenTotalWidth;\n        internal int CollapsedSuffixTotalWidth;\n\n        public DomTreeItem(\n            DomNode node,\n            string uniqueKey,\n            string? parentKey,\n            int depth,\n            DomDisplayPart[] openParts,\n            DomDisplayPart[] collapsedSuffixParts,\n            int estimatedCharLength)\n        {\n            Node = node;\n            UniqueKey = unique",
      "ModelExplanation": "### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Virtualized, Flicker-Free \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 Control (\u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060)**:\n   - Replaced the eager Win32 \u0060SysTreeView32\u0060 node creation (\u0060TreeNode\u0060 per DOM element) with a virtualized, double-buffered owner-drawn tree control that only renders the rows visible in the viewport (~25\u201340 rows regardless of whether the DOM has 100 or 100,000\u002B nodes).\n   - Removed \u0060WS_EX_COMPOSITED\u0060 (which conflicted with \u0060SysTreeView32\u0060 expand/scroll animations) in favor of \u0060OptimizedDoubleBuffer | AllPaintingInWmPaint | UserPaint\u0060, cached GDI brushes/pens, token width caching, horizontal viewport culling, and dark-themed scrollbars.\n   - Added \u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060 to pre-index all DOM nodes into an \u0060O(1)\u0060 path lookup table (\u0060ItemsByKey\u0060), parent lookup chain, and pre-tokenized syntax-highlighted display segments (with automatic truncation of massive inline attributes like base64 data URIs or SVG paths for tree display).\n   - Added \u0060SelectNodeByPath\u0060 to expand ancestor paths in memory, update the flat visible row list, center the target row in the viewport, and repaint in a single frame with zero flicker.\n\n2. **Multi-Threaded DOM Deserialization, Coalesced Refreshes \u0026 Debounced Highlighting (\u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060, \u0060ReactExtensions.cs\u0060, \u0060DomNode.cs\u0060, \u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060)**:\n   - Offloaded JSON deserialization (\u0060GetDomNodeAsync\u0060) and \u0060DomTreeSnapshot.Build\u0060 to background worker threads (\u0060Task.Run\u0060) so large DOM payloads never block the UI thread.\n   - Added a coalescing refresh queue in \u0060MainForm.RefreshDomAsync\u0060 so rapid \u0060DOM_CHANGED\u0060 events do not overlap or freeze the UI, while preserving scroll position and any recent user selection.\n   - Added debounced browser highlighting (\u0060HighlightElementInBrowserDebounced\u0060) and immediate browser-side highlight on middle-click in \u0060ScriptGenerator.cs\u0060 to avoid redundant IPC round-trips and \u0060DOM_CHANGED\u0060 feedback loops.\n   - Optimized \u0060DomNode.FindByPath\u0060 to use \u0060O(depth)\u0060 prefix matching instead of scanning the entire tree.\n\n### How to Test\n1. Build and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060, start the server, and connect to a site with a very large DOM.\n2. Open the **DOM Explorer** tab and scroll, expand, and collapse nodes; verify that scrolling and expanding are instantaneous with no UI lag.\n3. Middle-click elements on the webpage to select them in the **DOM Explorer**; verify that the highlight appears immediately on the page and the DOM tree jumps directly to the element without freezing or flickering.\n4. Use the arrow keys (\u0060Up\u0060, \u0060Down\u0060, \u0060Left\u0060, \u0060Right\u0060) and right-click context menu actions in the DOM Explorer to verify smooth navigation and element inspection.",
