oes**: \u0060BrowserClient.RefreshDomSnapshotCoalescedAsync\u0060 fetches a \u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060, hands it to the UI callback, and discards it. Because \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 does not retain its own \u0060CurrentDomSnapshot\u0060 / \u0060CurrentDomRoot\u0060 property, \u0060MainForm\u0060 has to pull \u0060tvDom.RootDomNode\u0060 out of the WinForms control and pass it back into \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 and \u0060ScrapeField\u0060 methods (\u0060scrape.GeneralizeAndSetContainer(..., tvDom.RootDomNode)\u0060, \u0060field.GeneralizeSelector(tvDom.RootDomNode)\u0060, \u0060scrape.AddFieldFromDomNode(..., tvDom.RootDomNode)\u0060).\n* **Migration to DLL**:\n  * Cache \u0060CurrentDomSnapshot\u0060 (\u0060DomTreeSnapshot?\u0060) and \u0060CurrentDomRoot\u0060 (\u0060DomNode?\u0060) directly on \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 whenever \u0060GetDomSnapshotAsync\u0060, \u0060GetDomNodeAsync\u0060, or \u0060RefreshDomSnapshotCoalescedAsync\u0060 completes.\n  * This allows headless/non-UI consumers and \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 extension methods to generalize selectors and inspect the latest DOM tree without needing a WinForms \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 instance.\n\n#### B. Chrome Extension Tab Switch Validation \u0026 Resolution (\u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060)\n* **Where it is now**: \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 (\u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060 and \u0060LstBrowserTabs_SelectedIndexChanged\u0060).\n* **What it does**: Validates \u0060tab.CanInject\u0060, checks \u0060tab.IsAlreadyActiveClient(...)\u0060, looks up \u0060_server.GetClientForTab(tab)\u0060 to see if a client session is already attached, and then calls \u0060_server.SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(tab.TabId, ...)\u0060.\n* **Migration to DLL**:\n  * Add an overload \u0060AutomationServer.SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(BrowserTabInfo tab, bool focusBrowserTab = false, bool detachOtherTabs = true, IpcMode mode = IpcMode.WebSocket, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\u0060 (returning the existing or pending \u0060BrowserClient?\u0060 or a status result) that encapsulates the \u0060CanInject\u0060 check and client lookup inside \u0060AutomationServer\u0060.\n\n#### C. Unified Save Helper for \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060 Active View (\u0060BtnSaveActiveDumpFile_Click\u0060)\n* **Where it is now**: \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 (\u0060BtnSaveActiveDumpFile_Click\u0060 and \u0060GetActiveDumpViewerText\u0060).\n* **What it does**: \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060 already has \u0060GetViewContent(SiteDumpType? viewType, SiteResourceItem? selectedResource, out string suggestedFileName)\u0060, which resolves whether the user is viewing an individual \u0060SiteResourceItem\u0060 or a combined \u0060SiteDumpType\u0060 bundle. However, when saving to disk in \u0060BtnSaveActiveDumpFile_Click\u0060, \u0060MainForm\u0060 manually branches between \u0060selectedResource.SaveToFile(...)\u0060 and \u0060_lastSiteDumpResult.SaveCombinedToFile(...)\u0060.\n* **Migration to DLL**:\n  * Add \u0060SaveViewContentToFile(string filePath, SiteDumpType? viewType, SiteResourceItem? selectedResource)\u0060 (and \u0060SaveViewContentToFileAsync\u0060) to \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060 so saving matches \u0060GetViewContent(...)\u0060 with a single call.\n\n#### D. Event Formatting Consistency Across \u0060BrowserEventArgs\u0060\n* **Where it is now**: \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 (constructor event wiring for \u0060_runner\u0060, \u0060_scraper\u0060, and \u0060Server_OnClientConnected\u0060 for \u0060OnPageLoaded\u0060).\n* **What it does**: While \u0060ScrapePageDelayEventArgs\u0060, \u0060ScrapeRateLimitEventArgs\u0060, \u0060ScrapeEventArgs\u0060, and \u0060SiteDumpEventArgs\u0060 have \u0060GetStatusMessage()\u0060 / \u0060GetLogMessage()\u0060 / \u0060GetCompletedLogMessage()\u0060 methods in the DLL, \u0060AutomationSequenceEventArgs\u0060, \u0060AutomationStepEventArgs\u0060, \u0060ScrapePageEventArgs\u0060, and \u0060PageLoadedEventArgs\u0060 still have their status/log messages constructed inline inside \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 (for example, checking \u0060e.StatusCode == 429\u0060 in \u0060OnPageLoaded\u0060).\n* **Migration to DLL**:\n  * Add \u0060GetLogMessage()\u0060 / \u0060GetStatusMessage()\u0060 helpers to \u0060AutomationSequenceEventArgs\u0060, \u0060AutomationStepEventArgs\u0060, \u0060ScrapePageEventArgs\u0060, and \u0060PageLoadedEventArgs\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\BrowserEventArgs.cs\u0060.\n\n#### E. Chrome Extension Setup Instructions (\u0060BtnExportExtension_Click\u0060)\n* **Where it is now**: \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 (\u0060BtnExportExtension_Click\u0060).\n* **What it does**: Hardcodes the step-by-step developer instructions for loading the unpacked Manifest V3 extension in Chromium browsers (\u0060chrome://extensions\u0060, Developer mode, Load unpacked).\n* **Migration to DLL**:\n  * Move the instructions generator to \u0060ChromeExtensionGenerator.GetLoadInstructions(string exportedDirectoryPath)\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ChromeExtensionGenerator.cs\u0060.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Viewport \u0026 Hit-Testing Math in \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060\n\nWhile \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 and \u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060 were already moved to \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060, \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060 still contains pure coordinate and scroll calculation logic that does not depend on GDI\u002B drawing:\n* **Row Hit-Testing (\u0060GetRowIndexAtY\u0060 \u0026 \u0060IsPointOnExpandGlyph\u0060)**: Computing which visible row index corresponds to a Y coordinate and whether an X coordinate falls within a row\u0027s expand/collapse glyph box (\u0060indentX\u0060 to \u0060indentX \u002B glyphColumnWidth\u0060).\n* **Viewport Scroll Clamping (\u0060EnsureRowVisible\u0060)**: Computing the new target \u0060scrollX\u0060 and \u0060scrollY\u0060 offsets to bring a specific \u0060rowIndex\u0060 into view (either centered vertically or edge-aligned).\n* **Row Width Calculation (\u0060GetMeasuredRowTextWidth\u0060)**: Summing \u0060OpenTotalWidth\u0060 and \u0060CollapsedSuffixTotalWidth\u0060 based on whether \u0060item.HasChildren \u0026\u0026 !IsExpanded(item.UniqueKey)\u0060.\n* **Migration to DLL**:\n  * Move these coordinate, hit-test, and scroll-offset calculations into \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060 so any UI framework (WinForms, WPF, Avalonia, etc.) can reuse the exact same virtualized viewport math.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Recommended Next Steps\n\nIf you would like me to proceed with migrating these items, I can:\n1. Enhance \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 to cache \u0060CurrentDomSnapshot\u0060 / \u0060CurrentDomRoot\u0060 and add \u0060DomNode\u0060 convenience overloads that use it automatically.\n2. Add the \u0060BrowserTabInfo\u0060 overload to \u0060AutomationServer.SwitchToExtensionTabAsync\u0060 and the \u0060GetLoadInstructions\u0060 helper to \u0060ChromeExtensionGenerator\u0060.\n3. Add \u0060SaveViewContentToFile\u0060 / \u0060SaveViewContentToFileAsync\u0060 to \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060 and log/status message helpers to the remaining \u0060EventArgs\u0060 classes in \u0060BrowserEventArgs.cs\u0060.\n4. Move the pure hit-testing and scroll-offset math from \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060 into \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n- **DOM Snapshot Caching on \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 (\u0060BrowserClient.cs\u0060, \u0060ReactExtensions.cs\u0060, \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Added \u0060CurrentDomSnapshot\u0060 (\u0060DomTreeSnapshot?\u0060) and \u0060CurrentDomRoot\u0060 (\u0060DomNode?\u0060) properties to \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 and updated \u0060GetDomNodeAsync\u0060, \u0060GetDomSnapshotAsync\u0060, and \u0060RefreshDomSnapshotCoalescedAsync\u0060 to cache the latest DOM tree on the client instance.\n- Updated \u0060MainForm\u0060 selector generalization and point-and-click scrape helpers to resolve the root DOM from the active \u0060BrowserClient.CurrentDomRoot\u0060 (with fallback to \u0060tvDom.RootDomNode\u0060).\n- **Chrome Extension Tab Switch Overload \u0026 Setup Instructions (\u0060AutomationServer.cs\u0060, \u0060ChromeExtensionGenerator.cs\u0060, \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Added \u0060AutomationServer.SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(BrowserTabInfo tab, ...)\u0060 to encapsulate \u0060CanInject\u0060 validation, existing \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 resolution, and tab attachment.\n- Added \u0060ChromeExtensionGenerator.GetLoadInstructions(string exportedDirectoryPath)\u0060 and updated \u0060MainForm.BtnExportExtension_Click\u0060 to use it.\n- **Unified View Saving \u0026 Event Formatting Helpers (\u0060SiteDumpResult.cs\u0060, \u0060BrowserEventArgs.cs\u0060, \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Added \u0060SaveViewContentToFile\u0060 and \u0060SaveViewContentToFileAsync\u0060 to \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060 and simplified \u0060MainForm.BtnSaveActiveDumpFile_Click\u0060.\n- Added log and status formatting methods (\u0060GetLogMessage\u0060, \u0060GetStatusMessage\u0060, \u0060GetStartedLogMessage\u0060, \u0060GetCompletedLogMessage\u0060, \u0060GetFailedLogMessage\u0060) to \u0060PageLoadedEventArgs\u0060, \u0060AutomationSequenceEventArgs\u0060, \u0060AutomationStepEventArgs\u0060, \u0060ScrapePageEventArgs\u0060, \u0060ScrapeEventArgs\u0060, and \u0060SiteDumpEventArgs\u0060.\n- **Virtualized Viewport \u0026 Hit-Testing Math (\u0060DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060, \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Migrated row Y-coordinate hit-testing (\u0060GetRowIndexAtY\u0060), expand/collapse glyph hit-testing (\u0060IsPointOnExpandGlyph\u0060), scroll offset clamping (\u0060CalculateScrollOffsetsForRow\u0060), and row width calculations (\u0060GetMeasuredRowTextWidth\u0060, \u0060CalculateFullRowWidth\u0060) from \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 into \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060.\n\n### How to Test\n\n- Build the solution (\u0060dotnet build\u0060) and verify both \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 and \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 compile cleanly with zero warnings or errors.\n- Launch \u0060TestBedApp\u0060, start the server, and attach to a browser tab via the Chrome Extension or Tampermonkey script.\n- Inspect the DOM in the **DOM Explorer** tab (expanding/collapsing nodes, keyboard navigation, and middle-clicking elements in the browser).\n- Test generalizing selectors in the **Data Scraper** tab and saving active resource/combined views in the **Reverse Engineering** tab.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\BrowserClient.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the CSS selector of the most recently highlighted element on this client, if any.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string? LastHighlightedSelector =\u003E _lastHighlightedSelector;\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the most recently fetched \u003Csee cref=\u0022DomTreeSnapshot\u0022/\u003E for this client, if any.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public DomTreeSnapshot? CurrentDomSnapshot { get; internal set; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the root \u003Csee cref=\u0022DomNode\u0022/\u003E of the most recently fetched DOM tree for this client, if any.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public DomNode? CurrentDomRoot { get; internal set; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the CSS selector of the most recently highlighted element on this client, if any.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string? LastHighlightedSelector =\u003E _lastHighlightedSelector;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n                    if (snapshot != null)\n                    {\n                        bool userSelectedDuringFetch = _lastUserSelectionUtc \u003E fetchStartedUtc \u0026\u0026\n                                                       !string.IsNullOrEmpty(_lastUserSelectedDomPath);\n==== REPLACE\n                    if (snapshot != null)\n                    {\n                        CurrentDomSnapshot = snapshot;\n                        CurrentDomRoot = snapshot.RootNode;\n\n                        bool userSelectedDuringFetch = _lastUserSelectionUtc \u003E fetchStartedUtc \u0026\u0026\n                                                       !string.IsNullOrEmpty(_lastUserSelectedDomPath);\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        internal void Disconnect()\n        {\n            _highlightDebounceCts?.Cancel();\n==== REPLACE\n        internal void Disconnect()\n        {\n            _highlightDebounceCts?.Cancel();\n            CurrentDomSnapshot = null;\n            CurrentDomRoot = null;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Extensions\\ReactExtensions.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Retrieves and deserializes the page DOM into a \u003Csee cref=\u0022DomNode\u0022/\u003E tree on a background thread.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static async Task\u003CDomNode?\u003E GetDomNodeAsync(this BrowserClient client, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var result = await client.GetDomAsync(cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n            if (result.Status == \u0022completed\u0022 \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrEmpty(result.Output))\n            {\n                string rawJson = result.Output;\n                return await Task.Run(\n                    () =\u003E JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CDomNode\u003E(rawJson, DomJsonSerializerOptions),\n                    cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n            }\n            return null;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Retrieves the page DOM and builds a pre-indexed, syntax-tokenized \u003Csee cref=\u0022DomTreeSnapshot\u0022/\u003E on a background thread.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static async Task\u003CDomTreeSnapshot?\u003E GetDomSnapshotAsync(this BrowserClient client, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var rootNode = await client.GetDomNodeAsync(cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n            if (rootNode == null)\n                return null;\n\n            return await Task.Run(() =\u003E DomTreeSnapshot.Build(rootNode), cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Retrieves and deserializes the page DOM into a \u003Csee cref=\u0022DomNode\u0022/\u003E tree on a background thread,\n        /// caching the result in \u003Csee cref=\u0022BrowserClient.CurrentDomRoot\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static async Task\u003CDomNode?\u003E GetDomNodeAsync(this BrowserClient client, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var result = await client.GetDomAsync(cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n            if (result.Status == \u0022completed\u0022 \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrEmpty(result.Output))\n            {\n                string rawJson = result.Output;\n                var rootNode = await Task.Run(\n                    () =\u003E JsonSerializer.Deserialize\u003CDomNode\u003E(rawJson, DomJsonSerializerOptions),\n                    cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n                client.CurrentDomRoot = rootNode;\n                return rootNode;\n            }\n            return null;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Retrieves the page DOM and builds a pre-indexed, syntax-tokenized \u003Csee cref=\u0022DomTreeSnapshot\u0022/\u003E on a background thread,\n        /// caching the result in \u003Csee cref=\u0022BrowserClient.CurrentDomSnapshot\u0022/\u003E and \u003Csee cref=\u0022BrowserClient.CurrentDomRoot\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static async Task\u003CDomTreeSnapshot?\u003E GetDomSnapshotAsync(this BrowserClient client, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            var rootNode = await client.GetDomNodeAsync(cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n            if (rootNode == null)\n                return null;\n\n            var snapshot = await Task.Run(() =\u003E DomTreeSnapshot.Build(rootNode), cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n            client.CurrentDomSnapshot = snapshot;\n            client.CurrentDomRoot = snapshot.RootNode;\n            return snapshot;\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\AutomationServer.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Instructs the connected Chrome Extension to inject the automation bridge into \u003Cparamref name=\u0022tabId\u0022/\u003E\n        /// and optionally detach any previously hooked tab so interaction switches cleanly to the selected tab.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(\n            int tabId,\n            bool focusBrowserTab = false,\n            bool detachOtherTabs = true,\n            IpcMode mode = IpcMode.WebSocket,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Validates that \u003Cparamref name=\u0022tab\u0022/\u003E allows script injection, instructs the connected Chrome Extension\n        /// to inject the automation bridge into the tab, and returns any already-connected \u003Csee cref=\u0022BrowserClient\u0022/\u003E for the tab.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task\u003CBrowserClient?\u003E SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(\n            BrowserTabInfo tab,\n            bool focusBrowserTab = false,\n            bool detachOtherTabs = true,\n            IpcMode mode = IpcMode.WebSocket,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (tab == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(tab));\n            if (!tab.CanInject)\n                throw new InvalidOperationException($\u0022Tab #{tab.TabId} (\u0027{tab.Url}\u0027) is a restricted internal browser page and cannot be injected.\u0022);\n\n            var existingClient = GetClientForTab(tab);\n            await SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(tab.TabId, focusBrowserTab, detachOtherTabs, mode, cancellationToken);\n            return existingClient;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Instructs the connected Chrome Extension to inject the automation bridge into \u003Cparamref name=\u0022tabId\u0022/\u003E\n        /// and optionally detach any previously hooked tab so interaction switches cleanly to the selected tab.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public async Task SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(\n            int tabId,\n            bool focusBrowserTab = false,\n            bool detachOtherTabs = true,\n            IpcMode mode = IpcMode.WebSocket,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\SiteDumpResult.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Saves the combined dump output (for \u003Cparamref name=\u0022viewType\u0022/\u003E or \u003Csee cref=\u0022DumpType\u0022/\u003E) to a single file.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void SaveCombinedToFile(string filePath, SiteDumpType? viewType = null)\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Saves the resolved view content (either a specific \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022/\u003E or the combined output for \u003Cparamref name=\u0022viewType\u0022/\u003E) to the specified file path.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void SaveViewContentToFile(string filePath, SiteDumpType? viewType, SiteResourceItem? selectedResource)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(filePath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022File path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(filePath));\n\n            if (selectedResource != null)\n            {\n                selectedResource.SaveToFile(filePath);\n                return;\n            }\n\n            SaveCombinedToFile(filePath, viewType ?? DumpType);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Asynchronously saves the resolved view content (either a specific \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022/\u003E or the combined output for \u003Cparamref name=\u0022viewType\u0022/\u003E) to the specified file path.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task SaveViewContentToFileAsync(\n            string filePath,\n            SiteDumpType? viewType,\n            SiteResourceItem? selectedResource,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(filePath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022File path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(filePath));\n\n            if (selectedResource != null)\n            {\n                return selectedResource.SaveToFileAsync(filePath, cancellationToken);\n            }\n\n            return SaveCombinedToFileAsync(filePath, viewType ?? DumpType, cancellationToken);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Saves the combined dump output (for \u003Cparamref name=\u0022viewType\u0022/\u003E or \u003Csee cref=\u0022DumpType\u0022/\u003E) to a single file.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void SaveCombinedToFile(string filePath, SiteDumpType? viewType = null)\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\BrowserEventArgs.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Initializes a new instance of the \u003Csee cref=\u0022PageLoadedEventArgs\u0022/\u003E class.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public PageLoadedEventArgs(string pageLoadId, string url, string readyState, int statusCode = 200, string? retryAfter = null)\n        {\n            PageLoadId = pageLoadId;\n            Url = url;\n            ReadyState = readyState;\n            StatusCode = statusCode;\n            RetryAfter = retryAfter;\n        }\n    }\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets whether the page load returned an HTTP 429 rate-limit status code.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public bool IsRateLimited =\u003E StatusCode == 429;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Initializes a new instance of the \u003Csee cref=\u0022PageLoadedEventArgs\u0022/\u003E class.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public PageLoadedEventArgs(string pageLoadId, string url, string readyState, int statusCode = 200, string? retryAfter = null)\n        {\n            PageLoadId = pageLoadId;\n            Url = url;\n            ReadyState = readyState;\n            StatusCode = statusCode;\n            RetryAfter = retryAfter;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message describing the page load or HTTP 429 rate-limit state.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022instanceId\u0022\u003EOptional client instance identifier to include in the prefix.\u003C/param\u003E\n        public string GetLogMessage(string? instanceId = null)\n        {\n            string prefix = !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(instanceId) ? $\u0022[NAV \u003C- {instanceId}] \u0022 : string.Empty;\n            return IsRateLimited\n                ? $\u0022{prefix}Page rate-limited (HTTP 429): {Url}\u0022\n                : $\u0022{prefix}Page loaded: {Url}\u0022;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a concise status message describing the page load or HTTP 429 rate-limit state.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetStatusMessage()\n        {\n            return IsRateLimited\n                ? $\u0022Page rate-limited (HTTP 429): {Url}\u0022\n                : $\u0022Page loaded: {Url}\u0022;\n        }\n    }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Initializes a new instance of the \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationSequenceEventArgs\u0022/\u003E class.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public AutomationSequenceEventArgs(AutomationSequence sequence)\n        {\n            Sequence = sequence;\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Event arguments raised when an \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationStep\u0022/\u003E starts, completes, or fails.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class AutomationStepEventArgs : EventArgs\n    {\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the parent \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationSequence\u0022/\u003E if the step is running as part of a sequence.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public AutomationSequence? Sequence { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationStep\u0022/\u003E being executed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public AutomationStep Step { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the \u003Csee cref=\u0022CommandResult\u0022/\u003E returned by the step when completed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public CommandResult? Result { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the exception thrown if the step failed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Exception? Error { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Initializes a new instance of the \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationStepEventArgs\u0022/\u003E class.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public AutomationStepEventArgs(AutomationSequence? sequence, AutomationStep step, CommandResult? result = null, Exception? error = null)\n        {\n            Sequence = sequence;\n            Step = step;\n            Result = result;\n            Error = error;\n        }\n    }\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Initializes a new instance of the \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationSequenceEventArgs\u0022/\u003E class.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public AutomationSequenceEventArgs(AutomationSequence sequence)\n        {\n            Sequence = sequence;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message indicating that the sequence has started.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetStartedLogMessage() =\u003E $\u0022--- Starting List: {Sequence.Name} ---\u0022;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message indicating that the sequence has completed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetCompletedLogMessage() =\u003E $\u0022--- Completed List: {Sequence.Name} ---\u0022;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message for this sequence event.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetLogMessage() =\u003E GetStartedLogMessage();\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a concise status message for this sequence event.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetStatusMessage() =\u003E $\u0022Running sequence \u0027{Sequence.Name}\u0027...\u0022;\n    }\n\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Event arguments raised when an \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationStep\u0022/\u003E starts, completes, or fails.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class AutomationStepEventArgs : EventArgs\n    {\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the parent \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationSequence\u0022/\u003E if the step is running as part of a sequence.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public AutomationSequence? Sequence { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationStep\u0022/\u003E being executed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public AutomationStep Step { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the \u003Csee cref=\u0022CommandResult\u0022/\u003E returned by the step when completed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public CommandResult? Result { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the exception thrown if the step failed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Exception? Error { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Initializes a new instance of the \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationStepEventArgs\u0022/\u003E class.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public AutomationStepEventArgs(AutomationSequence? sequence, AutomationStep step, CommandResult? result = null, Exception? error = null)\n        {\n            Sequence = sequence;\n            Step = step;\n            Result = result;\n            Error = error;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message indicating that the step has started executing.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetStartedLogMessage() =\u003E $\u0022Executing: {Step.Name}\u0022;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message for the step\u0027s completion result.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetCompletedLogMessage() =\u003E\n            Result != null ? $\u0022{Result.Status} | {Result.Output}\u0022 : $\u0022Completed: {Step.Name}\u0022;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message describing the step failure.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetFailedLogMessage() =\u003E $\u0022Step \u0027{Step.Name}\u0027 failed: {Error?.Message}\u0022;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message based on the current state of the step event.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetLogMessage()\n        {\n            if (Error != null) return GetFailedLogMessage();\n            if (Result != null) return GetCompletedLogMessage();\n            return GetStartedLogMessage();\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a concise status bar message for this step event.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetStatusMessage()\n        {\n            if (Error != null) return $\u0022Step \u0027{Step.Name}\u0027 failed: {Error.Message}\u0022;\n            if (Result != null) return $\u0022Completed step \u0027{Step.Name}\u0027.\u0022;\n            return $\u0022Executing step \u0027{Step.Name}\u0027...\u0022;\n        }\n    }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted completion summary message when \u003Csee cref=\u0022Result\u0022/\u003E is available.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetCompletedLogMessage()\n        {\n            if (Result == null)\n                return $\u0022Completed \u0027{Definition.Name}\u0027.\u0022;\n            return $\u0022Completed \u0027{Definition.Name}\u0027: {Result.RecordCount} total record(s) across {Result.PagesScraped} page(s).\u0022;\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Event arguments raised when a single page of a \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeDefinition\u0022/\u003E finishes extracting records.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class ScrapePageEventArgs : EventArgs\n    {\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeDefinition\u0022/\u003E being executed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapeDefinition Definition { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the 1-based page number that completed extraction.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public int PageNumber { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the records extracted from this page.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList\u003CSystem.Collections.Generic.Dictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E PageRecords { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Initializes a new instance of the \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapePageEventArgs\u0022/\u003E class.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapePageEventArgs(\n            ScrapeDefinition definition,\n            int pageNumber,\n            System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList\u003CSystem.Collections.Generic.Dictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E pageRecords)\n        {\n            Definition = definition;\n            PageNumber = pageNumber;\n            PageRecords = pageRecords;\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Event arguments raised when a reverse-engineering site dump starts, completes, or fails.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class SiteDumpEventArgs : EventArgs\n    {\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpType\u0022/\u003E of the dump operation.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public SiteDumpType DumpType { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpResult\u0022/\u003E containing the extracted site resources.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public SiteDumpResult? Result { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the exception thrown if the site dump operation failed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Exception? Error { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Initializes a new instance of the \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpEventArgs\u0022/\u003E class.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public SiteDumpEventArgs(SiteDumpType dumpType, SiteDumpResult? result = null, Exception? error = null)\n        {\n            DumpType = dumpType;\n            Result = result;\n            Error = error;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted completion summary message when \u003Csee cref=\u0022Result\u0022/\u003E is available.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetCompletedLogMessage()\n        {\n            if (Result == null)\n                return $\u0022Dump ({DumpType}) completed.\u0022;\n            return $\u0022Dump ({DumpType}) completed: {Result.HtmlResources.Count} HTML, {Result.CssResources.Count} CSS, {Result.JavaScriptResources.Count} JS resource(s) ({Result.GetFormattedTotalSize()}).\u0022;\n        }\n    }\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message indicating that the scrape operation has started.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetStartedLogMessage() =\u003E $\u0022--- Starting Scrape: {Definition.Name} ---\u0022;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted completion summary message when \u003Csee cref=\u0022Result\u0022/\u003E is available.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetCompletedLogMessage()\n        {\n            if (Result == null)\n                return $\u0022Completed \u0027{Definition.Name}\u0027.\u0022;\n            return $\u0022Completed \u0027{Definition.Name}\u0027: {Result.RecordCount} total record(s) across {Result.PagesScraped} page(s).\u0022;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message describing the scrape failure.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetFailedLogMessage() =\u003E $\u0022\u0027{Definition.Name}\u0027 failed: {Error?.Message}\u0022;\n    }\n\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Event arguments raised when a single page of a \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeDefinition\u0022/\u003E finishes extracting records.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class ScrapePageEventArgs : EventArgs\n    {\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeDefinition\u0022/\u003E being executed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapeDefinition Definition { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the 1-based page number that completed extraction.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public int PageNumber { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the records extracted from this page.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList\u003CSystem.Collections.Generic.Dictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E PageRecords { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Initializes a new instance of the \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapePageEventArgs\u0022/\u003E class.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public ScrapePageEventArgs(\n            ScrapeDefinition definition,\n            int pageNumber,\n            System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList\u003CSystem.Collections.Generic.Dictionary\u003Cstring, string?\u003E\u003E pageRecords)\n        {\n            Definition = definition;\n            PageNumber = pageNumber;\n            PageRecords = pageRecords;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message summarizing the number of records extracted on this page.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetLogMessage() =\u003E $\u0022Page {PageNumber} extracted {PageRecords.Count} record(s).\u0022;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a concise status message summarizing the number of records extracted on this page.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetStatusMessage() =\u003E $\u0022Page {PageNumber}: {PageRecords.Count} record(s) extracted.\u0022;\n    }\n\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Event arguments raised when a reverse-engineering site dump starts, completes, or fails.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public class SiteDumpEventArgs : EventArgs\n    {\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpType\u0022/\u003E of the dump operation.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public SiteDumpType DumpType { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpResult\u0022/\u003E containing the extracted site resources.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public SiteDumpResult? Result { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the exception thrown if the site dump operation failed.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Exception? Error { get; }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Initializes a new instance of the \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpEventArgs\u0022/\u003E class.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public SiteDumpEventArgs(SiteDumpType dumpType, SiteDumpResult? result = null, Exception? error = null)\n        {\n            DumpType = dumpType;\n            Result = result;\n            Error = error;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message indicating that the site dump operation has started.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetStartedLogMessage() =\u003E $\u0022--- Starting Site Dump ({DumpType}) ---\u0022;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted completion summary message when \u003Csee cref=\u0022Result\u0022/\u003E is available.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetCompletedLogMessage()\n        {\n            if (Result == null)\n                return $\u0022Dump ({DumpType}) completed.\u0022;\n            return $\u0022Dump ({DumpType}) completed: {Result.HtmlResources.Count} HTML, {Result.CssResources.Count} CSS, {Result.JavaScriptResources.Count} JS resource(s) ({Result.GetFormattedTotalSize()}).\u0022;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a formatted log message describing the site dump failure.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string GetFailedLogMessage() =\u003E $\u0022Dump ({DumpType}) failed: {Error?.Message}\u0022;\n    }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Generators\\ChromeExtensionGenerator.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Generates the Manifest V3 \u003Cc\u003Emanifest.json\u003C/c\u003E content for the BAF Chrome Extension.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static string GenerateManifestJson()\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns step-by-step user instructions for loading the exported unpacked Chrome Extension into a Chromium browser.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022exportedDirectoryPath\u0022\u003EThe directory path where the unpacked extension files were exported.\u003C/param\u003E\n        public static string GetLoadInstructions(string exportedDirectoryPath)\n        {\n            return $\u0022Chrome Extension exported successfully to:\\n{exportedDirectoryPath}\\n\\n\u0022 \u002B\n                   \u0022To load in Chrome / Edge / Brave:\\n\u0022 \u002B\n                   \u00221. Open chrome://extensions in your browser.\\n\u0022 \u002B\n                   \u00222. Enable \u0027Developer mode\u0027 (top-right toggle).\\n\u0022 \u002B\n                   \u00223. Click \u0027Load unpacked\u0027 and select the exported folder.\\n\\n\u0022 \u002B\n                   \u0022Once loaded, all open browser tabs will appear automatically in the \u0027Chrome Extension - Open Tabs\u0027 panel!\u0022;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Generates the Manifest V3 \u003Cc\u003Emanifest.json\u003C/c\u003E content for the BAF Chrome Extension.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static string GenerateManifestJson()\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Handles Left-arrow keyboard navigation (collapses an expanded node or selects its parent node).\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void NavigateLeft(out bool expandedChanged, out int? newSelectedRowIndex)\n        {\n            expandedChanged = false;\n            newSelectedRowIndex = null;\n            if (_visibleRows.Count == 0) return;\n\n            int currentRow = GetCurrentOrFirstRowIndex();\n            var item = _visibleRows[currentRow];\n            if (item.HasChildren \u0026\u0026 _expandedKeys.Contains(item.UniqueKey))\n            {\n                _expandedKeys.Remove(item.UniqueKey);\n                RebuildVisibleRows();\n                expandedChanged = true;\n            }\n            else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(item.ParentKey) \u0026\u0026 _rowIndexByKey.TryGetValue(item.ParentKey, out int parentRow))\n            {\n                newSelectedRowIndex = parentRow;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Handles Left-arrow keyboard navigation (collapses an expanded node or selects its parent node).\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void NavigateLeft(out bool expandedChanged, out int? newSelectedRowIndex)\n        {\n            expandedChanged = false;\n            newSelectedRowIndex = null;\n            if (_visibleRows.Count == 0) return;\n\n            int currentRow = GetCurrentOrFirstRowIndex();\n            var item = _visibleRows[currentRow];\n            if (item.HasChildren \u0026\u0026 _expandedKeys.Contains(item.UniqueKey))\n            {\n                _expandedKeys.Remove(item.UniqueKey);\n                RebuildVisibleRows();\n                expandedChanged = true;\n            }\n            else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(item.ParentKey) \u0026\u0026 _rowIndexByKey.TryGetValue(item.ParentKey, out int parentRow))\n            {\n                newSelectedRowIndex = parentRow;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Computes the 0-based visible row index at the specified vertical coordinate \u003Cparamref name=\u0022y\u0022/\u003E,\n        /// or returns -1 if the coordinate is outside the viewport or visible row range.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public int GetRowIndexAtY(int y, int viewportTop, int viewportHeight, int scrollY, int itemHeight)\n        {\n            if (itemHeight \u003C= 0 || viewportHeight \u003C= 0)\n                return -1;\n\n            int viewportBottom = viewportTop \u002B viewportHeight;\n            if (y \u003C viewportTop || y \u003E= viewportBottom)\n                return -1;\n\n            int row = (y - viewportTop \u002B scrollY) / itemHeight;\n            return (row \u003E= 0 \u0026\u0026 row \u003C _visibleRows.Count) ? row : -1;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Determines whether the horizontal coordinate \u003Cparamref name=\u0022x\u0022/\u003E falls within the expand/collapse glyph box of \u003Cparamref name=\u0022item\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public bool IsPointOnExpandGlyph(\n            DomTreeItem? item,\n            int x,\n            int viewportLeft,\n            int paddingLeft,\n            int indentWidth,\n            int glyphColumnWidth,\n            int scrollX,\n            int hitSlop = 2)\n        {\n            if (item == null || !item.HasChildren)\n                return false;\n\n            int indentX = viewportLeft \u002B paddingLeft \u002B (item.Depth * indentWidth) - scrollX;\n            return x \u003E= indentX - hitSlop \u0026\u0026 x \u003C indentX \u002B glyphColumnWidth \u002B hitSlop;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Computes updated horizontal and vertical scroll offsets to ensure the row at \u003Cparamref name=\u0022rowIndex\u0022/\u003E is visible within the viewport.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public bool CalculateScrollOffsetsForRow(\n            int rowIndex,\n            int viewportWidth,\n            int viewportHeight,\n            int itemHeight,\n            int paddingLeft,\n            int indentWidth,\n            int minVisibleTextWidth,\n            int horizontalScrollMargin,\n            bool centerVertically,\n            ref int scrollX,\n            ref int scrollY)\n        {\n            if (rowIndex \u003C 0 || rowIndex \u003E= _visibleRows.Count || viewportHeight \u003C= 0 || itemHeight \u003C= 0)\n                return false;\n\n            int rowTop = rowIndex * itemHeight;\n            int rowBottom = rowTop \u002B itemHeight;\n\n            if (rowTop \u003C scrollY || rowBottom \u003E scrollY \u002B viewportHeight)\n            {\n                if (centerVertically)\n                {\n                    scrollY = rowTop - (viewportHeight / 2) \u002B (itemHeight / 2);\n                }\n                else if (rowTop \u003C scrollY)\n                {\n                    scrollY = rowTop;\n                }\n                else\n                {\n                    scrollY = rowBottom - viewportHeight;\n                }\n            }\n\n            var item = _visibleRows[rowIndex];\n            int itemTextStart = paddingLeft \u002B (item.Depth * indentWidth);\n            if (itemTextStart \u003C scrollX || itemTextStart \u002B minVisibleTextWidth \u003E scrollX \u002B viewportWidth)\n            {\n                scrollX = Math.Max(0, itemTextStart - horizontalScrollMargin);\n            }\n\n            return true;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Calculates the total rendered text width for \u003Cparamref name=\u0022item\u0022/\u003E given its measured open tag width\n        /// and collapsed suffix width, accounting for whether the item is currently expanded.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public int GetMeasuredRowTextWidth(DomTreeItem item, int openTotalWidth, int collapsedSuffixTotalWidth)\n        {\n            if (item == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(item));\n            bool includeCollapsedSuffix = item.HasChildren \u0026\u0026 !_expandedKeys.Contains(item.UniqueKey);\n            return openTotalWidth \u002B (includeCollapsedSuffix ? collapsedSuffixTotalWidth : 0);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Calculates the total horizontal pixel width of a row including indentation, expand glyph column, text width, and trailing padding.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public static int CalculateFullRowWidth(\n            DomTreeItem item,\n            int textWidth,\n            int paddingLeft,\n            int indentWidth,\n            int glyphColumnWidth,\n            int trailingPadding = 32)\n        {\n            if (item == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(item));\n            return paddingLeft \u002B (item.Depth * indentWidth) \u002B glyphColumnWidth \u002B textWidth \u002B trailingPadding;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        private void RecalculateContentWidth()\n        {\n            var rows = _state.VisibleRows;\n            int maxEstimatedW = 200;\n            for (int i = 0; i \u003C rows.Count; i\u002B\u002B)\n            {\n                var row = rows[i];\n                int textWidth = (_measureCache.TryGetValue(row.UniqueKey, out var cached) \u0026\u0026 cached.MeasuredFontGeneration == _fontGeneration)\n                    ? GetMeasuredRowTextWidth(row, cached)\n                    : (row.EstimatedCharLength * _avgCharWidth);\n\n                int rowWidth = _paddingLeft \u002B (row.Depth * _indentWidth) \u002B _glyphColumnWidth \u002B textWidth \u002B 32;\n                if (rowWidth \u003E maxEstimatedW)\n                    maxEstimatedW = rowWidth;\n            }\n\n            _maxContentWidth = maxEstimatedW;\n            UpdateScrollBars();\n        }\n\n        private int GetMeasuredRowTextWidth(DomTreeItem item, RowMeasureCache cache)\n        {\n            bool includeCollapsedSuffix = item.HasChildren \u0026\u0026 !_state.IsExpanded(item.UniqueKey);\n            return cache.OpenTotalWidth \u002B (includeCollapsedSuffix ? cache.CollapsedSuffixTotalWidth : 0);\n        }\n\n        private RowMeasureCache EnsureItemMeasured(Graphics g, DomTreeItem item)\n        {\n            if (_measureCache.TryGetValue(item.UniqueKey, out var existing) \u0026\u0026\n                existing.MeasuredFontGeneration == _fontGeneration)\n            {\n                return existing;\n            }\n\n            const TextFormatFlags measureFlags = TextFormatFlags.NoPadding | TextFormatFlags.SingleLine | TextFormatFlags.NoPrefix;\n\n            var openParts = item.OpenParts;\n