      "UserPrompt": "Please migrate all of the above logic into BrowserAutomationFramework and refactor TestBedApp to consume the new DLL APIs",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\n### Summary of Migrated Logic \u0026 Refactoring\n\n1. **Server Lifecycle \u0026 Active Client State (\u0060AutomationServer\u0060 \u0026 \u0060BrowserClient\u0060)**:\n   - Implemented \u0060IDisposable\u0060, \u0060IsRunning\u0060, \u0060ExclusiveTabMode\u0060, \u0060ActiveClient\u0060, \u0060OnActiveClientChanged\u0060, and \u0060OnClientMetadataUpdated\u0060 in \u0060AutomationServer\u0060, plus internal \u0060CancellationTokenSource\u0060 management so callers do not need external cancellation tokens or UI polling timers.\n   - Added \u0060BrowserClient.ResolveDomRoot(...)\u0060 to resolve the active DOM tree root directly from the client.\n2. **DOM Tree Virtualization Math, Measurement Cache \u0026 Syntax Colors (\u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060 \u0026 \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060)**:\n   - Added \u0060DomTokenColorExtensions.GetDefaultRgb(...)\u0060, \u0060DomRowMeasureCache\u0060, and \u0060DomScrollBarMetrics\u0060 to \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\u0060.\n   - Migrated row token width caching (\u0060EnsureItemMeasured\u0060), content width calculation (\u0060RecalculateContentWidth\u0060), two-pass scrollbar visibility/range calculation (\u0060CalculateScrollBarMetrics\u0060), visible row range calculation (\u0060GetVisibleRowRange\u0060), and mouse wheel scrolling (\u0060ApplyMouseWheel\u0060) into \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060.\n   - Refactored \u0060TestBedApp.Controls.DomTreeView\u0060 to delegate all measurement caching and scroll math to \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060.\n3. **Reverse Engineering View Mode \u0026 Validation Helpers (\u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060, \u0060SiteResourceItem\u0060, \u0060AutomationProject\u0060, \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060, \u0060ScrapeResult\u0060)**:\n   - Added \u0060SiteDumpViewMode\u0060 (\u0060SelectedResource\u0060, \u0060CombinedHtml\u0060, \u0060CombinedCss\u0060, \u0060CombinedJavaScript\u0060, \u0060CombinedAll\u0060) and updated \u0060SiteDumpResult.GetViewContent\u0060 / \u0060SaveViewContentToFile\u0060 / \u0060GetDefaultViewMode\u0060 so unselected resources return empty strings rather than falling back to the full combined dump.\n   - Added \u0060AutomationProject.HasActiveSequences\u0060, \u0060AutomationProject.HasActiveScrapes\u0060, \u0060AutomationProject.GetSequenceDropdownOptions\u0060, \u0060AutomationProject.ResolveSequenceDropdownSelection\u0060, \u0060ScrapeDefinition.HasFields\u0060, \u0060ScrapeResult.HasRecords\u0060, and \u0060SiteDumpResult.HasResources\u0060.\n4. **File Association \u0026 Utility Cleanup (\u0060FileAssociationHelper\u0060 \u0026 \u0060ReThemer\u0060)**:\n   - Migrated the Windows Registry file association logic to \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.Utils.FileAssociationHelper\u0060 and turned \u0060TestBedApp.Utils.FileAssociationHelper\u0060 into a thin wrapper.\n   - Removed the unused \u0060RestartExplorer()\u0060 method from \u0060TestBedApp.Utils.ReThemer\u0060.\n   - Refactored \u0060TestBedApp.MainForm\u0060 to consume the new DLL APIs and removed \u0060_cts\u0060 and \u0060_clientRefreshTimer\u0060.\n\n### How to Test\n1. Build the solution (\u0060dotnet build\u0060) and verify both \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 and \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 compile with zero warnings or errors.\n2. Launch \u0060TestBedApp\u0060, start and stop the server, switch tabs via the Chrome Extension list, inspect the DOM tree (scrolling, expanding/collapsing, selecting elements), configure/run scrapes, and run Reverse Engineering dumps.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Utils\\FileAssociationHelper.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\nusing System;\nusing System.Runtime.InteropServices;\nusing System.Runtime.Versioning;\nusing Microsoft.Win32;\n\nnamespace BrowserAutomationFramework.Utils\n{\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Provides Windows shell file-extension association utilities for registering project file types with an application executable.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    [SupportedOSPlatform(\u0022windows\u0022)]\n    public static class FileAssociationHelper\n    {\n        [DllImport(\u0022shell32.dll\u0022, CharSet = CharSet.Auto, SetLastError = true)]\n        private static extern void SHChangeNotify(uint wEventId, uint uFlags, IntPtr dwItem1, IntPtr dwItem2);\n\n        private const uint SHCNE_ASSOCCHANGED = 0x08000000;\n        private const uint SHCNF_IDLIST = 0x0000;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Ensures that the specified file extension is associated with the given ProgID and application executable in the current user\u0027s Windows Registry.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022extension\u0022\u003EThe file extension including the leading period (e.g., \u003Cc\u003E\u0022.baf\u0022\u003C/c\u003E).\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022progId\u0022\u003EThe programmatic identifier for the file type.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022description\u0022\u003EThe human-readable description of the file type.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022applicationFilePath\u0022\u003EThe full path to the application executable that opens the file.\u003C/param\u003E\n        public static void EnsureAssociation(string extension, string progId, string description, string applicationFilePath)\n        {\n            if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())\n                return;\n\n            try\n            {\n                bool needsUpdate = false;\n\n                using (var key = Registry.CurrentUser.OpenSubKey($@\u0022Software\\Classes\\{extension}\u0022))\n                {\n                    if (key?.GetValue(\u0022\u0022) as string != progId) needsUpdate = true;\n                }\n\n                using (var key = Registry.CurrentUser.OpenSubKey($@\u0022Software\\Classes\\{progId}\\shell\\open\\command\u0022))\n                {\n                    string expectedCommand = $\u0022\\\u0022{applicationFilePath}\\\u0022 \\\u0022%1\\\u0022\u0022;\n                    if (key?.GetValue(\u0022\u0022) as string != expectedCommand) needsUpdate = true;\n                }\n\n                if (!needsUpdate) return;\n\n                using (var key = Registry.CurrentUser.CreateSubKey($@\u0022Software\\Classes\\{extension}\u0022))\n                {\n                    key.SetValue(\u0022\u0022, progId);\n                }\n\n                using (var key = Registry.CurrentUser.CreateSubKey($@\u0022Software\\Classes\\{progId}\u0022))\n                {\n                    key.SetValue(\u0022\u0022, description);\n                }\n\n                using (var key = Registry.CurrentUser.CreateSubKey($@\u0022Software\\Classes\\{progId}\\DefaultIcon\u0022))\n                {\n                    key.SetValue(\u0022\u0022, $\u0022\\\u0022{applicationFilePath}\\\u0022,0\u0022);\n                }\n\n                using (var key = Registry.CurrentUser.CreateSubKey($@\u0022Software\\Classes\\{progId}\\shell\\open\\command\u0022))\n                {\n                    key.SetValue(\u0022\u0022, $\u0022\\\u0022{applicationFilePath}\\\u0022 \\\u0022%1\\\u0022\u0022);\n                }\n\n                SHChangeNotify(SHCNE_ASSOCCHANGED, SHCNF_IDLIST, IntPtr.Zero, IntPtr.Zero);\n            }\n            catch\n            {\n                // Silently ignore if registry permissions are restricted\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\AutomationProject.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets whether this project has valid URL match rules configured (either \u003Csee cref=\u0022MatchAnySite\u0022/\u003E is true or at least one URL is present in \u003Csee cref=\u0022MatchUrls\u0022/\u003E).\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public bool HasValidMatchRules =\u003E MatchAnySite || (MatchUrls != null \u0026\u0026 MatchUrls.Any(u =\u003E !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(u)));\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets whether this project has at least one active \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationSequence\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public bool HasActiveSequences =\u003E Sequences != null \u0026\u0026 Sequences.Any(s =\u003E s.IsActive);\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets whether this project has at least one active \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeDefinition\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public bool HasActiveScrapes =\u003E Scrapes != null \u0026\u0026 Scrapes.Any(s =\u003E s.IsActive);\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets whether this project has valid URL match rules configured (either \u003Csee cref=\u0022MatchAnySite\u0022/\u003E is true or at least one URL is present in \u003Csee cref=\u0022MatchUrls\u0022/\u003E).\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public bool HasValidMatchRules =\u003E MatchAnySite || (MatchUrls != null \u0026\u0026 MatchUrls.Any(u =\u003E !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(u)));\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns the names of all configured \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationSequence\u0022/\u003E items in the project.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public IReadOnlyList\u003Cstring\u003E GetSequenceNames()\n        {\n            return Sequences\n                .Where(s =\u003E !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(s.Name))\n                .Select(s =\u003E s.Name)\n                .ToList();\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns the names of all configured \u003Csee cref=\u0022AutomationSequence\u0022/\u003E items in the project.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public IReadOnlyList\u003Cstring\u003E GetSequenceNames()\n        {\n            return Sequences\n                .Where(s =\u003E !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(s.Name))\n                .Select(s =\u003E s.Name)\n                .ToList();\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns a list of sequence names prefixed with \u003Cparamref name=\u0022noneLabel\u0022/\u003E suitable for populating pre/post-scrape sequence dropdown controls.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public IReadOnlyList\u003Cstring\u003E GetSequenceDropdownOptions(string noneLabel = \u0022(None)\u0022)\n        {\n            var options = new List\u003Cstring\u003E(Sequences.Count \u002B 1) { noneLabel };\n            options.AddRange(GetSequenceNames());\n            return options;\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Resolves a configured sequence name against the sequences currently present in this project, returning \u003Cparamref name=\u0022noneLabel\u0022/\u003E if not found.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public string ResolveSequenceDropdownSelection(string? sequenceName, string noneLabel = \u0022(None)\u0022)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(sequenceName))\n                return noneLabel;\n\n            string trimmed = sequenceName.Trim();\n            bool exists = Sequences.Any(s =\u003E string.Equals(s.Name, trimmed, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));\n            return exists ? trimmed : noneLabel;\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\ScrapeDefinition.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets or sets whether duplicate rows should be filtered out across pages.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022deduplicateRows\u0022)]\n        public bool DeduplicateRows { get; set; } = false;\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets or sets whether duplicate rows should be filtered out across pages.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonPropertyName(\u0022deduplicateRows\u0022)]\n        public bool DeduplicateRows { get; set; } = false;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets whether this scrape definition has at least one \u003Csee cref=\u0022ScrapeField\u0022/\u003E configured.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public bool HasFields =\u003E Fields != null \u0026\u0026 Fields.Count \u003E 0;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\ScrapeResult.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the total number of records in \u003Csee cref=\u0022Records\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public int RecordCount =\u003E Records.Count;\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the total number of records in \u003Csee cref=\u0022Records\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public int RecordCount =\u003E Records.Count;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets whether this scrape result contains at least one extracted record.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public bool HasRecords =\u003E Records != null \u0026\u0026 Records.Count \u003E 0;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\SiteResourceItem.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Dumps all HTML, CSS, and JavaScript assets.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        All\n    }\n\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Represents a single HTML, CSS, or JavaScript resource captured during a \u003Csee cref=\u0022ReverseEngineering.SiteDumper\u0022/\u003E operation.\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Dumps all HTML, CSS, and JavaScript assets.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        All\n    }\n\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Specifies the active viewer mode when inspecting or exporting a \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpResult\u0022/\u003E.\n    /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n    public enum SiteDumpViewMode\n    {\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Displays or exports an individual selected \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteResourceItem\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        SelectedResource,\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Displays or exports the combined HTML source across the document and iframes.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        CombinedHtml,\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Displays or exports the combined CSS source across all stylesheets.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        CombinedCss,\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Displays or exports the combined JavaScript source across all scripts.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        CombinedJavaScript,\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Displays or exports the full combined summary across HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        CombinedAll\n    }\n\n    /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n    /// Represents a single HTML, CSS, or JavaScript resource captured during a \u003Csee cref=\u0022ReverseEngineering.SiteDumper\u0022/\u003E operation.\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\SiteDumpResult.cs**\n\u0060\u0060\u0060cs\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the total number of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript resources captured in this dump.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public int TotalResourceCount =\u003E HtmlResources.Count \u002B CssResources.Count \u002B JavaScriptResources.Count;\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets the total number of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript resources captured in this dump.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public int TotalResourceCount =\u003E HtmlResources.Count \u002B CssResources.Count \u002B JavaScriptResources.Count;\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Gets whether this site dump contains at least one captured HTML, CSS, or JavaScript resource.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        [JsonIgnore]\n        public bool HasResources =\u003E TotalResourceCount \u003E 0;\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Resolves the source text and suggested export filename for either a specific \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022/\u003E or a combined \u003Cparamref name=\u0022viewType\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022viewType\u0022\u003EThe combined dump type to view if \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022/\u003E is null.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022\u003EAn optional individual resource item to view instead of combined output.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022suggestedFileName\u0022\u003EOutputs the recommended filename for saving the returned content.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Creturns\u003EThe resolved resource or combined source text.\u003C/returns\u003E\n        public string GetViewContent(SiteDumpType? viewType, SiteResourceItem? selectedResource, out string suggestedFileName)\n        {\n            if (selectedResource != null)\n            {\n                suggestedFileName = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedResource.Name) ? \u0022resource.txt\u0022 : selectedResource.Name;\n                return selectedResource.Content;\n            }\n\n            var resolvedType = viewType ?? DumpType;\n            suggestedFileName = GetSuggestedCombinedFileName(resolvedType);\n            return GetCombinedContent(resolvedType);\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Returns the recommended initial \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpViewMode\u0022/\u003E to display after this dump completes.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public SiteDumpViewMode GetDefaultViewMode()\n        {\n            return DumpType switch\n            {\n                SiteDumpType.Html =\u003E SiteDumpViewMode.CombinedHtml,\n                SiteDumpType.Css =\u003E SiteDumpViewMode.CombinedCss,\n                SiteDumpType.JavaScript =\u003E SiteDumpViewMode.CombinedJavaScript,\n                _ =\u003E HasResources ? SiteDumpViewMode.SelectedResource : SiteDumpViewMode.CombinedAll\n            };\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Resolves the source text and suggested export filename for the specified \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpViewMode\u0022/\u003E and optional \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022viewMode\u0022\u003EThe active viewer mode.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022\u003EThe currently selected resource when \u003Cparamref name=\u0022viewMode\u0022/\u003E is \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpViewMode.SelectedResource\u0022/\u003E.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022suggestedFileName\u0022\u003EOutputs the recommended filename for saving the returned content.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Creturns\u003EThe resolved resource or combined source text.\u003C/returns\u003E\n        public string GetViewContent(SiteDumpViewMode viewMode, SiteResourceItem? selectedResource, out string suggestedFileName)\n        {\n            if (viewMode == SiteDumpViewMode.SelectedResource)\n            {\n                if (selectedResource == null)\n                {\n                    suggestedFileName = \u0022resource.txt\u0022;\n                    return string.Empty;\n                }\n\n                suggestedFileName = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedResource.Name) ? \u0022resource.txt\u0022 : selectedResource.Name;\n                return selectedResource.Content;\n            }\n\n            var resolvedType = viewMode switch\n            {\n                SiteDumpViewMode.CombinedHtml =\u003E SiteDumpType.Html,\n                SiteDumpViewMode.CombinedCss =\u003E SiteDumpType.Css,\n                SiteDumpViewMode.CombinedJavaScript =\u003E SiteDumpType.JavaScript,\n                _ =\u003E DumpType\n            };\n\n            suggestedFileName = GetSuggestedCombinedFileName(resolvedType);\n            return GetCombinedContent(resolvedType);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Resolves the source text and suggested export filename for either a specific \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022/\u003E or a combined \u003Cparamref name=\u0022viewType\u0022/\u003E.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022viewType\u0022\u003EThe combined dump type to view if \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022/\u003E is null.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022\u003EAn optional individual resource item to view instead of combined output.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Cparam name=\u0022suggestedFileName\u0022\u003EOutputs the recommended filename for saving the returned content.\u003C/param\u003E\n        /// \u003Creturns\u003EThe resolved resource or combined source text.\u003C/returns\u003E\n        public string GetViewContent(SiteDumpType? viewType, SiteResourceItem? selectedResource, out string suggestedFileName)\n        {\n            if (selectedResource != null)\n            {\n                suggestedFileName = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedResource.Name) ? \u0022resource.txt\u0022 : selectedResource.Name;\n                return selectedResource.Content;\n            }\n\n            var resolvedType = viewType ?? DumpType;\n            suggestedFileName = GetSuggestedCombinedFileName(resolvedType);\n            return GetCombinedContent(resolvedType);\n        }\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Saves the resolved view content (either a specific \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022/\u003E or the combined output for \u003Cparamref name=\u0022viewType\u0022/\u003E) to the specified file path.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void SaveViewContentToFile(string filePath, SiteDumpType? viewType, SiteResourceItem? selectedResource)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(filePath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022File path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(filePath));\n\n            if (selectedResource != null)\n            {\n                selectedResource.SaveToFile(filePath);\n                return;\n            }\n\n            SaveCombinedToFile(filePath, viewType ?? DumpType);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Asynchronously saves the resolved view content (either a specific \u003Cparamref name=\u0022selectedResource\u0022/\u003E or the combined output for \u003Cparamref name=\u0022viewType\u0022/\u003E) to the specified file path.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task SaveViewContentToFileAsync(\n            string filePath,\n            SiteDumpType? viewType,\n            SiteResourceItem? selectedResource,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(filePath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022File path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(filePath));\n\n            if (selectedResource != null)\n            {\n                return selectedResource.SaveToFileAsync(filePath, cancellationToken);\n            }\n\n            return SaveCombinedToFileAsync(filePath, viewType ?? DumpType, cancellationToken);\n        }\n==== REPLACE\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Saves the resolved view content for the specified \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpViewMode\u0022/\u003E to the given file path.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public void SaveViewContentToFile(string filePath, SiteDumpViewMode viewMode, SiteResourceItem? selectedResource)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(filePath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022File path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(filePath));\n\n            if (viewMode == SiteDumpViewMode.SelectedResource)\n            {\n                if (selectedResource == null)\n                    throw new InvalidOperationException(\u0022No resource is selected to save.\u0022);\n\n                selectedResource.SaveToFile(filePath);\n                return;\n            }\n\n            var resolvedType = viewMode switch\n            {\n                SiteDumpViewMode.CombinedHtml =\u003E SiteDumpType.Html,\n                SiteDumpViewMode.CombinedCss =\u003E SiteDumpType.Css,\n                SiteDumpViewMode.CombinedJavaScript =\u003E SiteDumpType.JavaScript,\n                _ =\u003E DumpType\n            };\n\n            SaveCombinedToFile(filePath, resolvedType);\n        }\n\n        /// \u003Csummary\u003E\n        /// Asynchronously saves the resolved view content for the specified \u003Csee cref=\u0022SiteDumpViewMode\u0022/\u003E to the given file path.\n        /// \u003C/summary\u003E\n        public Task SaveViewContentToFileAsync(\n            string filePath,\n            SiteDumpViewMode viewMode,\n            SiteResourceItem? selectedResource,\n            CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\n        {\n            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(filePath))\n                throw new ArgumentException(\u0022File path cannot be empty.\u0022, nameof(filePat