    {
      "Id": "5c24e066",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-27T23:33:18.4137737-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\nPlease study this codebase. I want you to document ANY code that is still in the testbed winforms project that isnt strictly UI wrapper code. I want to ensure all the real logic of the browser automation framework is inside the dll. If you find any code in the winforms app that can be migrated to the dll project, please document that. We want to ensure that the winforms app is just a UI wrapper around the dll. This will ensure that other developers can easily work with the framework. Please also ignore all code files in the utils folder in the winforms project, for as those dont need to be migrated at all and can stay where theyre atl.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nHere is a complete audit of the \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 WinForms project (excluding \u0060TestBedApp\\utils\\*\u0060) documenting all remaining logic that is not strictly UI wrapper code and can be migrated into the \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 DLL.\n\n### 1. \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060\n\nAlthough \u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060 and \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060 already hold the tree index and scroll state, \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060 still contains non-GDI layout math, hit-testing rules, and keyboard/mouse navigation logic that can be moved into \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060:\n\n- **Row Render Geometry \u0026 Viewport Culling Math (\u0060OnPaint\u0060, lines 409\u2013481)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060DomTreeView.OnPaint\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Computes per-row pixel coordinates (\u0060rowY\u0060, \u0060centerY\u0060, \u0060indentX\u0060, \u0060textStartX\u0060, \u0060textY\u0060), selection/hover highlight bounds (\u0060textStartX - 2\u0060, \u0060textTotalW \u002B 6\u0060), hierarchy guide-line X/Y segments across ancestor depths, expand/collapse \u0060\u002B/-\u0060 glyph box bounds (\u0060boxLeft\u0060, \u0060boxTop\u0060, \u0060midX\u0060, \u0060midY\u0060, \u0060signMargin\u0060), and horizontal token visibility culling (\u0060curX \u002B w \u003E= view.Left\u0060 and \u0060curX \u003C= view.Right\u0060).\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060). A platform-agnostic \u0060DomRowRenderLayout\u0060 struct and token-visibility iterator can compute all row geometry in the DLL so \u0060DomTreeView.OnPaint\u0060 only issues GDI\u002B draw calls.\n- **Keyboard Navigation \u0026 Page-Step Calculation (\u0060OnKeyDown\u0060, lines 569\u2013632)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060DomTreeView.OnKeyDown\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Calculates \u0060pageRows = Math.Max(1, viewportHeight / _itemHeight)\u0060 and implements row clamping and state transitions for \u0060Up\u0060, \u0060Down\u0060, \u0060PageUp\u0060, \u0060PageDown\u0060, \u0060Home\u0060, \u0060End\u0060, \u0060Left\u0060, and \u0060Right\u0060 navigation keys.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 (e.g., a unified \u0060NavigateByKey(...)\u0060 method that takes a platform-independent navigation command enum and viewport height, returning whether expansion or selection changed and the new row index).\n- **Mouse Click / Double-Click Interaction Rules (\u0060OnMouseDown\u0060 \u0026 \u0060OnMouseDoubleClick\u0060, lines 491\u2013539)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060DomTreeView.OnMouseDown\u0060 and \u0060DomTreeView.OnMouseDoubleClick\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Determines whether a click at \u0060(x, y)\u0060 hits a valid row, whether a left-click hits the expand glyph (toggling expansion vs. selecting the row), and whether a double-click outside the expand glyph on a parent node should toggle expansion.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 (e.g., \u0060HandlePointerDown(...)\u0060 and \u0060HandlePointerDoubleClick(...)\u0060 methods).\n- **Font \u0026 Row Metric Calculation (\u0060UpdateMetrics\u0060, lines 163\u2013173)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060DomTreeView.UpdateMetrics\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Computes \u0060_itemHeight = Math.Max(_codeFont.Height \u002B ScaleDpi(6), ScaleDpi(24))\u0060 and derives \u0060avgCharWidth = Math.Max(6, (int)Math.Ceiling(charSample.Width / 10.0))\u0060 from a 10-character \u0060\u0022MMMMMMMMMM\u0022\u0060 sample.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 (e.g., \u0060UpdateFontMetrics(int fontHeight, int tenCharSampleWidth, float dpiScale)\u0060).\n- **DOM Tree Theme Color Palette (\u0060DomTreeView\u0060 fields, lines 21\u201333)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 class fields (\u0060_selBgColor\u0060, \u0060_hoverBgColor\u0060, \u0060_borderColor\u0060, \u0060_glyphFillColor\u0060, \u0060_linePen\u0060, \u0060_glyphBorderPen\u0060).\n- **What It Does:** Hardcodes dark-mode RGB values for tree chrome while syntax token RGB values live in \u0060DomTokenColorExtensions.GetDefaultRgb()\u0060 inside the DLL.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060DomTokenColorExtensions\u0060 / \u0060DomTreeThemePalette\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060.\n\n### 2. \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060\n\nWhile most domain models and engines live in the DLL, \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 still performs several pieces of framework orchestration, DOM node resolution, and state coordination that can be migrated to \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060:\n\n- **Separated Engine Instances \u0026 Event Forwarding (\u0060MainForm\u0060 constructor, lines 102\u2013157)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060MainForm()\u0060 constructor\n- **What It Does:** Instantiates \u0060_runner = new AutomationRunner()\u0060, \u0060_scraper = new DataScraper(_runner)\u0060, and \u0060_siteDumper = new SiteDumper()\u0060 separately and manually bridges events (\u0060_runner.OnScrapeCompleted\u0060 -\u003E \u0060DisplayScrapeResult\u0060). Furthermore, when \u0060AutomationRunner\u0060 executes \u0060AutomationActionType.Scrape\u0060 or \u0060AutomationActionType.DumpSite\u0060 steps internally (\u0060AutomationRunner.cs\u0060, lines 98 and 154), it instantiates throwaway \u0060new DataScraper(this)\u0060 and \u0060new SiteDumper()\u0060 instances rather than using shared instances, meaning granular events on \u0060_scraper\u0060 (\u0060OnRateLimitDetected\u0060, \u0060OnPageTurnDelay\u0060, \u0060OnScrapePageCompleted\u0060) and \u0060_siteDumper\u0060 (\u0060OnDumpStarted\u0060, \u0060OnDumpFailed\u0060) do not fire during automation sequence steps.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060AutomationRunner\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Automation\\AutomationRunner.cs\u0060) should own or accept shared \u0060DataScraper\u0060 and \u0060SiteDumper\u0060 properties so all scrape and site-dump lifecycle events flow through a single unified pipeline.\n- **Active-Client Event Filtering \u0026 Auto-Refresh Orchestration (\u0060Server_OnClientConnected\u0060, lines 252\u2013322)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060MainForm.Server_OnClientConnected\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Subscribes to every connected \u0060BrowserClient\u0060\u0027s \u0060OnPageLoaded\u0060, \u0060OnDomChanged\u0060, \u0060OnHighlightedElementRemoved\u0060, \u0060OnElementClicked\u0060, \u0060OnModeChanged\u0060, and \u0060OnStreamDataReceived\u0060 events, and repeatedly checks \u0060if (lstClients.SelectedItem is BrowserClient selectedClient \u0026\u0026 selectedClient.InstanceId == client.InstanceId)\u0060 to decide whether to trigger a DOM snapshot refresh or update the active view.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\AutomationServer.cs\u0060). Because \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 already manages \u0060ActiveClient\u0060, it can expose server-level events for all clients and active-client-filtered events (e.g., \u0060OnActiveClientPageLoaded\u0060, \u0060OnActiveClientDomChanged\u0060, \u0060OnActiveClientElementClicked\u0060, \u0060OnActiveClientHighlightedElementRemoved\u0060, \u0060OnClientStreamDataReceived\u0060), eliminating per-client event subscription boilerplate in the UI.\n- **Element Selection \u0026 Debounced Highlighting Logic (\u0060TvDom_AfterSelect\u0060, lines 456\u2013470)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060MainForm.TvDom_AfterSelect\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Checks \u0060if (domNode != null)\u0060, calls \u0060client.RecordUserDomSelection(domNode.Path)\u0060, and checks \u0060if (domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022 \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrEmpty(domNode.Path))\u0060 before calling \u0060client.HighlightElementDebounced(domNode.Path)\u0060.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\BrowserClient.cs\u0060), e.g., \u0060client.SelectDomNode(DomNode? domNode, bool highlightInBrowser = true, int debounceMs = 25)\u0060.\n- **\u0060DomNode\u0060-Based Action \u0026 Extraction Overloads (\u0060MnuClickElement_Click\u0060, \u0060MnuSetValue_Click\u0060, \u0060MnuQuickScrapeText_Click\u0060, lines 479\u2013491, 594\u2013608, 1364\u20131379)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060MainForm\u0060 context menu handlers\n- **What It Does:** Extracts \u0060domNode.Path\u0060 and \u0060domNode.GetSuggestedExtractionType()\u0060 in the UI before calling \u0060client.ClickReactElementAsync(domNode.Path)\u0060, \u0060client.SetReactInputValueAsync(domNode.Path, value)\u0060, or \u0060client.ScrapeElementAsync(domNode.Path, extType)\u0060.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060ReactExtensions\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Extensions\\ReactExtensions.cs\u0060) can provide overloads accepting a \u0060DomNode\u0060 directly (e.g., \u0060client.ClickReactElementAsync(DomNode node)\u0060, \u0060client.SetReactInputValueAsync(DomNode node, string value)\u0060, and \u0060client.ScrapeElementAsync(DomNode node, ScrapeExtractionType? extractionType = null)\u0060).\n- **Duplicate Event Subscription \u0026 Tab Switch Pre-Checks (\u0060InitializeExtensionTabsSidebarUi\u0060 \u0026 \u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060, lines 715\u2013727, 868\u2013900)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060MainForm.InitializeExtensionTabsSidebarUi\u0060 and \u0060MainForm.SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060\n- **What It Does:**\n\n- Lines 715\u2013727 subscribe \u0060chkExclusiveTab.CheckedChanged\u0060 twice to the exact same lambda.\n- \u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060 duplicates the \u0060!tab.CanInject\u0060 validation that \u0060AutomationServer.SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(BrowserTabInfo, ...)\u0060 already performs.\n\n### How to Proceed\n\nIf you would like me to migrate any or all of the items documented above into the \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 DLL and update \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 to call the new DLL APIs, let me know and I will apply the changes.",
      "ModelExplanation": "Here is a complete audit of the \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 WinForms project (excluding \u0060TestBedApp\\utils\\*\u0060) documenting all remaining logic that is not strictly UI wrapper code and can be migrated into the \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 DLL.\n\n### 1. \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060\n\nAlthough \u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060 and \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060 already hold the tree index and scroll state, \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060 still contains non-GDI layout math, hit-testing rules, and keyboard/mouse navigation logic that can be moved into \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060:\n\n- **Row Render Geometry \u0026 Viewport Culling Math (\u0060OnPaint\u0060, lines 409\u2013481)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060DomTreeView.OnPaint\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Computes per-row pixel coordinates (\u0060rowY\u0060, \u0060centerY\u0060, \u0060indentX\u0060, \u0060textStartX\u0060, \u0060textY\u0060), selection/hover highlight bounds (\u0060textStartX - 2\u0060, \u0060textTotalW \u002B 6\u0060), hierarchy guide-line X/Y segments across ancestor depths, expand/collapse \u0060\u002B/-\u0060 glyph box bounds (\u0060boxLeft\u0060, \u0060boxTop\u0060, \u0060midX\u0060, \u0060midY\u0060, \u0060signMargin\u0060), and horizontal token visibility culling (\u0060curX \u002B w \u003E= view.Left\u0060 and \u0060curX \u003C= view.Right\u0060).\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060). A platform-agnostic \u0060DomRowRenderLayout\u0060 struct and token-visibility iterator can compute all row geometry in the DLL so \u0060DomTreeView.OnPaint\u0060 only issues GDI\u002B draw calls.\n- **Keyboard Navigation \u0026 Page-Step Calculation (\u0060OnKeyDown\u0060, lines 569\u2013632)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060DomTreeView.OnKeyDown\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Calculates \u0060pageRows = Math.Max(1, viewportHeight / _itemHeight)\u0060 and implements row clamping and state transitions for \u0060Up\u0060, \u0060Down\u0060, \u0060PageUp\u0060, \u0060PageDown\u0060, \u0060Home\u0060, \u0060End\u0060, \u0060Left\u0060, and \u0060Right\u0060 navigation keys.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 (e.g., a unified \u0060NavigateByKey(...)\u0060 method that takes a platform-independent navigation command enum and viewport height, returning whether expansion or selection changed and the new row index).\n- **Mouse Click / Double-Click Interaction Rules (\u0060OnMouseDown\u0060 \u0026 \u0060OnMouseDoubleClick\u0060, lines 491\u2013539)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060DomTreeView.OnMouseDown\u0060 and \u0060DomTreeView.OnMouseDoubleClick\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Determines whether a click at \u0060(x, y)\u0060 hits a valid row, whether a left-click hits the expand glyph (toggling expansion vs. selecting the row), and whether a double-click outside the expand glyph on a parent node should toggle expansion.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 (e.g., \u0060HandlePointerDown(...)\u0060 and \u0060HandlePointerDoubleClick(...)\u0060 methods).\n- **Font \u0026 Row Metric Calculation (\u0060UpdateMetrics\u0060, lines 163\u2013173)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060DomTreeView.UpdateMetrics\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Computes \u0060_itemHeight = Math.Max(_codeFont.Height \u002B ScaleDpi(6), ScaleDpi(24))\u0060 and derives \u0060avgCharWidth = Math.Max(6, (int)Math.Ceiling(charSample.Width / 10.0))\u0060 from a 10-character \u0060\u0022MMMMMMMMMM\u0022\u0060 sample.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 (e.g., \u0060UpdateFontMetrics(int fontHeight, int tenCharSampleWidth, float dpiScale)\u0060).\n- **DOM Tree Theme Color Palette (\u0060DomTreeView\u0060 fields, lines 21\u201333)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 class fields (\u0060_selBgColor\u0060, \u0060_hoverBgColor\u0060, \u0060_borderColor\u0060, \u0060_glyphFillColor\u0060, \u0060_linePen\u0060, \u0060_glyphBorderPen\u0060).\n- **What It Does:** Hardcodes dark-mode RGB values for tree chrome while syntax token RGB values live in \u0060DomTokenColorExtensions.GetDefaultRgb()\u0060 inside the DLL.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060DomTokenColorExtensions\u0060 / \u0060DomTreeThemePalette\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060.\n\n### 2. \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060\n\nWhile most domain models and engines live in the DLL, \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 still performs several pieces of framework orchestration, DOM node resolution, and state coordination that can be migrated to \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060:\n\n- **Separated Engine Instances \u0026 Event Forwarding (\u0060MainForm\u0060 constructor, lines 102\u2013157)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060MainForm()\u0060 constructor\n- **What It Does:** Instantiates \u0060_runner = new AutomationRunner()\u0060, \u0060_scraper = new DataScraper(_runner)\u0060, and \u0060_siteDumper = new SiteDumper()\u0060 separately and manually bridges events (\u0060_runner.OnScrapeCompleted\u0060 -\u003E \u0060DisplayScrapeResult\u0060). Furthermore, when \u0060AutomationRunner\u0060 executes \u0060AutomationActionType.Scrape\u0060 or \u0060AutomationActionType.DumpSite\u0060 steps internally (\u0060AutomationRunner.cs\u0060, lines 98 and 154), it instantiates throwaway \u0060new DataScraper(this)\u0060 and \u0060new SiteDumper()\u0060 instances rather than using shared instances, meaning granular events on \u0060_scraper\u0060 (\u0060OnRateLimitDetected\u0060, \u0060OnPageTurnDelay\u0060, \u0060OnScrapePageCompleted\u0060) and \u0060_siteDumper\u0060 (\u0060OnDumpStarted\u0060, \u0060OnDumpFailed\u0060) do not fire during automation sequence steps.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060AutomationRunner\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Automation\\AutomationRunner.cs\u0060) should own or accept shared \u0060DataScraper\u0060 and \u0060SiteDumper\u0060 properties so all scrape and site-dump lifecycle events flow through a single unified pipeline.\n- **Active-Client Event Filtering \u0026 Auto-Refresh Orchestration (\u0060Server_OnClientConnected\u0060, lines 252\u2013322)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060MainForm.Server_OnClientConnected\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Subscribes to every connected \u0060BrowserClient\u0060\u0027s \u0060OnPageLoaded\u0060, \u0060OnDomChanged\u0060, \u0060OnHighlightedElementRemoved\u0060, \u0060OnElementClicked\u0060, \u0060OnModeChanged\u0060, and \u0060OnStreamDataReceived\u0060 events, and repeatedly checks \u0060if (lstClients.SelectedItem is BrowserClient selectedClient \u0026\u0026 selectedClient.InstanceId == client.InstanceId)\u0060 to decide whether to trigger a DOM snapshot refresh or update the active view.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\AutomationServer.cs\u0060). Because \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 already manages \u0060ActiveClient\u0060, it can expose server-level events for all clients and active-client-filtered events (e.g., \u0060OnActiveClientPageLoaded\u0060, \u0060OnActiveClientDomChanged\u0060, \u0060OnActiveClientElementClicked\u0060, \u0060OnActiveClientHighlightedElementRemoved\u0060, \u0060OnClientStreamDataReceived\u0060), eliminating per-client event subscription boilerplate in the UI.\n- **Element Selection \u0026 Debounced Highlighting Logic (\u0060TvDom_AfterSelect\u0060, lines 456\u2013470)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060MainForm.TvDom_AfterSelect\u0060\n- **What It Does:** Checks \u0060if (domNode != null)\u0060, calls \u0060client.RecordUserDomSelection(domNode.Path)\u0060, and checks \u0060if (domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022 \u0026\u0026 !string.IsNullOrEmpty(domNode.Path))\u0060 before calling \u0060client.HighlightElementDebounced(domNode.Path)\u0060.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\BrowserClient.cs\u0060), e.g., \u0060client.SelectDomNode(DomNode? domNode, bool highlightInBrowser = true, int debounceMs = 25)\u0060.\n- **\u0060DomNode\u0060-Based Action \u0026 Extraction Overloads (\u0060MnuClickElement_Click\u0060, \u0060MnuSetValue_Click\u0060, \u0060MnuQuickScrapeText_Click\u0060, lines 479\u2013491, 594\u2013608, 1364\u20131379)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060MainForm\u0060 context menu handlers\n- **What It Does:** Extracts \u0060domNode.Path\u0060 and \u0060domNode.GetSuggestedExtractionType()\u0060 in the UI before calling \u0060client.ClickReactElementAsync(domNode.Path)\u0060, \u0060client.SetReactInputValueAsync(domNode.Path, value)\u0060, or \u0060client.ScrapeElementAsync(domNode.Path, extType)\u0060.\n- **Migration Target:** \u0060ReactExtensions\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Extensions\\ReactExtensions.cs\u0060) can provide overloads accepting a \u0060DomNode\u0060 directly (e.g., \u0060client.ClickReactElementAsync(DomNode node)\u0060, \u0060client.SetReactInputValueAsync(DomNode node, string value)\u0060, and \u0060client.ScrapeElementAsync(DomNode node, ScrapeExtractionType? extractionType = null)\u0060).\n- **Duplicate Event Subscription \u0026 Tab Switch Pre-Checks (\u0060InitializeExtensionTabsSidebarUi\u0060 \u0026 \u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060, lines 715\u2013727, 868\u2013900)**\n\n- **Current Location:** \u0060MainForm.InitializeExtensionTabsSidebarUi\u0060 and \u0060MainForm.SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060\n- **What It Does:**\n\n- Lines 715\u2013727 subscribe \u0060chkExclusiveTab.CheckedChanged\u0060 twice to the exact same lambda.\n- \u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060 duplicates the \u0060!tab.CanInject\u0060 validation that \u0060AutomationServer.SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(BrowserTabInfo, ...)\u0060 already performs.\n\n### How to Proceed\n\nIf you would like me to migrate any or all of the items documented above into the \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 DLL and update \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 to call the new DLL APIs, let me know and I will apply the changes.",
