    {
      "Id": "eb9454f6",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-27T23:40:18.3893893-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\nPlease study this codebase. I want you to document ANY code that is still in the testbed winforms project that isnt strictly UI wrapper code. I want to ensure all the real logic of the browser automation framework is inside the dll. If you find any code in the winforms app that can be migrated to the dll project, please document that. We want to ensure that the winforms app is just a UI wrapper around the dll. This will ensure that other developers can easily work with the framework. Please also ignore all code files in the utils folder in the winforms project, for as those dont need to be migrated at all and can stay where theyre atl.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nHere is a complete audit of \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 (ignoring \u0060TestBedApp\\utils\\*\u0060) documenting all remaining logic that is not strictly WinForms UI wrapper code and can be migrated into \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060.\n\n### Executive Summary\n\nMost of the core engine logic\u2014IPC transport (\u0060AutomationServer\u0060, \u0060BrowserClient\u0060), workflow execution (\u0060AutomationRunner\u0060), scraping (\u0060DataScraper\u0060, \u0060ScrapeBuilder\u0060, \u0060SelectorHelper\u0060), site dumping (\u0060SiteDumper\u0060), script/extension generation (\u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060, \u0060ChromeExtensionGenerator\u0060), and virtualized DOM tree state/geometry (\u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060, \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060)\u2014already lives in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060.\n\nHowever, several pieces of **session orchestration, state tracking, fallback branching, status formatting, and viewport geometry math** still reside in \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060 and \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060. Migrating the items below into \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060 will allow external developers to consume the framework with minimal boilerplate and make \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 a pure UI skin.\n\n### 1. \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060 \u2014 Non-UI Logic to Migrate\n\n#### A. Multi-Engine Orchestration \u0026 State Management (Lines 19\u201326, 89\u2013144, 159\u2013215)\n\n- **What is in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\u0060MainForm\u0060 manually instantiates, lifecycles, and coordinates four separate framework services plus result caches:\n\n- \u0060_server\u0060 (\u0060AutomationServer\u0060)\n- \u0060_project\u0060 (\u0060AutomationProject\u0060)\n- \u0060_runner\u0060 (\u0060AutomationRunner\u0060)\n- \u0060_scraper\u0060 (\u0060DataScraper\u0060)\n- \u0060_siteDumper\u0060 (\u0060SiteDumper\u0060)\n- \u0060_lastScrapeResult\u0060 (\u0060ScrapeResult?\u0060)\n- \u0060_lastSiteDumpResult\u0060 (\u0060SiteDumpResult?\u0060)\n- **Why it belongs in the DLL:**\nAny developer building a custom host (CLI, WPF, Avalonia, Web API, or WinForms) currently has to manually instantiate these classes, keep \u0060_server.ExclusiveTabMode\u0060 and Chrome Extension exports in sync when starting the server (\u0060BtnStart_Click\u0060), and store the latest \u0060ScrapeResult\u0060 and \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060 for export/inspection.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\nIntroduce a high-level facade/session controller (e.g., \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 or \u0060AutomationWorkspace\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060) that owns \u0060Project\u0060, \u0060Server\u0060, \u0060Runner\u0060, \u0060Scraper\u0060, \u0060SiteDumper\u0060, \u0060LastScrapeResult\u0060, and \u0060LastSiteDumpResult\u0060, and exposes \u0060StartServerAsync(port, ipcMode, syncExtension: true)\u0060 / \u0060StopServer()\u0060.\n\n#### B. Unified Log \u0026 Status Event Aggregation (Lines 93\u2013144, 178\u2013194)\n\n- **What is in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\u0060MainForm\u0060 subscribes to **25\u002B individual events** across \u0060_runner\u0060, \u0060_scraper\u0060, \u0060_siteDumper\u0060, and \u0060_server\u0060, manually formatting log category tags (\u0060[SYS]\u0060, \u0060[EXT]\u0060, \u0060[AUTO]\u0060, \u0060[AUTO-RX]\u0060, \u0060[SCRAPE]\u0060, \u0060[RATE-LIMIT 429]\u0060, \u0060[SCRAPE-ERR]\u0060, \u0060[REV-ENG]\u0060, \u0060[REV-ENG-ERR]\u0060, \u0060[STREAM \u003C- ...]\u0060, \u0060[TX -\u003E ...]\u0060, \u0060[RX \u003C- ...]\u0060) and assigning severity levels/colors.\n- **Why it belongs in the DLL:**\nFormatting raw command transmissions, stream outputs, client mode switches, and lifecycle events into structured log entries is framework telemetry logic.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\nAdd a unified event/logging pipeline in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\u0060 (e.g., \u0060AutomationLogEventArgs\u0060 with \u0060Timestamp\u0060, \u0060Category\u0060, \u0060Message\u0060, and \u0060AutomationLogLevel\u0060 enum: \u0060Info\u0060, \u0060Success\u0060, \u0060Warning\u0060, \u0060Error\u0060, \u0060CommandTx\u0060, \u0060CommandRx\u0060, \u0060Stream\u0060, \u0060Navigation\u0060, \u0060Scrape\u0060, \u0060ReverseEngineering\u0060).\n\n#### C. Chrome Extension Connection Status Formatting \u0026 Tab Switch Guard (Lines 857\u2013879, 938\u2013980)\n\n- **What is in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\n- \u0060UpdateExtensionStatusLabel(bool connected, int tabCount)\u0060 (lines 857\u2013879) manually pluralizes and builds the extension status string:\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\n$\u0022Extension: Connected ({tabCount} open tab{(tabCount == 1 ? \u0022\u0022 : \u0022s\u0022)})\u0022\n\u0022Extension: Waiting for connection...\u0022\n\u0022Extension: Server stopped\u0022\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n- \u0060LstBrowserTabs_SelectedIndexChanged\u0060 (lines 938\u2013948) manually checks \u0060selectedTab.IsAlreadyActiveClient(...)\u0060 before calling \u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060.\n- \u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060 (lines 959\u2013980) calls \u0060_server.SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(...)\u0060 and then manually checks \u0060if (existingClient != null \u0026\u0026 lstClients.SelectedItem == existingClient)\u0060 to decide whether a DOM refresh is needed.\n- **Why it belongs in the DLL:**\nOther status messages (\u0060PageLoadedEventArgs.GetStatusMessage()\u0060, \u0060ScrapeResult.GetStatusSummary()\u0060, \u0060SiteDumpResult.GetStatusSummary()\u0060) are already generated by the DLL. Furthermore, \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 already tracks \u0060IsRunning\u0060, \u0060IsExtensionConnected\u0060, \u0060ActiveClient\u0060, and \u0060ExclusiveTabMode\u0060.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\n\n- Add \u0060AutomationServer.GetExtensionStatusMessage()\u0060 (and a static helper for stopped state) in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\AutomationServer.cs\u0060.\n- Add \u0060skipIfAlreadyActive\u0060 parameter support directly to \u0060AutomationServer.SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(...)\u0060.\n\n#### D. DOM Node Resolution \u0026 Fallback Refresh Branching (Lines 354\u2013370, 502\u2013536, 1344\u20131361)\n\n- **What is in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\n- \u0060Server_OnActiveClientElementClicked\u0060 (lines 354\u2013370) checks if the middle-clicked path is already present in the tree (\u0060tvDom.SelectNodeByPath(e.Path)\u0060); if not, it falls back to fetching a fresh DOM snapshot (\u0060RefreshDomAsync(client, e.Path, hasTargetPath: true)\u0060).\n- \u0060GetCurrentRootDomNode()\u0060 (lines 1344\u20131345) manually chains \u0060(lstClients.SelectedItem as BrowserClient)?.ResolveDomRoot(tvDom.RootDomNode) ?? tvDom.RootDomNode\u0060.\n- \u0060BtnGeneralizeContainer_Click\u0060 (lines 1347\u20131361) and \u0060BtnHighlightContainer_Click\u0060 (lines 1363\u20131388) manually branch on whether a \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 is selected or if raw selector strings should be generalized/highlighted via \u0060SelectorHelper\u0060 / \u0060HighlightElementsAsync\u0060.\n- **Why it belongs in the DLL:**\n\u0060BrowserClient\u0060 already caches \u0060CurrentDomSnapshot\u0060 and \u0060CurrentDomRoot\u0060 and owns \u0060RefreshDomSnapshotCoalescedAsync\u0060. Deciding whether a clicked element path exists in the cached snapshot or requires a coalesced DOM refresh is client DOM state logic.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\n\n- Add a helper on \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 (or \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060) to resolve an element click against the current snapshot or automatically trigger \u0060RefreshDomSnapshotCoalescedAsync\u0060.\n- Add convenience overloads on \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 (e.g., \u0060GeneralizeContainerSelector(string rawSelector, ScrapeDefinition? definition = null)\u0060 and \u0060HighlightContainerAsync(string rawSelector, ScrapeDefinition? definition = null)\u0060) that automatically use \u0060client.ResolveDomRoot()\u0060 and handle the \u0060ScrapeDefinition != null\u0060 vs. ad-hoc selector branching.\n\n#### E. Client List Collection Synchronization (Lines 393\u2013421, 456\u2013488, 829\u2013855)\n\n- **What is in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\u0060UpsertClientInListUi\u0060, \u0060HandleClientRemovedFromUi\u0060, and \u0060RefreshClientListItemDisplay\u0060 manually iterate \u0060lstClients.Items\u0060 comparing \u0060item.InstanceId == client.InstanceId\u0060 to find indices to insert, replace, or remove. Meanwhile, \u0060AutomationServer.GetClientListDelta(...)\u0060 exists in the DLL (lines 285\u2013301 of \u0060AutomationServer.cs\u0060) but isn\u0027t used.\n- **Why it belongs in the DLL:**\nIndex lookup and list synchronization by \u0060InstanceId\u0060 can be exposed as clean helper methods on \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 (or a bindable client list model) so UI controls don\u0027t have to write manual \u0060for\u0060 loops comparing \u0060InstanceId\u0060 strings.\n\n### 2. \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060 \u2014 Non-UI Logic to Migrate\n\nWhile \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060 already encapsulates most of the virtual tree logic, a few pieces of pure geometry/scroll math remain in \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060:\n\n#### A. Viewport \u0026 ScrollBar Bounds Calculation (Lines 190\u2013218, 466\u2013476)\n\n- **What is in \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\n- \u0060GetViewportBounds()\u0060 (lines 190\u2013196) calculates the inner viewport \u0060(X, Y, Width, Height)\u0060 from \u0060ClientSize\u0060, \u0060BorderInset\u0060, and scrollbar visibility/sizes.\n- \u0060LayoutScrollBars()\u0060 (lines 198\u2013218) calculates the exact \u0060(X, Y, Width, Height)\u0060 bounds for the vertical scrollbar and horizontal scrollbar.\n- \u0060OnPaint\u0060 (lines 466\u2013476) calculates the bottom-right scrollbar intersection corner rectangle (\u0060_vScrollBar.Left, _hScrollBar.Top, _vScrollBar.Width, _hScrollBar.Height\u0060).\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\nInclude these precomputed rectangles (\u0060ViewportX\u0060, \u0060ViewportY\u0060, \u0060ViewportWidth\u0060, \u0060ViewportHeight\u0060, \u0060VerticalScrollBarBounds\u0060, \u0060HorizontalScrollBarBounds\u0060, \u0060ScrollCornerBounds\u0060) directly inside \u0060DomScrollBarMetrics\u0060 returned by \u0060DomTreeViewportState.CalculateScrollBarMetrics(...)\u0060.\n\n#### B. Mouse Wheel Maximum Scroll Calculation (Lines 566\u2013598)\n\n- **What is in \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\u0060OnMouseWheel\u0060 manually computes \u0060maxScrollX = Math.Max(0, _hScrollBar.Maximum - _hScrollBar.LargeChange \u002B 1)\u0060 and \u0060maxScrollY = Math.Max(0, _vScrollBar.Maximum - _vScrollBar.LargeChange \u002B 1)\u0060 from the WinForms scrollbars before calling \u0060_state.ApplyMouseWheel(...)\u0060.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\nAdd an overload to \u0060DomTreeViewportState.ApplyMouseWheel(int wheelDelta, bool horizontal, int viewportWidth, int viewportHeight, int itemHeight, int mouseWheelLines = 3)\u0060 that computes the maximum scroll bounds internally from \u0060_visibleRows.Count\u0060, \u0060MaxContentWidth\u0060, and the viewport dimensions without requiring the UI control to read scrollbar widget properties.\n\n#### C. Ancestor Guide Line Iteration (Lines 426\u2013432)\n\n- **What is in \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\u0060OnPaint\u0060 loops \u0060for (int d = (ShowRootLines ? 0 : 1); d \u003C item.Depth; d\u002B\u002B)\u0060 and calls \u0060_state.TryGetAncestorGuideLineX(...)\u0060.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\nAdd \u0060DomTreeViewportState.EnumerateAncestorGuideLineXs(DomTreeItem item, bool showLines, bool showRootLines, int viewportLeft, int viewportRight, int paddingLeft, int indentWidth, int glyphColumnWidth)\u0060 so the UI paint loop simply iterates the returned \u0060int\u0060 X-coordinates.\n\n### How to Verify / Next Steps\n\n- Review the items documented above in \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060 and \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060.\n- If you would like me to migrate all of these items into \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060 and update \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 to use them, let me know and I will apply the changes across both projects.",
      "ModelExplanation": "Here is a complete audit of \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 (ignoring \u0060TestBedApp\\utils\\*\u0060) documenting all remaining logic that is not strictly WinForms UI wrapper code and can be migrated into \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060.\n\n### Executive Summary\n\nMost of the core engine logic\u2014IPC transport (\u0060AutomationServer\u0060, \u0060BrowserClient\u0060), workflow execution (\u0060AutomationRunner\u0060), scraping (\u0060DataScraper\u0060, \u0060ScrapeBuilder\u0060, \u0060SelectorHelper\u0060), site dumping (\u0060SiteDumper\u0060), script/extension generation (\u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060, \u0060ChromeExtensionGenerator\u0060), and virtualized DOM tree state/geometry (\u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060, \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060)\u2014already lives in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060.\n\nHowever, several pieces of **session orchestration, state tracking, fallback branching, status formatting, and viewport geometry math** still reside in \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060 and \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060. Migrating the items below into \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060 will allow external developers to consume the framework with minimal boilerplate and make \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 a pure UI skin.\n\n### 1. \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060 \u2014 Non-UI Logic to Migrate\n\n#### A. Multi-Engine Orchestration \u0026 State Management (Lines 19\u201326, 89\u2013144, 159\u2013215)\n\n- **What is in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\u0060MainForm\u0060 manually instantiates, lifecycles, and coordinates four separate framework services plus result caches:\n\n- \u0060_server\u0060 (\u0060AutomationServer\u0060)\n- \u0060_project\u0060 (\u0060AutomationProject\u0060)\n- \u0060_runner\u0060 (\u0060AutomationRunner\u0060)\n- \u0060_scraper\u0060 (\u0060DataScraper\u0060)\n- \u0060_siteDumper\u0060 (\u0060SiteDumper\u0060)\n- \u0060_lastScrapeResult\u0060 (\u0060ScrapeResult?\u0060)\n- \u0060_lastSiteDumpResult\u0060 (\u0060SiteDumpResult?\u0060)\n- **Why it belongs in the DLL:**\nAny developer building a custom host (CLI, WPF, Avalonia, Web API, or WinForms) currently has to manually instantiate these classes, keep \u0060_server.ExclusiveTabMode\u0060 and Chrome Extension exports in sync when starting the server (\u0060BtnStart_Click\u0060), and store the latest \u0060ScrapeResult\u0060 and \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060 for export/inspection.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\nIntroduce a high-level facade/session controller (e.g., \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 or \u0060AutomationWorkspace\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060) that owns \u0060Project\u0060, \u0060Server\u0060, \u0060Runner\u0060, \u0060Scraper\u0060, \u0060SiteDumper\u0060, \u0060LastScrapeResult\u0060, and \u0060LastSiteDumpResult\u0060, and exposes \u0060StartServerAsync(port, ipcMode, syncExtension: true)\u0060 / \u0060StopServer()\u0060.\n\n#### B. Unified Log \u0026 Status Event Aggregation (Lines 93\u2013144, 178\u2013194)\n\n- **What is in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\u0060MainForm\u0060 subscribes to **25\u002B individual events** across \u0060_runner\u0060, \u0060_scraper\u0060, \u0060_siteDumper\u0060, and \u0060_server\u0060, manually formatting log category tags (\u0060[SYS]\u0060, \u0060[EXT]\u0060, \u0060[AUTO]\u0060, \u0060[AUTO-RX]\u0060, \u0060[SCRAPE]\u0060, \u0060[RATE-LIMIT 429]\u0060, \u0060[SCRAPE-ERR]\u0060, \u0060[REV-ENG]\u0060, \u0060[REV-ENG-ERR]\u0060, \u0060[STREAM \u003C- ...]\u0060, \u0060[TX -\u003E ...]\u0060, \u0060[RX \u003C- ...]\u0060) and assigning severity levels/colors.\n- **Why it belongs in the DLL:**\nFormatting raw command transmissions, stream outputs, client mode switches, and lifecycle events into structured log entries is framework telemetry logic.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\nAdd a unified event/logging pipeline in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.Models\u0060 (e.g., \u0060AutomationLogEventArgs\u0060 with \u0060Timestamp\u0060, \u0060Category\u0060, \u0060Message\u0060, and \u0060AutomationLogLevel\u0060 enum: \u0060Info\u0060, \u0060Success\u0060, \u0060Warning\u0060, \u0060Error\u0060, \u0060CommandTx\u0060, \u0060CommandRx\u0060, \u0060Stream\u0060, \u0060Navigation\u0060, \u0060Scrape\u0060, \u0060ReverseEngineering\u0060).\n\n#### C. Chrome Extension Connection Status Formatting \u0026 Tab Switch Guard (Lines 857\u2013879, 938\u2013980)\n\n- **What is in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\n- \u0060UpdateExtensionStatusLabel(bool connected, int tabCount)\u0060 (lines 857\u2013879) manually pluralizes and builds the extension status string:\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\n$\u0022Extension: Connected ({tabCount} open tab{(tabCount == 1 ? \u0022\u0022 : \u0022s\u0022)})\u0022\n\u0022Extension: Waiting for connection...\u0022\n\u0022Extension: Server stopped\u0022\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n- \u0060LstBrowserTabs_SelectedIndexChanged\u0060 (lines 938\u2013948) manually checks \u0060selectedTab.IsAlreadyActiveClient(...)\u0060 before calling \u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060.\n- \u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060 (lines 959\u2013980) calls \u0060_server.SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(...)\u0060 and then manually checks \u0060if (existingClient != null \u0026\u0026 lstClients.SelectedItem == existingClient)\u0060 to decide whether a DOM refresh is needed.\n- **Why it belongs in the DLL:**\nOther status messages (\u0060PageLoadedEventArgs.GetStatusMessage()\u0060, \u0060ScrapeResult.GetStatusSummary()\u0060, \u0060SiteDumpResult.GetStatusSummary()\u0060) are already generated by the DLL. Furthermore, \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 already tracks \u0060IsRunning\u0060, \u0060IsExtensionConnected\u0060, \u0060ActiveClient\u0060, and \u0060ExclusiveTabMode\u0060.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\n\n- Add \u0060AutomationServer.GetExtensionStatusMessage()\u0060 (and a static helper for stopped state) in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Server\\AutomationServer.cs\u0060.\n- Add \u0060skipIfAlreadyActive\u0060 parameter support directly to \u0060AutomationServer.SwitchToExtensionTabAsync(...)\u0060.\n\n#### D. DOM Node Resolution \u0026 Fallback Refresh Branching (Lines 354\u2013370, 502\u2013536, 1344\u20131361)\n\n- **What is in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\n- \u0060Server_OnActiveClientElementClicked\u0060 (lines 354\u2013370) checks if the middle-clicked path is already present in the tree (\u0060tvDom.SelectNodeByPath(e.Path)\u0060); if not, it falls back to fetching a fresh DOM snapshot (\u0060RefreshDomAsync(client, e.Path, hasTargetPath: true)\u0060).\n- \u0060GetCurrentRootDomNode()\u0060 (lines 1344\u20131345) manually chains \u0060(lstClients.SelectedItem as BrowserClient)?.ResolveDomRoot(tvDom.RootDomNode) ?? tvDom.RootDomNode\u0060.\n- \u0060BtnGeneralizeContainer_Click\u0060 (lines 1347\u20131361) and \u0060BtnHighlightContainer_Click\u0060 (lines 1363\u20131388) manually branch on whether a \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 is selected or if raw selector strings should be generalized/highlighted via \u0060SelectorHelper\u0060 / \u0060HighlightElementsAsync\u0060.\n- **Why it belongs in the DLL:**\n\u0060BrowserClient\u0060 already caches \u0060CurrentDomSnapshot\u0060 and \u0060CurrentDomRoot\u0060 and owns \u0060RefreshDomSnapshotCoalescedAsync\u0060. Deciding whether a clicked element path exists in the cached snapshot or requires a coalesced DOM refresh is client DOM state logic.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\n\n- Add a helper on \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 (or \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060) to resolve an element click against the current snapshot or automatically trigger \u0060RefreshDomSnapshotCoalescedAsync\u0060.\n- Add convenience overloads on \u0060BrowserClient\u0060 (e.g., \u0060GeneralizeContainerSelector(string rawSelector, ScrapeDefinition? definition = null)\u0060 and \u0060HighlightContainerAsync(string rawSelector, ScrapeDefinition? definition = null)\u0060) that automatically use \u0060client.ResolveDomRoot()\u0060 and handle the \u0060ScrapeDefinition != null\u0060 vs. ad-hoc selector branching.\n\n#### E. Client List Collection Synchronization (Lines 393\u2013421, 456\u2013488, 829\u2013855)\n\n- **What is in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\u0060UpsertClientInListUi\u0060, \u0060HandleClientRemovedFromUi\u0060, and \u0060RefreshClientListItemDisplay\u0060 manually iterate \u0060lstClients.Items\u0060 comparing \u0060item.InstanceId == client.InstanceId\u0060 to find indices to insert, replace, or remove. Meanwhile, \u0060AutomationServer.GetClientListDelta(...)\u0060 exists in the DLL (lines 285\u2013301 of \u0060AutomationServer.cs\u0060) but isn\u0027t used.\n- **Why it belongs in the DLL:**\nIndex lookup and list synchronization by \u0060InstanceId\u0060 can be exposed as clean helper methods on \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 (or a bindable client list model) so UI controls don\u0027t have to write manual \u0060for\u0060 loops comparing \u0060InstanceId\u0060 strings.\n\n### 2. \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060 \u2014 Non-UI Logic to Migrate\n\nWhile \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060 already encapsulates most of the virtual tree logic, a few pieces of pure geometry/scroll math remain in \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060:\n\n#### A. Viewport \u0026 ScrollBar Bounds Calculation (Lines 190\u2013218, 466\u2013476)\n\n- **What is in \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\n- \u0060GetViewportBounds()\u0060 (lines 190\u2013196) calculates the inner viewport \u0060(X, Y, Width, Height)\u0060 from \u0060ClientSize\u0060, \u0060BorderInset\u0060, and scrollbar visibility/sizes.\n- \u0060LayoutScrollBars()\u0060 (lines 198\u2013218) calculates the exact \u0060(X, Y, Width, Height)\u0060 bounds for the vertical scrollbar and horizontal scrollbar.\n- \u0060OnPaint\u0060 (lines 466\u2013476) calculates the bottom-right scrollbar intersection corner rectangle (\u0060_vScrollBar.Left, _hScrollBar.Top, _vScrollBar.Width, _hScrollBar.Height\u0060).\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\nInclude these precomputed rectangles (\u0060ViewportX\u0060, \u0060ViewportY\u0060, \u0060ViewportWidth\u0060, \u0060ViewportHeight\u0060, \u0060VerticalScrollBarBounds\u0060, \u0060HorizontalScrollBarBounds\u0060, \u0060ScrollCornerBounds\u0060) directly inside \u0060DomScrollBarMetrics\u0060 returned by \u0060DomTreeViewportState.CalculateScrollBarMetrics(...)\u0060.\n\n#### B. Mouse Wheel Maximum Scroll Calculation (Lines 566\u2013598)\n\n- **What is in \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\u0060OnMouseWheel\u0060 manually computes \u0060maxScrollX = Math.Max(0, _hScrollBar.Maximum - _hScrollBar.LargeChange \u002B 1)\u0060 and \u0060maxScrollY = Math.Max(0, _vScrollBar.Maximum - _vScrollBar.LargeChange \u002B 1)\u0060 from the WinForms scrollbars before calling \u0060_state.ApplyMouseWheel(...)\u0060.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\nAdd an overload to \u0060DomTreeViewportState.ApplyMouseWheel(int wheelDelta, bool horizontal, int viewportWidth, int viewportHeight, int itemHeight, int mouseWheelLines = 3)\u0060 that computes the maximum scroll bounds internally from \u0060_visibleRows.Count\u0060, \u0060MaxContentWidth\u0060, and the viewport dimensions without requiring the UI control to read scrollbar widget properties.\n\n#### C. Ancestor Guide Line Iteration (Lines 426\u2013432)\n\n- **What is in \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060 right now:**\n\u0060OnPaint\u0060 loops \u0060for (int d = (ShowRootLines ? 0 : 1); d \u003C item.Depth; d\u002B\u002B)\u0060 and calls \u0060_state.TryGetAncestorGuideLineX(...)\u0060.\n- **Where to migrate in DLL:**\nAdd \u0060DomTreeViewportState.EnumerateAncestorGuideLineXs(DomTreeItem item, bool showLines, bool showRootLines, int viewportLeft, int viewportRight, int paddingLeft, int indentWidth, int glyphColumnWidth)\u0060 so the UI paint loop simply iterates the returned \u0060int\u0060 X-coordinates.\n\n### How to Verify / Next Steps\n\n- Review the items documented above in \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060 and \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060.\n- If you would like me to migrate all of these items into \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060 and update \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 to use them, let me know and I will apply the changes across both projects.",
