      "Id": "bdb9b16c",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-28T00:19:34.5790533-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\nPlease study this codebase. I want you to document ANY code that is still in the testbed winforms project that isnt strictly UI wrapper code. I want to ensure all the real logic of the browser automation framework is inside the dll. If you find any code in the winforms app that can be migrated to the dll project, please document that. We want to ensure that the winforms app is just a UI wrapper around the dll. This will ensure that other developers can easily work with the framework. Please also ignore all code files in the utils folder in the winforms project, for as those dont need to be migrated at all and can stay where they\u0027re at.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nHere is a complete audit of \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 (excluding \u0060TestBedApp\\utils\\*\u0060) documenting all remaining logic that is not strictly UI wrapper code and can be migrated into the \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 DLL project.\n\n### Overall Architecture Assessment\n\nThe vast majority of core automation, IPC, DOM snapshotting,\u865A\u62DF\u5316 tree layout math (\u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060), scraping, and reverse-engineering logic already lives in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 and is coordinated through \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060.\n\nHowever, several pieces of domain state management, model inspection, measurement assumptions, and session-level helpers still reside in \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060, \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060, \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060, and \u0060TestBedApp\\Program.cs\u0060.\n\n### 1. \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060\n\n#### A. Coupled Font Measurement Sample String (\u0060UpdateMetrics\u0060, lines 146\u2013155)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060DomTreeView.UpdateMetrics()\u0060 hardcodes the 10-character sample string \u0060\u0022MMMMMMMMMM\u0022\u0060 when calling \u0060TextRenderer.MeasureText(\u0022MMMMMMMMMM\u0022, ...)\u0060 and passes \u0060charSample.Width\u0060 as \u0060tenCharSampleWidth\u0060 to \u0060_state.UpdateFontMetrics(...)\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\n\u0060DomTreeViewportState.UpdateFontMetrics\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060, line 696) hardcodes the \u0060/ 10.0\u0060 divisor (\u0060Math.Ceiling(tenCharSampleWidth / 10.0)\u0060), which implicitly depends on the caller measuring a 10-character string.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nMove the sample string constant (\u0060public const string FontMeasurementSample = \u0022MMMMMMMMMM\u0022;\u0060) into \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060, or overload \u0060DomTreeViewportState.UpdateFontMetrics(int fontHeight, Func\u003Cstring, int\u003E measureTextWidth, float dpiScale, int borderInset)\u0060 so \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 invokes \u0060measureTextWidth(FontMeasurementSample)\u0060 internally.\n\n#### B. \u0060ItemHeight\u0060 Minimum Clamping (\u0060ItemHeight\u0060 property, lines 62\u201376)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060DomTreeView.ItemHeight\u0060 clamps incoming values via \u0060int clamped = Math.Max(16, value);\u0060 before assigning \u0060_state.ItemHeight = clamped;\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\n\u0060DomTreeViewportState.ItemHeight\u0060 in the DLL is an unclamped auto-property (\u0060public int ItemHeight { get; set; } = 24;\u0060). Any non-WinForms consumer manipulating \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 directly could set an invalid or zero \u0060ItemHeight\u0060.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nEnforce \u0060Math.Max(16, value)\u0060 directly inside the \u0060DomTreeViewportState.ItemHeight\u0060 setter in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060.\n\n#### C. \u0060DomNode\u0060 Display Label Fallback \u0026 Synthetic \u0060TreeNode\u0060 Wrapping (\u0060CreateShimTreeNode\u0060, lines 501\u2013507)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060DomTreeView.CreateShimTreeNode(DomNode domNode)\u0060 computes \u0060domNode.TagName ?? domNode.Text ?? string.Empty\u0060 to construct a dummy \u0060System.Windows.Forms.TreeNode\u0060 wrapper around \u0060DomNode\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\nDetermining the display label for a \u0060DomNode\u0060 (\u0060TagName ?? Text ?? string.Empty\u0060) is domain model logic.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nAdd a \u0060DisplayName\u0060 property and \u0060ToString()\u0060 override to \u0060DomNode\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomNode.cs\u0060. (Optionally, \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 can also raise events carrying \u0060DomNode\u0060 directly instead of wrapping it in a WinForms \u0060TreeNode\u0060 shim.)\n\n#### D. Redundant Scrollbar Visibility Guards in \u0060OnMouseWheel\u0060 (\u0060OnMouseWheel\u0060, lines 437\u2013462)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060DomTreeView.OnMouseWheel\u0060 checks \u0060(ModifierKeys \u0026 Keys.Shift) == Keys.Shift\u0060 and branches on \u0060_hScrollBar.Visible\u0060 and \u0060_vScrollBar.Visible\u0060 before delegating to \u0060_state.ApplyMouseWheel(...)\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\n\u0060DomTreeViewportState.ApplyMouseWheel\u0060 already calculates \u0060maxScrollOffset\u0060 from \u0060MaxContentWidth\u0060 / \u0060VisibleRows.Count\u0060 and returns \u0060false\u0060 when scrolling is not applicable (\u0060maxScrollOffset \u003C= 0\u0060). Having \u0060DomTreeViewportState.ApplyMouseWheel\u0060 handle both axes and return updated scroll state eliminates the extra branching in the control.\n\n### 2. \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060\n\n#### A. Direct Calls to \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 List Helpers Instead of \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 (\u0060UpsertClientInListUi\u0060, \u0060HandleClientRemovedFromUi\u0060, \u0060RefreshClientListItemDisplay\u0060, lines 294\u2013305, 344\u2013358, 565\u2013584)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060MainForm\u0060 bypasses \u0060_session\u0060 (\u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060) to call static methods on \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 (\u0060AutomationServer.UpsertClientInList\u0060, \u0060AutomationServer.RemoveClientFromList\u0060, \u0060AutomationServer.FindClientIndex\u0060, \u0060AutomationServer.RefreshClientInList\u0060). Additionally, \u0060RefreshClientListItemDisplay\u0060 (lines 565\u2013584) manually checks \u0060bool wasSelected = lstClients.SelectedIndex == idx;\u0060, refreshes the item, and restores \u0060lstClients.SelectedIndex = idx;\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\nDevelopers using \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 as their single facade shouldn\u0027t need to call \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 static methods or manually write selection-preserving list update logic.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nAdd instance/facade methods on \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 (and/or enhance \u0060AutomationServer.RefreshClientInList\u0060 to output whether the refreshed item was selected or accept a selection callback).\n\n#### B. Raw String Inspection of \u0060DomNode.Type\u0060 (\u0060TvDom_NodeMouseClick\u0060, line 380)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\nif (e.Button == MouseButtons.Right \u0026\u0026 e.Node?.Tag is DomNode domNode \u0026\u0026 domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022)\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\nChecking \u0060domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022\u0060 leaks the internal JSON discriminator string (\u0060\u0022element\u0022\u0060 vs. \u0060\u0022text\u0022\u0060) of the DOM serialization protocol into the UI layer.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nAdd \u0060[JsonIgnore] public bool IsElement =\u003E string.Equals(Type, \u0022element\u0022, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\u0060 and \u0060[JsonIgnore] public bool IsText =\u003E string.Equals(Type, \u0022text\u0022, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\u0060 to \u0060DomNode\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomNode.cs\u0060 (and optionally a helper on \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 or \u0060DomNode\u0060 indicating whether context actions are supported).\n\n#### C. DOM Snapshot Details Resolution (\u0060ApplyDomSnapshotResultToUi\u0060 \u0026 \u0060Server_OnActiveClientElementClicked\u0060, lines 259, 360\u2013370)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\nAfter applying a \u0060DomSnapshotRefreshResult\u0060, \u0060MainForm\u0060 manually queries \u0060tvDom.SelectedDomNode?.GetFormattedDetails() ?? string.Empty\u0060 and compares it with \u0060txtElementDetails.Text\u0060 using \u0060string.Equals(..., StringComparison.Ordinal)\u0060 before updating the details pane.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\n\u0060DomSnapshotRefreshResult\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060 already holds \u0060Snapshot\u0060 and \u0060ResolvedSelectedPath\u0060.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nAdd \u0060SelectedNode\u0060 (\u0060Snapshot.FindNodeByPath(ResolvedSelectedPath)\u0060) and \u0060SelectedNodeDetails\u0060 (\u0060SelectedNode?.GetFormattedDetails() ?? string.Empty\u0060) properties directly onto \u0060DomSnapshotRefreshResult\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060.\n\n#### D. Hardcoded Default Scrape Configuration Values (\u0060InitializeScraperTabUi\u0060 \u0026 \u0060LoadSelectedScrapeToUi\u0060, lines 728, 744, 759, 976\u2013986)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\nWhen no \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 is selected in \u0060LoadSelectedScrapeToUi()\u0060 (lines 976\u2013986), \u0060MainForm\u0060 resets the controls using hardcoded literals (\u0060chkEnablePagination.Checked = false\u0060, \u0060numMaxPages.Value = 1\u0060, \u0060numStartPage.Value = 1\u0060, \u0060numPageDelayMs.Value = 1000\u0060, etc.). In \u0060InitializeScraperTabUi()\u0060 (line 728), \u0060numMaxPages.Value\u0060 is initialized to \u00603\u0060, which differs from \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060\u0027s default \u0060MaxPages = 1\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\nDefault values for a scrape configuration belong in \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 in the DLL so that UI reset state never drifts from the model defaults.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nExpose a static \u0060ScrapeDefinition.Default\u0060 (or constants on \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\ScrapeDefinition.cs\u0060) and bind \u0060LoadSelectedScrapeToUi()\u0060 to \u0060chkLstScrapes.SelectedItem as ScrapeDefinition ?? ScrapeDefinition.Default\u0060.\n\n#### E. Context Menu Building from UI Control Collections (\u0060CtxDomNode_Opening\u0060 \u0026 \u0060PopulateScrapeSubMenu\u0060, lines 473\u2013521)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060CtxDomNode_Opening\u0060 iterates \u0060chkLstSequences.Items\u0060 and \u0060PopulateScrapeSubMenu\u0060 iterates \u0060chkLstScrapes.Items\u0060 instead of reading \u0060_session.Project.Sequences\u0060 and \u0060_session.Project.Scrapes\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\nUsing \u0060_session.Project.Sequences\u0060 and \u0060_session.Project.Scrapes\u0060 (or session helper methods) avoids coupling action menu population to WinForms \u0060CheckedListBox.ObjectCollection\u0060 state.\n\n#### F. Proportional Splitter Distance Calculations (\u0060EnsureTabSplittersConfigured\u0060, lines 642\u2013695)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060EnsureTabSplittersConfigured()\u0060 contains DPI-scaled clamping math (\u0060Math.Clamp((int)(totalSize * ratio), minPx, maxPx)\u0060) repeated across 6 different \u0060SplitContainer\u0060 instances with hardcoded ratios (\u00600.58\u0060, \u00600.45\u0060, \u00600.28\u0060, \u00600.36\u0060, \u00600.32\u0060, \u00600.52\u0060, \u00600.35\u0060, \u00600.34\u0060, \u00600.65\u0060) and minimum/maximum pixel bounds.\n- **Why It Could Be Migrated (Optional)**:\nWhile splitter sizing is UI layout logic, the reusable DPI-aware proportional splitter clamp calculation can be extracted into a small layout helper if desired, or kept in WinForms as pure UI layout code.\n\n#### G. File Dialog Filters, Default Extensions, and Studio Metadata (\u0060MnuFileOpen_Click\u0060, \u0060MnuFileSave_Click\u0060, \u0060MnuHelpAbout_Click\u0060, \u0060BtnExportScrapeJson_Click\u0060, \u0060BtnExportScrapeCsv_Click\u0060, \u0060BtnSaveActiveDumpFile_Click\u0060, lines 407\u2013445, 1218\u20131249, 1428\u20131445)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\nFile dialog filter strings (\u0060\u0022JSON Files (*.json)|*.json|All Files (*.*)|*.*\u0022\u0060, \u0060\u0022CSV Files (*.csv)|*.csv|All Files (*.*)|*.*\u0022\u0060, \u0060\u0022All Files (*.*)|*.*|HTML Files (*.html)|*.html|CSS Files (*.css)|*.css|JavaScript Files (*.js)|*.js\u0022\u0060) and application title/version strings in \u0060MnuHelpAbout_Click\u0060 are hardcoded in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nExpose standard file dialog filter/extension constants on \u0060AutomationProject\u0060, \u0060ScrapeResult\u0060, and \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060 (or \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060).\n\n### 3. \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060\n\n#### Default Port \u0026 Raw Command Test Defaults (\u0060InitializeComponent\u0060, lines 155, 405, 429)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\n- \u0060numPort.Value = 9999\u0060\n- \u0060txtCmdType.Text = \u0022EVAL\u0022\u0060\n- \u0060txtPayload.Text = \u0022console.log(\u0027Hello from C#\u0027); return \u0027Success\u0027;\u0022\u0060\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nExpose default studio constants (e.g., \u0060AutomationStudioSession.DefaultPort = 9999\u0060, \u0060DefaultTestCommandType = \u0022EVAL\u0022\u0060, \u0060DefaultTestPayload = \u0022console.log(\u0027Hello from C#\u0027); return \u0027Success\u0027;\u0022\u0060) on \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 so the UI reads its initial values from the session.\n\n### 4. \u0060TestBedApp\\Program.cs\u0060\n\n#### Command-Line Project File Startup Handling (\u0060Main\u0060, lines 9\u201315)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060Program.Main()\u0060 takes no \u0060string[] args\u0060 and does not pass a startup file path to \u0060MainForm\u0060 or \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060, even though \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Utils\\FileAssociationHelper.cs\u0060 registers \u0060\u0022%1\u0022\u0060 command-line file opening.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nAdd a helper on \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 (e.g., \u0060TryHandleStartupArguments(string[]? args)\u0060) that resolves and loads a project file path passed via command-line arguments if present on disk.\n\n### Summary Checklist of Recommended DLL Migrations\n\n- **\u0060DomNode\u0060 (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomNode.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Add \u0060IsElement\u0060, \u0060IsText\u0060, \u0060DisplayName\u0060, and \u0060ToString()\u0060.\n- **\u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 \u0026 \u0060DomSnapshotRefreshResult\u0060 (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Add \u0060FontMeasurementSample = \u0022MMMMMMMMMM\u0022\u0060 (or a measurement callback overload to \u0060UpdateFontMetrics\u0060).\n- Clamp \u0060ItemHeight\u0060 (\u0060Math.Max(16, value)\u0060) inside \u0060DomTreeViewportState.ItemHeight\u0060.\n- Add \u0060SelectedNode\u0060 and \u0060SelectedNodeDetails\u0060 properties to \u0060DomSnapshotRefreshResult\u0060.\n- **\u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\ScrapeDefinition.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Provide a static \u0060Default\u0060 instance or default constants for UI fallback binding when no scrape is selected.\n- **\u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Automation\\AutomationStudioSession.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Expose client-list synchronization helpers (\u0060UpsertClientInList\u0060, \u0060RemoveClientFromList\u0060, \u0060RefreshClientInList\u0060) so \u0060MainForm\u0060 never needs to call \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 static methods directly.\n- Expose default studio constants (\u0060DefaultPort\u0060, \u0060DefaultTestCommandType\u0060, \u0060DefaultTestPayload\u0060, file dialog filters) and optional command-line startup project loading (\u0060TryLoadProjectFromCommandLineArgs\u0060).\n\nTo test any of these migrations once implemented, build the solution with \u0060dotnet build\u0060 and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 to verify that DOM exploration, right-click context menus, scrape configuration resets, and client list updates behave identically.",
      "ModelExplanation": "Here is a complete audit of \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 (excluding \u0060TestBedApp\\utils\\*\u0060) documenting all remaining logic that is not strictly UI wrapper code and can be migrated into the \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 DLL project.\n\n### Overall Architecture Assessment\n\nThe vast majority of core automation, IPC, DOM snapshotting,\u865A\u62DF\u5316 tree layout math (\u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060), scraping, and reverse-engineering logic already lives in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 and is coordinated through \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060.\n\nHowever, several pieces of domain state management, model inspection, measurement assumptions, and session-level helpers still reside in \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060, \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060, \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060, and \u0060TestBedApp\\Program.cs\u0060.\n\n### 1. \u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060\n\n#### A. Coupled Font Measurement Sample String (\u0060UpdateMetrics\u0060, lines 146\u2013155)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060DomTreeView.UpdateMetrics()\u0060 hardcodes the 10-character sample string \u0060\u0022MMMMMMMMMM\u0022\u0060 when calling \u0060TextRenderer.MeasureText(\u0022MMMMMMMMMM\u0022, ...)\u0060 and passes \u0060charSample.Width\u0060 as \u0060tenCharSampleWidth\u0060 to \u0060_state.UpdateFontMetrics(...)\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\n\u0060DomTreeViewportState.UpdateFontMetrics\u0060 (in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060, line 696) hardcodes the \u0060/ 10.0\u0060 divisor (\u0060Math.Ceiling(tenCharSampleWidth / 10.0)\u0060), which implicitly depends on the caller measuring a 10-character string.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nMove the sample string constant (\u0060public const string FontMeasurementSample = \u0022MMMMMMMMMM\u0022;\u0060) into \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060, or overload \u0060DomTreeViewportState.UpdateFontMetrics(int fontHeight, Func\u003Cstring, int\u003E measureTextWidth, float dpiScale, int borderInset)\u0060 so \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 invokes \u0060measureTextWidth(FontMeasurementSample)\u0060 internally.\n\n#### B. \u0060ItemHeight\u0060 Minimum Clamping (\u0060ItemHeight\u0060 property, lines 62\u201376)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060DomTreeView.ItemHeight\u0060 clamps incoming values via \u0060int clamped = Math.Max(16, value);\u0060 before assigning \u0060_state.ItemHeight = clamped;\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\n\u0060DomTreeViewportState.ItemHeight\u0060 in the DLL is an unclamped auto-property (\u0060public int ItemHeight { get; set; } = 24;\u0060). Any non-WinForms consumer manipulating \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 directly could set an invalid or zero \u0060ItemHeight\u0060.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nEnforce \u0060Math.Max(16, value)\u0060 directly inside the \u0060DomTreeViewportState.ItemHeight\u0060 setter in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060.\n\n#### C. \u0060DomNode\u0060 Display Label Fallback \u0026 Synthetic \u0060TreeNode\u0060 Wrapping (\u0060CreateShimTreeNode\u0060, lines 501\u2013507)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060DomTreeView.CreateShimTreeNode(DomNode domNode)\u0060 computes \u0060domNode.TagName ?? domNode.Text ?? string.Empty\u0060 to construct a dummy \u0060System.Windows.Forms.TreeNode\u0060 wrapper around \u0060DomNode\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\nDetermining the display label for a \u0060DomNode\u0060 (\u0060TagName ?? Text ?? string.Empty\u0060) is domain model logic.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nAdd a \u0060DisplayName\u0060 property and \u0060ToString()\u0060 override to \u0060DomNode\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomNode.cs\u0060. (Optionally, \u0060DomTreeView\u0060 can also raise events carrying \u0060DomNode\u0060 directly instead of wrapping it in a WinForms \u0060TreeNode\u0060 shim.)\n\n#### D. Redundant Scrollbar Visibility Guards in \u0060OnMouseWheel\u0060 (\u0060OnMouseWheel\u0060, lines 437\u2013462)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060DomTreeView.OnMouseWheel\u0060 checks \u0060(ModifierKeys \u0026 Keys.Shift) == Keys.Shift\u0060 and branches on \u0060_hScrollBar.Visible\u0060 and \u0060_vScrollBar.Visible\u0060 before delegating to \u0060_state.ApplyMouseWheel(...)\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\n\u0060DomTreeViewportState.ApplyMouseWheel\u0060 already calculates \u0060maxScrollOffset\u0060 from \u0060MaxContentWidth\u0060 / \u0060VisibleRows.Count\u0060 and returns \u0060false\u0060 when scrolling is not applicable (\u0060maxScrollOffset \u003C= 0\u0060). Having \u0060DomTreeViewportState.ApplyMouseWheel\u0060 handle both axes and return updated scroll state eliminates the extra branching in the control.\n\n### 2. \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060\n\n#### A. Direct Calls to \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 List Helpers Instead of \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 (\u0060UpsertClientInListUi\u0060, \u0060HandleClientRemovedFromUi\u0060, \u0060RefreshClientListItemDisplay\u0060, lines 294\u2013305, 344\u2013358, 565\u2013584)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060MainForm\u0060 bypasses \u0060_session\u0060 (\u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060) to call static methods on \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 (\u0060AutomationServer.UpsertClientInList\u0060, \u0060AutomationServer.RemoveClientFromList\u0060, \u0060AutomationServer.FindClientIndex\u0060, \u0060AutomationServer.RefreshClientInList\u0060). Additionally, \u0060RefreshClientListItemDisplay\u0060 (lines 565\u2013584) manually checks \u0060bool wasSelected = lstClients.SelectedIndex == idx;\u0060, refreshes the item, and restores \u0060lstClients.SelectedIndex = idx;\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\nDevelopers using \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 as their single facade shouldn\u0027t need to call \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 static methods or manually write selection-preserving list update logic.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nAdd instance/facade methods on \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 (and/or enhance \u0060AutomationServer.RefreshClientInList\u0060 to output whether the refreshed item was selected or accept a selection callback).\n\n#### B. Raw String Inspection of \u0060DomNode.Type\u0060 (\u0060TvDom_NodeMouseClick\u0060, line 380)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\nif (e.Button == MouseButtons.Right \u0026\u0026 e.Node?.Tag is DomNode domNode \u0026\u0026 domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022)\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\nChecking \u0060domNode.Type == \u0022element\u0022\u0060 leaks the internal JSON discriminator string (\u0060\u0022element\u0022\u0060 vs. \u0060\u0022text\u0022\u0060) of the DOM serialization protocol into the UI layer.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nAdd \u0060[JsonIgnore] public bool IsElement =\u003E string.Equals(Type, \u0022element\u0022, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\u0060 and \u0060[JsonIgnore] public bool IsText =\u003E string.Equals(Type, \u0022text\u0022, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);\u0060 to \u0060DomNode\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomNode.cs\u0060 (and optionally a helper on \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 or \u0060DomNode\u0060 indicating whether context actions are supported).\n\n#### C. DOM Snapshot Details Resolution (\u0060ApplyDomSnapshotResultToUi\u0060 \u0026 \u0060Server_OnActiveClientElementClicked\u0060, lines 259, 360\u2013370)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\nAfter applying a \u0060DomSnapshotRefreshResult\u0060, \u0060MainForm\u0060 manually queries \u0060tvDom.SelectedDomNode?.GetFormattedDetails() ?? string.Empty\u0060 and compares it with \u0060txtElementDetails.Text\u0060 using \u0060string.Equals(..., StringComparison.Ordinal)\u0060 before updating the details pane.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\n\u0060DomSnapshotRefreshResult\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060 already holds \u0060Snapshot\u0060 and \u0060ResolvedSelectedPath\u0060.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nAdd \u0060SelectedNode\u0060 (\u0060Snapshot.FindNodeByPath(ResolvedSelectedPath)\u0060) and \u0060SelectedNodeDetails\u0060 (\u0060SelectedNode?.GetFormattedDetails() ?? string.Empty\u0060) properties directly onto \u0060DomSnapshotRefreshResult\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060.\n\n#### D. Hardcoded Default Scrape Configuration Values (\u0060InitializeScraperTabUi\u0060 \u0026 \u0060LoadSelectedScrapeToUi\u0060, lines 728, 744, 759, 976\u2013986)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\nWhen no \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 is selected in \u0060LoadSelectedScrapeToUi()\u0060 (lines 976\u2013986), \u0060MainForm\u0060 resets the controls using hardcoded literals (\u0060chkEnablePagination.Checked = false\u0060, \u0060numMaxPages.Value = 1\u0060, \u0060numStartPage.Value = 1\u0060, \u0060numPageDelayMs.Value = 1000\u0060, etc.). In \u0060InitializeScraperTabUi()\u0060 (line 728), \u0060numMaxPages.Value\u0060 is initialized to \u00603\u0060, which differs from \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060\u0027s default \u0060MaxPages = 1\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\nDefault values for a scrape configuration belong in \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 in the DLL so that UI reset state never drifts from the model defaults.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nExpose a static \u0060ScrapeDefinition.Default\u0060 (or constants on \u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 in \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\ScrapeDefinition.cs\u0060) and bind \u0060LoadSelectedScrapeToUi()\u0060 to \u0060chkLstScrapes.SelectedItem as ScrapeDefinition ?? ScrapeDefinition.Default\u0060.\n\n#### E. Context Menu Building from UI Control Collections (\u0060CtxDomNode_Opening\u0060 \u0026 \u0060PopulateScrapeSubMenu\u0060, lines 473\u2013521)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060CtxDomNode_Opening\u0060 iterates \u0060chkLstSequences.Items\u0060 and \u0060PopulateScrapeSubMenu\u0060 iterates \u0060chkLstScrapes.Items\u0060 instead of reading \u0060_session.Project.Sequences\u0060 and \u0060_session.Project.Scrapes\u0060.\n- **Why It Should Be Migrated**:\nUsing \u0060_session.Project.Sequences\u0060 and \u0060_session.Project.Scrapes\u0060 (or session helper methods) avoids coupling action menu population to WinForms \u0060CheckedListBox.ObjectCollection\u0060 state.\n\n#### F. Proportional Splitter Distance Calculations (\u0060EnsureTabSplittersConfigured\u0060, lines 642\u2013695)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060EnsureTabSplittersConfigured()\u0060 contains DPI-scaled clamping math (\u0060Math.Clamp((int)(totalSize * ratio), minPx, maxPx)\u0060) repeated across 6 different \u0060SplitContainer\u0060 instances with hardcoded ratios (\u00600.58\u0060, \u00600.45\u0060, \u00600.28\u0060, \u00600.36\u0060, \u00600.32\u0060, \u00600.52\u0060, \u00600.35\u0060, \u00600.34\u0060, \u00600.65\u0060) and minimum/maximum pixel bounds.\n- **Why It Could Be Migrated (Optional)**:\nWhile splitter sizing is UI layout logic, the reusable DPI-aware proportional splitter clamp calculation can be extracted into a small layout helper if desired, or kept in WinForms as pure UI layout code.\n\n#### G. File Dialog Filters, Default Extensions, and Studio Metadata (\u0060MnuFileOpen_Click\u0060, \u0060MnuFileSave_Click\u0060, \u0060MnuHelpAbout_Click\u0060, \u0060BtnExportScrapeJson_Click\u0060, \u0060BtnExportScrapeCsv_Click\u0060, \u0060BtnSaveActiveDumpFile_Click\u0060, lines 407\u2013445, 1218\u20131249, 1428\u20131445)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\nFile dialog filter strings (\u0060\u0022JSON Files (*.json)|*.json|All Files (*.*)|*.*\u0022\u0060, \u0060\u0022CSV Files (*.csv)|*.csv|All Files (*.*)|*.*\u0022\u0060, \u0060\u0022All Files (*.*)|*.*|HTML Files (*.html)|*.html|CSS Files (*.css)|*.css|JavaScript Files (*.js)|*.js\u0022\u0060) and application title/version strings in \u0060MnuHelpAbout_Click\u0060 are hardcoded in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nExpose standard file dialog filter/extension constants on \u0060AutomationProject\u0060, \u0060ScrapeResult\u0060, and \u0060SiteDumpResult\u0060 (or \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060).\n\n### 3. \u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060\n\n#### Default Port \u0026 Raw Command Test Defaults (\u0060InitializeComponent\u0060, lines 155, 405, 429)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\n- \u0060numPort.Value = 9999\u0060\n- \u0060txtCmdType.Text = \u0022EVAL\u0022\u0060\n- \u0060txtPayload.Text = \u0022console.log(\u0027Hello from C#\u0027); return \u0027Success\u0027;\u0022\u0060\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nExpose default studio constants (e.g., \u0060AutomationStudioSession.DefaultPort = 9999\u0060, \u0060DefaultTestCommandType = \u0022EVAL\u0022\u0060, \u0060DefaultTestPayload = \u0022console.log(\u0027Hello from C#\u0027); return \u0027Success\u0027;\u0022\u0060) on \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 so the UI reads its initial values from the session.\n\n### 4. \u0060TestBedApp\\Program.cs\u0060\n\n#### Command-Line Project File Startup Handling (\u0060Main\u0060, lines 9\u201315)\n\n- **Current Code in WinForms**:\n\u0060Program.Main()\u0060 takes no \u0060string[] args\u0060 and does not pass a startup file path to \u0060MainForm\u0060 or \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060, even though \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Utils\\FileAssociationHelper.cs\u0060 registers \u0060\u0022%1\u0022\u0060 command-line file opening.\n- **Where to Migrate in DLL**:\nAdd a helper on \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 (e.g., \u0060TryHandleStartupArguments(string[]? args)\u0060) that resolves and loads a project file path passed via command-line arguments if present on disk.\n\n### Summary Checklist of Recommended DLL Migrations\n\n- **\u0060DomNode\u0060 (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomNode.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Add \u0060IsElement\u0060, \u0060IsText\u0060, \u0060DisplayName\u0060, and \u0060ToString()\u0060.\n- **\u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 \u0026 \u0060DomSnapshotRefreshResult\u0060 (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\DomTreeSnapshot.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Add \u0060FontMeasurementSample = \u0022MMMMMMMMMM\u0022\u0060 (or a measurement callback overload to \u0060UpdateFontMetrics\u0060).\n- Clamp \u0060ItemHeight\u0060 (\u0060Math.Max(16, value)\u0060) inside \u0060DomTreeViewportState.ItemHeight\u0060.\n- Add \u0060SelectedNode\u0060 and \u0060SelectedNodeDetails\u0060 properties to \u0060DomSnapshotRefreshResult\u0060.\n- **\u0060ScrapeDefinition\u0060 (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Models\\ScrapeDefinition.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Provide a static \u0060Default\u0060 instance or default constants for UI fallback binding when no scrape is selected.\n- **\u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\Automation\\AutomationStudioSession.cs\u0060)**:\n\n- Expose client-list synchronization helpers (\u0060UpsertClientInList\u0060, \u0060RemoveClientFromList\u0060, \u0060RefreshClientInList\u0060) so \u0060MainForm\u0060 never needs to call \u0060AutomationServer\u0060 static methods directly.\n- Expose default studio constants (\u0060DefaultPort\u0060, \u0060DefaultTestCommandType\u0060, \u0060DefaultTestPayload\u0060, file dialog filters) and optional command-line startup project loading (\u0060TryLoadProjectFromCommandLineArgs\u0060).\n\nTo test any of these migrations once implemented, build the solution with \u0060dotnet build\u0060 and run \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 to verify that DOM exploration, right-click context menus, scrape configuration resets, and client list updates behave identically.",
