      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n\nPlease study this codebase. I want you to document ANY code that is still in the testbed winforms project that isnt strictly UI wrapper code. I want to ensure all the real logic of the browser automation framework is inside the dll. If you find any code in the winforms app that can be migrated to the dll project, please document that. We want to ensure that the winforms app is just a UI wrapper around the dll. This will ensure that other developers can easily work with the framework. Please also ignore all code files in the utils folder in the winforms project, for as those dont need to be migrated at all and can stay where they\u0027re at.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nBelow is a complete audit of the non-\u0060utils\u0060 files in \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 (\u0060MainForm.cs\u0060, \u0060MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060, \u0060Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060, and \u0060Program.cs\u0060), documenting all remaining logic that is not strictly UI wrapper code and how it can be migrated into the \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060 DLL project.\n\n### 1. Active Client DOM Refresh \u0026 Event Coordination (\u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060)\n\n- **Current Location**: \u0060MainForm.Server_OnActiveClientPageLoaded\u0060, \u0060MainForm.Server_OnActiveClientDomChanged\u0060, \u0060MainForm.Server_OnActiveClientHighlightedElementRemoved\u0060, \u0060MainForm.Server_OnActiveClientElementClicked\u0060, \u0060MainForm.SyncActiveClientSelectionToUi\u0060, and \u0060MainForm.ApplyDomSnapshotResultToUi\u0060 (lines 286\u2013334, 355\u2013385, 421\u2013433).\n- **What It Does**:\n\n- Subscribes to low-level client DOM/navigation events on \u0060_session\u0060 only to immediately call back into \u0060_session.RefreshActiveClientDomAsync(...)\u0060 and \u0060_session.HandleActiveClientElementClickedAsync(...)\u0060.\n- Passes lambdas (\u0060getCurrentSelectedPath: () =\u003E tvDom.SelectedPath\u0060, \u0060trySelectExistingPath\u0060, \u0060onSelectedInExistingTree\u0060) back into \u0060_session\u0060 to coordinate coalesced DOM refreshes and middle-click selection fallback.\n- **How to Migrate to DLL**:\n\n- Move the \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 instance (or active DOM selection tracking) directly onto \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 (e.g., \u0060_session.DomViewportState\u0060 or \u0060_session.SelectedDomNode\u0060 / \u0060_session.SelectedDomPath\u0060).\n- Have \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 handle \u0060OnActiveClientPageLoaded\u0060, \u0060OnActiveClientDomChanged\u0060, \u0060OnActiveClientHighlightedElementRemoved\u0060, and \u0060OnActiveClientElementClicked\u0060 internally, automatically triggering coalesced DOM snapshot refreshes and updating its \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060.\n- Expose a single high-level session event (e.g., \u0060OnDomViewportUpdated\u0060 / \u0060OnSelectedDomNodeChanged\u0060) so \u0060MainForm\u0060 only needs to invalidate \u0060tvDom\u0060 and set \u0060txtElementDetails.Text = _session.SelectedDomNodeDetails\u0060.\n\n### 2. Studio Selection \u0026 Session State Management (\u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060)\n\n- **Current Location**: Scattered across \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 event handlers for sequences, steps, scrapes, scrape fields, and Chrome Extension tabs (lines 93\u2013108, 436\u2013467, 520\u2013607, 687\u2013715, 1110\u20131370).\n- **What It Does**:\n\n- While \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 already tracks reverse-engineering UI state (\u0060SelectedDumpResource\u0060, \u0060ActiveDumpViewMode\u0060, \u0060ResourceFilterText\u0060, \u0060DumpOptions\u0060), it does **not** track:\n\n- \u0060SelectedSequence\u0060 (\u0060AutomationSequence?\u0060) and \u0060SelectedStep\u0060 (\u0060AutomationStep?\u0060)\n- \u0060SelectedScrape\u0060 (\u0060ScrapeDefinition?\u0060) and \u0060SelectedScrapeField\u0060 (\u0060ScrapeField?\u0060)\n- \u0060SelectedExtensionTab\u0060 (\u0060BrowserTabInfo?\u0060) and \u0060ExtensionTabFilterText\u0060 (\u0060string?\u0060)\n- Consequently, \u0060MainForm\u0060 manually resolves the current selection from WinForms controls on every action, contains conditional branching to decide whether a newly added step/field/container/pagination selector belongs to the currently viewed sequence or scrape (\u0060AddStepToSequence\u0060, \u0060AddFieldFromSelectedDomNode\u0060, \u0060SetContainerFromSelectedDomNode\u0060, \u0060SetPaginationNextFromSelectedDomNode\u0060), and manually checks \u0060e.ShouldUpdatePageDelayFor(chkLstScrapes.SelectedItem as ScrapeDefinition)\u0060 on HTTP 429 rate-limit events.\n- **How to Migrate to DLL**:\n\n- Add \u0060SelectedSequence\u0060, \u0060SelectedStep\u0060, \u0060SelectedScrape\u0060, \u0060SelectedScrapeField\u0060, \u0060SelectedExtensionTab\u0060, and \u0060ExtensionTabFilterText\u0060 properties to \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060.\n- Overload or update session methods (\u0060AddStepToSequence()\u0060, \u0060RemoveSelectedStep()\u0060, \u0060MoveSelectedStepUp()\u0060, \u0060AddFieldToSelectedScrape()\u0060, \u0060PreviewSelectedScrapeAsync()\u0060, \u0060SwitchToSelectedExtensionTabAsync()\u0060, etc.) to operate directly on the session\u0027s tracked selection state and emit state-change events when the active scrape or sequence configuration changes (such as when a 429 rate-limit updates \u0060PageDelayMs\u0060).\n\n### 3. Server Port \u0026 IPC Mode State (\u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060)\n\n- **Current Location**: \u0060MainForm\u0060 constructor, \u0060BtnStart_Click\u0060, \u0060BtnGenerate_Click\u0060, \u0060BtnExportExtension_Click\u0060, and \u0060SwitchToBrowserTabAsync\u0060 (lines 79, 134\u2013148, 250\u2013255, 257\u2013280, 697\u2013701).\n- **What It Does**:\n\n- Stores the configured server \u0060Port\u0060 and \u0060IpcMode\u0060 exclusively inside WinForms controls (\u0060numPort.Value\u0060 and \u0060cmbMode.SelectedItem\u0060), requiring \u0060MainForm\u0060 to repeatedly cast, fallback-check (\u0060cmbMode.SelectedItem is IpcMode m ? m : AutomationStudioSession.DefaultIpcMode\u0060), and pass \u0060port\u0060 and \u0060mode\u0060 into \u0060_session\u0060 methods.\n- **How to Migrate to DLL**:\n\n- Add \u0060Port\u0060 (auto-clamped via \u0060ClampPort\u0060) and \u0060IpcMode\u0060 properties to \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060.\n- Allow \u0060StartServerAsync()\u0060, \u0060TryStartServerAsync()\u0060, \u0060GenerateUserscript()\u0060, \u0060TryExportChromeExtension()\u0060, \u0060TrySyncDefaultChromeExtensionQuietly()\u0060, and \u0060SwitchToExtensionTabAsync()\u0060 to use the session\u0027s \u0060Port\u0060 and \u0060IpcMode\u0060 properties directly.\n\n### 4. Splitter Initialization Thresholds \u0026 Default Layout Constants (\u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060)\n\n- **Current Location**: \u0060MainForm.EnsureTabSplittersConfigured\u0060, \u0060MainForm.ScaleDpi\u0060, \u0060MainForm.InitializeScraperTabUi\u0060, and \u0060MainForm.InitializeReverseEngineeringTabUi\u0060 (lines 601, 717\u2013763, 1074\u20131076, 1561\u20131562).\n- **What It Does**:\n\n- Contains hardcoded minimum pixel thresholds (\u0060splitLeftSidebar.Height \u003E 220\u0060, \u0060splitDom.Width \u003E 200\u0060, \u0060splitSequences.Width \u003E 300\u0060, \u0060splitEditor.Width \u003E 250\u0060, \u0060splitScraperMain.Width \u003E 300\u0060, \u0060splitScraperRight.Height \u003E 200\u0060, \u0060splitFields.Width \u003E 250\u0060, \u0060splitRevEngMain.Width \u003E 300\u0060, \u0060splitRevEngLeft.Height \u003E 200\u0060) and initial fallback splitter distances (\u0060300\u0060, \u0060220\u0060, \u0060210\u0060, \u0060240\u0060) before delegating to \u0060StudioLayoutMetrics\u0060.\n- Implements its own \u0060ScaleDpi(int value)\u0060 math (\u0060(int)Math.Ceiling(value * (DeviceDpi / 96f))\u0060), duplicating the DPI scaling helper in \u0060StudioLayoutMetrics\u0060 and \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060.\n- **How to Migrate to DLL**:\n\n- Move \u0060ScaleDpi(int value, float dpiScale)\u0060 (or \u0060ScaleDpi(int value, int deviceDpi)\u0060) to \u0060StudioLayoutMetrics\u0060 as a public helper.\n- Add \u0060TryCalculate...SplitterDistance(int totalSize, float dpiScale, out int splitterDistance)\u0060 methods and default splitter distance constants to \u0060StudioLayoutMetrics\u0060 so threshold validation lives inside the DLL rather than \u0060MainForm\u0060.\n\n### 5. DOM Tree Paint-Pass \u0026 Scrollbar Synchronization Orchestration (\u0060TestBedApp\\Controls\\DomTreeView.cs\u0060)\n\n- **Current Location**: \u0060DomTreeView.OnPaint\u0060, \u0060DomTreeView.EnsureItemMeasured\u0060, and \u0060DomTreeView.OnMouseWheel\u0060 (lines 336\u2013446, 528\u2013550).\n- **What It Does**:\n\n- \u0060DomTreeView.OnPaint\u0060 manually orchestrates the visible row range loop (\u0060firstRow..lastRow\u0060), triggers lazy token width measurement (\u0060EnsureItemMeasured\u0060) during painting\u2014which can trigger \u0060UpdateScrollBars()\u0060 mid-paint if \u0060widthIncreased\u0060 is true\u2014and queries \u0060CalculateRowRenderLayout\u0060, \u0060EnumerateAncestorGuideLineXs\u0060, and \u0060EnumerateVisibleTokens\u0060 separately.\n- \u0060DomTreeView.OnMouseWheel\u0060 manually synchronizes \u0060_hScrollBar.Value\u0060 or \u0060_vScrollBar.Value\u0060 after calling \u0060_state.ApplyMouseWheel(...)\u0060.\n- **How to Migrate to DLL**:\n\n- Add a single frame-preparation method on \u0060DomTreeViewportState\u0060 (e.g., \u0060PrepareVisibleRowsForRender\u0060 or \u0060BuildVisibleRowRenderPlans\u0060) that measures all visible rows in \u0060[firstRow, lastRow]\u0060 up front, reports once whether \u0060MaxContentWidth\u0060 increased, and returns the precomputed row layouts, guide line coordinates, and visible token slices for each visible row.\n\n### 6. Hardcoded Status Strings, Fonts, \u0026 Session Disposal (\u0060TestBedApp\\MainForm.cs\u0060 \u0026 \u0060MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060)\n\n- **Current Location**:\n\n- Default status bar strings in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060 (lines 631, 1003, 1460).\n- Font family/size literals (\u0060\u0022Consolas\u0022, 10F\u0060, \u0060\u0022Consolas\u0022, 9.5F\u0060, \u0060\u0022Segoe UI\u0022, 10F\u0060) in \u0060MainForm.cs\u0060, \u0060MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060, and \u0060DomTreeView.cs\u0060.\n- \u0060MainForm.Dispose(bool disposing)\u0060 in \u0060MainForm.Designer.cs\u0060 (lines 14\u201321).\n- **What It Does**:\n\n- Hardcodes initial status label strings (\u0060\u0022Extension: Waiting for connection...\u0022\u0060, \u0060\u0022Scrape Results Preview (0 records)\u0022\u0060, \u0060\u0022Ready \u2014 Connect a browser client and click one of the 4 dump buttons.\u0022\u0060) and font names/sizes in the WinForms layer.\n- Does not dispose \u0060_session\u0060 inside \u0060MainForm.Dispose(bool disposing)\u0060, leaving \u0060_session\u0060\u0027s disposal implicit on process exit.\n- **How to Migrate to DLL**:\n\n- Move default status bar messages and standard font family/point-size constants (\u0060UiFontFamily = \u0022Segoe UI\u0022\u0060, \u0060UiFontSizePt = 10f\u0060, \u0060CodeFontFamily = \u0022Consolas\u0022\u0060, \u0060CodeFontSizePt = 10f\u0060, \u0060CodeDetailsFontSizePt = 9.5f\u0060) into \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 and \u0060StudioTheme\u0060.\n- Call \u0060_session.Dispose()\u0060 in \u0060MainForm.Dispose(bool disposing)\u0060.",
