      "UserPrompt": "The root directory for this project is: C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\nThe following directories are currently tracked/active for this project (place new files in these directories unless otherwise specified):\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\TestBedApp\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BAF Studio\n- C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\n\nPlease update both the readme and the api reference docs so that they correctly identrify the BAF Studio project, its csproj file, and all references to it are renamed from TestBedApp to BAF Studio.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nUpdated \u0060README.md\u0060 and \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\API_REFERENCE.md\u0060 to replace all \u0060TestBedApp\u0060 references with \u0060BAF Studio\u0060 and explicitly document the \u0060BAF Studio\u0060 project directory and \u0060BAF Studio.csproj\u0060 project file:\n\n- **\u0060README.md\u0060**:\n\n- Updated the header icon path from \u0060TestBedApp/baf-studio-icon.svg\u0060 to \u0060BAF Studio/baf-studio-icon.svg\u0060.\n- Updated the CLI run command in Quick Start to \u0060dotnet run --project \u0022BAF Studio/BAF Studio.csproj\u0022\u0060.\n- Standardized UI references to **BAF Studio**.\n- Updated the Repository Structure tree to replace \u0060TestBedApp/\u0060 with \u0060BAF Studio/\u0060 and list \u0060BAF Studio.csproj\u0060 and \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.csproj\u0060.\n- **\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\API_REFERENCE.md\u0060**:\n\n- Added project file (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework/BrowserAutomationFramework.csproj\u0060 and \u0060BAF Studio/BAF Studio.csproj\u0060) and assembly metadata to the document header and Architecture Overview.\n- Updated \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 documentation to include \u0060StudioShortTitle\u0060 and reference **BAF Studio**.\n\n### How to Test\n\n- Open \u0060README.md\u0060 and \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\API_REFERENCE.md\u0060 in a Markdown previewer to verify all links, image paths, and project tree entries render properly.\n- Run \u0060dotnet run --project \u0022BAF Studio/BAF Studio.csproj\u0022\u0060 from the solution root to verify the documented command launches **BAF Studio**.\n\n--CODESTART--\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\README.md**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060md\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n\u003Cp align=\u0022center\u0022\u003E\n  \u003Cimg src=\u0022TestBedApp/baf-studio-icon.svg\u0022 alt=\u0022BAF Studio Icon\u0022 width=\u0022180\u0022 height=\u0022180\u0022 /\u003E\n\u003C/p\u003E\n==== REPLACE\n\u003Cp align=\u0022center\u0022\u003E\n  \u003Cimg src=\u0022BAF Studio/baf-studio-icon.svg\u0022 alt=\u0022BAF Studio Icon\u0022 width=\u0022180\u0022 height=\u0022180\u0022 /\u003E\n\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n\u003E **Important Note for Firefox Users:**  \n\u003E There is **no native Firefox extension yet** for the BAF Browser Extension. If you are automating or scraping in **Firefox**, you must use the **legacy Tampermonkey userscript** (\u0060Generate \u0026 Copy Script (TM)\u0060 in Automation Studio or \u0060ScriptGenerator.Generate(...)\u0060 in C#) until dedicated Firefox extension support is built.\n\n---\n\n## Key Features\n\n### 1. Dual-Transport IPC Engine (WebSocket \u002B CSP-Safe HTTP Fallback)\n* **Full-Duplex WebSockets (\u0060IpcMode.WebSocket\u0060):** Instantaneous command execution, live DOM mutation streaming, and real-time navigation tracking over \u0060ws://127.0.0.1:{port}\u0060.\n* **Automatic CSP Bypass (\u0060IpcMode.HttpPolling\u0060):** If a target website enforces a strict \u0060Content-Security-Policy\u0060 (\u0060connect-src\u0060) that blocks local WebSocket connections, the BAF bridge automatically detects the violation and seamlessly switches to privileged \u0060GM_xmlhttpRequest\u0060 HTTP polling without dropping the session.\n\n### 2. Unpacked Manifest V3 Chrome Extension \u0026 Live Tab Manager\n* **Zero-Config Generation:** Automatically exports and synchronizes the unpacked Manifest V3 Chrome Extension (\u0060manifest.json\u0060, \u0060background.js\u0060, \u0060content_relay.js\u0060, \u0060bridge.js\u0060, \u0060popup.html\u0060, \u0060popup.js\u0060) to match your configured server port.\n* **Live Open-Tab Discovery:** View and filter every open tab in your browser directly from C# or the Automation Studio sidebar.\n==== REPLACE\n\u003E **Important Note for Firefox Users:**  \n\u003E There is **no native Firefox extension yet** for the BAF Browser Extension. If you are automating or scraping in **Firefox**, you must use the **legacy Tampermonkey userscript** (\u0060Generate \u0026 Copy Script (TM)\u0060 in BAF Studio or \u0060ScriptGenerator.Generate(...)\u0060 in C#) until dedicated Firefox extension support is built.\n\n---\n\n## Key Features\n\n### 1. Dual-Transport IPC Engine (WebSocket \u002B CSP-Safe HTTP Fallback)\n* **Full-Duplex WebSockets (\u0060IpcMode.WebSocket\u0060):** Instantaneous command execution, live DOM mutation streaming, and real-time navigation tracking over \u0060ws://127.0.0.1:{port}\u0060.\n* **Automatic CSP Bypass (\u0060IpcMode.HttpPolling\u0060):** If a target website enforces a strict \u0060Content-Security-Policy\u0060 (\u0060connect-src\u0060) that blocks local WebSocket connections, the BAF bridge automatically detects the violation and seamlessly switches to privileged \u0060GM_xmlhttpRequest\u0060 HTTP polling without dropping the session.\n\n### 2. Unpacked Manifest V3 Chrome Extension \u0026 Live Tab Manager\n* **Zero-Config Generation:** Automatically exports and synchronizes the unpacked Manifest V3 Chrome Extension (\u0060manifest.json\u0060, \u0060background.js\u0060, \u0060content_relay.js\u0060, \u0060bridge.js\u0060, \u0060popup.html\u0060, \u0060popup.js\u0060) to match your configured server port.\n* **Live Open-Tab Discovery:** View and filter every open tab in your browser directly from C# or the BAF Studio sidebar.\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n### Option A: Using the BAF Studio GUI\n\n1. **Build and Run BAF Studio:**\n   ~~~bash\n   dotnet build\n   dotnet run --project TestBedApp\n   ~~~\n2. **Start the Server:** Set your desired port (default \u00609999\u0060) and IPC mode (\u0060WebSocket\u0060), then click **Start Server**.\n3. **Connect Your Browser:**\n   * **Chrome / Edge / Brave (Recommended):**\n     1. Click **Export Chrome Extension...** (or use the auto-synced \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\ChromeExtension\u0060 folder).\n     2. Open \u0060chrome://extensions\u0060, enable **Developer mode**, click **Load unpacked**, and select the folder.\n     3. Select any open browser tab in the **Chrome Extension - Open Tabs** panel to inject and switch to it immediately.\n   * **Firefox (or Legacy Userscript Mode):**\n     1. Install the [Tampermonkey](https://www.tampermonkey.net/) extension in Firefox.\n     2. In Automation Studio, configure your target **Match URLs** (or leave **Match Any Site** checked) and click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script (TM)**.\n     3. Create a new userscript in Tampermonkey, paste the clipboard contents, save, and reload your target webpage.\n==== REPLACE\n### Option A: Using the BAF Studio GUI\n\n1. **Build and Run BAF Studio:**\n   ~~~bash\n   dotnet build\n   dotnet run --project \u0022BAF Studio/BAF Studio.csproj\u0022\n   ~~~\n2. **Start the Server:** Set your desired port (default \u00609999\u0060) and IPC mode (\u0060WebSocket\u0060), then click **Start Server**.\n3. **Connect Your Browser:**\n   * **Chrome / Edge / Brave (Recommended):**\n     1. Click **Export Chrome Extension...** (or use the auto-synced \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\\ChromeExtension\u0060 folder).\n     2. Open \u0060chrome://extensions\u0060, enable **Developer mode**, click **Load unpacked**, and select the folder.\n     3. Select any open browser tab in the **Chrome Extension - Open Tabs** panel to inject and switch to it immediately.\n   * **Firefox (or Legacy Userscript Mode):**\n     1. Install the [Tampermonkey](https://www.tampermonkey.net/) extension in Firefox.\n     2. In BAF Studio, configure your target **Match URLs** (or leave **Match Any Site** checked) and click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script (TM)**.\n     3. Create a new userscript in Tampermonkey, paste the clipboard contents, save, and reload your target webpage.\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n## Repository Structure\n\n~~~text\nBrowserAutomationFramework/\n\u251C\u2500\u2500 BrowserAutomationFramework/          # Core .NET 10 Class Library (DLL)\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Automation/                      # AutomationRunner \u0026 AutomationStudioSession facade\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 ChromeExtension/                 # Synced Manifest V3 Chrome Extension files\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Extensions/                      # ReactExtensions for BrowserClient\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Generators/                      # ScriptGenerator (TM) \u0026 ChromeExtensionGenerator\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Models/                          # Project, Scrape, DOM Snapshot, Dump \u0026 Event models\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 ReverseEngineering/              # SiteDumper engine\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Scraping/                        # DataScraper, ScrapeBuilder \u0026 SelectorHelper\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Server/                          # AutomationServer \u0026 BrowserClient IPC engine\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Utils/                           # Windows file-association utilities\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 API_REFERENCE.md                 # Full public API \u0026 IPC protocol reference\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 TestBedApp/                          # BAF Studio \u2014 Dark-mode WinForms IDE (BAF Studio.exe)\n    \u251C\u2500\u2500 Controls/                        # Virtualized DomTreeView control\n    \u251C\u2500\u2500 utils/                           # Dark mode theming utilities\n    \u251C\u2500\u2500 baf-studio-icon.svg              # BAF Studio 512x512 vector application icon\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 MainForm.cs                      # BAF Studio UI wrapper\n~~~\n==== REPLACE\n## Repository Structure\n\n~~~text\nBrowserAutomationFramework/\n\u251C\u2500\u2500 BrowserAutomationFramework/          # Core .NET 10 Class Library (BrowserAutomationFramework.dll)\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Automation/                      # AutomationRunner \u0026 AutomationStudioSession facade\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 ChromeExtension/                 # Synced Manifest V3 Chrome Extension files\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Extensions/                      # ReactExtensions for BrowserClient\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Generators/                      # ScriptGenerator (TM) \u0026 ChromeExtensionGenerator\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Models/                          # Project, Scrape, DOM Snapshot, Dump \u0026 Event models\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 ReverseEngineering/              # SiteDumper engine\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Scraping/                        # DataScraper, ScrapeBuilder \u0026 SelectorHelper\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Server/                          # AutomationServer \u0026 BrowserClient IPC engine\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 Utils/                           # Windows file-association utilities\n\u2502   \u251C\u2500\u2500 BrowserAutomationFramework.csproj# Core library project file\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 API_REFERENCE.md                 # Full public API \u0026 IPC protocol reference\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 BAF Studio/                          # BAF Studio \u2014 Dark-mode WinForms IDE (BAF Studio.exe)\n    \u251C\u2500\u2500 Controls/                        # Virtualized DomTreeView control\n    \u251C\u2500\u2500 utils/                           # Dark mode theming utilities\n    \u251C\u2500\u2500 BAF Studio.csproj                # BAF Studio WinForms project file\n    \u251C\u2500\u2500 baf-studio-icon.svg              # BAF Studio 512x512 vector application icon\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 MainForm.cs                      # BAF Studio UI wrapper\n~~~\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**C:\\Users\\Devtop1\\Documents\\GitHub\\baf\\BrowserAutomationFramework\\API_REFERENCE.md**\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060md\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n**Target Framework:** \u0060.NET 10.0\u0060 (\u0060net10.0\u0060)  \n**Assembly:** \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060  \n**Root Namespace:** \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060\n==== REPLACE\n**Target Framework:** \u0060.NET 10.0\u0060 (\u0060net10.0\u0060)  \n**Core Library Project:** \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework/BrowserAutomationFramework.csproj\u0060 (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060)  \n**Studio IDE Project:** \u0060BAF Studio/BAF Studio.csproj\u0060 (\u0060BAF Studio.exe\u0060, Root Namespace: \u0060BAFStudio\u0060)  \n**Root Namespace:** \u0060BrowserAutomationFramework\u0060\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n| **Generators** | \u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060, \u0060ChromeExtensionGenerator\u0060 | Programmatic generation of Tampermonkey userscripts and Manifest V3 Chrome Extensions. |\n| **High-Level Facade** | \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 | Coordinates \u0060AutomationServer\u0060, \u0060AutomationProject\u0060, \u0060AutomationRunner\u0060, \u0060DataScraper\u0060, and \u0060SiteDumper\u0060 with unified logging. |\n==== REPLACE\n| **Generators** | \u0060ScriptGenerator\u0060, \u0060ChromeExtensionGenerator\u0060 | Programmatic generation of Tampermonkey userscripts and Manifest V3 Chrome Extensions. |\n| **High-Level Facade** | \u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060 | Coordinates \u0060AutomationServer\u0060, \u0060AutomationProject\u0060, \u0060AutomationRunner\u0060, \u0060DataScraper\u0060, and \u0060SiteDumper\u0060 with unified logging for **BAF Studio** (\u0060BAF Studio/BAF Studio.csproj\u0060) and custom hosts. |\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u003C\u003C\u003C\u003C SEARCH\n| \u0060DefaultPort\u0060 | \u0060int\u0060 (\u00609999\u0060) | Default TCP port used by the Automation Studio server. |\n| \u0060MinPort\u0060 / \u0060MaxPort\u0060 | \u0060int\u0060 (\u00601024\u0060 / \u006065535\u0060) | Valid TCP port range bounds. |\n| \u0060ClampPort(int port)\u0060 | \u0060static int\u0060 | Clamps \u0060port\u0060 to \u0060[MinPort, MaxPort]\u0060. |\n| \u0060DefaultTestCommandType\u0060 | \u0060string\u0060 (\u0060\u0022EVAL\u0022\u0060) | Default command type for raw command testing. |\n| \u0060DefaultTestPayload\u0060 | \u0060string\u0060 | Default JS payload for raw command testing. |\n| \u0060DefaultIpcMode\u0060 | \u0060IpcMode\u0060 (\u0060WebSocket\u0060) | Default IPC transport mode. |\n| \u0060StudioTitle\u0060, \u0060StudioVersion\u0060, \u0060StudioDescription\u0060, \u0060StudioAboutMessage\u0060 | \u0060string\u0060 | Application metadata constants. |\n==== REPLACE\n| \u0060DefaultPort\u0060 | \u0060int\u0060 (\u00609999\u0060) | Default TCP port used by the BAF Studio server. |\n| \u0060MinPort\u0060 / \u0060MaxPort\u0060 | \u0060int\u0060 (\u00601024\u0060 / \u006065535\u0060) | Valid TCP port range bounds. |\n| \u0060ClampPort(int port)\u0060 | \u0060static int\u0060 | Clamps \u0060port\u0060 to \u0060[MinPort, MaxPort]\u0060. |\n| \u0060DefaultTestCommandType\u0060 | \u0060string\u0060 (\u0060\u0022EVAL\u0022\u0060) | Default command type for raw command testing. |\n| \u0060DefaultTestPayload\u0060 | \u0060string\u0060 | Default JS payload for raw command testing. |\n| \u0060DefaultIpcMode\u0060 | \u0060IpcMode\u0060 (\u0060WebSocket\u0060) | Default IPC transport mode. |\n| \u0060StudioShortTitle\u0060, \u0060StudioTitle\u0060, \u0060StudioVersion\u0060, \u0060StudioDescription\u0060, \u0060StudioAboutMessage\u0060 | \u0060string\u0060 | BAF Studio application metadata constants. |\n\u003E\u003E\u003E\u003E\n\u0060\u0060\u0060",
