    {
      "Id": "ce63ce00",
      "Timestamp": "2026-10-28T02:34:46.0313482-05:00",
      "UserPrompt": "Perfect! Now lets make a release markdown file (dont dump it to disk). Make the title and the release markdown body.",
      "ModelResponse": "Anti-Agent v1.0\n\nHere is the release title and markdown body for **Browser Automation Framework \u0026 BAF Studio v1.0.0** (not written to disk):\n\n### Release Title\n\n**v1.0.0 \u2014 Browser Automation Framework (BAF) \u0026 BAF Studio**\n\n### Release Markdown Body\n\n# Browser Automation Framework (BAF) \u0026 BAF Studio v1.0.0\n\n**A stealth-first, .NET 10 browser automation, web scraping, and site reverse-engineering framework powered by real browser sessions.**\n\n## Highlights \u0026 Stealth Architecture\n\nUnlike traditional automation tools (**Playwright**, **Puppeteer**, **Selenium**, or **Patchright**) that spawn instrumented browser binaries over the Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) or WebDriver, **BAF** operates inside your **real, everyday browser instance**:\n\n- **Zero CDP / WebDriver Leaks:** No \u0060Runtime.enable\u0060, \u0060navigator.webdriver\u0060, or patched binary signatures.\n- **100% Authentic Browser Fingerprint:** Uses your native TLS/JA3/JA4 handshakes, HTTP/2 frame ordering, GPU/WebGL state, cookies, and established session trust tokens.\n- **Dual-Transport IPC Bridge:** Full-duplex local WebSockets (\u0060ws://127.0.0.1:{port}\u0060) with automatic, seamless fallback to privileged \u0060GM_xmlhttpRequest\u0060 HTTP polling when strict page \u0060Content-Security-Policy\u0060 (\u0060connect-src\u0060) rules block local sockets.\n\n## What\u0027s Included in v1.0.0\n\n### 1. BAF Studio (\u0060BAF Studio.exe\u0060)\n\nA full-featured, dark-mode \u0060.NET 10\u0060 desktop IDE for building, testing, and running browser workflows:\n\n- **Chrome Extension Live Tab Manager:** View, filter, focus, detach, and one-click inject into any open Chromium browser tab in real time.\n- **Virtualized DOM Explorer (\u0060DomTreeView\u0060):** Flicker-free 60\u002B FPS virtualized tree view backed by an O(1) indexed \u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060 (supporting DOM trees up to 300 levels deep).\n- **Two-Way Live Element Highlighting:** Select nodes in the DOM tree to highlight them in the browser, or **middle-click any element in the browser** to immediately highlight, select, and scroll to it in BAF Studio.\n- **Visual Automation Editor:** Build and reorder multi-step \u0060AutomationSequence\u0060 lists with \u0060Click\u0060, \u0060SetValue\u0060, \u0060Navigate\u0060, \u0060EvaluateScript\u0060, \u0060Scrape\u0060, \u0060DumpSite\u0060, and \u0060Custom\u0060 actions.\n- **Interactive Data Scraper Workspace:** Point-and-click field/container selection from the DOM tree, live selector generalization and highlighting,  table/JSON  preview tabs, and one-click CSV/JSON export.\n- **Reverse Engineering Suite:** 4-mode site asset dumper with instant resource filtering and built-in source viewers.\n\n### 2. Core Library (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060)\n\nA 100% UI-agnostic \u0060.NET 10\u0060 class library with zero dependency on Windows Forms, ready to embed in console apps, background workers, or custom hosts:\n\n- **\u0060AutomationServer\u0060 \u0026 \u0060BrowserClient\u0060:** Local HTTP/WebSocket IPC server, automatic WebSocket reconnection across full-page navigations, and coalesced DOM snapshot refreshing.\n- **React \u0026 SPA Extensions (\u0060ReactExtensions\u0060):**\n\n- \u0060ClickReactElementAsync\u0060: Invokes React \u0060__reactProps$\u0060 / \u0060__reactEventHandlers$\u0060 \u0060onClick\u0060 handlers with proxied \u0060isTrusted: true\u0060 events or executes safe in-place/SPA navigation.\n- \u0060SetReactInputValueAsync\u0060: Bypasses React\u0027s native value setter tracker via prototype descriptors and dispatches \u0060input\u0060 and \u0060change\u0060 events.\n- **Fluent \u0026 Declarative Scraping (\u0060DataScraper\u0060 \u0026 \u0060ScrapeBuilder\u0060):**\n\n- **12 Extraction Types:** \u0060InnerText\u0060, \u0060TextContent\u0060, \u0060InnerHtml\u0060, \u0060OuterHtml\u0060, \u0060Value\u0060, \u0060Attribute\u0060, \u0060Href\u0060, \u0060Src\u0060, \u0060DataAttribute\u0060, \u0060ComputedStyle\u0060, \u0060Exists\u0060, and \u0060Count\u0060.\n- **Smart Selector Generalization (\u0060SelectorHelper\u0060):** Automatically generalizes repeating sibling/container selectors and relativizes child selectors to \u0060:scope\u0060.\n- **Multi-Page Pagination:** Supports Next-button clicking, URL pattern templates (\u0060?page={page}\u0060, \u0060?p=1\u0060, etc.), and custom pagination sequences.\n- **Automatic HTTP 429 Rate-Limit Recovery:** Detects HTTP 429 responses via Navigation Timing and header probing, parses \u0060Retry-After\u0060 (relative seconds or HTTP-date), displays an in-browser status banner, waits out the cooldown, adjusts \u0060PageDelayMs\u0060, and retries automatically.\n- **Flexible Output:** Export to JSON, CSV, \u0060DataTable\u0060, or bind directly to strongly-typed C# POCOs via \u0060result.BindTo\u003CT\u003E()\u0060.\n- **Site Reverse Engineering (\u0060SiteDumper\u0060):**\n\n- Dumps **HTML** (clean document \u002B accessible/fetched \u0060\u003Ciframe\u003E\u0060 documents), **CSS** (external \u0060\u003Clink\u003E\u0060, inline \u0060\u003Cstyle\u003E\u0060, CSSOM constructed sheets, and \u0060adoptedStyleSheets\u0060), and **JavaScript** (external \u0060\u003Cscript src\u003E\u0060, inline scripts/JSON, and dynamic scripts via the Performance Resource Timing API).\n- Exports individual assets, combined bundles (\u0060combined.css\u0060, \u0060combined.js\u0060), and a structured \u0060manifest.json\u0060 via \u0060SaveToDirectoryAsync\u0060.\n- **Unified Session Controller (\u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060):** High-level facade coordinating server lifecycle, project persistence, scraping, automation, reverse engineering, and structured color-coded logging.\n\n## Browser Compatibility\n\nBrowserUnpacked MV3 Extension (Recommended)Legacy Tampermonkey Userscript**Google Chrome**SupportedSupported**Microsoft Edge**SupportedSupported**Brave / Vivaldi / Opera**SupportedSupported**Mozilla Firefox**Not Yet Available**Required (Supported)**\n\n**Note for Firefox Users:** Native Firefox extension support is not yet available. To use BAF with Firefox, click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script (TM)** in BAF Studio (or call \u0060ScriptGenerator.Generate(...)\u0060) and install the generated bridge script in **Tampermonkey**.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n- **Launch BAF Studio** (or build from source with \u0060.NET 10.0 SDK\u0060 via \u0060dotnet run --project \u0022BAF Studio/BAF Studio.csproj\u0022\u0060).\n- **Start the Server:** Keep the default port (\u00609999\u0060) and \u0060WebSocket\u0060 IPC mode, then click **Start Server**.\n- **Load the Browser Bridge:**\n\n- **Chromium Browsers:** Click **Export Chrome Extension...**, open \u0060chrome://extensions\u0060, enable **Developer mode**, click **Load unpacked**, and select the exported folder.\n- **Firefox / Tampermonkey:** Click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script (TM)** and paste the script into a new Tampermonkey userscript.\n- **Select a Tab \u0026 Automate:** Click any open tab in the **Chrome Extension - Open Tabs** panel to inject the bridge and begin inspecting the DOM, running workflows, scraping data, or dumping site assets.\n\n## Documentation\n\nSee **[API_REFERENCE.md](https://www.google.com/url?sa=E\u0026q=BrowserAutomationFramework/API_REFERENCE.md)** for complete namespace, class, method, event, and browser IPC protocol documentation.",
      "ModelExplanation": "Here is the release title and markdown body for **Browser Automation Framework \u0026 BAF Studio v1.0.0** (not written to disk):\n\n### Release Title\n\n**v1.0.0 \u2014 Browser Automation Framework (BAF) \u0026 BAF Studio**\n\n### Release Markdown Body\n\n# Browser Automation Framework (BAF) \u0026 BAF Studio v1.0.0\n\n**A stealth-first, .NET 10 browser automation, web scraping, and site reverse-engineering framework powered by real browser sessions.**\n\n## Highlights \u0026 Stealth Architecture\n\nUnlike traditional automation tools (**Playwright**, **Puppeteer**, **Selenium**, or **Patchright**) that spawn instrumented browser binaries over the Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) or WebDriver, **BAF** operates inside your **real, everyday browser instance**:\n\n- **Zero CDP / WebDriver Leaks:** No \u0060Runtime.enable\u0060, \u0060navigator.webdriver\u0060, or patched binary signatures.\n- **100% Authentic Browser Fingerprint:** Uses your native TLS/JA3/JA4 handshakes, HTTP/2 frame ordering, GPU/WebGL state, cookies, and established session trust tokens.\n- **Dual-Transport IPC Bridge:** Full-duplex local WebSockets (\u0060ws://127.0.0.1:{port}\u0060) with automatic, seamless fallback to privileged \u0060GM_xmlhttpRequest\u0060 HTTP polling when strict page \u0060Content-Security-Policy\u0060 (\u0060connect-src\u0060) rules block local sockets.\n\n## What\u0027s Included in v1.0.0\n\n### 1. BAF Studio (\u0060BAF Studio.exe\u0060)\n\nA full-featured, dark-mode \u0060.NET 10\u0060 desktop IDE for building, testing, and running browser workflows:\n\n- **Chrome Extension Live Tab Manager:** View, filter, focus, detach, and one-click inject into any open Chromium browser tab in real time.\n- **Virtualized DOM Explorer (\u0060DomTreeView\u0060):** Flicker-free 60\u002B FPS virtualized tree view backed by an O(1) indexed \u0060DomTreeSnapshot\u0060 (supporting DOM trees up to 300 levels deep).\n- **Two-Way Live Element Highlighting:** Select nodes in the DOM tree to highlight them in the browser, or **middle-click any element in the browser** to immediately highlight, select, and scroll to it in BAF Studio.\n- **Visual Automation Editor:** Build and reorder multi-step \u0060AutomationSequence\u0060 lists with \u0060Click\u0060, \u0060SetValue\u0060, \u0060Navigate\u0060, \u0060EvaluateScript\u0060, \u0060Scrape\u0060, \u0060DumpSite\u0060, and \u0060Custom\u0060 actions.\n- **Interactive Data Scraper Workspace:** Point-and-click field/container selection from the DOM tree, live selector generalization and highlighting,  table/JSON  preview tabs, and one-click CSV/JSON export.\n- **Reverse Engineering Suite:** 4-mode site asset dumper with instant resource filtering and built-in source viewers.\n\n### 2. Core Library (\u0060BrowserAutomationFramework.dll\u0060)\n\nA 100% UI-agnostic \u0060.NET 10\u0060 class library with zero dependency on Windows Forms, ready to embed in console apps, background workers, or custom hosts:\n\n- **\u0060AutomationServer\u0060 \u0026 \u0060BrowserClient\u0060:** Local HTTP/WebSocket IPC server, automatic WebSocket reconnection across full-page navigations, and coalesced DOM snapshot refreshing.\n- **React \u0026 SPA Extensions (\u0060ReactExtensions\u0060):**\n\n- \u0060ClickReactElementAsync\u0060: Invokes React \u0060__reactProps$\u0060 / \u0060__reactEventHandlers$\u0060 \u0060onClick\u0060 handlers with proxied \u0060isTrusted: true\u0060 events or executes safe in-place/SPA navigation.\n- \u0060SetReactInputValueAsync\u0060: Bypasses React\u0027s native value setter tracker via prototype descriptors and dispatches \u0060input\u0060 and \u0060change\u0060 events.\n- **Fluent \u0026 Declarative Scraping (\u0060DataScraper\u0060 \u0026 \u0060ScrapeBuilder\u0060):**\n\n- **12 Extraction Types:** \u0060InnerText\u0060, \u0060TextContent\u0060, \u0060InnerHtml\u0060, \u0060OuterHtml\u0060, \u0060Value\u0060, \u0060Attribute\u0060, \u0060Href\u0060, \u0060Src\u0060, \u0060DataAttribute\u0060, \u0060ComputedStyle\u0060, \u0060Exists\u0060, and \u0060Count\u0060.\n- **Smart Selector Generalization (\u0060SelectorHelper\u0060):** Automatically generalizes repeating sibling/container selectors and relativizes child selectors to \u0060:scope\u0060.\n- **Multi-Page Pagination:** Supports Next-button clicking, URL pattern templates (\u0060?page={page}\u0060, \u0060?p=1\u0060, etc.), and custom pagination sequences.\n- **Automatic HTTP 429 Rate-Limit Recovery:** Detects HTTP 429 responses via Navigation Timing and header probing, parses \u0060Retry-After\u0060 (relative seconds or HTTP-date), displays an in-browser status banner, waits out the cooldown, adjusts \u0060PageDelayMs\u0060, and retries automatically.\n- **Flexible Output:** Export to JSON, CSV, \u0060DataTable\u0060, or bind directly to strongly-typed C# POCOs via \u0060result.BindTo\u003CT\u003E()\u0060.\n- **Site Reverse Engineering (\u0060SiteDumper\u0060):**\n\n- Dumps **HTML** (clean document \u002B accessible/fetched \u0060\u003Ciframe\u003E\u0060 documents), **CSS** (external \u0060\u003Clink\u003E\u0060, inline \u0060\u003Cstyle\u003E\u0060, CSSOM constructed sheets, and \u0060adoptedStyleSheets\u0060), and **JavaScript** (external \u0060\u003Cscript src\u003E\u0060, inline scripts/JSON, and dynamic scripts via the Performance Resource Timing API).\n- Exports individual assets, combined bundles (\u0060combined.css\u0060, \u0060combined.js\u0060), and a structured \u0060manifest.json\u0060 via \u0060SaveToDirectoryAsync\u0060.\n- **Unified Session Controller (\u0060AutomationStudioSession\u0060):** High-level facade coordinating server lifecycle, project persistence, scraping, automation, reverse engineering, and structured color-coded logging.\n\n## Browser Compatibility\n\nBrowserUnpacked MV3 Extension (Recommended)Legacy Tampermonkey Userscript**Google Chrome**SupportedSupported**Microsoft Edge**SupportedSupported**Brave / Vivaldi / Opera**SupportedSupported**Mozilla Firefox**Not Yet Available**Required (Supported)**\n\n**Note for Firefox Users:** Native Firefox extension support is not yet available. To use BAF with Firefox, click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script (TM)** in BAF Studio (or call \u0060ScriptGenerator.Generate(...)\u0060) and install the generated bridge script in **Tampermonkey**.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n- **Launch BAF Studio** (or build from source with \u0060.NET 10.0 SDK\u0060 via \u0060dotnet run --project \u0022BAF Studio/BAF Studio.csproj\u0022\u0060).\n- **Start the Server:** Keep the default port (\u00609999\u0060) and \u0060WebSocket\u0060 IPC mode, then click **Start Server**.\n- **Load the Browser Bridge:**\n\n- **Chromium Browsers:** Click **Export Chrome Extension...**, open \u0060chrome://extensions\u0060, enable **Developer mode**, click **Load unpacked**, and select the exported folder.\n- **Firefox / Tampermonkey:** Click **Generate \u0026 Copy Script (TM)** and paste the script into a new Tampermonkey userscript.\n- **Select a Tab \u0026 Automate:** Click any open tab in the **Chrome Extension - Open Tabs** panel to inject the bridge and begin inspecting the DOM, running workflows, scraping data, or dumping site assets.\n\n## Documentation\n\nSee **[API_REFERENCE.md](https://www.google.com/url?sa=E\u0026q=BrowserAutomationFramework/API_REFERENCE.md)** for complete namespace, class, method, event, and browser IPC protocol documentation.",
